window.NPR=[{"code": "20261120-1", "ch": "2026-11-20　週五", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Judges have put Trump's arch and golf course on hold, but only for a matter of days　／　法官暫停了川普的拱門和高爾夫球場，但只持續了幾天", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Rachel Treisman，全文共 11 段、17 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：一名聯邦法官曾兩度推遲川普拱門的建設。另一個是保持東波托馬克公園開放。週四，擬議的高爾夫球場重新設計得到了聯邦藝術小組的不同回饋。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6047151/trump-arch-golf-course-judge-orders"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "一名聯邦法官將川普總統華盛頓拱門的建設禁令延長了兩週，對於不想看到這…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "A federal judge has extended her block on construction of President Trump's D.C. arch for two weeks, another short-term victory for those who don't want to see the 250-foot structure break ground.", "zh": "一名聯邦法官將川普總統華盛頓拱門的建設禁令延長了兩週，對於不想看到這座 250 英尺高的建築破土動工的人來說，這又是一次短期勝利。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "華盛頓地區法官 Tanya Chutkan 週三延長了臨時限制令，即…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "D.C. District Judge Tanya Chutkan extended her temporary **restraining** order on Wednesday, the day before it was set to **expire**.", "zh": "華盛頓地區法官 Tanya Chutkan 週三延長了臨時限制令，即臨時限制令**到期**的前一天。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She originally stepped in to block construction on the night of Nov. 5, after the National Capital Planning Commission and National Park Service gave the arch final approval and the Trump administration said construction could begin imminently.", "zh": "在國家首都規劃委員會和國家公園管理局給予拱門最終批准以及川普政府表示施工可以立即開始之後，她最初於 11 月 5 日晚介入阻止施工。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "川普政府並未尋求批准，稱拱門是由國會於 1925 年授權在同一地點建…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "The Trump administration has not sought that approval, arguing the arch is covered by Congress' authorization in 1925 of a pair of 166-foot columns at the same location, which were never built.", "zh": "川普政府並未尋求批准，稱拱門是由國會於 1925 年授權在同一地點建造一對 166 英尺高的柱子覆蓋的，但這些柱子從未建成。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "在法庭文件和最近公佈的網站中，政府將建造這座拱門視為緊急事項——既是…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "In court filings and a recently unveiled website, the administration **characterizes** building the arch as a matter of **urgency** — both to complete that century-old vision and to facilitate national security.", "zh": "在法庭文件和最近公佈的網站中，政府將建造這座拱門視為緊急事項——既是為了完成百年願景，也是為了促進國家安全。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Trump said in September that the arch would double as a military complex, but the plans that got final approval this month don't include any details to that effect.", "zh": "川普在九月表示，拱門將兼作軍事設施，但本月獲得最終批准的計畫並未包含任何相關細節。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "在本週的一份聲明中，國防部長皮特·赫格斯的幕僚長里基·布里亞告訴法庭…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "In a declaration this week, Ricky Buria, chief of staff to Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, told the court that the agency is \"currently in the planning process to determine how to **integrate** national defense uses … into the Arch without changing the existing plans for the Arch.\"", "zh": "在本週的一份聲明中，國防部長皮特·赫格斯的幕僚長里基·布里亞告訴法庭，該機構“目前正在規劃過程中，以確定如何將國防用途……**整合**到拱門中，而不改變拱門的現有計劃。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "但高爾夫球場本身目前無人值守，因為其營運商租約已於週日到期。但這並沒…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "But the golf course itself is currently unstaffed, since its operator lease **expired** on Sunday.", "zh": "但高爾夫球場本身目前無人值守，因為其營運商租約已於週日**到期**。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That hasn't stopped locals from showing up and teeing off, finding creative ways to mark the holes after the flagsticks were removed from the course.", "zh": "但這並沒有阻止當地人出現並開球，在旗桿從球場上拆除後，他們尋找創意的方法來標記球洞。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "雷耶斯已命令雙方權衡她是否有權命令政府保持高爾夫球場開放。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Reyes has ordered both parties to weigh in on whether she has the authority to order the government to keep the golf course open.", "zh": "雷耶斯已命令雙方權衡她是否有權命令政府保持高爾夫球場開放。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "與此同時，政府週四在聯邦審查程序中又向前邁出了一步。內政部向美術委員…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "In the meantime, the administration took another step forward in the federal review process on Thursday.", "zh": "與此同時，政府週四在聯邦審查程序中又向前邁出了一步。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The Interior Department presented its plan for the golf course to the Commission of Fine Arts, one of two federal agencies which would need to approve the project.", "zh": "內政部向美術委員會提交了高爾夫球場的計劃，該委員會是需要批准該專案的兩個聯邦機構之一。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "委員會秘書 Thomas Luebke 表示，大約 700 名公眾在…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Commission Secretary Thomas Luebke said some 700 members of the public submitted comments ahead of the meeting, all but three in opposition to the golf course proposal.", "zh": "委員會秘書 Thomas Luebke 表示，大約 700 名公眾在會議前提交了意見，其中除三人外均反對高爾夫球場提案。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "最大的擔憂在於，公園的周邊環線將被取消，所有級別的高爾夫球手、騎自行…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "The biggest concerns had to do with making the park less accessible to **golfers** of all levels, as well as **cyclists**, runners and picnickers who use the park's **perimeter** loop, which would be eliminated.", "zh": "最大的擔憂在於，公園的周邊環線將被取消，所有級別的**高爾夫球手**、騎自行車者、跑步者和野餐者都難以進入公園。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "There were other concerns about the impact of major road races — like the Marine Corps Marathon — that use that road, the loss of historic cherry trees and the cost of the project (the Interior Department said **deferred** maintenance alone would cost $43 million but did not specify how much the renovations would cost).", "zh": "人們也擔心使用這條道路的主要公路比賽（例如海軍陸戰隊馬拉鬆比賽）的影響、歷史悠久的櫻桃樹的消失以及該專案的成本（內政部表示，僅延期維護就將花費 4300 萬美元，但沒有具體說明翻修費用是多少）。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "政治法官下令對司法部在川普高爾夫球場案中可能存在的不當行為進行調查 …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Politics Judge orders an inquiry into potential DOJ **misconduct** in Trump's golf course case Trump has repeatedly described the East Potomac golf course as **decrepit** and dangerous, and challenged Reyes' authority over the project.", "zh": "政治法官下令對司法部在川普高爾夫球場案中可能存在的**不當行為**進行調查 川普多次稱東波托馬克高爾夫球場破舊且危險，並挑戰雷耶斯對該專案的權威。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Over the weekend, he **reiterated** that Reyes was appointed by President Biden and slammed her decision as \"highly destructive and political.\"", "zh": "週末，他**重申**雷耶斯是由拜登總統任命的，並抨擊她的決定「具有高度破壞性和政治性」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "一名聯邦法官將川普總統華盛頓拱門的建設禁令延長了兩週，對於不想看到這座 250 英尺高的建築破土動工的人來說，這又是一次短期勝利。　華盛頓地區法官 Tanya Chutkan 週三延長了臨時限制令，即臨時限制令到期的前一天。在國家首都規劃委員會和國家公園管理局給予拱門最終批准以及川普政府表示施工可以立即開始之後，她最初於 11 月 5 日晚介入阻止施工。　川普政府並未尋求批准，稱拱門是由國會於 1925 年授權在同一地點建造一對 166 英尺高的柱子覆蓋的，但這些柱子從未建成。　在法庭文件和最近公佈的網站中，政府將建造這座拱門視為緊急事項——既是為了完成百年願景，也是為了促進國家安全。川普在九月表示，拱門將兼作軍事設施，但本月獲得最終批准的計畫並未包含任何相關細節。　在本週的一份聲明中，國防部長皮特·赫格斯的幕僚長里基·布里亞告訴法庭，該機構“目前正在規劃過程中，以確定如何將國防用途……整合到拱門中，而不改變拱門的現有計劃。”　但高爾夫球場本身目前無人值守，因為其營運商租約已於週日到期。但這並沒有阻止當地人出現並開球，在旗桿從球場上拆除後，他們尋找創意的方法來標記球洞。　雷耶斯已命令雙方權衡她是否有權命令政府保持高爾夫球場開放。　與此同時，政府週四在聯邦審查程序中又向前邁出了一步。內政部向美術委員會提交了高爾夫球場的計劃，該委員會是需要批准該專案的兩個聯邦機構之一。　委員會秘書 Thomas Luebke 表示，大約 700 名公眾在會議前提交了意見，其中除三人外均反對高爾夫球場提案。　最大的擔憂在於，公園的周邊環線將被取消，所有級別的高爾夫球手、騎自行車者、跑步者和野餐者都難以進入公園。人們也擔心使用這條道路的主要公路比賽（例如海軍陸戰隊馬拉鬆比賽）的影響、歷史悠久的櫻桃樹的消失以及該專案的成本（內政部表示，僅延期維護就將花費 4300 萬美元，但沒有具體說明翻修費用是多少）。　政治法官下令對司法部在川普高爾夫球場案中可能存在的不當行為進行調查 川普多次稱東波托馬克高爾夫球場破舊且危險，並挑戰雷耶斯對該專案的權威。週末，他重申雷耶斯是由拜登總統任命的，並抨擊她的決定「具有高度破壞性和政治性」。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "decrepit", "sf": "decrepit", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "老化", "syn": "aged, timeworn, withered", "tip": "其他意思　衰老、衰朽　|　英英定義　Weakened or worn out from age or wear.　|　本文例句　Politics Judge orders an inquiry into potential DOJ misconduct in Trump's golf course case Trump has repeatedly described the East Potomac golf course as decrepit and dangerous, and challenged Reyes' authority over the project.　|　例句中譯　政治法官下令對司法部在川普高爾夫球場案中可能存在的不當行為進行調查 川普多次稱東波托馬克高爾夫球場破舊且危險，並挑戰雷耶斯對該專案的權威。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "reiterated", "sf": "reiterated", "pos": "v.", "zh": "重申", "syn": "repeat, repeat", "tip": "英英定義　To say or do (something) for a second time, such as for emphasis.　|　本文例句　Over the weekend, he reiterated that Reyes was appointed by President Biden and slammed her decision as \"highly destructive and political.　|　例句中譯　週末，他重申雷耶斯是由拜登總統任命的，並抨擊她的決定「具有高度破壞性和政治性」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "characterize", "sf": "characterizes", "pos": "v.", "zh": "表徵", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　表示 ... 的特色、賦予 ... 特色、臧否　|　英英定義　To depict someone or something a particular way (often negative).　|　本文例句　In court filings and a recently unveiled website, the administration characterizes building the arch as a matter of urgency — both to complete that century-old vision and to facilitate national security.　|　例句中譯　在法庭文件和最近公佈的網站中，政府將建造這座拱門視為緊急事項——既是為了完成百年願景，也是為了促進國家安全。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "golfer", "sf": "golfers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "高爾夫球手", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Someone who plays golf.　|　本文例句　But the golf course itself is currently unstaffed, since its operator lease expired on Sunday.　|　例句中譯　但高爾夫球場本身目前無人值守，因為其營運商租約已於週日到期。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "restraining", "sf": "restraining", "pos": "v.", "zh": "抑制", "syn": "check, limit, restrain", "tip": "其他意思　礙、按、按捺、憋　|　英英定義　To control or keep in check.　|　本文例句　District Judge Tanya Chutkan extended her temporary restraining order on Wednesday, the day before it was set to expire.　|　例句中譯　地區法官 Tanya Chutkan 於週三延長了臨時限制令，即臨時限制令到期的前一天。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "deferred", "sf": "deferred", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "延後的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　緩召的、延期的　|　英英定義　To delay or postpone　|　本文例句　There were other concerns about the impact of major road races — like the Marine Corps Marathon — that use that road, the loss of historic cherry trees and the cost of the project (the Interior Department said deferred maintenance alone would cost $43 million but did not specify how much the renovations would cost).　|　例句中譯　人們也擔心使用這條道路的主要公路比賽（例如海軍陸戰隊馬拉鬆比賽）的影響、歷史悠久的櫻桃樹的消失以及該專案的成本（內政部表示，僅延期維護就將花費 4300 萬美元，但沒有具體說明翻修費用是多少）。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "expire", "sf": "expire", "pos": "v.", "zh": "到期", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　斷气、絕氣、滿　|　英英定義　To die.　|　本文例句　District Judge Tanya Chutkan extended her temporary restraining order on Wednesday, the day before it was set to expire.　|　例句中譯　地區法官 Tanya Chutkan 於週三延長了臨時限制令，即臨時限制令到期的前一天。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "urgency", "sf": "urgency", "pos": "n.", "zh": "緊迫性", "syn": "clamancy, exigency", "tip": "其他意思　急、迫切性、毅、毅力　|　英英定義　The quality or condition of being urgent　|　本文例句　In court filings and a recently unveiled website, the administration characterizes building the arch as a matter of urgency — both to complete that century-old vision and to facilitate national security.　|　例句中譯　在法庭文件和最近公佈的網站中，政府將建造這座拱門視為緊急事項——既是為了完成百年願景，也是為了促進國家安全。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "misconduct", "sf": "misconduct", "pos": "n.", "zh": "不當行為", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　不規矩、壞事、處理不當、幹壞事　|　英英定義　Behavior that is considered to be unacceptable.　|　本文例句　Politics Judge orders an inquiry into potential DOJ misconduct in Trump's golf course case Trump has repeatedly described the East Potomac golf course as decrepit and dangerous, and challenged Reyes' authority over the project.　|　例句中譯　政治法官下令對司法部在川普高爾夫球場案中可能存在的不當行為進行調查 川普多次稱東波托馬克高爾夫球場破舊且危險，並挑戰雷耶斯對該專案的權威。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "perimeter", "sf": "perimeter", "pos": "n.", "zh": "週長", "syn": "premises, circumference", "tip": "其他意思　埸　|　英英定義　The sum of the distance of all the lengths of the sides of an object.　|　本文例句　The biggest concerns had to do with making the park less accessible to golfers of all levels, as well as cyclists, runners and picnickers who use the park's perimeter loop, which would be eliminated.　|　例句中譯　最大的擔憂在於，公園的周邊環線將被取消，所有級別的高爾夫球手、騎自行車者、跑步者和野餐者都難以進入公園。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "cyclists", "sf": "cyclists", "pos": "n.", "zh": "騎自行車的人", "syn": "bicyclist, biker, cycler", "tip": "英英定義　A person who rides a cycle, especially a bicycle, or who habitually engages in cycling.　|　本文例句　The biggest concerns had to do with making the park less accessible to golfers of all levels, as well as cyclists, runners and picnickers who use the park's perimeter loop, which would be eliminated.　|　例句中譯　最大的擔憂在於，公園的周邊環線將被取消，所有級別的高爾夫球手、騎自行車者、跑步者和野餐者都難以進入公園。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "integrate", "sf": "integrate", "pos": "v.", "zh": "整合", "syn": "embody, fuse, merge", "tip": "其他意思　合成、合流、結合、聯繫　|　英英定義　To form into one whole; to make entire; to complete; to renew; to restore; to perfect.　|　本文例句　In a declaration this week, Ricky Buria, chief of staff to Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, told the court that the agency is \"currently in the planning process to determine how to integrate national defense uses … into the Arch without changing the existing plans for the Arch.　|　例句中譯　在本週的聲明中，國防部長皮特·赫格斯的幕僚長里基·布里亞告訴法庭，該機構「目前正在規劃過程中，以確定如何將國防用途……整合到拱門中，而不改變拱門的現有計劃。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6047151/trump-arch-golf-course-judge-orders"}, {"code": "20261120-2", "ch": "2026-11-20　週五", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "The 'Magic Six': How to strengthen your marriage in midlife　／　「魔法六」：如何在中年鞏固你的婚姻", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Allison Aubrey，全文共 18 段、51 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：隨著年齡的增長，我們如何維持健康的戀愛關係？艾莉森·奧布里和斯科特·德特羅談論健康的晚年關係的科學。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-5996688/magic-6-marriage-tips-nina-totenberg-relationships"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "本篇較長，站上只收前 18 段；想讀完整篇請點上方的 NPR 原文連結。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "你曾在車上與配偶爭吵過嗎？ NPR 的 Nina Totenberg…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Ever argued with your spouse in the car?", "zh": "你曾在車上與配偶爭吵過嗎？"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "NPR's Nina Totenberg can relate.", "zh": "NPR 的 Nina Totenberg 也有同感。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "她和她的丈夫 David Reines 已經結婚 26 年了，而在路…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "She and her husband, David Reines, have been married for 26 years, and it's on the road where they're most likely to have a spat.", "zh": "她和她的丈夫 David Reines 已經結婚 26 年了，而在路上他們最有可能發生口角。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The car is awful,\" Totenberg told me, laughing.", "zh": "「這輛車太糟糕了，」托滕伯格笑著告訴我。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It comes down partly to the brakes.", "zh": "部分原因在於煞車。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She taps them \"way before\" Reines does.", "zh": "她「遠早於」雷恩斯敲擊了它們。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And when another driver cuts him off, he sometimes wants to return the favor.", "zh": "當另一位司機超車時，他有時會想要回報。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Totenberg's advice from the passenger seat: \"Don't take the bait.\"", "zh": "托滕伯格在乘客座位上的建議是：“不要上當。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "它是如此相關。正如 Reines 所說，“26 年後你不可能沒有衝突…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "It's so **relatable**.", "zh": "它是如此相關。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And as Reines put it, \"You can't not have some conflict after 26 years.", "zh": "正如 Reines 所說，「26 年後你不可能不發生一些衝突。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I think the secret is how you deal with it.\" (They began our interview for this episode of Your Turn by giving each other a kiss!)", "zh": "我認為秘密在於你如何處理它。 」（他們以互相親吻開始我們這一集《輪到你了》的採訪！）", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "當我們問「接下來會發生什麼事？」人到中年，誰站在我們身邊很重要。孩子…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "As we ask \"What comes next?\" in **midlife**, who's standing beside us matters a lot.", "zh": "當我們問「接下來會發生什麼事？」人到**中年**，誰站在我們身邊很重要。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Kids leave home, careers shift, and relationships can change, too.", "zh": "孩子離開家、職業轉變、人際關係也會改變。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So what does a good partnership look like at this stage?", "zh": "那麼現階段良好的合作關係是什麼樣的呢？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "當人們問雷恩斯他們的婚姻為何成功時，他指出了四個「L」：", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "When people ask Reines why their marriage works, he points to four L's:", "zh": "當人們問雷恩斯他們的婚姻為何成功時，他指出了四個「L」："}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "喜歡。你們真的互相喜歡嗎？對萊因斯來說，尊重是其中的一部分。他說他完…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Do you actually like each other?", "zh": "你們真的互相喜歡嗎？"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "For Reines, respect is part of this.", "zh": "對萊因斯來說，尊重是其中的一部分。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He says he has total respect for her work, and she respects his career, too.", "zh": "他說他完全尊重她的工作，她也尊重他的職業生涯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He is a retired trauma surgeon and now keeps busy as a volunteer at the Library of Congress and serves on boards.", "zh": "他是一名退休的創傷外科醫生，現在作為國會圖書館的志工而忙碌，並在董事會任職。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Each of them also keeps a strong sense of self.", "zh": "他們每個人也都保持著強烈的自我意識。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Although we meld,\" Reines says.", "zh": "「儘管我們融為一體，」雷因斯說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"I still have me, and she still has her.\"", "zh": "“我還有我，她還有她。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "慾望。身體上的親密關係很重要。他們每天接吻，「一直」牽手，並且推遲購…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Physical **intimacy** matters.", "zh": "身體上的親密關係很重要。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They kiss every day, hold hands, \"all the time,\" and have held off on buying a king-size bed.", "zh": "他們每天接吻，「一直」牽手，並且推遲購買特大號床。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In hotel beds, they joke, they can't find each other if the bed is too big.", "zh": "他們開玩笑說，在飯店的床上，如果床太大，他們就找不到彼此。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "笑。他說她是他所知道的最有幽默感的人之一。他們每天都在一起歡笑。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "He says she has one of the best senses of humor he knows.", "zh": "他說她是他所知道的最有幽默感的人之一。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They laugh together every day.", "zh": "他們每天都在一起歡笑。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "我還與臨床心理學家朱莉·施瓦茨·戈特曼進行了交談，我在我的書《輪到你…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "I also talked with clinical psychologist Julie Schwartz Gottman who I interviewed for my book, Your Turn.", "zh": "我還與臨床心理學家朱莉·施瓦茨·戈特曼進行了交談，我在我的書《輪到你了》中採訪了她。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She and her husband, John Gottman, co-founded the Gottman Institute and are two of the best-known names in relationship science, and co-authors of Fight Right: How Successful Couples Turn Conflict Into Connection, where they describe the \"Four Horseman\" which are four destructive communication patterns that can help predict the breakdown of a relationship.", "zh": "她和她的丈夫約翰·戈特曼 (John Gottman) 共同創立了戈特曼研究所，是關係科學領域最知名的兩位人物，也是《正確鬥爭：成功夫妻如何將衝突轉化為聯繫》一書的合著者，他們在書中描述了“四騎士”，這是四種破壞性的溝通模式，可以幫助預測關係的破裂。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "戈特曼指出，研究表明，許多雙薪夫婦在一起的時間很少，而且大部分的交流…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "Gottman points to research that shows many dual-career couples spend little time together and much of the communication can be **transactional**.", "zh": "戈特曼指出，研究表明，許多雙薪夫婦在一起的時間很少，而且大部分的交流都是交易性。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Did you call the **plumber**? Did you walk the dog?", "zh": "你打電話給**水管工**了嗎？你遛狗了嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "戈特曼夫婦發現，夫妻可以透過每週有意識地抽出大約六個小時在一起，並改…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "The Gottmans found that couples can improve their relationships by intentionally **carving** out about six hours a week together, and making changes to small, daily and weekly habits.", "zh": "戈特曼夫婦發現，夫妻可以透過每週有意識地抽出大約六個小時在一起，並改變每天和每週的小習慣來改善他們的關係。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They call it the Magic Six.", "zh": "他們稱之為「神奇六人組」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "其中一些事情可能聽起來很明顯，但通常當夫妻太忙或分心時，這些事情就會…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "Some of these things may sound obvious, yet **oftentimes** these are the very things that can fall away when couples are too busy or distracted.", "zh": "其中一些事情可能聽起來很明顯，但通常當夫妻太忙或分心時，這些事情就會消失。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And she says it's **illuminating** when couples actually track progress.", "zh": "她說，當夫妻真正追蹤進步時，這很有啟發性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "分別（每天幾分鐘）。早上離開之前，花幾分鐘時間與伴侶交流當天發生的事…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "Partings (a few minutes each day).", "zh": "分別（每天幾分鐘）。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Before you leave in the morning, spend a few minutes communicating about what's happening in your partner's day.", "zh": "早上離開之前，花幾分鐘時間與伴侶交流當天發生的事情。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "聚會（每天約 20 分鐘）。在一天的工作結束時，分享一個親吻或身體上…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "Reunions (about 20 minutes a day).", "zh": "聚會（每天約 20 分鐘）。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "At the end of the **workday**, share a kiss or physical affection.", "zh": "在一天的工作結束時，分享一個親吻或身體上的愛撫。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Then have a 20-minute stress-reducing conversation about your day.", "zh": "然後進行 20 分鐘的關於您一天的減壓談話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "欽佩和欣賞（每週 35 分鐘）。每天花大約五分鐘表達真誠的感激之情或…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "Admiration and appreciation (35 minutes a week).", "zh": "欽佩和欣賞（每週 35 分鐘）。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Spend about five minutes a day expressing genuine gratitude or naming a **trait** you admire in your partner.", "zh": "每天花大約五分鐘表達真誠的感激之情或說出你欣賞伴侶的一個特質。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Or tell a story to remind each other.", "zh": "或講一個故事來互相提醒。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "關懷（每週 35 分鐘）。每天大約進行五分鐘的身體接觸，例如睡前牽手…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Affection (35 minutes a week).", "zh": "關懷（每週 35 分鐘）。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That works out to about five minutes a day on physical touch, such as holding hands or **cuddling** before sleep.", "zh": "每天大約進行五分鐘的身體接觸，例如睡前牽手或擁抱。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "約會之夜（每週 2 小時）。一起享受無干擾的時光，享受在一起的時光。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "Date night (2 hours a week).", "zh": "約會之夜（每週 2 小時）。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Have **distraction-free** time together to enjoy being together.", "zh": "一起享受無干擾的時光，享受在一起的時光。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It doesn't need to be dinner and a show.", "zh": "它不需要是晚餐和表演。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It can be a low-key hike, a museum visit or any activity you enjoy.", "zh": "它可以是低調的徒步旅行、參觀博物館或任何您喜歡的活動。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "工會狀況會議（每週 1 小時）。回顧哪些進展順利，以及哪些問題或不起…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "State of the union meeting (1 hour a week).", "zh": "工會狀況會議（每週 1 小時）。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Review what's going well as well as concerns or things that are not working, and then talk things out.", "zh": "回顧哪些進展順利，以及哪些問題或不起作用，然後將問題說出來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "你曾在車上與配偶爭吵過嗎？ NPR 的 Nina Totenberg 也有同感。　她和她的丈夫 David Reines 已經結婚 26 年了，而在路上他們最有可能發生口角。 「這輛車太糟糕了，」托滕伯格笑著告訴我。部分原因在於煞車。她「遠早於」雷恩斯敲擊了它們。當另一位司機超車時，他有時會想要回報。托滕伯格在乘客座位上的建議是：“不要上當。”　它是如此相關。正如 Reines 所說，“26 年後你不可能沒有衝突。我認為秘密在於你如何處理它。” （他們以互相親吻開始了我們這一集《輪到你了》的採訪！）　當我們問「接下來會發生什麼事？」人到中年，誰站在我們身邊很重要。孩子離開家、職業轉變、人際關係也會改變。那麼現階段良好的合作關係是什麼樣的呢？　當人們問雷恩斯他們的婚姻為何成功時，他指出了四個「L」：　喜歡。你們真的互相喜歡嗎？對萊因斯來說，尊重是其中的一部分。他說他完全尊重她的工作，她也尊重他的職業生涯。他是一名退休的創傷外科醫生，現在作為國會圖書館的志工而忙碌，並在董事會任職。他們每個人也都保持著強烈的自我意識。 「儘管我們融為一體，」雷因斯說。 “我還有我，她還有她。”　慾望。身體上的親密關係很重要。他們每天接吻，「一直」牽手，並且推遲購買特大號床。他們開玩笑說，在飯店的床上，如果床太大，他們就找不到彼此。　笑。他說她是他所知道的最有幽默感的人之一。他們每天都在一起歡笑。　我還與臨床心理學家朱莉·施瓦茨·戈特曼進行了交談，我在我的書《輪到你了》中採訪了她。她和她的丈夫約翰·戈特曼 (John Gottman) 共同創立了戈特曼研究所，是關係科學領域最知名的兩位人物，也是《正確鬥爭：成功夫妻如何將衝突轉化為聯繫》一書的合著者，他們在書中描述了“四騎士”，這是四種破壞性的溝通模式，可以幫助預測關係的破裂。　戈特曼指出，研究表明，許多雙薪夫婦在一起的時間很少，而且大部分的交流都是交易性。你打電話給水管工了嗎？你遛狗了嗎？　戈特曼夫婦發現，夫妻可以透過每週有意識地抽出大約六個小時在一起，並改變每天和每週的小習慣來改善他們的關係。他們稱之為「神奇六人組」。　其中一些事情可能聽起來很明顯，但通常當夫妻太忙或分心時，這些事情就會消失。她說，當夫妻真正追蹤進步時，這很有啟發性。　分別（每天幾分鐘）。早上離開之前，花幾分鐘時間與伴侶交流當天發生的事情。　聚會（每天約 20 分鐘）。在一天的工作結束時，分享一個親吻或身體上的愛撫。然後進行 20 分鐘的關於您一天的減壓談話。　欽佩和欣賞（每週 35 分鐘）。每天花大約五分鐘表達真誠的感激之情或說出你欣賞伴侶的一個特質。或講一個故事來互相提醒。　關懷（每週 35 分鐘）。每天大約進行五分鐘的身體接觸，例如睡前牽手或擁抱。　約會之夜（每週 2 小時）。一起享受無干擾的時光，享受在一起的時光。它不需要是晚餐和表演。它可以是低調的徒步旅行、參觀博物館或任何您喜歡的活動。　工會狀況會議（每週 1 小時）。回顧哪些進展順利，以及哪些問題或不起作用，然後將問題說出來。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "midlife", "sf": "midlife", "pos": "n.", "zh": "中年", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　The middle period of one's life.　|　本文例句　As we ask \"What comes next?\" in midlife, who's standing beside us matters a lot.　|　例句中譯　當我們問「接下來會發生什麼事？」人到中年，誰站在我們身邊很重要。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "transactional", "sf": "transactional", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "交易性的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Of, pertaining to or involving transactions　|　本文例句　Gottman points to research that shows many dual-career couples spend little time together and much of the communication can be transactional.　|　例句中譯　戈特曼指出，研究表明，許多雙薪夫婦在一起的時間很少，而且大部分的交流都是交易性。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "workday", "sf": "workday", "pos": "n.", "zh": "工作日", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　勞動日　|　英英定義　Suitable for everyday use.　|　本文例句　At the end of the workday, share a kiss or physical affection.　|　例句中譯　在一天的工作結束時，分享一個親吻或身體上的愛撫。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "oftentimes", "sf": "oftentimes", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "很多時候", "syn": "oftentime", "tip": "英英定義　Frequently　|　本文例句　Some of these things may sound obvious, yet oftentimes these are the very things that can fall away when couples are too busy or distracted.　|　例句中譯　其中一些事情可能聽起來很明顯，但通常當夫妻太忙或分心時，這些事情就會消失。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "illuminate", "sf": "illuminating", "pos": "v.", "zh": "照亮", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　發光、暉映、耀、耀眼　|　英英定義　Someone thought to have an unusual degree of enlightenment.　|　本文例句　And she says it's illuminating when couples actually track progress.　|　例句中譯　她說，當夫妻真正追蹤進步時，這很有啟發性。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "relatable", "sf": "relatable", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "相關的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Able to be related to something else; connected with.", "trap": ""}, {"w": "plumber", "sf": "plumber", "pos": "n.", "zh": "水管工", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　管子工、水管工人　|　英英定義　One who works in or with lead.", "trap": ""}, {"w": "cuddle", "sf": "cuddling", "pos": "v.", "zh": "偎", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　撫抱、摟、摟抱　|　英英定義　A snuggle; an affectionate embrace, often given to family members and close friends.　|　本文例句　That works out to about five minutes a day on physical touch, such as holding hands or cuddling before sleep.　|　例句中譯　每天大約進行五分鐘的身體接觸，例如睡前牽手或擁抱。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "carving", "sf": "carving", "pos": "n.", "zh": "雕刻", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　版刻、雕花、雕飾　|　英英定義　To cut.　|　本文例句　The Gottmans found that couples can improve their relationships by intentionally carving out about six hours a week together, and making changes to small, daily and weekly habits.　|　例句中譯　戈特曼夫婦發現，夫妻可以透過每週有意識地抽出大約六個小時在一起，並改變每天和每週的小習慣來改善他們的關係。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "intimacy", "sf": "intimacy", "pos": "n.", "zh": "親密感", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Feeling or atmosphere of closeness and openness towards someone else, not necessarily involving sexuality.　|　本文例句　Physical intimacy matters.　|　例句中譯　身體上的親密關係很重要。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "trait", "sf": "trait", "pos": "n.", "zh": "特徵", "syn": "characteristic", "tip": "其他意思　跡、跡縱、特點、特征　|　英英定義　An identifying characteristic, habit or trend.　|　本文例句　Spend about five minutes a day expressing genuine gratitude or naming a trait you admire in your partner.　|　例句中譯　每天花大約五分鐘表達真誠的感激之情或說出你欣賞伴侶的一個特質。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "distraction-free", "sf": "distraction-free", "pos": "", "zh": "不受干擾", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　Have distraction-free time together to enjoy being together.　|　例句中譯　一起享受無干擾的時光，享受在一起的時光。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-5996688/magic-6-marriage-tips-nina-totenberg-relationships"}, {"code": "20261120-3", "ch": "2026-11-20　週五", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "'Bigger than Barack Obama's election': Scholars reflect on Mississippi Senate race　／　「比巴拉克‧歐巴馬的選舉更重要」：學者們反思密西西比州參議員競選", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Tonya Mosley，全文共 4 段、386 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：史考特·科洛姆現在是這個南方州近 150 年來第一位黑人美國參議員。學者們和密西西比人埃迪·格勞德和基澤·雷蒙討論了他的勝利的歷史意義。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6047338/bigger-than-barack-obamas-election-scholars-reflect-on-mississippi-senate-race"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "史考特·科洛姆現在是這個南方州近 150 年來第一位黑人美國參議員。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Scott Colom is now this Southern state's first Black U.S. senator in nearly 150 years.", "zh": "史考特·科洛姆現在是這個南方州近 150 年來第一位黑人美國參議員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Scholars and Mississippi natives Eddie Glaude and Kiese Laymon discuss the historic significance of his victory.", "zh": "學者們和密西西比人埃迪·格勞德和基澤·雷蒙討論了他的勝利的歷史意義。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "TONYA MOSLEY, HOST: This is FRESH AIR. I'm Tonya Mosley.", "zh": "主持人托妮亞·莫斯利：這是新鮮空氣。我是托妮亞·莫斯利。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In the final weeks of Mississippi's Senate race, Democrat Scott Colom showed up outside a Donald Trump rally for his opponent and started talking to voters waiting to get in.", "zh": "在密西西比州參議院競選的最後幾週，民主黨人史考特·科洛姆出現在唐納德·川普為對手舉行的集會外，並開始與等待入場的選民交談。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He spent more than a year traveling across Mississippi, trying to convince people he could win, and last week, he did.", "zh": "他花了一年多的時間穿越密西西比州，試圖讓人們相信他能夠獲勝，上週他做到了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Three years earlier, his opponent, Cindy Hyde-Smith, had blocked Colom's nomination to become a federal judge.", "zh": "三年前，他的對手辛蒂·海德·史密斯（Cindy Hyde-Smith）阻止了科羅姆成為聯邦法官的提名。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Now he's headed to Washington to take her seat in the Senate.But there's a much longer history behind the victory.", "zh": "現在他將前往華盛頓，接替她在參議院的席位。但這場勝利背後還有更悠久的歷史。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Colom is a seventh-generation Mississippian, descended from an enslaved woman.", "zh": "科羅姆是第七代密西西比人，是一名奴隸婦女的後裔。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He's now the state's first Black U.S. senator in nearly a hundred and fifty years.", "zh": "他現在是該州近一百五十年來第一位黑人美國參議員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's a remarkable moment in a state where Black political power was once built, then violently dismantled in the years after Reconstruction.", "zh": "在這個曾經建立過黑人政治權力，又在重建後的幾年裡被暴力拆除的州裡，這是一個非凡的時刻。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "During the Great Migration, generations of Black Americans, including my family, fled Mississippi to escape Jim Crow and racial terror.", "zh": "在大遷徙期間，幾代美國黑人，包括我的家人，逃離密西西比州，逃避種族歧視和種族恐怖。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Others, like Colom's family, stayed and fought for change.My guests today are two sons of Mississippi who have spent their lives examining the place they call home.", "zh": "其他人，例如科羅姆的家人，留下來並為變革而奮鬥。今天我的客人是密西西比州的兩個兒子，他們一生都在審視這個他們稱之為家的地方。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Eddie Glaude is a professor of African American studies at Princeton University and grew up in Moss Point, a small town on the state's Gulf Coast.", "zh": "埃迪·格勞德是普林斯頓大學非裔美國人研究教授，在該州墨西哥灣沿岸的一個小鎮莫斯波因特長大。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Writer Kiese Laymon grew up in the state's capital of Jackson.", "zh": "作家基斯雷蒙 (Kiese Laymon) 在該州首府傑克遜長大。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He's the author of the memoir \"Heavy\" and a professor of creative writing at Rice University.", "zh": "他是回憶錄《Heavy》的作者，也是萊斯大學創意寫作教授。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Kiese and Eddie, welcome to FRESH AIR.EDDIE GLAUDE: Thanks for having us.KIESE LAYMON: Good to be here with y'all.", "zh": "Kiese 和 Eddie，歡迎來到新鮮空氣。 EDDIE GLAUDE： 感謝您邀請我們。 KIESE LAYMON： 很高興和你們在一起。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Thank you.MOSLEY: Well, Eddie, I want to start with you.", "zh": "謝謝。 莫斯利：嗯，艾迪，我想從你開始。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "When Colom won, you talked about being that little boy growing up in Moss Point, who never could have imagined a moment like this. And now we are here.", "zh": "當科羅姆獲勝時，你談到了在莫斯波因特長大的那個小男孩，他從來沒有想像過這樣的時刻。現在我們在這裡。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I'm actually just wondering, at what point in this race did you start to believe that it was possible?GLAUDE: When the state of Mississippi hinted that it was about to redistrict, that they were going to engage in that project of **gerrymandering** that Donald Trump called for, there were these marches all throughout the South, and they were organized under the banner, All Roads Lead to the South.", "zh": "我實際上只是想知道，在這場競選中，你從什麼時候開始相信這是可能的？ 格勞德：當密西西比州暗示即將**重新劃分選區**時，他們將參與唐納德·川普所呼籲的不公正劃分選區的專案，整個南方都有這些遊行，他們是在“條條道路通南方”的旗幟下組織的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And Derrick Johnson gave me a call.", "zh": "德里克·約翰遜給我打了電話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He's the president and CEO of the NAACP, and I think in addition to that, he is the former president of the Mississippi chapter of the NAACP.So he gave me a call and asked me to come down to Jackson to participate in the march there. And I did. And I was overwhelmed. I saw the organizing.", "zh": "他是全國有色人種協進會的主席兼首席執行官，我想除此之外，他還是全國有色人種協進會密西西比州分會的前主席。所以他給我打電話，要我去傑克森參加那裡的遊行。我做到了。我不知所措。我看到了組織。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I saw the infrastructure.", "zh": "我看到了基礎設施。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I saw young people and older folk.", "zh": "我看到了年輕人和老年人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And one of the things I did not hear was just this kind of nostalgic longing for the movement of the mid-20th century.", "zh": "而我沒有聽到的事情之一就是這種對20世紀中葉運動的懷舊渴望。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What I heard instead and saw was organizing. They were counting.", "zh": "相反，我聽到和看到的是組織。他們在數數。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They were doing the math, Tonya.", "zh": "他們正在做數學計算，托妮亞。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "How many people do we need to turn out in DeSoto?", "zh": "德索托需要多少人參加？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "How many people do we need to turn out in Holmes, in Jackson County, you know, in Hinds?And what was so **fascinating** is that I knew then - and I was on stage with Congressman Bennie Thompson and Scott Colom.", "zh": "在福爾摩斯、傑克遜縣、海因茲，我們需要有多少人參加？令人**著迷**的是，我當時就知道了——我和國會議員本尼·湯普森和斯科特·科洛姆一起在台上。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I heard Scott speak, and I believed at that moment that he had a chance.", "zh": "我聽到斯科特說話，那一刻我相信他有機會。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, he's a political athlete, that's clear.", "zh": "你知道，他是一名政治運動員，這一點很明顯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But what was clearer to me was that these folks were ready.", "zh": "但我更清楚的是，這些人已經準備好了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They were coming after us, and they were about to see the full weight and power of Black voters in Mississippi.", "zh": "他們追隨我們，他們即將看到密西西比州黑人選民的全部分量和力量。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They were going to undermine the math that was informing the **redistricting** effort.", "zh": "他們將破壞為選區重新劃分工作提供資訊的數學原理。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I looked at Scott, and I looked at him closely, and I listened and, you know, I felt that Mississippi charm, and I said...LAYMON: (Laughter).GLAUDE: ...OK. All right.", "zh": "所以我看著史考特，我仔細地看著他，我聽著，你知道，我感受到了密西西比的魅力，我說… 雷蒙：（笑聲）。 格勞德：……好吧。好的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We about to shock the world up in here.MOSLEY: Kiese, how would you describe the mobilization, what it looked like on the ground there that maybe the national audience didn't really see?", "zh": "我們即將讓這裡的世界震驚。 莫斯利：基澤，你會如何描述這次動員？全國觀眾可能沒有真正看到的地面是什麼樣子？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We just kind of - we know about the win and that there was a great mobilization.LAYMON: I think that's a great question.", "zh": "我們只是有點 - 我們知道勝利，並且有一個偉大的動員。 LAYMON：我認為這是一個很好的問題。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, one of the things I think with this particular mobilization, unlike what we saw with Espy, and this goes to...MOSLEY: And Espy - just to describe who Espy - Mike Espy...LAYMON: Mike Espy...MOSLEY: ...Actually ran against Hyde-Smith...LAYMON: Yeah.MOSLEY: ...Several years ago.LAYMON: Right, ran against Cindy Hyde-Smith a few years ago.", "zh": "你知道，我認為這次特殊動員的一件事，與我們在 Espy 上看到的不同，這涉及到...MOSLEY：還有 Espy - 只是為了描述誰 Espy - Mike Espy...LAYMON：Mike Espy...MOSLEY：...實際上與 Hyde-Smith 競爭...LAYMON：是的。 MOSLEY：...幾年前。 LAYMON：對，幾年前與 Cindy Hyde-Smith 競爭。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I worked hard on that campaign.", "zh": "我為那次競選付出了很大的努力。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I was living in Oxford at the time.", "zh": "當時我住在牛津。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I remember one morning, and Espy's - I don't want to say this person's name, but Espy's primary donor knocked on my door, sat on my porch.", "zh": "我記得有一天早上，埃斯皮的——我不想說出這個人的名字，但埃斯皮的主要捐贈者敲了我的門，坐在我的門廊上。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And the thing he was trying to, like, get me to understand was that we have to get Mike to let his hands go.", "zh": "他想讓我明白的是，我們必須讓麥克放開他的手。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That's what he kept saying.", "zh": "這就是他一直說的話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We have to let Mike let his hands go.Now, Mike Espy, I think we need to understand - this is important for what Scott Colom did - was seen as a traditional, clean, electable Democrat, meaning that the people who put Mike Espy forward did not think he would offend many Republicans.", "zh": "我們必須讓麥克放開他的手。現在，麥克·埃斯皮，我認為我們需要明白——這對斯科特·科洛姆所做的事情很重要——被視為傳統的、乾淨的、可當選的民主黨人，這意味著那些推舉邁克·埃斯皮的人認為他不會冒犯許多共和黨人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What I loved about what Scott was doing this year was Scott, I think, took off that cloak of what some people call political **respectability** in terms of the look.", "zh": "我認為史考特今年所做的事情讓我喜歡的是，史考特脫下了一些人所謂的政治尊嚴的外衣。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And that was part of the galvanization.", "zh": "這是電鍍的一部分。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so when I realized that Scott could win was when I saw, obviously, the commercial, the pick-a-protein commercial.", "zh": "因此，當我意識到斯科特可能獲勝時，我顯然看到了廣告，即選擇蛋白質的廣告。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Now, for me, I thought, Scott - my mother is a political scientist.", "zh": "現在，對我來說，史考特——我的母親是一位政治學家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She said, Kiese, I think Scott's going to have the votes.", "zh": "她說，基斯，我認為史考特會獲得選票。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But in Mississippi, having the votes doesn't mean you're going to win.And when I saw that pick another protein commercial, I thought that he had the cultural force to stop the Republican Party from doing what a lot of us assumed the Republican Party would do if it was too close.", "zh": "但在密西西比州，擁有選票並不代表你會贏。當我看到另一個蛋白質廣告時，我認為他有文化力量阻止共和黨做我們許多人認為共和黨會做的事情，如果它太接近了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So for me on the ground, I saw a different kind of candidate, followed by different kinds of potential voters.", "zh": "因此，對我來說，我看到的是不同類型的候選人，其次是不同類型的潛在選民。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And what I love about this moment is that those people, like my mother, who grew up in a political Mississippi that was very close, very contained, you had to bring your best visual self to every situation.", "zh": "我喜歡這一刻的地方是，那些人，像我的母親，在密西西比州的政治環境中長大，那裡的政治環境非常封閉，你必須在任何情況下展現出最好的視覺自我。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They walked with those young sisters and brothers in hoodies, you know, with earrings all over their faces.", "zh": "他們和那些穿著連帽衫的年輕姊妹和兄弟一起散步，你知道，臉上掛滿了耳環。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It was not just, like, an **intergenerational** march.", "zh": "這不僅僅是一場代際遊行。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It was an **intercultural** march and an intercultural election.", "zh": "這是一場跨文化遊行和跨文化選舉。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I just feel like that is some of what I don't hear much of the national media talking about.MOSLEY: Also it's just so interesting, you know, Colom didn't have much money from the National Democratic Party.", "zh": "我只是覺得這是我在國家媒體中很少聽到的一些內容。 莫斯利：這也很有趣，你知道，科洛姆從國家民主黨沒有多少錢。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And this particular political ad that you're talking about is just one of the creative ways that they were able to reach voters.", "zh": "你所談論的這個特殊的政治廣告只是他們能夠接觸選民的創意方式之一。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I actually want to play the one that you're talking about, where essentially the background of this ad is that his opponent, Cindy Hyde-Smith, during an interview, suggested that people struggling with the rising price of beef could simply choose another protein.", "zh": "我實際上想播放你正在談論的那個，這則廣告的背景基本上是他的對手辛迪·海德·史密斯在接受采訪時建議，因牛肉價格上漲而苦苦掙扎的人們可以選擇另一種蛋白質。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And here is how Colom's campaign responded.", "zh": "以下是科羅姆競選團隊的回應。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Let's listen.(SOUNDBITE OF AD)UNIDENTIFIED PERSON: The price of beef continuing to go up.CINDY HYDE-SMITH: You know, you have so many proteins to choose from.UNIDENTIFIED ACTOR #1: (As MS Voter) Pick another protein? [Expletive] I'd rather pick another senator instead.UNIDENTIFIED ACTOR #2: (As MS Voter) Pick another protein?", "zh": "讓我們聽聽。 （廣告聲音）身份不明的人：牛肉的價格持續上漲。辛蒂海德史密斯：你知道，你有很多蛋白質可供選擇。未知的演員#1：（身為選民女士）選擇另一種蛋白質？ [咒罵]我寧願選擇另一位參議員。未知的演員#2：（作為 MS 選民）選擇另一種蛋白質？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She done lost her damn mind.", "zh": "她確實失去了理智。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I'd rather pick another senator.UNIDENTIFIED ACTOR #3: (As MS Voter) Pick another protein?", "zh": "我寧願選擇另一位參議員。未知的演員#3：（作為 MS 選民）選擇另一種蛋白質？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What the F?UNIDENTIFIED ACTOR #4: (As MS Voter) Pick another senator instead.(SOUNDBITE OF MUSIC)MOSLEY: That's a political ad...LAYMON: It's great.MOSLEY: ...For now Senator-elect Scott Colom.", "zh": "什麼鬼？未知的演員 #4：（作為 MS 選民）選擇另一位參議員。 （音樂原聲）莫斯利：那是政治廣告...萊蒙：太棒了。莫斯利：...現在當選參議員史考特‧科洛姆。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, Kiese, you said that when you saw that commercial, you knew that he'd win.", "zh": "而且，基澤，你說過當你看到那個廣告時，你就知道他會贏。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I want to know from you, Eddie.", "zh": "我想知道你的情況，艾迪。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, beyond the humor, he's actually talking about something really real - the cost of living in one of the poorest states in the country.", "zh": "我的意思是，除了幽默之外，他實際上談論的是一些真實的事情——美國最貧窮的州之一的生活成本。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "How much of this victory do you think was about the way he spoke to people, and how much was it about actually what he's saying, you know?GLAUDE: It's a combination of both, I think.", "zh": "你認為這場勝利在多大程度上取決於他與人們交談的方式，以及他實際上所說的話有多少，你知道嗎？ 格勞德：我認為這是兩者的結合。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, what was so brilliant about the ad is that you can see and hear - right? - the cultural residences.", "zh": "你知道，這則廣告的精彩之處在於你可以看到和聽到 - 對嗎？ - 文化住宅。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's **quintessentially** Mississippi.", "zh": "這是典型的密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's Mississippi concentrated.LAYMON: (Laughter).GLAUDE: And what you hear is that it cuts across racial boundaries.", "zh": "這是密西西比州的集中地。 雷蒙：（笑聲）。 格勞德：你聽到的是，它跨越了種族界線。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So the rhythm of the speech that you heard, the white man who, you know, who drew out...MOSLEY: Right.GLAUDE: ...You know, the expletive.", "zh": "所以你聽到的演講的節奏，那個白人，你知道，他拉出了…莫斯利：對。 格勞德：……你知道，罵人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, the white woman who asked in a very **shrill** kind of way, what the?", "zh": "你知道，那個白人婦女以一種非常**尖銳**的方式問，那是什麼？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, that - and the rhythm of it is everybody in Mississippi knows that's how you cuss, right?", "zh": "你知道，密西西比州的每個人都知道你就是這樣罵人的，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So...LAYMON: (Laughter).MOSLEY: You, like, really draw it out, huh? Yeah.GLAUDE: Right.", "zh": "所以... LAYMON: (笑聲). MOSLEY: 你真的把它畫出來了，對吧？是的。格勞德：是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, so it sounded familiar.", "zh": "我的意思是，所以聽起來很熟悉。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But the thing is that on top of that performance was the substantive issue.", "zh": "但問題是，除了表現之外，還有實質問題。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Cindy Hyde-Smith had been absent.", "zh": "辛蒂·海德·史密斯缺席。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She hasn't been representing the state.", "zh": "她沒有代表國家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so here she is, in this very kind of crude and callous way, saying, let them eat cake, too, right?", "zh": "所以她在這裡，以一種非常粗魯和冷酷的方式，說，讓他們也吃蛋糕，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Having her Marie Antoinette moment on television in some ways.And so they were able to bring these two things together, the kind of cultural resonances that Kiese was talking about and then connect it with the substantive critique of Hyde-Smith that she wasn't representing the state.", "zh": "以某種方式讓她的瑪麗安托瓦內特時刻出現在電視上。所以他們能夠將這兩件事結合在一起，即基斯正在談論的那種文化共鳴，然後將其與海德史密斯的實質批評聯繫起來，即她不代表國家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She wasn't addressing the fundamental material conditions of Mississippians, no matter what side of town they live on, no matter what color their skin.", "zh": "她沒有談到密西西比人的基本物質條件，無論他們住在城鎮的哪一邊，無論他們的膚色是什麼。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so it was a kind of wonderful distillation of both of those elements.LAYMON: And can I just say one more thing about that, just hopping off what Eddie said?", "zh": "所以這是對這兩種元素的一種美妙的昇華。 雷蒙：我可以再說一件事嗎，只是跳出艾迪所說的話？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The wonder to me also, just as, like, a person who creates, you know, words and word culture, is that they made Scott the subject and the viewer.", "zh": "對我來說，同樣令人驚訝的是，就像一個創造文字和文字文化的人一樣，他們讓史考特成為主體和觀眾。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So the wonder of that is like, yes, the beginning, we see this young, white man cussing the way white boys in Mississippi cuss.", "zh": "因此，令人驚訝的是，是的，一開始，我們看到這個年輕的白人男子像密西西比州的白人男孩那樣咒罵。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We see the older sister in the beginning eating catfish, talking the way all my aunties cuss.", "zh": "我們一開始就看到姊姊在吃鯰魚，一路上都在罵我的阿姨們。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We see the older white woman at the end, at the grocery store, trying to get something that's not affordable.", "zh": "我們看到最後一位年長的白人婦女在雜貨店裡試圖買一些買不起的東西。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And then we see Scott doing what?", "zh": "然後我們看到斯科特在做什麼？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Watching as we watched, laughing as we laughed and saying pick another senator instead.So that move - right? - he starts to embody the viewer.", "zh": "我們邊看邊笑，邊笑邊說選另一位參議員。所以這一舉動 - 對吧？ - 他開始體現觀眾。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I don't care what political persuasion you are.", "zh": "我不在乎你的政治傾向是什麼。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Every viewer had Scott Colom's response to that, which is to laugh.", "zh": "每個觀眾對此都有斯科特·科羅姆的反應，那就是笑。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So it's smart and it's genius.", "zh": "所以它是聰明的，也是天才的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But it also does something that I think most word sort of assemblages can't, which is take the subject, and then the subject becomes the viewer.", "zh": "但它也做了一些我認為大多數單字組合都做不到的事情，那就是接受主題，然後主題就變成了觀眾。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So the point of view shifts.", "zh": "於是觀點就轉變了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And we start to look at this ad through Scott, or Scott starts to look at this ad through us.", "zh": "我們開始透過史考特看這個廣告，或者史考特開始透過我們看這個廣告。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I just think it was like the most impactful political ad of my life by far.MOSLEY: Let's take a short break.", "zh": "我只是覺得這就像我一生中迄今為止最有影響力的政治廣告。 莫斯利：讓我們休息一下。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "If you're just joining us, my guests are Princeton scholar Eddie Glaude and Rice University Professor Kiese Laymon.", "zh": "如果您剛加入我們，我的嘉賓是普林斯頓大學學者埃迪·格勞德和萊斯大學教授基斯·雷蒙。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We'll be right back after a short break.", "zh": "短暫休息後我們就會回來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This is FRESH AIR.(SOUNDBITE OF JULIAN LAGE GROUP'S \"IOWA TAKEN\")MOSLEY: This is FRESH AIR.", "zh": "這是新鮮空氣。 （朱利安·拉格集團的「愛荷華州佔領」原聲片段） 莫斯利：這是新鮮空氣。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And today I am talking with Eddie Glaude and Kiese Laymon about Scott Colom's historic Senate election win in Mississippi.I want to break down something a little bit.", "zh": "今天，我正在與埃迪·格勞德和基斯·雷蒙談論斯科特·科羅姆在密西西比州歷史性的參議院選舉勝利。我想稍微解釋一下。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I just want us to get a deeper understanding of Cindy Hyde-Smith just for a brief moment, especially through the context of the last few years.", "zh": "我只是想讓我們對辛蒂·海德·史密斯有一個短暫的更深入的了解，特別是透過過去幾年的背景。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You mentioned, Kiese, that she ran against Mike Espy, who was a Black Democrat who lost in 2018 and then 2020 against her.", "zh": "Kiese，你提到她的對手是黑人民主黨人邁克·埃斯皮 (Mike Espy)，後者在 2018 年和 2020 年都輸給了她。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But there's this particular moment that you wrote about for Mississippi Today back in 2020.", "zh": "但您在 2020 年為《今日密西西比》撰寫的文章中提到了這個特殊時刻。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And it was about a campaign stop she made where she praised a supporter by saying that if that supporter invited her to a public hanging, she'd be in the front row.LAYMON: Right.MOSLEY: When folks asked her about this, she called it a figure of speech.", "zh": "這是關於她在一次競選活動中讚揚一位支持者的故事，她說如果該支持者邀請她參加公開絞刑，她就會坐在前排。 雷蒙：對。 莫斯利：當人們問她這個問題時，她稱這是一種修辭手法。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And she later went on to win.", "zh": "後來她繼續獲勝。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And you wrote this essay about that very sentence.", "zh": "你就這句話寫了這篇文章。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What did you hear when she said that?LAYMON: It's so easy to sound hyperbolic, I think, when you talk about Mississippi, but specifically Cindy Hyde-Smith.", "zh": "當她這麼說時，你聽到了什麼？ 雷蒙：我認為，當你談論密西西比州，特別是辛蒂海德史密斯時，聽起來很誇張。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In some way, that sentence sort of, like, **obliterates** analysis.", "zh": "某種程度上，這句話有點抹殺了分析。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But what she literally said was, if there were a public hanging, I'd be on the front row.", "zh": "但她的字面意思是，如果有公開絞刑，我會坐在前排。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And my critique of that was there are so many amazing sentences born of Mississippi one could have, you know, said or used as a refrain.And what I heard was, you know, premature death, killing.", "zh": "我對此的批評是，密西西比州誕生了許多令人驚嘆的句子，人們可以說出來或用作副歌。我聽到的是，你知道，過早死亡，殺戮。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And what I also heard was her giving her voters what they wanted.", "zh": "我還聽到的是她給了選民他們想要的東西。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I was living in Mississippi at the time.", "zh": "當時我住在密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so what I really heard was fear and anger.", "zh": "所以我真正聽到的是恐懼和憤怒。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And at that point - you know, I think we have to be honest - like, I knew she was going to win again.And I think sometimes when you live in Mississippi, you get used to this.", "zh": "在那一點上 - 你知道，我認為我們必須誠實 - 就像，我知道她會再次獲勝。我認為有時當你住在密西西比州時，你會習慣這一點。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But, like, I remember talking to my mother about, like, what does it mean that the Blackest state in the union is now going to have a senator who publicly says, if there were a hanging, I'd be on the front row?", "zh": "但是，就像，我記得和我母親談論過，例如，聯邦最黑的州現在將有一位參議員公開表示，如果有絞刑，我會坐在前排，這意味著什麼？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I felt, like, humiliated, which I feel like lynchings were supposed to do, public hangings were supposed to do.", "zh": "所以我覺得，就像，羞辱，我覺得私刑應該要這樣做，公開絞刑應該要這樣做。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I'm not trying to equate my experience of listening to that. But I did.", "zh": "我並不是想把我聽這首歌的經驗等同起來。但我做到了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I felt humiliated and I felt angry.MOSLEY: I think outsiders of Mississippi might be surprised that someone who says something like that would then get elected.", "zh": "我感到羞辱和憤怒。 莫斯利：我認為密西西比州的局外人可能會感到驚訝，因為說出這樣的話的人會當選。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's just such a charged statement.LAYMON: Yeah.", "zh": "這只是一個充滿指責的聲明。 LAYMON： 是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Especially in the Blackest state in the union, right?", "zh": "尤其是在聯邦最黑的州，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, this is - and those Black voters, we don't vote Republican.", "zh": "我的意思是，這是 - 而那些黑人選民，我們不投票給共和黨。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I just think sometimes when you live in Mississippi - and I love Mississippi.", "zh": "所以我有時會想，當你住在密西西比州時 - 我愛密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I lived there for so many - I write to and from it.", "zh": "我在那裡住了很多年——我在那裡寫信。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I think - I talked to Eddie before that piece, you know?", "zh": "我想——在那篇文章之前我和艾迪談過，你知道嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And one of the things Eddie said is, like, if we solve Mississippi, we solve the Sphinx.", "zh": "艾迪說的其中一件事是，如果我們解決了密西西比河，我們就解決了獅身人面像。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so, after hearing Cindy Hyde-Smith say that out loud, honestly, I just had little faith that the Sphinx could be solved, because that wasn't something that we heard her say offline. You know what I mean?", "zh": "因此，在聽到辛蒂·海德·史密斯大聲說出這句話後，老實說，我對獅身人面像問題的解決幾乎沒有信心，因為這不是我們在線下聽到她說的話。你知道我的意思？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That in some way was a campaign kind of call.MOSLEY: The question specifically that, Kiese, you asked Eddie for that piece - you asked him, essentially, what would it take for Mississippi to live up to its promise?", "zh": "這在某種程度上是一種競選呼籲。 莫斯利：具體的問題是，基澤，你向艾迪要了那篇文章——本質上你問他，密西西比州需要做什麼才能兌現其承諾？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, Eddie, you told him Mississippi is where the country's hardest problems sit, and that if they can solve the problems there, they can solve them anywhere.", "zh": "艾迪，你告訴他密西西比州是這個國家最困難的問題所在，如果他們能夠解決那裡的問題，他們就可以在任何地方解決問題。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I think that's what you were saying when you said it's like solving the riddle of the Sphinx.GLAUDE: Right.MOSLEY: What part of that riddle do you think Mississippi has figured out with this election?GLAUDE: Well, you know, I think it's really important for us to pump the brakes, you know, as I revel in what I could not have imagined.", "zh": "我想這就是你所說的，當你說這就像在解決獅身人面像之謎。格勞德：對。莫斯利：你認為密西西比州在這次選舉中解開了這個謎語的哪一部分？格勞德：嗯，你知道，我認為踩剎車對我們來說非常重要，你知道，因為我陶醉於我無法想像的事情。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, I believed that Scott could win.", "zh": "你知道，我相信史考特能夠獲勝。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I just didn't know how I would feel if he did, right?MOSLEY: Oh, that's...GLAUDE: So I'm still grappling with that.MOSLEY: Yes.", "zh": "我只是不知道如果他這樣做我會有什麼感覺，對吧？ 莫斯利：哦，那是……格勞德：所以我還在努力解決這個問題。莫斯利：是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Say more on that feeling.", "zh": "多說點這種感覺吧。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You just weren't...GLAUDE: Oh, my God.", "zh": "你只是沒有... GLAUDE：哦，我的上帝。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, this is - for me, this is bigger than Barack Obama's election.", "zh": "你知道，對我來說，這比巴拉克·歐巴馬的選舉更重要。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mississippi, James Silver - this is the closed society, right?", "zh": "密西西比州，詹姆斯·西爾弗 - 這是一個封閉的社會，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, our soil is soaked in blood.", "zh": "我的意思是，我們的土壤被鮮血浸透了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, all of the contradictions of the country are distilled here.", "zh": "我的意思是，這個國家的所有矛盾都集中在這裡。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, you know, Mississippi, I like to say, you know, it has amazing beauty.", "zh": "我的意思是，你知道，密西西比州，我喜歡說，你知道，它有令人驚嘆的美麗。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, I grew up on the water with magnolia trees and moss.", "zh": "我的意思是，我是在有玉蘭花樹和苔蘚的水面上長大的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, I mean, just gorgeous.", "zh": "而且，我的意思是，太漂亮了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And then you got black snakes that could chase you down the street.LAYMON: (Laughter) That's right.", "zh": "然後黑蛇會在街上追你。 雷蒙：（笑聲）沒錯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That's...GLAUDE: You know, I mean, it's a bundle of contradictions, people who are sweet and who are murderous and monstrous, all at the same time.", "zh": "那是……格勞德：你知道，我的意思是，這是一群矛盾體，人們既可愛，又兇殘、可怕，同時又如此。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so, you know, I think there's a reason why the blues comes out of here.", "zh": "所以，你知道，我認為布魯斯從這裡出現是有原因的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "There's a reason why Faulkner comes out of there.", "zh": "福克納從那裡出來是有原因的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "There's a reason why Kiese comes out of there.", "zh": "基澤從那裡出來是有原因的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I think part of what I'm arguing - and, you know, Imani Perry makes this claim about the South generally - is that the South is the beating heart of the country.", "zh": "因此，我認為我所爭論的部分內容——而且，你知道，伊馬尼·佩里對南方做出了這樣的概括——是南方是這個國家跳動的心臟。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And when you really want to get at the heart of the South, Mississippi is right there.And so, you know, when you think about the poverty in the Delta, when you think about, you know, organized elites who have seized government, when you think about, you know, people who are just trying to figure out how to make ends meet, when you think about race and all of its complexity, Mississippi offers a kind of telescoped view of it all.", "zh": "當你真正想到達南方的中心時，密西西比州就在那裡。所以，當你想到三角洲的貧困時，當你想到奪取政府的有組織的精英時，當你想到那些只是想弄清楚如何維持收支平衡的人時，當你想到種族及其所有複雜性時，密西西比州提供了一種對這一切的望遠鏡視角。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So when I said to Kiese back then that if we can figure it out - right? - then we opened the black box for the country.LAYMON: Right.", "zh": "所以當我當時對 Kiese 說如果我們能解決這個問題時 - 對吧？ - 然後我們打開了國家的黑盒子。 LAYMON： 是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Yeah.MOSLEY: I want to play, actually, a clip from an interview that Scott Colom gave to MS NOW on the weekly podcast \"Clock It\" shortly after the race was called.", "zh": "是的。莫斯利：實際上，我想播放斯科特·科洛姆在比賽宣布後不久在每周播客“Clock It”上接受 MS NOW 採訪的片段。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He expounds upon what you are talking about there.", "zh": "他解釋了你在那裡談論的內容。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He talks about the advances and setbacks of political power in Mississippi, specifically Black political power.", "zh": "他談論了密西西比州政治權力的進步和挫折，特別是黑人政治權力。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And then he goes on to say the rest of the country's responsibility for what happens there.", "zh": "然後他接著說該國其他國家對那裡發生的事情負有責任。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Let's listen.(SOUNDBITE OF PODCAST, \"CLOCK IT WITH SYMONE & EUGENE\")SCOTT COLOM: People need to know that in America, we've made progress before.", "zh": "讓我們聽聽。 （播客原聲片段，“與西蒙和尤金一起計時”）斯科特·科洛姆：人們需要知道，在美國，我們以前已經取得了進步。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, Hiram Revels gave an amazing prayer that resulted in him getting momentum to be elected - not elected, but selected to be a senator.", "zh": "我的意思是，海勒姆·雷維爾斯做了一次令人驚嘆的祈禱，這讓他獲得了當選的動力——不是當選，而是被選為參議員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And there was a lot of progress in Mississippi on public education, on voting rights.", "zh": "密西西比州在公共教育和投票權方面取得了很大進展。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And we lost that progress for a century.", "zh": "我們在一個世紀內失去了這種進步。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, you know, oftentimes people look at Mississippi and ignore the fact that the country allowed it to happen, too.", "zh": "而且，你知道，人們常常看著密西西比州，卻忽略了這個國家也允許這種情況發生的事實。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, there was - you know, Mississippi didn't just take away voting rights from African Americans.", "zh": "我的意思是，你知道，密西西比州不僅僅剝奪了非裔美國人的投票權。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The country allowed that to happen.", "zh": "國家允許這樣的事情發生。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mississippi didn't just do Jim Crow.", "zh": "密西西比州不只是實行吉姆·克勞法。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The country allowed Jim Crow to happen.And so, for me, I wanted that story to be a reminder of the progress, but I also wanted people to understand the promise of our country, because here you are at a time where people thought that this was not possible.", "zh": "這個國家允許吉姆·克勞的發生。所以，對我來說，我希望這個故事能提醒人們進步，但我也希望人們了解我們國家的承諾，因為現在人們認為這是不可能的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I believed in Mississippi.", "zh": "我相信密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I believed in the values of our state.", "zh": "我相信我們國家的價值觀。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I believed in the progress.", "zh": "我相信進步。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so that faith, those prayers and that work showed the country that Mississippi matters.MOSLEY: That was Scott Colom speaking shortly after his win on the weekly podcast, produced by MS NOW, \"Clock It.\" And we heard him mention Hiram Revels, who became the first Black man to serve in the United States Senate back in 1870, during the Reconstruction era.", "zh": "因此，信仰、祈禱和工作向全國展示了密西西比州的重要性。 莫斯利：這是斯科特·科羅姆在獲勝後不久在由 MS NOW 製作的每周播客“Clock It”中發表的講話。我們聽到他提到了海勒姆·雷維爾斯 (Hiram Revels)，他於 1870 年重建時期成為第一位在美國參議院任職的黑人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But Eddie, we often talk about Mississippi's racial history.", "zh": "但是艾迪，我們經常談論密西西比州的種族歷史。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You're able to speak about it so beautifully and poignantly.", "zh": "你能夠如此美麗而深刻地談論它。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But we often talk about it as though it happened and happens in isolation.", "zh": "但我們經常談論它，就好像它是單獨發生的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What responsibility does the rest of the country bear for what happens there, I mean, and making people understand this is not just an isolated state win, but it's something that potentially is much bigger?GLAUDE: Well, you know, I mean, this is a kind of Southern **exceptionalism** that defines so much of the nation.", "zh": "我的意思是，這個國家的其他地區對那裡發生的事情負有什麼責任，讓人們明白這不僅僅是一個孤立的國家勝利，而且可能是更大的事情？ 格勞德：嗯，你知道，我的意思是，這是一種南方**例外論**，它定義了這個國家的大部分人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And what I mean by that is that, you know, the South is made to bear the nation's sins, right?", "zh": "我的意思是，你知道，南方注定要承擔這個國家的罪過，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mississippi becomes a kind of exaggerated example of the backwardness of that region that holds the country, holds the country back that undermines its democracy.", "zh": "密西西比州成為該地區落後的誇張例子，該地區控制著這個國家，阻礙了這個國家的發展，破壞了其民主。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So if only the South would get itself together, you know, you heard that kind of argument at the heart of Gunnar Myrdal's the \"American Dilemma,\" right?", "zh": "因此，如果南方能夠團結起來就好了，你知道，你在古納·米爾達爾的《美國困境》中聽過這種爭論，對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, you know, Malcolm X was clear, as long as you south of the Canadian border, you're in the South.LAYMON: (Laughter).GLAUDE: Right?", "zh": "而且，你知道，馬爾科姆 X 很清楚，只要你在加拿大邊境以南，你就在南方。 雷蒙：（笑聲）。 格勞德：對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so the point is that - you know, and Scott is very clear about this, that, you know, when we think about slavery and the relationship between Southern plantation owners and cotton and Northern industry, when you think about the Civil War and the collapse of Reconstruction and the ways in which the North - those - interest in the North who thought initially that they could leverage Black voter - or Black enfranchisement for their own ends and aims, and then they were quick to abandon it as, you know, white men in the South and North reconciled and Black folk had to bear the brunt of that reconciliation in blood.", "zh": "所以重點是 - 你知道，斯科特對此非常清楚，你知道，當我們思考奴隸制以及南方種植園主和棉花與北方工業之間的關係時，當你思考內戰和重建的崩潰以及北方的方式 - 那些對北方感興趣的人，他們最初認為他們可以利用黑人選民 - 或黑人選舉權來實現自己的目的和目標，然後他們很快就必須放棄了它，因為，你知道這種和解。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So when we talk about the history of the country, you know, the idea is to displace our sins onto the South - right? - so that we can **absolve** the nation of its sins in so many ways.And what Scott is suggesting in a very, I think, polite way - right? - is that, no, no, no, no, Mississippi is a reflection of the nation itself and that all the things that we attribute to the state is really a reflection in so many ways of choices, historic choices that have guided the country since its founding.LAYMON: Absolutely.MOSLEY: Kiese, I was giving you a moment 'cause I could hear your mm hmm, mm hmm.", "zh": "因此，當我們談論這個國家的歷史時，你知道，我們的想法是將我們的罪惡轉移到南方 - 對嗎？ - 這樣我們就可以透過多種方式赦免這個國家的罪過。我認為斯科特以一種非常禮貌的方式提出了建議 - 對嗎？ - 是不是，不，不，不，不，密西西比州是國家本身的反映，我們賦予國家的所有東西實際上反映了許多選擇的方式，歷史性的選擇，自建國以來一直指導著這個國家。 雷蒙： 絕對。 莫斯利： 基斯，我給你一點時間，因為我聽得到你的嗯嗯，嗯嗯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I didn't know you want to reply to that.LAYMON: (Inaudible) preaching. I'm sorry.", "zh": "我不知道你想回覆這個問題。 LAYMON：（聽不清楚）說教。對不起。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That's like call and response.", "zh": "這就像呼叫和響應。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I'm like - this is something I think Eddie just lays out profoundly in his book, \"America, U.S.A.\" You know, I find myself at once being completely elated, overwhelmed with joy because I am a Mississippian.", "zh": "我想——我認為艾迪在他的書《美國，美國》中深刻地闡述了這一點。你知道，我發現自己立刻感到非常高興，因為我是密西西比人而欣喜若狂。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And then I find myself soberly looking forward to what the Colom family and what Colom the politician will have to do going forward.MOSLEY: Our guests today are professors Eddie Glaude and Kiese Laymon.", "zh": "然後我發現自己清醒地期待著科洛姆家族和政客科洛姆未來要做的事情。 莫斯利：今天我們的來賓是艾迪‧格勞德教授和基澤‧雷蒙教授。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We'll be right back after a short break.", "zh": "短暫休息後我們就會回來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I'm Tonya Mosley, and this is FRESH AIR.(SOUNDBITE OF ART BLAKEY & THE JAZZ MESSENGERS' \"OH-BY THE WAY\")MOSLEY: This is FRESH AIR. I'm Tonya Mosley.", "zh": "我是托妮亞‧莫斯利 (Tonya Mosley)，這裡有新鮮空氣。 （ART BLAKEY 和爵士信使的“OH-BY THE WAY”的原聲片段）莫斯利：這裡是新鮮空氣。我是托妮亞·莫斯利。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And my guests today are Eddie Glaude and Kiese Laymon, two Mississippi natives whose work explores the history of race, democracy and the complicated meaning of home.", "zh": "今天我的客人是埃迪·格勞德和基澤·雷蒙，兩位密西西比人，他們的作品探討了種族、民主和家庭的複雜意義的歷史。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Eddie Glaude is a professor of African American studies at Princeton University and the author of several books, including \"Begin Again\" and \"America, U.S.A.: How Race Shadows The Nation's Anniversaries.\" Kiese Laymon is a professor of English and creative writing at Rice University and the author of the acclaimed memoir \"Heavy.\" His forthcoming memoir, \"Good, God: A Creation Story,\" will be published this spring.", "zh": "艾迪·格勞德是普林斯頓大學非裔美國人研究教授，也是多本書的作者，包括《重新開始》和《美國，美國：種族如何影響國家週年紀念日》。基斯‧雷蒙 (Kisee Laymon) 是萊斯大學英語和創意寫作教授，也是廣受好評的回憶錄《Heavy》的作者。他即將出版的回憶錄《上帝啊：創世故事》將於今年春天出版。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We're talking about the historic election of Scott Colom, Mississippi's first Black U.S. senator since Reconstruction, and what his victory tells us about the changing political landscape of the South and the country.OK.", "zh": "我們談論的是密西西比州重建以來第一位黑人美國參議員斯科特·科洛姆的歷史性選舉，以及他的勝利告訴我們有關南方和國家不斷變化的政治格局的資訊。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We talked for a little bit about Hiram Revels, who became the first Black man to serve in the United States Senate in 1870.", "zh": "我們談論了一些關於海勒姆·雷維爾斯 (Hiram Revels) 的事，他於 1870 年成為第一位在美國參議院任職的黑人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I want to delve into his historic win a little bit more.", "zh": "我想進一步深入研究他的歷史性勝利。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But I want to get into this with an \"SNL\" sketch.", "zh": "但我想透過「SNL」草圖來探討這個問題。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I don't know if you guys saw it this weekend.(LAUGHTER)MOSLEY: So \"Saturday Night Live\" did this sketch with Kam Patterson, who plays Revels, who appears alongside Michael Che on Weekend Update.", "zh": "我不知道你們這個週末有沒有看過。 （笑聲）莫斯利：所以《週六夜現場》和扮演狂歡的卡姆·帕特森一起做了這個草圖，他和邁克爾·切一起出現在周末更新中。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Let's listen.(SOUNDBITE OF TV SHOW, \"SATURDAY NIGHT LIVE\")MICHAEL CHE: The midterms saw historic wins for Black candidates across the country, including an unexpected victory for Mississippi's new senator, Scott Colom.", "zh": "讓我們聽聽。 （電視節目《週六夜現場》原聲帶）邁克爾·切：中期選舉見證了全國黑人候選人的歷史性勝利，其中包括密西西比州新參議員斯科特·科洛姆的意外勝利。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Here to comment is Mississippi's first-ever Black Senator, Hiram Revels.(CHEERING)KAM PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) Hello, Michael.CHE: Wow.", "zh": "這裡發表評論的是密西西比州有史以來第一位黑人參議員 Hiram Revels。 （歡呼）KAM PATTERSON：（正如 Hiram Revels）你好，邁克爾。 CHE：哇。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So you were the first Black senator in the United States.PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) That's right, Michael. 1870, five years after the Civil War.", "zh": "所以你是美國第一位黑人參議員。 帕特森：（正如海勒姆·雷維爾斯）是的，邁克爾。 1870 年，內戰五年後。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But I'm sure you've read all about me.", "zh": "但我確信你已經讀過關於我的一切。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You probably got a national holiday named for me, right?CHE: Oh, no.(LAUGHTER)PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) OK.", "zh": "你可能有一個以我的名字命名的國家假日，對吧？ 切：哦，沒有。 （笑）帕特森：（如海勒姆·雷維爾斯）好的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Just schools then?CHE: No.(LAUGHTER)PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) A little statue in the mall?CHE: No.PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) Oh, maybe a couple of Jay-Z songs.(LAUGHTER)CHE: How do you know Jay-Z?PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) Everyone knows Jay-Z. You know who I am, right, Michael?CHE: Look, I don't even think the guy playing you knows who you are.(LAUGHTER)PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) Hey, leave Kam Patterson out of it.CHE: OK.(LAUGHTER)PATTERSON: (As Hiram Revels) He took a real long glance at my Wikipedia page before coming out here.(LAUGHTER)MOSLEY: That was from this weekend's \"Saturday Night Live.\" OK.", "zh": "那就只有學校嗎？ 切：沒有。 （笑）帕特森：（像海勒姆·狂歡）商場裡的一個小雕像？切：沒有。帕特森：（像海勒姆·狂歡）哦，也許有幾首 Jay-Z 的歌。 （笑）切：你怎麼認識 Jay-Z？帕特森：（像海勒姆·狂歡）每個人都知道 Jay-Z。你知道我是誰，對吧，麥可？ 切：看，我甚至不認為扮演你的人知道你是誰。 （笑）帕特森：（飾海勒姆·雷維爾斯）嘿，把卡姆·帕特森排除在外。切：好的。 （笑）帕特森：（作為海勒姆·雷維爾斯）他在出來之前仔細看了我的維基百科頁面。 （笑）莫斯利：那是這個週末的「週六夜現場。」好的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Growing up in Mississippi, did you guys grow up learning about Revels?LAYMON: Well, sadly and wonderfully, I learned a lot about Revels growing up.", "zh": "你們在密西西比州長大，是在成長過程中了解狂歡的嗎？ 雷蒙：嗯，悲傷又美妙的是，我在成長過程中學到了很多關於狂歡的知識。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "My mother wrote - her first book was called \"Legislators, Law And Public Policy.\" She graduated from Jackson State, went to University of Wisconsin and did her graduate work on legislators, law and public policy in Mississippi.", "zh": "我母親寫道──她的第一本書叫做《立法者、法律與公共政策》。她畢業於傑克遜州立大學，後來進入威斯康辛大學，並在密西西比州完成了立法者、法律和公共政策的研究生工作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So, yeah, I had to write...(LAUGHTER)LAYMON: I had to write a little, short essay about Revels.", "zh": "所以，是的，我必須寫…（笑聲）LAYMON：我必須寫一篇關於狂歡的小短文。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And what's interesting about that sketch is that my mother at the time was still one of those encyclopedia mothers, meaning her mother gave her the greatest gift she could ever give her in the '50s, late '50s, which was a set of encyclopedias.MOSLEY: Right, yes.LAYMON: So I remember, in the 1980s, I came home.", "zh": "那個草圖的有趣之處在於，我的母親當時仍然是那些百科全書母親之一，這意味著她的母親給了她她在 50 年代、50 年代末能給她的最好的禮物，那就是一套百科全書。 莫斯利： 是的，是的。 雷蒙： 所以我記得，在 20 世紀 80 年代，我回家了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And all my boys were getting Nintendos.", "zh": "我所有的孩子都買了任天堂。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And my mom was like, I got something waiting for you, baby.GLAUDE: (Laughter).LAYMON: And I'm like, oh, bro, I'm finna get a Nintendo. Duck Hunt, all that.", "zh": "我媽媽說，我有東西在等你，寶貝。 GLAUDE：（笑聲）。 LAYMON：我想，哦，兄弟，我終於得到一台任天堂了。獵鴨，等等。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Man, I came in there and there was these electric blue encyclopedias.GLAUDE: Yeah.LAYMON: And, you know, my mom didn't want me to just look at the color.", "zh": "夥計，我進來了，那裡有這些電藍色百科全書。 GLAUDE： 是的。 LAYMON： 而且，你知道，我媽媽不想讓我只看顏色。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I had to get up in there.", "zh": "我必須站起來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And one of the things was that, you know, Hiram Revels wasn't in those encyclopedias.", "zh": "其中之一是，你知道，海勒姆·雷維爾斯並不在那些百科全書中。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So my mother had - you know, made me go back to work.", "zh": "所以我媽媽——你知道，讓我回去工作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She worked at Jackson State University.And, you know, the critique from my mother and her friends was that Hiram Revels, because he wasn't elected - right, he was just, like, you know, he was placed - didn't do enough.", "zh": "她在傑克遜州立大學工作。而且，你知道，我母親和她朋友的批評是海勒姆·雷維爾斯，因為他沒有當選 - 是的，他只是，就像，你知道，他被安置 - 做得不夠。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Now, this is coming from Mississippi sort of - not Mississippi radicals, but people who were really critical of Mississippi history.", "zh": "現在，這來自密西西比州——不是密西西比州的激進分子，而是真正批評密西西比州歷史的人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I definitely had to write a little four- or five-sentence little essay about Hiram Revels when I was a kid that I forgot until Scott Colom's election.", "zh": "因此，當我還是個孩子的時候，我肯定必須寫一篇關於海勒姆·雷維爾斯的四五句小文章，直到斯科特·科洛姆當選為止，我才忘記了這一點。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That's what's so interesting, because Mom hit me, Ki, remember when I made you?GLAUDE: (Laughter).LAYMON: And then she was like, I still have it.GLAUDE: See, I didn't have that experience at all.", "zh": "這就是有趣的地方，因為媽媽打了我，Ki，還記得我做你的時候嗎？ GLAUDE：（笑聲）。 LAYMON：然後她就說，我還留著它。 GLAUDE：看，我根本沒有那種經驗。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "My mom, you know, cleaned toilets at Ingalls shipyard.", "zh": "你知道，我媽媽在英格爾斯造船廠打掃廁所。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And my dad was a postman.", "zh": "我的父親是郵差。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, you know, I learned about the Civil War from my history teacher, Ms.", "zh": "而且，你知道，我從我的歷史老師，女士那裡了解到了內戰。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mitchell, who had a vocal injury.", "zh": "米切爾，聲帶受傷。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So she was a little, tiny things.", "zh": "所以她是個小東西。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She had to use a mic to teach.", "zh": "她必須使用麥克風來教學。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And she taught the Civil War so well that I found myself worshipping Stonewall Jackson.LAYMON: Wow.GLAUDE: You hear that?LAYMON: Wow.GLAUDE: See, Kiese grew up in the big city.", "zh": "她對內戰的教導非常好，以至於我發現自己崇拜斯通沃爾傑克遜。 雷蒙：哇。格勞德：你聽到了嗎？ 雷蒙：哇。格勞德：你看，基斯在大城市長大。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I grew up on the water, you know?LAYMON: (Laughter).GLAUDE: And so, you know, for me, getting to Hattiesburg and then to Jackson was, you know, the biggest thing I could ever see outside of going to - you know, we rarely went to Mobile or New Orleans.", "zh": "我是在水邊長大的，你知道嗎？ 雷蒙：（笑聲）。 格勞德：所以，你知道，對我來說，先到哈蒂斯堡，然後再到傑克遜，是我除了去莫比爾或新奧爾良之外能看到的最重要的事情——你知道，我們很少去莫比爾或新奧爾良。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But, you know, I think, for me, I was educated in the context of the lost cause, right?", "zh": "但是，你知道，我認為，對我來說，我是在失敗的背景下接受教育的，對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So Hiram Revels came to me, I think, probably - you remember that Stevie Wonder track off of \"Songs In The Key Of Life,\" that history track?", "zh": "所以我想 Hiram Revels 來找我了，你還記得 Stevie Wonder 的《Songs In The Key Of Life》那首歷史曲目嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "(Singing) First man to die - (vocalizing)...LAYMON: Oh, yeah.", "zh": "（唱）第一個死去的人 - （發聲）...LAYMON：哦，是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Yeah.GLAUDE: ...You know, (singing) was a Black man.", "zh": "是的。格勞德：……你知道，（唱）是個黑人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That track?LAYMON: Yeah.GLAUDE: So I began to learn a lot of history from that particular 1976 track.", "zh": "那首歌？ LAYMON：是的。 GLAUDE：所以我開始從那首 1976 年的歌曲中了解很多歷史。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But...LAYMON: That's amazing.GLAUDE: In school, no, no, no, no.", "zh": "但是... LAYMON：那太棒了。 GLAUDE：在學校，不，不，不，不。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "There was no real attention.", "zh": "沒有得到真正的關注。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In a town that is majority Black, there was no real attention to Reconstruction in any substantive or significant way.", "zh": "在一個黑人佔多數的城鎮中，沒有人以​​任何實質或重要的方式真正關注重建。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So Hiram Revels never came to me until I actually got to Morehouse.MOSLEY: But I'm just wondering.", "zh": "所以直到我真正到達莫爾豪斯之後，海勒姆·雷維爾斯才來找過我。 莫斯利：但我只是想知道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Both of you are educators, you're professors, you're teaching young people.", "zh": "你們都是教育家，你們是教授，你們在教導年輕人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What does it do to our understanding of our own possibilities when we grow up knowing about the oppression of our ancestors?", "zh": "當我們在成長過程中了解祖先所受的壓迫時，這對我們理解自己的可能性有什麼影響？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Because you learned that growing up, I'm sure, Eddie.GLAUDE: Yeah.", "zh": "我敢肯定，因為你在成長過程中就知道了這一點。 Eddie.GLAUDE： 是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Absolutely.MOSLEY: But not the power they possessed, not a Revels.GLAUDE: Right.", "zh": "絕對可以。 莫斯利： 但不是他們擁有的權力，不是狂歡。 格勞德： 是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I think, you know, I think it's, for me, there were some things that just came by way of the household in which I grew up.", "zh": "我想，你知道，我認為，對我來說，有些事情是我長大的家庭帶來的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, even though my dad and my mom weren't readers, there was a fundamental insistence on the power of who we were as human beings, irrespective of what the world told us.", "zh": "你知道，儘管我的父親和母親不讀書，但無論世界告訴我們什麼，我們都堅信我們作為人類的力量。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But it's also the case that, you know, the kinds of stories we tell, the kinds of histories we tell ourselves have an immediate impact on the kinds of people we take ourselves to be.", "zh": "但事實也是如此，你知道，我們所講述的故事類型、我們所講述的歷史類型會對我們將自己視為什麼樣的人產生直接影響。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Who and what you choose to leave out of your stories actually reveal the limits of your conceptions of justice.So, you know, the kinds of stories we tell ourselves and what we leave out can actually lead to a deformation of character.", "zh": "你選擇在故事中省略的人物和內容實際上揭示了你的正義觀念的局限性。所以，你知道，我們告訴自己的故事類型以及我們省略的內容實際上會導致性格的變形。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You have these gaps that you have to fill.", "zh": "你必須填補這些空白。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Then those gaps can impact judgment and empathy and the like.", "zh": "這些差距會影響判斷力和同理心等。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So - and your own sense of possibility.", "zh": "所以——以及你自己的可能性感。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I think it's impactful for young African American men and women, young children, irrespective of the agenda, to be denied access to the fullness of our story.", "zh": "因此，我認為，無論議程如何，被拒絕了解我們故事的全部內容對於年輕的非裔美國男女、幼兒來說都是有影響的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But it's also impacting the folk who are doing the denying.", "zh": "但這也影響了那些否認的人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It distorts and disfigures them.", "zh": "它扭曲並毀壞了它們。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And they don't have people like my mom and daddy to help them out.LAYMON: And I'm thinking a lot, also, Eddie, about the way that distortion and disfigurement lands in the sentence.", "zh": "他們沒有像我媽媽和爸爸這樣的人來幫助他們。 雷蒙：艾迪，我也想了很多關於句子中扭曲和毀容的方式。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And as an English professor, you know, I have to land in the sentence, right?", "zh": "作為一名英語教授，你知道，我必須在句子中著陸，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "For better or worse, these sentences have created movements, you know?", "zh": "無論好壞，這些句子都創造了運動，你知道嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Make America Great Again is a sentence.", "zh": "讓美國再次偉大是一句話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Black Lives Matter is a sentence, right?", "zh": "Black Lives Matter 是一句話，對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I just think it's important that the sentence that I grew up - because I grew up in Jackson, named for the most, one of the most, if not the most destructive members of the Confederate Party.MOSLEY: Oh, I didn't even know that.LAYMON: Yeah.", "zh": "我只是認為我長大這句話很重要 - 因為我在傑克遜長大，傑克遜以南方邦聯黨中最具破壞性的成員之一命名。 莫斯利： 哦，我甚至不知道這一點。 雷蒙： 是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So when I say Jackson...MOSLEY: Named after Louis Jackson.LAYMON: ...That's what I'm saying. Like, Jackson, right?", "zh": "所以當我說傑克森時...莫斯利：以路易斯傑克森命名。 雷蒙：...這就是我的意思。就像，傑克遜，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Like, Jackson, 95% Black.", "zh": "例如傑克遜，95% 是黑人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So for me as a professor, I'm trying to encourage myself and my students to understand that every sentence that we construct is a possibility.", "zh": "因此，對我來說，身為教授，我試著鼓勵自己和我的學生明白，我們建構的每一個句子都是一種可能性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And every sentence that has carried a movement is a possibility to what?", "zh": "而每一個帶有動感的句子都是一種什麼的可能性？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "To engage, but to also revise.", "zh": "參與，但也要修改。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so what I see in Pick Another Senator is another sentence.", "zh": "所以我在《挑選另一位參議員》中看到的又是另一句話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Pick Another Senator that we've given a profundity to. But who is the we?", "zh": "選擇另一位我們給予深刻評價的參議員。但我們是誰？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The we is the people, right?", "zh": "我們就是人民，對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I just think it's really important as sentence creators and sentence makers, as all three of us are, with Mississippi roots, to really contend with the ways that these sentences have created sentences for some of our people, but also the way that these sentences are portals of entry into a possibility that we don't understand but they necessarily are. You know what I mean?", "zh": "所以我认为，作为造句者和造句者，就像我们三个人一样，都来自密西西比州，真正重要的是要真正应对这些句子为我们一些人创造句子的方式，而且这些句子是进入我们不理解但它们必然理解的可能性的门户。你知道我的意思？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Make America Great Again - worst sentence in my life.GLAUDE: Oh, my God.LAYMON: But also possibly one of the most profound sentences in my life.", "zh": "讓美國再次偉大——我一生中最糟糕的一句話。格劳德：哦，我的上帝。雷蒙：但也可能是我人生中最深刻的句子之一。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I just want - as English teacher, it's an occasion for us to recommit to sort of, like, the holiness of sentences.GLAUDE: Wow.LAYMON: And in creative writing programs, that means a lot because we're not trained to do that work.MOSLEY: If you're just joining us, my guests are Princeton scholar Eddie Glaude and Rice University professor Kiese Laymon.", "zh": "所以我只是想 - 作為英語老師，這是我們重新致力於句子的神聖性的一個機會。 格勞德：哇。 雷蒙： 在創意寫作專案中，這意義重大，因為我們沒有接受過這項工作的訓練。 莫斯利： 如果你剛加入我們，我的來賓是普林斯頓大學學者艾迪‧格勞德和萊斯大學教授基斯‧雷蒙。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We'll be right back after a short break.", "zh": "短暫休息後我們就會回來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This is FRESH AIR.(SOUNDBITE OF SLOWBERN'S \"WHEN WAR WAS KING\")MOSLEY: This is FRESH AIR, and today, I am talking with Eddie Glaude and Kiese Laymon about Scott Colom's historic Senate election win in Mississippi.Something that **fascinates** me about Scott Colom's history is his family's political history.", "zh": "這是新鮮空氣。 （斯洛伯恩的《當戰爭為王時》的原聲片段）莫斯利：這是新鮮空氣，今天，我正在與埃迪·格勞德和基斯·萊蒙談論斯科特·科羅姆在密西西比州歷史性的參議院選舉勝利。史考特·科羅姆的歷史讓我**著迷**的是他家族的政治史。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So his family is very politically active in the same way Kiese, your family was, but his father, Wilbur, was a Civil Rights activist who actually became a Republican and worked on Ronald Reagan's presidential transition team, and his mother, Dorothy, was a lifelong Democrat.", "zh": "因此，他的家人在政治上非常活躍，就像基澤（Kiese）和你的家人一樣，但他的父親威爾伯（Wilbur）是一名民權活動家，實際上成為了共和黨人，並在羅納德·裡根（Ronald Reagan）的總統過渡團隊中工作，而他的母親多蘿西（Dorothy）是終身民主黨人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Both of them were lawyers, deeply engaged in Mississippi politics.", "zh": "他們兩人都是律師，深入參與密西西比州政治。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Now, his father argued that Black voters shouldn't automatically give their votes to Democrats.", "zh": "現在，他的父親認為黑人選民不應該自動把票投給民主黨。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I'm thinking about that standing as it relates to today.", "zh": "我正在考慮與今天相關的立場。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I just wonder from you, Kiese, was his dad making a legitimate argument about political independence?", "zh": "我只是想知道你，基澤，他的父親對政治獨立提出了合理的論點嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What do we lose when we treat Black political allegiance kind of as a **foregone** conclusion, you know?", "zh": "當我們將黑人的政治忠誠視為已成定局時，我們會失去什麼，你知道嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This is a discussion that we've been having about the Democratic base in particular.LAYMON: Yeah.", "zh": "這是我們一直在特別針對民主黨基礎的討論。 雷蒙：是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, I think when you treat Black vote for Democrat as a **foregone** conclusion, you lose the people.", "zh": "我的意思是，我認為當你將黑人投票給民主黨視為已成定局時，你就會失去人民。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I think the people are perpetually letting candidates know what they need to survive, what they need to thrive.", "zh": "我認為人們總是讓候選人知道他們需要什麼才能生存，需要什麼才能茁壯成長。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, you know, like, again, I grew up in that political class of people where, you know, my mother knew Scott's parents, and, you know, like, early on, I think some of the Democrats were a little questioning of Mr.", "zh": "而且，你知道，就像，我是在那個政治階層長大的，你知道，我的母親認識史考特的父母，而且，你知道，就像，早期，我認為一些民主黨人對川普先生有點質疑。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Wilbur for you know, encouraging us to vote Republican, but that does not mean that those people who were critical wanted Black people in Mississippi to blindly vote Democrat.", "zh": "威爾伯，你知道，鼓勵我們投票共和黨，但這並不意味著那些持批評態度的人希望密西西比州的黑人盲目投票民主黨。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I just want to say this - if I learned anything from my mother - and I learned a few things - my mother was like, Kiese, the right to vote - great.", "zh": "我只想說這一點 - 如果我從我母親那裡學到了任何東西 - 我學到了一些東西 - 我的母親就像，基澤，投票權 - 太棒了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, my mother didn't have it till I was 40. We need it.", "zh": "你知道，我媽媽直到我 40 歲才擁有它。我們需要它。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But the problem she says is that we did not have anybody to vote for.", "zh": "但她說的問題是我們沒有人可以投票。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She says that all throughout the late 20th century.", "zh": "她在整個 20 世紀末都這麼說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "There were no incredible candidates in Mississippi to vote for.If there were an incredible candidate who I think valued clean water and incredible healthcare, wonderful food, that happened to be a Republican, my mother would have loved that person.", "zh": "密西西比州没有令人难以置信的候选人可供投票。如果有一位我認為重視清潔水和令人難以置信的醫療保健、美味食物的令人難以置信的候選人，而他恰好是共和黨人，我的母親會喜歡那個人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But my mother's critique was that person never existed on the Democratic side.", "zh": "但我母親的批評是民主黨從來不存在這個人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So it was always when we have to vote for the lesser of two evils on a larger scale.", "zh": "因此，我們總是必須在更大範圍內投票支持兩害相權取其輕。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But on the local scale - I think this is where Mississippi politics gets confused - the state with one of the most counties that are Democrat has always been Mississippi.", "zh": "但在地方範圍內 - 我認為這就是密西西比州政治混亂的地方 - 民主黨縣最多的州之一一直是密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We have - half the state is almost, in terms of counties, because, again, we're almost 40% Black, half the state is almost Democratic if you look at the counties.", "zh": "我們有 - 就縣而言，幾乎有一半的州是黑人，因為，再一次，我們幾乎有 40% 的黑人，如果你看一下縣，一半的州幾乎是民主黨的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I'm saying all that to say that my mother's critique has always been that Black people vote Democrat, and we don't have great candidates running.", "zh": "所以我說這一切是為了說我母親的批評一直是黑人投票給民主黨，而我們沒有優秀的候選人參選。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I will say, I don't know anybody who's more critical of Mississippi politicians than Mary Coleman, my mother.", "zh": "我要說的是，我不知道有誰比我的母親瑪麗·科爾曼更批評密西西比州的政客了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And when I - and actually, when I knew he was going to win, it was when my mother looked at that man in a hoodie, and she was like, that's a Mississippi senator.", "zh": "當我——實際上，當我知道他會贏的時候，我母親看著那個穿著連帽衫的男人，她說，那是密西西比州的參議員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This is the same mama who told me never wear a hoodie.(LAUGHTER)LAYMON: Ever.MOSLEY: I'm just thinking about, as we step out more broadly and thinking about the historic first, 'cause Colom is part of an election filled with historic firsts.", "zh": "這就是告訴我永遠不要穿連帽衫的媽媽。 （笑聲）雷蒙：永遠。莫斯利：我只是在思考，當我們更廣泛地邁出一步並思考歷史性的第一次時，因為科羅姆是充滿歷史性第一次的選舉的一部分。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Voters turned out and elected, of course, Colom, but a Hispanic governor in Texas, a Black woman governor in Georgia, a Native American woman governor in New Mexico.", "zh": "選民當然選舉了科洛姆，但他是德州的西班牙裔州長、喬治亞州的黑人女州長、新墨西哥州的美國原住民女州長。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But we're also a country that has spent the last few years arguing about identity politics and political correctness and diversity.", "zh": "但我們也是一個在過去幾年一直在爭論身份政治、政治正確性和多樣性的國家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We have leaders in the Democratic Party who say the path forward is to not focus on identity politics.", "zh": "民主黨領袖表示，前進的道路是不要關注身分政治。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Eddie, what do you think these victories tell us?GLAUDE: Look, what happened in the South has everything to do with the fact that Black folk turned out in historic numbers without Obama on the ticket.", "zh": "艾迪，你認為這些勝利告訴我們什麼？ 格勞德：聽著，南方發生的事情與這樣一個事實有關：黑人在沒有歐巴馬的情況下以歷史性的數字參加了投票。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Think about what happened in Texas, y'all.", "zh": "你們大家想想德州發生的事。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It wasn't some Black celebrity on the ballot.", "zh": "選票上並不是某個黑人名人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And Black folk in Texas turned out in historic numbers and voted for Hinojosa.", "zh": "德州的黑人人數創下歷史新高，並投票支持伊諾霍薩。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And then you think about what happened in North Carolina, what happened in South Carolina, what happened in Georgia, what happened in Louisiana, what happened in Florida, and part of what I'm suggesting here is to kind of reduce that turnout to a return-to-identity politics is condescending. It's enraging, alright?", "zh": "然後你想想北卡羅來納州發生的事情，南卡羅來納州發生的事情，佐治亞州發生的事情，路易斯安那州發生的事情，佛羅裡達州發生的事情，我在這裡建議的部分內容是減少回歸身份政治的投票率居高臨下。很氣憤好嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You have Black voters engaging in the process in light of their interest.", "zh": "黑人選民根據自己的興趣參與這個過程。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That is to say, you had Republicans who sought to disenfranchise us, to throw us back to the 1950s.", "zh": "也就是說，共和黨人試圖剝奪我們的選舉權，讓我們回到 20 世紀 50 年代。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We organized in defense of our democratic rights and in response to the assault on our economic and material conditions.", "zh": "我們組織起來捍衛我們的民主權利，並回應對我們經濟和物質條件的攻擊。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, and so to reduce that to identity, politics - right? - reveals - how can I put this in a delicate way?", "zh": "我的意思是，因此將其簡化為身份、政治——對吧？ - 揭示 - 我該如何以微妙的方式表達這一點？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Well, let's not be delicate.LAYMON: (Laughter).GLAUDE: The Democratic Party all too often thinks of Black voters as cattle chewing cud...LAYMON: Yep.GLAUDE: ...To be herded every two and four years as if we're not a constituency that has interest.", "zh": "好吧，我們不要太敏感了。 萊蒙：（笑聲） 格勞德：民主黨經常認為黑人選民是反芻的牛... 萊蒙：是的。 格勞德：...每兩年和四年就會被趕走，就好像我們不是一個有興趣的選區一樣。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, Baldwin used to loathe this question - what else does the Negro want?", "zh": "你知道，鮑德溫曾經討厭這個問題──黑人還想要什麼？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And Baldwin would say, if you thought of me as a human being, you would know exactly what I want.", "zh": "鮑德溫會說，如果你把我視為一個人，你就會確切地知道我想要什麼。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I want the exact same things you do for your babies, right?", "zh": "我希望你為你的寶寶做同樣的事情，對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I think it's a red herring. That's the short answer.", "zh": "所以我認為這是一條紅鯡魚。這就是簡短的答案。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I think that the worry about identity politics is a red herring.", "zh": "我認為對身分政治的擔憂是轉移注意力的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But you need to speak to the conditions of a constituency that fundamentally just handed the Congress to you.MOSLEY: Let's take a short break.", "zh": "但你需要談談從根本上把國會交給你的選區的情況。 莫斯利：讓我們休息一下。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "If you're just joining us, my guests are Princeton scholar Eddie Glaude and Rice University professor Kiese Laymon.", "zh": "如果您剛加入我們，我的嘉賓是普林斯頓大學學者埃迪·格勞德和萊斯大學教授基斯·雷蒙。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We'll be right back after a short break.", "zh": "短暫休息後我們就會回來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This is FRESH AIR.(SOUNDBITE OF MUSIC)MOSLEY: This is FRESH AIR.", "zh": "這是新鮮空氣。 （音樂原聲）莫斯利：這是新鮮空氣。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And today, I am talking with Eddie Glaude and Kiese Laymon about Scott Colom's historic Senate election win in Mississippi.Colom's campaign got a lot of attention for its humorous ads, but he closed with a very different ad filmed in Jackson at the home of Medgar Evers, who was the NAACP leader who was assassinated in his own driveway back in 1963.", "zh": "今天，我正在與埃迪·格勞德和基斯·雷蒙談論斯科特·科羅姆在密西西比州歷史性的參議院選舉中獲勝。科羅姆的競選活動因其幽默的廣告而受到廣泛關注，但他以在傑克遜梅德加·埃弗斯的家中拍攝的一個截然不同的廣告作為結束，埃弗斯是全國有色人種協進會領導人，1963年在自家車道上被暗殺。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I just want to play it.", "zh": "我只是想玩它。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Let's listen.(SOUNDBITE OF ARCHIVED RECORDING)COLOM: There's a house in Jackson every Mississippian ought to walk through once.", "zh": "讓我們聽聽。 （存檔錄音的聲音片段）COLOM：傑克遜有一棟房子，每個密西西比人都應該走過一次。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It looks like every other house on the street, except for it isn't.(SOUNDBITE OF MUSIC)COLOM: It has no front door.", "zh": "它看起來就像街上的所有其他房子，但事實並非如此。 （音樂片段）COLOM：它沒有前門。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You come in through the carport, where the walls give you some cover.", "zh": "你從車庫進來，那裡的牆壁為你提供了一些掩護。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The children slept on the floor below the windows.", "zh": "孩子們睡在窗戶下面的地板上。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Their father taught them that if they ever heard gunfire, they should crawl to the bathroom.", "zh": "他們的父親告訴他們，如果聽到槍聲，就應該爬到浴室。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He made it a game.I've been a prosecutor for 10 years.", "zh": "他把它變成了一個遊戲。我當檢察官已經十年了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Unfortunately, I've stood in a lot of houses where something terrible happened. This isn't any house.", "zh": "不幸的是，我曾經去過很多發生過可怕事情的房子。這不是任何房子。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This isn't any tragedy.(SOUNDBITE OF CAMERA FLASH)COLOM: This is where Medgar Evers died.", "zh": "这不是什么悲剧。 （攝影機閃光燈的聲音） 科洛姆：這就是梅德加·埃弗斯去世的地方。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He fought for this country in Normandy.(SOUNDBITE OF CAMERA FLASH)COLOM: He came home to Mississippi, and they wouldn't let him vote.(SOUNDBITE OF CAMERA FLASH)COLOM: So he organized, helping other people register.", "zh": "他在諾曼第為這個國家而戰。 （攝影機閃光燈的聲音）科洛姆：他回到密西西比州的家鄉，他們不讓他投票。 （攝影機閃光燈的聲音）科洛姆：所以他組織起來，幫助其他人登記。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Just after midnight on June 12, 1963, he pulled into here with an arm full of T-shirts that said, Jim Crow must go.", "zh": "1963 年 6 月 12 日午夜過後，他滿懷寫著「吉姆克勞必須走開」的 T 卹來到這裡。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "A man hiding across the street shot him in the back.(SOUNDBITE OF CAMERA FLASH)COLOM: Two juries let that man walk.", "zh": "一名躲在街對面的男子從背後開槍射中了他。 （攝影機閃光燈的聲音） 科洛姆：兩個陪審團讓那個人走了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "His wife, Myrlie...(SOUNDBITE OF CAMERA FLASH)COLOM: ...Never stopped.", "zh": "他的妻子，Myrlie...（攝影機閃光燈的聲音片段）COLOM：...從未停止過。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It took 31 years, then a Mississippi prosecutor reopened the case, and a Mississippi jury, both Black and white, convicted him.", "zh": "31年後，密西西比州檢察官重新審理此案，密西西比州黑人和白人陪審團對他定罪。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In Mississippi, no one is above the law, and no one should be outside its protection.", "zh": "在密西西比州，沒有人可以凌駕於法律之上，也沒有人可以脫離法律的保護。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He was killed for helping Mississippians vote.", "zh": "他因幫助密西西比人投票而被殺。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "On Tuesday, use your vote and honor everyone who died for that right.MOSLEY: That was one of the last ads before the election of Scott Colom.", "zh": "週二，用你的選票向每一個為這項權利犧牲的人致敬。 莫斯利：那是史考特·科羅姆當選前最後的廣告之一。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And you could hear those flashes.", "zh": "你可以聽到那些閃光的聲音。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Those were photo flashes.", "zh": "那些是照片閃光燈。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That ad made me think about - we keep hearing people call this victory a political miracle.", "zh": "那則廣告讓我想到──我們不斷聽到人們稱這次勝利為政治奇蹟。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But this ad is a reminder that, in a way, calling it a miracle misses the people who made it possible.", "zh": "但這一廣告提醒人們，在某種程度上，稱其為奇蹟是懷念那些使之成為可能的人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What does it make you guys think about?LAYMON: Well, I can just say, you know, I - for four years that I went to high school, I went to - you had to drive every day Medgar Evers Boulevard.", "zh": "這讓你們想到了什麼？ LAYMON：嗯，我只能說，你知道，我 - 在我上高中的四年裡，我 - 你必須每天開車前往 Medgar Evers Boulevard。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "My mother's mentor, Margaret Walker, lived a few streets over from Medgar Evers.", "zh": "我母親的導師瑪格麗特·沃克住在離梅德加·埃弗斯幾條街的地方。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We used to play football right in front of Medgar Evers' house.", "zh": "我們過去常常在梅德加·埃弗斯家門口踢足球。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And it's not one of these situations where we never know who Medgar Evers was.", "zh": "這並不是我們永遠不知道梅德加·埃弗斯是誰的情況之一。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Like, to us, Medgar Evers wanted the best for Black Mississippians, and he wanted the best for Mississippi.", "zh": "就像，對我們來說，梅德加·埃弗斯希望密西西比黑人得到最好的待遇，他也希望密西西比州得到最好的待遇。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And that is why he was shot.So hearing Scott in his campaign with that ad, when the tone of the campaign - right? - had been so lifted with the pick a protein, pick another senator ad, one, I think, speaks to the daring, and I think whether or not we know it or not, speaks to Scott and his people's desire to connect his ability to govern to historic Black activists of the past.", "zh": "這就是他被槍殺的原因。所以聽到斯科特在他的競選活動中使用那則廣告，當時競選的基調 - 對吧？ - 我對選擇一種蛋白質、選擇另一位參議員的廣告感到如此振奮，我認為，這則廣告體現了大膽的精神，而且我認為無論我們是否知道，它都體現了斯科特和他的人民希望將他的執政能力與過去歷史悠久的黑人活動家聯繫起來。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Now, whether or not that is a good idea, as far as governance goes, I'm not sure, right?", "zh": "現在，就治理而言，這是否是一個好主意，我不確定，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Because Medgar Evers had a different role to play than Scott does I believe.", "zh": "因為梅德加·埃弗斯扮演的角色與我認為的斯科特不同。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But what I love about it is that it animates, like, a reality for Mississippians.", "zh": "但我喜歡它的是它為密西西比人帶來了現實。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Medgar Evers, like, we - that's our street.", "zh": "Medgar Evers，就像，我們——那是我們的街道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "His house is where we - you know, we play ball there.", "zh": "他的房子是我們——你知道的，我們在那裡打球的地方。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And it makes me remember that, like, we grew up living what people call history.", "zh": "這讓我想起，我們是在人們所謂的歷史中長大的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I think that can be very important for young people trying to find some sense of self in this nation.GLAUDE: Right, it was the closing ad of the campaign that suggested or presented or projected the fact that the campaign itself carried the weight of history itself.", "zh": "我認為這對於試圖在這個國家尋找自我意識的年輕人來說非常重要。 格勞德：是的，正是競選的結束廣告暗示、呈現或預測了這樣一個事實：競選本身承載著歷史本身的重量。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "When I saw it, I was trying to process it in a number of different ways.", "zh": "當我看到它時，我試著用多種不同的方式來處理它。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And, ironically, you know, Kiese, I reached for Faulkner and \"Requiem For A Nun,\" that line, you know, the past is never dead.", "zh": "而且，諷刺的是，你知道，基澤，我伸手去聽福克納和《修女安魂曲》，那句台詞，你知道，過去永遠不會死。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's not even past, right?", "zh": "甚至還沒過去，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And so there was this sense in which the invocation of Medgar Evers in that moment is to not just simply recall a horrific act of murder, right?", "zh": "因此，在那一刻召喚梅德加·埃弗斯不僅僅是簡單地回憶起可怕的謀殺行為，對嗎？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But to bring it into the present in a way such that it can inform and shape our choices in very clear and concrete ways.MOSLEY: Colom won by exactly 8,031 votes.", "zh": "但要以一種能夠以非常清晰和具體的方式告知和塑造我們選擇的方式將其帶入當下。 莫斯利：科羅姆以 8,031 票準確獲勝。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I'm thinking about the last time a Black man went to the Senate for the state of Mississippi - a very long time ago.", "zh": "我想起了上次一位黑人進入密西西比州參議院的情況——那是很久以前的事了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It was undone - that progress during Reconstruction - undone within a generation.", "zh": "它被毀了——重建期間的進展——在一代之內就被毀了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "What are you both watching for this time?LAYMON: Wow.", "zh": "這次你們兩個在看什麼？ LAYMON：哇。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, honestly, because we're talking to y'all, I'm watching for and hoping for immense health and safety to come to Scott Colom and his wife, Nadia, and their incredible children.", "zh": "我的意思是，老實說，因為我們正在與你們所有人交談，所以我正在關注並希望斯科特·科洛姆和他的妻子納迪亞以及他們令人難以置信的孩子們獲得巨大的健康和安全。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "None of this is possible unless we keep them safe.", "zh": "除非我們保證他們的安全，否則這一切都是不可能的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I wish this wasn't something we had to say.", "zh": "我希望這不是我們必須說的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This is something we have to say.", "zh": "這是我們不得不說的話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So I have no doubt that that man is going to go out there and push and make a path for more potential young folks who have his gumption to lead Mississippi.", "zh": "因此，我毫不懷疑，那個人會走出去，推動並為更多有潛力的年輕人開闢一條道路，這些年輕人有他的進取心來領導密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I just know that in a state that has taken this long to change, the movement from Candidate Colom to Senator Colom has to be taken seriously, and he has to be protected along the way.And similarly, I will just say, as someone who loves Mississippi, I expect Scott Colom to risk for all of the Mississippi's children.", "zh": "我只知道，在一個花了這麼長時間才改變的州，必須認真對待從候選人科羅姆到參議員科羅姆的轉變，並且必須一路保護他。同样，我只想说，作为一个热爱密西西比州的人，我希望斯科特·科罗姆为密西西比州的所有孩子冒险。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Scott Colom is not an artist. He's not a writer.", "zh": "史考特·科羅姆不是藝術家。他不是作家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He can't say things we can say.", "zh": "他不能說我們能說的話。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "When I say all of Mississippi's children, I'm talking about all of Mississippi's children - the queer children, the poor children, the trans children.", "zh": "當我說所有密西西比州的孩子時，我指的是所有密西西比州的孩子——酷兒兒童、貧困兒童、跨性別兒童。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I think his role was made possible because of radical interventions from folks like Fannie Lou Hamer.", "zh": "我認為他的角色之所以成為可能，是因為范妮·盧·哈默（Fannie Lou Hamer）等人的激進干預。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I don't know how much radical intervention we can expect from a senator, but I expect Scott Colom, while keeping himself and his family safe, to also keep all children of Mississippi safe by all means necessary or to attempt to.", "zh": "我不知道我們可以期待參議員採取多少激進的干預措施，但我希望史考特·科洛姆在確保自己和家人安全的同時，也透過一切必要的手段或嘗試的手段來確保密西西比州所有兒童的安全。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I think that will lead to this being not just the first, but the first of a real, sustained movement for love, progress and connectivity in Mississippi.GLAUDE: Yeah. Yeah, that's it.", "zh": "我認為這將不僅僅是密西西比州第一次真正、持續的愛、進步和連結性運動。格勞德：是的。是的，就是這樣。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You know, I pray that he doesn't fall for the siren song of Washington, D.C.MOSLEY: Oh.LAYMON: Yeah.", "zh": "你知道，我祈禱他不會愛上華盛頓特區的海妖之歌。 莫斯利：哦。 雷蒙：是的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Yeah.GLAUDE: You know, Washington, D.C., offers, you know, all sorts of temptations about the nature of power, about what it means to be the first and the like.", "zh": "是的。格勞德：你知道，華盛頓特區提供了各種關於權力本質、關於成為第一意味著什麼等等的誘惑。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I hope he takes that gift of Mississippi that orients us in a certain sort of way to the world.", "zh": "我希望他能接受密西西比州的這份禮物，以某種方式引導我們走向世界。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I hope he brings it to Washington, D.C., and he lets all of them see it for what it is and all of its power.", "zh": "我希望他把它帶到華盛頓特區，讓所有人看到它的本質和它的所有力量。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I know that's being abstract, but that has everything to do with, I think, the power of what it means to be from this place.", "zh": "我知道這很抽象，但我認為這與來自這個地方的力量有關。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That's the first thing.The second thing, I think, you know, politicians inevitably disappoint. I learned that early on.", "zh": "這是第一件事。第二件事，我認為，政客們不可避免地會失望。我很早就知道了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But I want to see what Cassandra Welchlin and Rukia Lumumba and...LAYMON: Yeah.GLAUDE: ...Sister Lambright-Haynes and all of those organizers on the ground who made this possible - I want to see what they do in holding Scott Colom accountable.", "zh": "但我想看看 Cassandra Welchlin 和 Rukia Lumumba 以及...LAYMON：是的。 GLAUDE：...Lambright-Haynes 修女以及所有使這一切成為可能的當地組織者 - 我想看看他們如何讓 Scott Colom 承擔責任。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I can't wait to continue to see what they do, and how Scott plays this role in that effort.LAYMON: Yes. I agree with Eddie.", "zh": "我迫不及待地想繼續看看他們做了什麼，以及史考特如何在這項工作中扮演這個角色。 雷蒙：是的。我同意埃迪的觀點。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I mean, I hope - and if there's any moment where Democrats could learn that you must follow the people, it is this moment.", "zh": "我的意思是，我希望 - 如果民主黨人能在任何時刻了解到你必須跟隨人民，那就是現在。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I hope that the Democrats - you follow the people by funding the people but also being open to the people's visions.", "zh": "我希望民主黨人透過資助人民來追隨人民，但同時也要對人民的願景持開放態度。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And I have **absolute** trust in that group of people that helped Scott get elected.", "zh": "我對幫助史考特當選的那群人有絕對的信任。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I have no doubt in my mind that their vision for Mississippi is the vision for Mississippi and actually the vision for this nation and the world.", "zh": "我毫不懷疑，他們對密西西比州的願景就是密西西比州的願景，其實也是這個國家和世界的願景。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Whether the Democratic Party sees that or not is something else.", "zh": "民主黨是否看到這一點是另一回事。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But...GLAUDE: (Laughter).LAYMON: ...It's right there.", "zh": "但是...GLAUDE：（笑聲）。 LAYMON：...就在那裡。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's right there for you.MOSLEY: Kiese Laymon and Eddie Glaude, thank you so much for this conversation.GLAUDE: Thank you.LAYMON: Thank you so much for giving us space.MOSLEY: Eddie Glaude is a professor of African American Studies at Princeton University and the author of several books, including \"Begin Again\" and \"America, U.S.A.\" Kiese Laymon is a professor of English and creative writing at Rice University and the author of the acclaimed memoir, \"Heavy.\" His new memoir, \"Good, God: A Creation Story,\" will be published this spring.(SOUNDBITE OF DEEP BLUE ORGAN TRIO'S \"YOU HAVEN'T DONE NOTHIN'\")MOSLEY: If you'd like to catch up on interviews you've missed, like our conversation with LeVar Burton about his new memoir or Lynn Novick about her new documentary on crime and punishment in America, check out our podcast.", "zh": "莫斯利：基斯·雷蒙和艾迪·格勞德，非常感謝你們的這段對話。格勞德：謝謝你們。雷蒙：非常感謝你們給我們空間。莫斯利：艾迪‧格勞德是普林斯頓大學非裔美國人研究教授，也是多本書的作者，包括《重新開始》和《美國，美國》。基斯‧雷蒙 (Kisee Laymon) 是萊斯大學英語和創意寫作教授，也是廣受好評的回憶錄《沉重》的作者。他的新回憶錄《天啊：創世故事》將於今年春天出版。 （《深藍風琴三重奏》《你什麼都沒做》的原聲片段） 莫斯利：如果您想趕上您錯過的採訪，例如我們與勒瓦爾·伯頓談論他的新回憶錄或林恩·諾維克談論她關於美國犯罪和懲罰的新紀錄片的對話，請查看我們的播客。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You'll find lots of FRESH AIR interviews.", "zh": "你會發現很多新鮮空氣採訪。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You can also watch some of our interviews on our YouTube page, thisisfreshair.FRESH AIR's executive producer is Sam Briger.", "zh": "您也可以在我們的 YouTube 頁面 thisisfreshair.FRESH AIR 的執行製片人 Sam Briger 上觀看我們的一些採訪。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Our technical director and engineer is Audrey Bentham.", "zh": "我們的技術總監和工程師是 Audrey Bentham。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Our interviews and reviews are produced and edited by Phyllis Myers, Roberta Shorrock, Ann Marie Baldonado, Lauren Krenzel, Therese Madden, Monique Nazareth, Susan Nyakundi, Anna Bauman and Nico Gonzalez-Wisler.", "zh": "我們的採訪和評論由 Phyllis Myers、Roberta Shorrock、Ann Marie Baldonado、Lauren Krenzel、Therese Madden、Monique Nazareth、Susan Nyakundi、Anna Bauman 和 Nico Gonzalez-Wisler 製作和編輯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Our digital media producer is Molly Seavy-Nesper.", "zh": "我們的數位媒體製作人是 Molly Seavy-Nesper。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Thea Chaloner directed today's show.", "zh": "西婭·查洛納 (Thea Chaloner) 執導了今天的節目。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "With Terry Gross, I'm Tonya Mosley.(SOUNDBITE OF DEEP BLUE ORGAN TRIO'S \"YOU HAVEN'T DONE NOTHIN'\")", "zh": "我是 Terry Gross，我是 Tonya Mosley。 （深蓝风琴三重奏“YOU HAVEN'T DONE NOTHIN'”原声片段）", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "版權所有 © 2026 NPR。版權所有。請造訪我們的網站使用條款和…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Copyright © 2026 NPR. All rights reserved.", "zh": "版權所有 © 2026 NPR。版權所有。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Visit our website terms of use and permissions pages at www.npr.org for further information.", "zh": "請造訪我們的網站使用條款和權限頁面 www.npr.org 以了解更多資訊。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "NPR 節目文字記錄的準確性和可用性可能會有所不同。轉錄文字也可能會…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Accuracy and availability of transcripts for NPR programming may vary.", "zh": "NPR 節目文字記錄的準確性和可用性可能會有所不同。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Transcript text may also be revised to correct errors or match updates to audio.", "zh": "轉錄文字也可能會被修改以糾正錯誤或匹配音訊更新。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Audio may be edited after its original broadcast or publication.", "zh": "音訊可以在其原始廣播或出版後進行編輯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The authoritative record of NPR’s programming is the audio record.", "zh": "NPR 節目的權威記錄是音訊記錄。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Please note that NPR platforms and products also include some programming produced by third parties; NPR cannot guarantee transcripts for that content and some transcripts may be produced using automated or other tools.", "zh": "請注意，NPR 平台和產品還包括一些第三方製作的節目； NPR 無法保證該內容的文字記錄，並且某些文字記錄可能是使用自動化或其他工具產生的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "史考特·科洛姆現在是這個南方州近 150 年來第一位黑人美國參議員。學者們和密西西比人埃迪·格勞德和基澤·雷蒙討論了他的勝利的歷史意義。　版權所有 © 2026 NPR。版權所有。請造訪我們的網站使用條款和權限頁面 www.npr.org 以了解更多資訊。　NPR 節目文字記錄的準確性和可用性可能會有所不同。轉錄文字也可能會被修改以糾正錯誤或匹配音訊更新。音訊可以在其原始廣播或出版後進行編輯。 NPR 節目的權威記錄是音訊記錄。請注意，NPR 平台和產品還包括一些第三方製作的節目； NPR 無法保證該內容的文字記錄，並且某些文字記錄可能是使用自動化或其他工具產生的。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "quintessentially", "sf": "quintessentially", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "典型地", "syn": "typically", "tip": "英英定義　In a manner that is typical or characteristic of a thing's nature.　|　本文例句　It's quintessentially Mississippi.　|　例句中譯　這是典型的密西西比州。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "fascinates", "sf": "fascinates", "pos": "v.", "zh": "著迷", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　迷住、吸引、誘惑　|　英英定義　To evoke an intense interest or attraction in someone.　|　本文例句　Something that fascinates me about Scott Colom's history is his family's political history.　|　例句中譯　史考特·科羅姆的歷史讓我著迷的是他家族的政治史。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "exceptionalism", "sf": "exceptionalism", "pos": "n.", "zh": "例外論", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　The state of being special, exceptional or unique.　|　本文例句　What responsibility does the rest of the country bear for what happens there, I mean, and making people understand this is not just an isolated state win, but it's something that potentially is much bigger?GLAUDE: Well, you know, I mean, this is a kind of Southern exceptionalism that defines so much of the nation.　|　例句中譯　我的意思是，這個國家的其他地區對那裡發生的事情負有什麼責任，讓人們明白這不僅僅是一個孤立的國家勝利，而且可能是更大的事情？ 格勞德：嗯，你知道，我的意思是，這是一種南方例外論，它定義了這個國家的大部分人。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "intergenerational", "sf": "intergenerational", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "世代的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Between or across generations.　|　本文例句　It was not just, like, an intergenerational march.　|　例句中譯　這不僅僅是一場代際遊行。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "gerrymandering", "sf": "gerrymandering", "pos": "v.", "zh": "不公正地劃分選區", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　To divide a geographic area into voting districts in such a way as to give an unfair advantage to one party in an election.", "trap": ""}, {"w": "foregone", "sf": "foregone", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "放棄的", "syn": "antecede, come before", "tip": "其他意思　過去的　|　英英定義　To precede, to go before.　|　本文例句　I mean, I think when you treat Black vote for Democrat as a foregone conclusion, you lose the people.　|　例句中譯　我的意思是，我認為當你將黑人投票給民主黨視為已成定局時，你就會失去人民。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "obliterate", "sf": "obliterates", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "泯", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　被忽視的、廢止、殲、抹殺　|　英英定義　To remove completely, leaving no trace; to wipe out; to destroy.　|　本文例句　In some way, that sentence sort of, like, obliterates analysis.　|　例句中譯　某種程度上，這句話有點抹殺了分析。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "redistricting", "sf": "redistricting", "pos": "n.", "zh": "重新劃分選區", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　An instance of adjusting the borders that delineate districts.　|　本文例句　They were going to undermine the math that was informing the redistricting effort.　|　例句中譯　他們將破壞為選區重新劃分工作提供資訊的數學原理。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "respectability", "sf": "respectability", "pos": "n.", "zh": "受人尊敬", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　The quality of being respectable.　|　本文例句　What I loved about what Scott was doing this year was Scott, I think, took off that cloak of what some people call political respectability in terms of the look.　|　例句中譯　我認為史考特今年所做的事情讓我喜歡的是，史考特脫下了一些人所謂的政治尊嚴的外衣。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "absolve", "sf": "absolve", "pos": "v.", "zh": "開脫", "syn": "acquit, exculpate, exonerate", "tip": "其他意思　豁免、免、免除　|　英英定義　To set free, release or discharge (from obligations, debts, responsibility etc.).　|　本文例句　So when we talk about the history of the country, you know, the idea is to displace our sins onto the South - right? - so that we can absolve the nation of its sins in so many ways.　|　例句中譯　因此，當我們談論這個國家的歷史時，你知道，我們的想法是將我們的罪惡轉移到南方 - 對嗎？ - 这样我们就可以通过多种方式赦免这个国家的罪孽。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "intercultural", "sf": "intercultural", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "跨文化的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Of, relating to, or between different cultures　|　本文例句　It was an intercultural march and an intercultural election.　|　例句中譯　這是一場跨文化遊行和跨文化選舉。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "shrill", "sf": "shrill", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "尖銳", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　尖、尖利　|　英英定義　A shrill sound.　|　本文例句　You know, the white woman who asked in a very shrill kind of way, what the? You know, that - and the rhythm of it is everybody in Mississippi knows that's how you cuss, right? So.　|　例句中譯　你知道，那個白人婦女以一種非常尖銳的方式問，那是什麼？你知道，密西西比州的每個人都知道你就是這樣罵人的，對吧？所以。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6047338/bigger-than-barack-obamas-election-scholars-reflect-on-mississippi-senate-race"}, {"code": "20261119-1", "ch": "2026-11-19　週四", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Anthropic IPO raises record $81.3 billion on strong AI demand　／　Anthropic 因強勁的人工智慧需求而首次公開募股籌集了創紀錄的 813 億美元資金", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 John Ruwitch，全文共 5 段、7 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：這家成立五年的人工智慧巨頭將其首次公開募股定價為每股 83 美元，擺脫了人們對人工智慧可能出現泡沫和科技股波動日益增長的擔憂。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6046212/anthropic-record-ipo-price"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "人工智慧公司 Anthropic 週三表示，在一次破紀錄的首次公開募…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The **artificial** intelligence company Anthropic said on Wednesday it sold more than 956 million shares at a price of $83 a piece in a record-breaking initial **public** offering that makes it one of the most valuable companies in the world.", "zh": "人工智慧公司 Anthropic 週三表示，在一次破紀錄的首次**公開**募股中，以每股 83 美元的價格出售了**超過** 9.56 億股股票，使其成為世界上最有價值的公司之一。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "這家成立五年的人工智慧巨頭透過此次發行籌集了約 794 億美元，超過…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The five-year-old AI **powerhouse** raised around $79.4 billion through the offering, **exceeding** the $75 billion IPO haul of Elon Musk's SpaceX earlier this year.", "zh": "這家成立五年的人工智慧巨頭透過此次發行籌集了約 794 億美元，**超過**了 Elon Musk 的 SpaceX 今年稍早 750 億美元的 IPO 金額。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Anthropic said in a statement that \"certain **stockholders**\" also sold more than 23 million shares as part of the IPO, bringing the total haul to more than $81.3 billion.", "zh": "Anthropic 在聲明中表示，作為 IPO 的一部分，「某些**股東**」還出售了**超過** 2,300 萬股股票，使總收益超過 813 億美元。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "Anthropic 的股票將於週四在納斯達克開始公開交易，股票代號為…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Anthropic's shares will start trading **publicly** on Thursday on the Nasdaq under the **ticker** symbol ANT.", "zh": "Anthropic 的股票將於週四在納斯達克開始**公開**交易，股票代號為 ANT。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "儘管人們越來越擔心人工智慧泡沫和科技股的波動，但此次上市還是獲得了超…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "The listing was oversubscribed, despite coming at a time of growing concern about a possible AI **bubble** and **volatility** in tech stocks.", "zh": "儘管人們越來越擔心人工智慧泡沫和科技股的波動，但此次上市還是獲得了超額認購。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "出售的股票數量和價格超出了 Anthropic 最初的預期。上市招股…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The number of shares sold and the price **exceeded** Anthropic's original expectations.", "zh": "出售的股票數量和價格超出了 Anthropic 最初的預期。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The listing **prospectus** targeted a sale of 825 million shares at $70 to $78 per share.", "zh": "上市**招股說明書**目標以每股70至78美元的價格出售8.25億股股票。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "人工智慧公司 Anthropic 週三表示，在一次破紀錄的首次公開募股中，以每股 83 美元的價格出售了超過 9.56 億股股票，使其成為世界上最有價值的公司之一。　這家成立五年的人工智慧巨頭透過此次發行籌集了約 794 億美元，超過了 Elon Musk 的 SpaceX 今年稍早 750 億美元的 IPO 金額。 Anthropic 在聲明中表示，作為 IPO 的一部分，「某些股東」還出售了超過 2,300 萬股股票，使總收益超過 813 億美元。　Anthropic 的股票將於週四在納斯達克開始公開交易，股票代號為 ANT。　儘管人們越來越擔心人工智慧泡沫和科技股的波動，但此次上市還是獲得了超額認購。　出售的股票數量和價格超出了 Anthropic 最初的預期。上市招股說明書目標以每股70至78美元的價格出售8.25億股股票。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "ticker", "sf": "ticker", "pos": "n.", "zh": "股票行情", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　斷續器、鐘擺　|　英英定義　One who makes a tick mark.　|　本文例句　Anthropic's shares will start trading publicly on Thursday on the Nasdaq under the ticker symbol ANT.　|　例句中譯　Anthropic 的股票將於週四在納斯達克開始公開交易，股票代號為 ANT。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "stockholders", "sf": "stockholders", "pos": "n.", "zh": "股東", "syn": "shareholder, stockist", "tip": "英英定義　One who owns stock.　|　本文例句　Anthropic said in a statement that \"certain stockholders\" also sold more than 23 million shares as part of the IPO, bringing the total haul to more than $81.　|　例句中譯　Anthropic 在聲明中表示，作為 IPO 的一部分，「某些股東」還出售了超過 2,300 萬股股票，使總收益超過 81 美元。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "prospectus", "sf": "prospectus", "pos": "n.", "zh": "招股說明書", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A document, distributed to prospective members, investors, buyers or participants, which describes an institution (such as a university), a publication or a business and what it has to offer.　|　本文例句　The listing prospectus targeted a sale of 825 million shares at $70 to $78 per share.　|　例句中譯　上市招股說明書目標以每股70至78美元的價格出售8.25億股股票。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "powerhouse", "sf": "powerhouse", "pos": "n.", "zh": "發電站", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　發電廠、發電所、配電站　|　英英定義　A power station.　|　本文例句　The five-year-old AI powerhouse raised around $79.　|　例句中譯　這家成立五年的人工智慧巨頭籌集了約 79 美元。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "volatility", "sf": "volatility", "pos": "n.", "zh": "揮發性", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　短暫、易變　|　英英定義　The state of being volatile　|　本文例句　The listing was oversubscribed, despite coming at a time of growing concern about a possible AI bubble and volatility in tech stocks.　|　例句中譯　儘管人們越來越擔心人工智慧泡沫和科技股的波動，但此次上市還是獲得了超額認購。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "exceed", "sf": "exceeding", "pos": "v.", "zh": "超過", "syn": "excel, outperform, surpass", "tip": "其他意思　超、超出、超過限度　|　英英定義　To be larger, greater than (something).　|　本文例句　4 billion through the offering, exceeding the $75 billion IPO haul of Elon Musk's SpaceX earlier this year.　|　例句中譯　此次發行籌集了 40 億美元，超過了 Elon Musk 旗下 SpaceX 今年稍早 750 億美元的 IPO 規模。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "bubble", "sf": "bubble", "pos": "v.", "zh": "氣泡", "syn": "ambience, circumstances, bubble and squeak", "tip": "其他意思　沸騰、潏、冒泡、起泡　|　英英定義　A spherically contained volume of air or other gas, especially one made from soapy liquid.　|　本文例句　The listing was oversubscribed, despite coming at a time of growing concern about a possible AI bubble and volatility in tech stocks.　|　例句中譯　儘管人們越來越擔心人工智慧泡沫和科技股的波動，但此次上市還是獲得了超額認購。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "artificial", "sf": "artificial", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "人造的", "syn": "artificious", "tip": "其他意思　假、武斷的、虛假　|　英英定義　Man-made; of artifice.　|　本文例句　The artificial intelligence company Anthropic said on Wednesday it sold more than 956 million shares at a price of $83 a piece in a record-breaking initial public offering that makes it one of the most valuable companies in the world.　|　例句中譯　人工智慧公司 Anthropic 週三表示，在一次破紀錄的首次公開募股中，以每股 83 美元的價格出售了超過 9.56 億股股票，使其成為世界上最有價值的公司之一。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "publicly", "sf": "publicly", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "公開", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　公然、輿論上　|　英英定義　In public, openly, in an open and public manner.　|　本文例句　Anthropic's shares will start trading publicly on Thursday on the Nasdaq under the ticker symbol ANT.　|　例句中譯　Anthropic 的股票將於週四在納斯達克開始公開交易，股票代號為 ANT。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6046212/anthropic-record-ipo-price"}, {"code": "20261119-2", "ch": "2026-11-19　週四", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "After Nepal's epic flood, they're restoring their community ... and their lives　／　尼泊爾經歷了史詩般的洪水之後，他們正在恢復他們的社區…以及他們的生活", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Jonathan Lambert，全文共 18 段、41 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：隨著洪水緊急應變結束，援助人員轉而投入重建失去一切的社區的艱苦工作。其中許多工人也失去了一切。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6022034/flood-nepal-survival-climate-change"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "本篇較長，站上只收前 18 段；想讀完整篇請點上方的 NPR 原文連結。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "「我以為我活不下去了，」賈努卡·迪塔爾 (Januka Dhital…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "\"I thought I wouldn't survive,\" says Januka Dhital.", "zh": "「我以為我活不下去了，」賈努卡·迪塔爾 (Januka Dhital) 說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "就在那個可怕的想法出現前幾分鐘，迪塔爾正忙著準備零食。她在尼泊爾烏塔…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Just minutes before that terrible thought, Dhital was busy preparing snacks.", "zh": "就在那個可怕的想法出現前幾分鐘，迪塔爾正忙著準備零食。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She ran a catering service out of her house in Uttargaya, Nepal, and was getting ready for an event later that day.", "zh": "她在尼泊爾烏塔加亞的家中經營餐飲服務，並為當天晚些時候的活動做準備。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Her work was interrupted by a man on a scooter, warning of a flood.", "zh": "她的工作被一名騎摩托車的男子打斷，他警告洪水。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She stepped outside to look.", "zh": "她走到外面去看。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "「當我轉身時，我看到黑暗、灰塵和看起來整個山坡都塌下來了，」她說。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"When I turned around, I saw darkness, dust and what looked like the entire **hillside** coming down,\" she says.", "zh": "「當我轉身時，我看到黑暗、灰塵和看起來整個**山坡**都塌下來了，」她說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "她抓住年幼的兒子，跳上那個男人的摩托車後座。他們跑向地勢較高的地方，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "She grabbed her young son and **hopped** onto the back of the man's scooter.", "zh": "她抓住年幼的兒子，跳上那個男人的摩托車後座。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They raced to higher ground, eventually reaching safety.", "zh": "他們跑向地勢較高的地方，最後到達安全地帶。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But she didn't know if her husband and daughter were safe, since they were at work and school when the waters came.", "zh": "但她不知道她的丈夫和女兒是否安全，因為洪水來臨時他們正在上班和上學。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "經過幾個小時的等待和尋找，他們終於團聚了。她說，她的丈夫赤身裸體，渾…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "After hours of waiting and searching, they were all reunited.", "zh": "經過幾個小時的等待和尋找，他們終於團聚了。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Her husband was naked, covered in blood and badly injured, she says, but alive.", "zh": "她說，她的丈夫赤身裸體，渾身是血，受了重傷，但還活著。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "「我們一家人竟然倖存下來，這真是令人難以置信，」迪塔爾說。但從山上沖…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "\"It felt unbelievable that our family had survived,\" says Dhital.", "zh": "「我們一家人竟然倖存下來，這真是令人難以置信，」迪塔爾說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But the wall of water and mud that descended from the mountains had **obliterated** their home, along with thousands of others.", "zh": "但從山上沖下來的水和泥牆摧毀了他們的家園，以及成千上萬的其他家園。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"We have lost everything. We have nothing now.\"", "zh": "“我們失去了一切。我們現在什麼都沒有了。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "冰川融化引發的毀滅性洪水擾亂了 10 萬多人的生活，而氣候變遷又使這…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Dhital and her family are among the 100,000-some people whose lives have been upended by the **devastating** floods sparked by **glacial** melt, a phenomenon made worse by climate change.", "zh": "冰川融化引發的毀滅性洪水擾亂了 10 萬多人的生活，而氣候變遷又使這一現象變得更加嚴重，Dhital 和她的家人就是其中之一。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "At least 1,500 have died, and more than 5,000 are still missing.", "zh": "至少1,500人死亡，5,000多人仍然失蹤。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Thousands are still living in temporary shelters or tents.", "zh": "數千人仍住在臨時避難所或帳篷裡。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "據聯合國稱，洪水損壞或摧毀了 7 個衛生設施、23 所學校、10,0…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "The flood damaged or destroyed seven health facilities, 23 schools, 10,000 toilets and 64 water systems, according to the United Nations.", "zh": "據聯合國稱，洪水損壞或摧毀了 7 個衛生設施、23 所學校、10,000 個廁所和 64 個供水系統。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And there are early signs that **malnutrition** is spiking as winter approaches.", "zh": "早期跡象表明，隨著冬季臨近，**營養不良**現象正在加劇。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "聯合國兒童基金會衛生主管希亞姆·帕塔克 (Shyam Pathak)…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"The magnitude of **devastation** is **unimaginable**,\" says Shyam Pathak, a chief of health at UNICEF.", "zh": "聯合國兒童基金會衛生主管希亞姆·帕塔克 (Shyam Pathak) 表示：“**破壞**的嚴重程度是難以想像的。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The din of helicopters circling the **wreckage** looking for survivors has faded, he says.", "zh": "他說，直升機在**殘骸**上盤旋尋找倖存者的喧鬧聲已經減弱。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "International attention and aid has fallen too, sources on the ground say, as the response turns to the **arduous**, but intimate work of helping these communities stitch their lives back together.", "zh": "當地消息人士稱，國際關注和援助也有所下降，因為應對措施轉向幫助這些社區重新恢復生活的**艱鉅**但密切的工作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "帕塔克說，這場災難有些獨特，因為許多從事這項工作的人同時也努力重建自…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "This disaster is somewhat unique, Pathak says, in that many of those doing the work are trying to rebuild their own lives at the same time. Dhital is one of them.", "zh": "帕塔克說，這場災難有些獨特，因為許多從事這項工作的人同時也努力重建自己的生活。迪塔爾就是其中之一。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "洪水過後，迪塔爾和她的家人立即搬進了一個收容中心，這是收容流離失所者…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "In the immediate aftermath of the flood, Dhital and her family moved into a holding center, one of a couple dozen that housed the displaced.", "zh": "洪水過後，迪塔爾和她的家人立即搬進了一個收容中心，這是收容流離失所者的數十個收容中心之一。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They stayed there for about a month before moving into a relative's house.", "zh": "他們在那裡住了大約一個月，然後搬進了親戚家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Those days were not easy.", "zh": "那些日子過得併不輕鬆。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "「近一個月來，我感覺自己快要失去理智了，」她說。 “除了錢之外，我更…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "\"For almost a month, I felt like I was losing my mind,\" she says.", "zh": "「近一個月來，我感覺自己快要失去理智了，」她說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"More than money, I am in great need of work.\"", "zh": "“除了錢之外，我更需要工作。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "她透過 Helen Keller Intl（幫助應對疫情的非營利組織…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "She found that work through Helen Keller Intl, a nonprofit that's helping the response.", "zh": "她透過 Helen Keller Intl（幫助應對疫情的非營利組織）找到了這項工作。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "After a short training program that included mental health support, she began helping her community rebuild. There's a lot to do.", "zh": "在接受了包括心理健康支持在內的短期培訓計劃後，她開始幫助社區重建。有很多事情要做。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "「我走進社區，與產後母親、孕婦和五歲以下兒童一起工作，」迪塔爾說。 …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "\"I go out into the community, we work with **postpartum** mothers, pregnant women and children under five,\" says Dhital.", "zh": "「我走進社區，與**產後**母親、孕婦和五歲以下兒童一起工作，」迪塔爾說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"This is the only thing keeping me going right now.\"", "zh": "“這是現在唯一讓我繼續前進的事情。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "她的工作之一是篩檢倖存者的營養不良。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "One of her jobs is screening for **malnutrition** among survivors.", "zh": "她的工作之一是篩檢倖存者的**營養不良**。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "初步數據顯示顯著增加。例如，在 Naukunda Gaunpalik…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Preliminary data suggest a notable increase.", "zh": "初步數據顯示顯著增加。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In Naukunda Gaunpalika, for instance, moderate acute **malnutrition** — a condition that can slow growth, weaken the immune system and become life threatening without treatment — appears to have gone up from 0.8% in June of this year to 8.7% in October, says Pooja Pandey Rana, who directs Hellen Keller's work in Nepal.", "zh": "例如，在 Naukunda Gaunpalika，中度急性**營養不良**（一種會減緩生長、削弱免疫系統並在不治療的情況下危及生命的疾病）似乎已從今年 6 月的 0.8% 上升到 10 月的 8.7%，海倫·凱勒 (Hellen Keller) 尼泊爾工作的負責人普賈·潘迪·拉納 (Poojaandey) 說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "These are likely conservative estimates too, she says.", "zh": "她說，這些可能也是保守的估計。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "潘迪·拉納（Pandey Rana）說：「這是一次巨大的跳躍，」這可…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "\"It's a big jump,\" says Pandey Rana, and likely driven by fallout from the flood.", "zh": "潘迪·拉納（Pandey Rana）說：「這是一次巨大的跳躍，」這可能是由洪水的影響所致。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "除了失去家園之外，許多家庭還失去了他們賴以獲取營養食物的花園或當地農…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "In addition to losing homes, many families lost the gardens or local farms they relied on for **nutritious** food.", "zh": "除了失去家園之外，許多家庭還失去了他們賴以獲取營養食物的花園或當地農場。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"As a result, they have to depend on dried and packaged foods, such as instant noodles and biscuits,\" says Dhital.", "zh": "「因此，他們不得不依賴乾燥和包裝食品，例如泡麵和餅乾，」迪塔爾說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Poor sanitation and lack of clean drinking water is an issue too, she says.", "zh": "她說，衛生條件差和缺乏清潔飲用水也是一個問題。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And many have lost their **livelihoods**, so they don't have money to pay for food.", "zh": "許多人失去了**生計**，因此沒有錢購買食物。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "「我以為我活不下去了，」賈努卡·迪塔爾 (Januka Dhital) 說。　就在那個可怕的想法出現前幾分鐘，迪塔爾正忙著準備零食。她在尼泊爾烏塔加亞的家中經營餐飲服務，並為當天晚些時候的活動做準備。她的工作被一名騎摩托車的男子打斷，他警告洪水。她走到外面去看。　「當我轉身時，我看到黑暗、灰塵和看起來整個山坡都塌下來了，」她說。　她抓住年幼的兒子，跳上那個男人的摩托車後座。他們跑向地勢較高的地方，最後到達安全地帶。但她不知道她的丈夫和女兒是否安全，因為洪水來臨時他們正在上班和上學。　經過幾個小時的等待和尋找，他們終於團聚了。她說，她的丈夫赤身裸體，渾身是血，受了重傷，但還活著。　「我們一家人竟然倖存下來，這真是令人難以置信，」迪塔爾說。但從山上沖下來的水和泥牆摧毀了他們的家園，以及成千上萬的其他家園。 “我們失去了一切。我們現在什麼都沒有了。”　冰川融化引發的毀滅性洪水擾亂了 10 萬多人的生活，而氣候變遷又使這一現象變得更加嚴重，Dhital 和她的家人就是其中之一。至少1,500人死亡，5,000多人仍然失蹤。數千人仍住在臨時避難所或帳篷裡。　據聯合國稱，洪水損壞或摧毀了 7 個衛生設施、23 所學校、10,000 個廁所和 64 個供水系統。早期跡象表明，隨著冬季臨近，營養不良現象正在加劇。　聯合國兒童基金會衛生主管希亞姆·帕塔克 (Shyam Pathak) 表示：「破壞的嚴重程度是難以想像的。」他說，直升機在殘骸上盤旋尋找倖存者的喧鬧聲已經減弱。當地消息人士稱，國際關注和援助也有所下降，因為應對措施轉向幫助這些社區重新恢復生活的艱鉅但密切的工作。　帕塔克說，這場災難有些獨特，因為許多從事這項工作的人同時也努力重建自己的生活。迪塔爾就是其中之一。　洪水過後，迪塔爾和她的家人立即搬進了一個收容中心，這是收容流離失所者的數十個收容中心之一。他們在那裡住了大約一個月，然後搬進了親戚家。那些日子過得併不輕鬆。　「近一個月來，我感覺自己快要失去理智了，」她說。 “除了錢之外，我更需要工作。”　她透過 Helen Keller Intl（幫助應對疫情的非營利組織）找到了這項工作。在接受了包括心理健康支持在內的短期培訓計劃後，她開始幫助社區重建。有很多事情要做。　「我走進社區，與產後母親、孕婦和五歲以下兒童一起工作，」迪塔爾說。 “這是現在唯一讓我繼續前進的事情。”　她的工作之一是篩檢倖存者的營養不良。　初步數據顯示顯著增加。例如，在 Naukunda Gaunpalika，中度急性營養不良（一種會減緩生長、削弱免疫系統並在不治療的情況下危及生命的疾病）似乎已從今年 6 月的 0.8% 上升到 10 月的 8.7%，海倫·凱勒 (Hellen Keller) 尼泊爾工作的負責人普賈·潘迪·拉納 (Poojaandey) 說。她說，這些可能也是保守的估計。　潘迪·拉納（Pandey Rana）說：「這是一次巨大的跳躍，」這可能是由洪水的影響所致。　除了失去家園之外，許多家庭還失去了他們賴以獲取營養食物的花園或當地農場。 「因此，他們不得不依賴乾燥和包裝食品，例如泡麵和餅乾，」迪塔爾說。她說，衛生條件差和缺乏清潔飲用水也是一個問題。許多人失去了生計，因此沒有錢購買食物。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "postpartum", "sf": "postpartum", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "產後", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　產后　|　英英定義　The period immediately following childbirth.　|　本文例句　\"I go out into the community, we work with postpartum mothers, pregnant women and children under five,\" says Dhital.　|　例句中譯　「我走進社區，與產後母親、孕婦和五歲以下兒童一起工作，」迪塔爾說。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "obliterated", "sf": "obliterated", "pos": "v.", "zh": "被抹殺的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　廢止、殲、泯、抹殺　|　英英定義　To remove completely, leaving no trace; to wipe out; to destroy.　|　本文例句　But the wall of water and mud that descended from the mountains had obliterated their home, along with thousands of others.　|　例句中譯　但從山上沖下來的水和泥牆摧毀了他們的家園，以及成千上萬的其他家園。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "unimaginable", "sf": "unimaginable", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "難以想的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　不可思議　|　英英定義　Unable to be imagined; inconceivable or mind-boggling; beyond belief　|　本文例句　\"The magnitude of devastation is unimaginable,\" says Shyam Pathak, a chief of health at UNICEF.　|　例句中譯　聯合國兒童基金會衛生主管希亞姆·帕塔克 (Shyam Pathak) 表示：“破壞的嚴重程度是難以想像的。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "arduous", "sf": "arduous", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "艱鉅", "syn": "burdensome, demanding, exhausting", "tip": "其他意思　吃重、費力的、嶡、艱巨　|　英英定義　Needing or using up much energy; testing powers of endurance.　|　本文例句　International attention and aid has fallen too, sources on the ground say, as the response turns to the arduous, but intimate work of helping these communities stitch their lives back together.　|　例句中譯　當地消息人士稱，國際關注和援助也有所下降，因為應對措施轉向幫助這些社區重新恢復生活的艱鉅但密切的工作。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "nutritious", "sf": "nutritious", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "有營養的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　(of food or drink) Providing nutrients; healthy to eat.　|　本文例句　In addition to losing homes, many families lost the gardens or local farms they relied on for nutritious food.　|　例句中譯　除了失去家園之外，許多家庭還失去了他們賴以獲取營養食物的花園或當地農場。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "malnutrition", "sf": "malnutrition", "pos": "n.", "zh": "營養不良", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A lack of adequate nourishment.　|　本文例句　And there are early signs that malnutrition is spiking as winter approaches.　|　例句中譯　早期跡象表明，隨著冬季臨近，營養不良現象正在加劇。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "wreckage", "sf": "wreckage", "pos": "n.", "zh": "殘骸", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　廢墟　|　英英定義　Something wrecked, especially the remains or debris of something which has been severely damaged or destroyed.　|　本文例句　The din of helicopters circling the wreckage looking for survivors has faded, he says.　|　例句中譯　他說，直升機在殘骸上盤旋尋找倖存者的喧鬧聲已經減弱。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "hopped", "sf": "hopped", "pos": "v.", "zh": "跳躍的", "syn": "jump, leap", "tip": "其他意思　蹦、跳、踴躍　|　英英定義　To jump a short distance.　|　本文例句　She grabbed her young son and hopped onto the back of the man's scooter.　|　例句中譯　她抓住年幼的兒子，跳上那個男人的摩托車後座。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "devastation", "sf": "devastation", "pos": "n.", "zh": "破壞", "syn": "devastavit", "tip": "其他意思　毀壞　|　英英定義　The act of devastating, or the state of being devastated; a laying waste.　|　本文例句　Dhital and her family are among the 100,000-some people whose lives have been upended by the devastating floods sparked by glacial melt, a phenomenon made worse by climate change.　|　例句中譯　冰川融化引發的毀滅性洪水擾亂了 10 萬多人的生活，而氣候變遷又使這一現象變得更加嚴重，Dhital 和她的家人就是其中之一。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "hillside", "sf": "hillside", "pos": "n.", "zh": "山坡", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　阪、坡、阤　|　英英定義　The side of a hill.　|　本文例句　\"When I turned around, I saw darkness, dust and what looked like the entire hillside coming down,\" she says.　|　例句中譯　「當我轉身時，我看到黑暗、灰塵和看起來整個山坡都塌下來了，」她說。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "glacial", "sf": "glacial", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "冰川的", "syn": "ice age", "tip": "其他意思　冰川時代的、冰河　|　英英定義　A glacial period (colloquially known as an ice age).　|　本文例句　Dhital and her family are among the 100,000-some people whose lives have been upended by the devastating floods sparked by glacial melt, a phenomenon made worse by climate change.　|　例句中譯　冰川融化引發的毀滅性洪水擾亂了 10 萬多人的生活，而氣候變遷又使這一現象變得更加嚴重，Dhital 和她的家人就是其中之一。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "livelihood", "sf": "livelihoods", "pos": "n.", "zh": "生計", "syn": "living, subsistence, sustenance", "tip": "其他意思　飯碗、生、生活　|　英英定義　A means of providing the necessities of life for oneself (for example, a job or income).　|　本文例句　And many have lost their livelihoods, so they don't have money to pay for food.　|　例句中譯　許多人失去了生計，因此沒有錢購買食物。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6022034/flood-nepal-survival-climate-change"}, {"code": "20261119-3", "ch": "2026-11-19　週四", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "As overdose deaths fall, White House makes misleading claims about who deserves credit　／　隨著服藥過量死亡人數下降，白宮對誰值得讚揚做出了誤導性的說法", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Brian Mann，全文共 15 段、24 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：白宮在一份慶祝毒品死亡歷史性下降的聲明中指出，自川普總統上任以來取得了一些成功。事實上，最大的進展發生在拜登政府時期。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6044209/drug-deaths-overdose-drop-trump-biden-fentanyl"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "當白宮本週稍早宣布因致命藥物過量死亡的人數大幅改善時，官員指出，疾病…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "When the White House announced big improvements in the number of people dying from fatal drug overdoses earlier this week, officials pointed to hopeful new data from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention showing U.S. drug deaths have **plunged** to their lowest level in roughly a decade, saving nearly 50,000 lives each year.", "zh": "當白宮本週稍早宣布因致命藥物過量死亡的人數大幅改善時，官員指出，疾病管制與預防中心的新數據充滿希望，顯示美國藥物**死亡人數**已降至大約十年來的最低水平，每年挽救近 5 萬人的生命。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "白宮沒有透露的是，在拜登政府領導下，服藥過量死亡人數的下降開始得更早…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "What the White House failed to disclose is that declines in overdose **fatalities** began much earlier, under the Biden administration, with most of the gains occurring before Trump returned to office.", "zh": "白宮沒有透露的是，在拜登政府領導下，服藥過量**死亡人數**的下降開始得更早，其中大部分進展發生在川普重返辦公室之前。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "布魯金斯學會毒品政策專家萬達·費爾巴布-布朗 (Vanda Felb…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"Since the spring of 2023, we have seen a steady decline in overdose deaths,\" said Vanda Felbab-Brown, a drug policy expert at the Brookings Institution.", "zh": "布魯金斯學會毒品政策專家萬達·費爾巴布-布朗 (Vanda Felbab-Brown) 表示：“自 2023 年春季以來，我們看到服藥過量**死亡人數**穩步下降。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The fact that it has been sustained is very important.\"", "zh": "“它一直持續下去這一事實非常重要。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "根據 CDC 數據，毒品死亡人數從 2023 年開始下降，並至少連續…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "According to CDC data, reductions in drug deaths began in 2023 and have continued steadily for at least 39 consecutive months — not 18 months as the ONDCP statement said.", "zh": "根據 CDC 數據，毒品**死亡人數**從 2023 年開始下降，並至少連續 39 個月穩定持續——而不是 ONDCP 聲明中所說的 18 個月。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "By the time Biden left office, fatal overdoses had already dropped by roughly one-third, an improvement described by addiction experts at the time as unprecedented.", "zh": "到拜登卸任時，致命的吸毒過量事件已經減少了大約三分之一，當時的成癮專家稱這一改善是前所未有的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "達斯古普塔、費爾巴布-布朗和其他成癮專家讚揚拜登政府推出的政策應對措…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Dasgupta, Felbab-Brown and other and addiction experts credit the Biden administration for rolling out policy responses that included wider access to healthcare, making the **opioid** overdose medication **naloxone** more readily available, and negotiating a deal with China that disrupted the flow of industrial chemicals used to make **fentanyl**.", "zh": "達斯古普塔、費爾巴布-布朗和其他成癮專家讚揚拜登政府推出的政策應對措施，包括更廣泛地獲得醫療保健、使**阿片類藥物**過量藥物**納洛酮**更容易獲得，以及與中國談判達成一項協議，擾亂用於製造**芬太尼**的工業化學品的流動。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "拜登團隊還在打擊走私芬太尼的墨西哥販毒集團方面取得了重大禁毒勝利。費…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "The Biden team also scored significant drug **interdiction** wins against the Mexican cartels that **smuggle** **fentanyl**.", "zh": "拜登團隊還在打擊**走私****芬太尼**的墨西哥販毒集團方面取得了重大禁毒勝利。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"We have certainly been seeing over many years, going back to the Biden administration, important efforts to crack down against them,\" said Felbab-Brown.", "zh": "費爾巴布-布朗說：“多年來，我們確實看到了拜登政府為打擊他們所做的重要努力。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "達斯古普塔和費爾巴布-布朗都表示，在川普的領導下，降低藥物死亡率的進…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Dasgupta and Felbab-Brown both said improvements in reducing drug mortality have continued under Trump.", "zh": "達斯古普塔和費爾巴布-布朗都表示，在川普的領導下，降低藥物死亡率的進展仍在持續。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They said it's important to have an accurate timeline of the overdose crisis because researchers are still trying to understand why deaths involving **fentanyl** surged and why so many fewer people are now dying.", "zh": "他們表示，掌握藥物過量危機的準確時間表非常重要，因為研究人員仍在試圖了解為什麼涉及**芬太尼**的**死亡人數**激增以及為什麼現在死亡人數如此之少。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "NPR 向白宮詢問拜登領導下的芬太尼鬥爭的進展。前播客、記者和福克斯…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "NPR asked the White House about progress in the **fentanyl** fight under Biden.", "zh": "NPR 向白宮詢問拜登領導下的**芬太尼**鬥爭的進展。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In an emailed statement, ONDCP director Carter, a former podcaster, journalist and Fox News contributor, blamed Biden for failing to secure the U.S.-Mexico border and for allowing drug deaths to surge in the first place.", "zh": "前播客、記者和福克斯新聞撰稿人、ONDCP 主任卡特在一份電子郵件聲明中指責拜登未能確保美墨邊境安全，並讓毒品**死亡人數**激增。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "卡特說：“雖然藥物過量死亡人數在達到峰值後最終開始下降，但拜登政府並…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"While drug overdose deaths eventually began to decline following the peak, the Biden Administration doesn't get to take credit for overseeing the highest drug overdose numbers in history, then bringing them down from their own failure,\" Carter said.", "zh": "卡特說：“雖然藥物過量**死亡人數**在達到峰值後最終開始下降，但拜登政府並沒有因監管歷史上最高的藥物過量人數，然後將其從自己的失敗中拉下來而獲得讚譽。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "但布魯金斯學會的費爾巴布-布朗表示，她不同意川普政府對「瓦解和消除」…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "But Felbab-Brown at Brookings said she doesn't share the Trump administration's confidence that there has been significant progress \"**dismantling** and eliminating\" **narco-terrorist** organizations.", "zh": "但布魯金斯學會的費爾巴布-布朗表示，她不同意川普政府對「瓦解和消除」毒品恐怖組織已取得重大進展的信心。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "國家安全 美國軍事打擊會減緩吸毒過量死亡嗎？專家說不「我想不出有哪個…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "National Security Will U.S. military strikes slow drug overdose deaths?", "zh": "國家安全 美國軍事打擊會減緩吸毒過量死亡嗎？"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Experts say no \"I cannot think of one **narco-terrorist** organization that has been **dismantled**,\" she said.", "zh": "專家說不「我想不出有哪個毒品恐怖組織已經被搗毀，」她說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"They all continue operating and they are all very strong.", "zh": "「他們都在繼續運營，而且都非常強大。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They all continue **smuggling** drugs.\"", "zh": "他們都在繼續**走私**毒品。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "軍事專家也質疑川普對加勒比海和東太平洋民用船隻持續打擊的有效性和合法…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "Military experts have also questioned the effectiveness, and **legality**, of Trump's ongoing strikes against civilian boats in the Caribbean and eastern Pacific, described as **smuggling** vessels by the Pentagon.", "zh": "軍事專家也質疑川普對加勒比海和東太平洋民用船隻持續打擊的有效性和**合法性**，五角大廈稱這些船隻為**走私**船隻。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "北卡羅來納大學成癮問題研究員達斯古普塔表示，隨著川普政府對共和黨國會…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "Dasgupta, the addiction researcher at UNC, said he's also concerned about whether progress reducing drug deaths can be sustained next year as the Trump administration implements deep cuts to Medicaid passed by the Republican Congress.", "zh": "北卡羅來納大學成癮問題研究員達斯古普塔表示，隨著川普政府對共和黨國會透過的醫療補助計劃進行大幅削減，他也擔心明年減少藥物死亡的進展能否持續。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "國會預算辦公室估計，削減可能意味著多達 1000 萬美國人失去醫療保…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "The Congressional Budget Office has estimated the cuts could mean as many as 10 million Americans losing access to health insurance coverage.", "zh": "國會預算辦公室估計，削減可能意味著多達 1000 萬美國人失去醫療保險。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "「醫療補助是美國戒癮服務最大的資助者，」達斯古普塔說。 “削減醫療補…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "\"Medicaid is the largest **funder** of addiction services in the United States,\" Dasgupta said.", "zh": "「醫療補助是美國戒癮服務最大的**資助者**，」達斯古普塔說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Cutting Medicaid eligibility or making it harder to access forms of effective addiction treatment is guaranteed to leave people out in the cold.\"", "zh": "“削減醫療補助資格或使其更難獲得有效的成癮治療形式肯定會讓人們陷入困境。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "當白宮本週稍早宣布因致命藥物過量死亡的人數大幅改善時，官員指出，疾病管制與預防中心的新數據充滿希望，顯示美國藥物死亡人數已降至大約十年來的最低水平，每年挽救近 5 萬人的生命。　白宮沒有透露的是，在拜登政府領導下，服藥過量死亡人數的下降開始得更早，其中大部分進展發生在川普重返辦公室之前。　布魯金斯學會毒品政策專家萬達·費爾巴布-布朗 (Vanda Felbab-Brown) 表示：“自 2023 年春季以來，我們看到服藥過量死亡人數穩步下降。” “它一直持續下去這一事實非常重要。”　根據 CDC 數據，毒品死亡人數從 2023 年開始下降，並至少連續 39 個月穩定持續——而不是 ONDCP 聲明中所說的 18 個月。到拜登卸任時，致命的吸毒過量事件已經減少了大約三分之一，當時的成癮專家稱這一改善是前所未有的。　達斯古普塔、費爾巴布-布朗和其他成癮專家讚揚拜登政府推出的政策應對措施，包括更廣泛地獲得醫療保健、使阿片類藥物過量藥物納洛酮更容易獲得，以及與中國談判達成一項協議，擾亂用於製造芬太尼的工業化學品的流動。　拜登團隊還在打擊走私芬太尼的墨西哥販毒集團方面取得了重大禁毒勝利。費爾巴布-布朗說：“多年來，我們確實看到了拜登政府為打擊他們所做的重要努力。”　達斯古普塔和費爾巴布-布朗都表示，在川普的領導下，降低藥物死亡率的進展仍在持續。他們表示，掌握藥物過量危機的準確時間表非常重要，因為研究人員仍在試圖了解為什麼涉及芬太尼的死亡人數激增以及為什麼現在死亡人數如此之少。　NPR 向白宮詢問拜登領導下的芬太尼鬥爭的進展。前播客、記者和福克斯新聞撰稿人、ONDCP 主任卡特在一份電子郵件聲明中指責拜登未能確保美墨邊境安全，並讓毒品死亡人數激增。　卡特說：“雖然藥物過量死亡人數在達到峰值後最終開始下降，但拜登政府並沒有因監管歷史上最高的藥物過量人數，然後將其從自己的失敗中拉下來而獲得讚譽。”　但布魯金斯學會的費爾巴布-布朗表示，她不同意川普政府對「瓦解和消除」毒品恐怖組織已取得重大進展的信心。　國家安全 美國軍事打擊會減緩吸毒過量死亡嗎？專家說不「我想不出有哪個毒品恐怖組織已經被搗毀，」她說。 “他們都在繼續經營，而且都非常強大。他們都在繼續走私毒品。”　軍事專家也質疑川普對加勒比海和東太平洋民用船隻持續打擊的有效性和合法性，五角大廈稱這些船隻為走私船隻。　北卡羅來納大學成癮問題研究員達斯古普塔表示，隨著川普政府對共和黨國會透過的醫療補助計劃進行大幅削減，他也擔心明年減少藥物死亡的進展能否持續。　國會預算辦公室估計，削減可能意味著多達 1000 萬美國人失去醫療保險。　「醫療補助是美國戒癮服務最大的資助者，」達斯古普塔說。 “削減醫療補助資格或使其更難獲得有效的成癮治療形式肯定會讓人們陷入困境。”"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "naloxone", "sf": "naloxone", "pos": "n.", "zh": "納洛酮", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　An opioid inverse agonist used to counter the effects of an overdose on opioids (such as heroin or morphine).", "trap": ""}, {"w": "funder", "sf": "funder", "pos": "n.", "zh": "資助者", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　One who funds.　|　本文例句　\"Medicaid is the largest funder of addiction services in the United States,\" Dasgupta said.　|　例句中譯　「醫療補助是美國戒癮服務最大的資助者，」達斯古普塔說。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "narco-terrorist", "sf": "narco-terrorist", "pos": "", "zh": "毒品恐怖分子", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　But Felbab-Brown at Brookings said she doesn't share the Trump administration's confidence that there has been significant progress \"dismantling and eliminating\" narco-terrorist organizations.　|　例句中譯　但布魯金斯學會的費爾巴布-布朗表示，她不同意川普政府對「瓦解和消除」毒品恐怖組織已取得重大進展的信心。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "interdiction", "sf": "interdiction", "pos": "n.", "zh": "攔截", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　禁忌、禁令　|　英英定義　The act of interdicting or something interdicted　|　本文例句　The Biden team also scored significant drug interdiction wins against the Mexican cartels that smuggle fentanyl.　|　例句中譯　拜登團隊還在打擊走私芬太尼的墨西哥販毒集團方面取得了重大禁毒勝利。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "fentanyl", "sf": "fentanyl", "pos": "n.", "zh": "芬太尼", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A particularly powerful opioid narcotic painkiller, N-phenyl-N-[1-(2-phenylethyl)piperidin-4-yl]propanamide.　|　本文例句　The Biden team also scored significant drug interdiction wins against the Mexican cartels that smuggle fentanyl.　|　例句中譯　拜登團隊還在打擊走私芬太尼的墨西哥販毒集團方面取得了重大禁毒勝利。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "smuggle", "sf": "smuggle", "pos": "v.", "zh": "走私", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　To import or export, illicitly or by stealth, without paying lawful customs charges or duties　|　本文例句　The Biden team also scored significant drug interdiction wins against the Mexican cartels that smuggle fentanyl.　|　例句中譯　拜登團隊還在打擊走私芬太尼的墨西哥販毒集團方面取得了重大禁毒勝利。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "dismantling", "sf": "dismantling", "pos": "v.", "zh": "拆解", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　拆、拆除、拆除 ... 的設備、拆掉　|　英英定義　To divest, strip of dress or covering.　|　本文例句　But Felbab-Brown at Brookings said she doesn't share the Trump administration's confidence that there has been significant progress \"dismantling and eliminating\" narco-terrorist organizations.　|　例句中譯　但布魯金斯學會的費爾巴布-布朗表示，她不同意川普政府對「瓦解和消除」毒品恐怖組織已取得重大進展的信心。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "dismantled", "sf": "dismantled", "pos": "v.", "zh": "拆除的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　拆、拆除、拆除 ... 的設備、拆掉　|　英英定義　To divest, strip of dress or covering.　|　本文例句　But Felbab-Brown at Brookings said she doesn't share the Trump administration's confidence that there has been significant progress \"dismantling and eliminating\" narco-terrorist organizations.　|　例句中譯　但布魯金斯學會的費爾巴布-布朗表示，她不同意川普政府對「瓦解和消除」毒品恐怖組織已取得重大進展的信心。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "opioid", "sf": "opioid", "pos": "n.", "zh": "阿片類藥物", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A substance that has effects similar to opium.", "trap": ""}, {"w": "legality", "sf": "legality", "pos": "n.", "zh": "合法性", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　法律義務、合法、墨守陳規　|　英英定義　Lawfulness.　|　本文例句　Military experts have also questioned the effectiveness, and legality, of Trump's ongoing strikes against civilian boats in the Caribbean and eastern Pacific, described as smuggling vessels by the Pentagon.　|　例句中譯　軍事專家也質疑川普對加勒比海和東太平洋民用船隻持續打擊的有效性和合法性，五角大廈稱這些船隻為走私船隻。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "fatalities", "sf": "fatalities", "pos": "n.", "zh": "死亡人數", "syn": "inevitability, mortality", "tip": "英英定義　The state proceeding from destiny; invincible necessity, superior to, and independent of, free and rational control.　|　本文例句　What the White House failed to disclose is that declines in overdose fatalities began much earlier, under the Biden administration, with most of the gains occurring before Trump returned to office.　|　例句中譯　白宮沒有透露的是，在拜登政府領導下，服藥過量死亡人數的下降開始得更早，其中大部分進展發生在川普重返辦公室之前。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "plunge", "sf": "plunged", "pos": "n.", "zh": "暴跌", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　跳進、跳水、紮　|　英英定義　The act of plunging or submerging　|　本文例句　drug deaths have plunged to their lowest level in roughly a decade, saving nearly 50,000 lives each year.　|　例句中譯　毒品死亡人數已降至約十年來的最低水平，每年挽救近 5 萬人的生命。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6044209/drug-deaths-overdose-drop-trump-biden-fentanyl"}, {"code": "20261118-1", "ch": "2026-11-18　週三", "sec": "Middle East conflict", "title": "Iran launches a third round of strikes on Bahrain, host of U.S. Navy's 5th Fleet　／　伊朗對美國海軍第五艦隊所在地巴林發動第三輪攻擊", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、The Associated Press，全文共 18 段、24 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：伊朗週二向巴林的一處美國雷達設施發射了無人機，美國則向一條重要航線沿線的伊朗目標開火進行報復。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/nx-s1-6044255/us-iran-war-latest-bahrain"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "CAIRO — Iran fired drones on Tuesday at a U.S. radar installation in Bahrain in the third Iranian attack in recent days on American military targets in the Persian Gulf island kingdom, and the U.S. retaliated by firing at Iranian targets along an important shipping route.", "zh": "開羅——週二，伊朗向巴林的美國雷達設施發射了無人機，這是伊朗最近幾天對波斯灣島國美國軍事目標的第三次襲擊，美國則向一條重要航線沿線的伊朗目標開火進行報復。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The attacks and counterattacks interrupted a roughly two-month lull in fighting, as Iran's targeting of Bahrain brought condemnations from the region.", "zh": "這些襲擊和反擊打斷了大約兩個月的停戰狀態，伊朗針對巴林的襲擊引起了該地區的譴責。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Analysts said stalled peace negotiations and Tehran's growing economic pressures were raising the risk of a substantial escalation.", "zh": "分析師表示，和平談判陷入僵局以及德黑蘭日益增長的經濟壓力正在增加局勢大幅升級的風險。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Iran has been suffering under a naval blockade that the U.S. has enforced on it for months in and around the Strait of Hormuz, a crucial waterway for the world's energy supplies where Iran and its proxies have disrupted shipping since the war began Feb. 28.", "zh": "幾個月來，伊朗一直受到美國在霍爾木茲海峽及其周邊實施的海上封鎖的影響。霍爾木茲海峽是世界能源供應的重要水道，自2月28日戰爭爆發以來，伊朗及其代理人一直在擾亂霍爾木茲海峽的航運。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "U.S. President Donald Trump has been circumspect on his next steps for the Iran war, now in its eighth month despite an initial promise it would last only a matter of weeks.", "zh": "美國總統川普對伊朗戰爭的下一步一直持謹慎態度，儘管最初承諾伊朗戰爭只會持續幾週，但現在已經進入第八個月。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He has said new strikes are highly unlikely, but he has also sent a third aircraft carrier and thousands more troops to the Middle East — and told Vice President JD Vance that talks aren't needed at this time.", "zh": "他表示，新的攻擊不太可能發生，但他也向中東派遣了第三艘航空母艦和數千名士兵，並告訴副總統 JD 萬斯，目前不需要談判。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The presence provides greater offensive firepower and missile interception capacity, according to a new analysis by Israel's Institute for National Security Studies.", "zh": "根據以色列國家安全研究所的最新分析，這種存在提供了更強的進攻火力和飛彈攔截能力。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "The Roosevelt joins the USS George H.W. Bush and the USS George Washington aircraft carriers, as well as smaller U.S. Navy ships, which are in the region to maintain the blockade of Iranian shipping.", "zh": "羅斯福號加入喬治·H·W·布希號航空母艦布希和喬治華盛頓號航空母艦以及較小的美國海軍艦艇都在該地區維持對伊朗航運的封鎖。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "U.S. Central Command wouldn't comment on whether it plans to keep all three carrier strike groups in the region.", "zh": "美國中央司令部沒有就是否計劃將所有三個航母打擊群留在該地區發表評論。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "伊朗週二對巴林發動攻擊，此前伊朗週五襲擊了美國在該國的預警雷達設施，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Iran's attack on Bahrain on Tuesday came after it targeted a U.S. early warning radar facility in the country on Friday, and on Sunday fired at a radar system at an American helicopter base there.", "zh": "伊朗週二對巴林發動攻擊，此前伊朗週五襲擊了美國在該國的預警雷達設施，週日又向美國直升機基地的雷達系統開火。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Despite claims of success, there appeared to be little or no damage done.", "zh": "儘管聲稱成功，但似乎沒有造成任何損害。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "這些攻擊是在美國襲擊伊朗通訊塔和正在進行的無人機監視行動之後發生的，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "The attacks followed U.S. strikes on Iranian communications towers and ongoing drone surveillance operations, and Iran said it was retaliating.", "zh": "這些攻擊是在美國襲擊伊朗通訊塔和正在進行的無人機監視行動之後發生的，伊朗表示正在進行報復。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "伊朗革命衛隊在聲明中表示，“持續侵犯該國領空，以及利用地區軍事基地和…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"Continued aggression against the country's airspace, as well as the use of regional military bases and facilities for hostile acts against Iran, will not go unanswered,\" Iran's Revolutionary Guard Corps said in a statement.", "zh": "伊朗革命衛隊在聲明中表示，“持續侵犯該國領空，以及利用地區軍事基地和設施對伊朗進行敵對行動，將不會得不到回應。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "埃及、卡達、沙烏地阿拉伯和阿聯酋均譴責伊朗對巴林的攻擊，稱其侵犯了巴…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "Egypt, Qatar, Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates each condemned Iran's attack on Bahrain, calling it a violation of Bahrain's sovereignty and a threat to its security and stability.", "zh": "埃及、卡達、沙烏地阿拉伯和阿聯酋均譴責伊朗對巴林的攻擊，稱其侵犯了巴林的主權並對其安全與穩定構成威脅。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "儘管卡達加強了調解努力，但結束戰爭的談判仍陷入停滯。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Negotiations to end the war have stagnated, despite intensified mediation efforts from Qatar.", "zh": "儘管卡達加強了調解努力，但結束戰爭的談判仍陷入停滯。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "卡達在一份聲明中表示，伊朗對巴林的“持續襲擊”“破壞了外交努力”，外…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "In a statement, Qatar said Iran's \"continued attacks\" on Bahrain \"undermine diplomatic efforts\" and Foreign Ministry spokesman Majed Al Ansari, speaking at a news briefing in Doha, warned that any escalation in fighting posed an \"extremely grave danger\" to the prospects of reaching an agreement.", "zh": "卡達在一份聲明中表示，伊朗對巴林的“持續襲擊”“破壞了外交努力”，外交部發言人馬吉德·安薩裡在多哈舉行的新聞發布會上警告說，任何戰鬥升級都會對達成協議的前景構成“極其嚴重的危險”。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "國際戰略研究所駐巴林國防分析師薩沙·布魯赫曼表示，這些攻擊顯示德黑蘭…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "The attacks are a sign that Tehran is growing impatient as its economic woes mount, said Sascha Bruchmann, a Bahrain-based defense analyst with the International Institute for Strategic Studies.", "zh": "國際戰略研究所駐巴林國防分析師薩沙·布魯赫曼表示，這些攻擊顯示德黑蘭隨著經濟困境的加劇而變得越來越不耐煩。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "布魯赫曼告訴美聯社：“向船隻開槍會引起恐懼，但不足以改變戰略平衡。”…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "\"Shooting at ships causes fear, but is not effective enough to change the strategic equation,\" Bruchmann told the AP.", "zh": "布魯赫曼告訴美聯社：“向船隻開槍會引起恐懼，但不足以改變戰略平衡。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Tehran knows it needs to do something, but I wouldn't overestimate what we saw against Bahrain this week. This is not it — yet.\"", "zh": "“德黑蘭知道它需要做點什麼，但我不會高估本週對陣巴林的比賽。現在還不是這樣。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "伊朗官員稱目前的局勢為“沒有戰爭，就沒有和平”，並誓言要結束它。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "Iranian officials have termed the current situation \"no war, no peace\" and vowed to end it.", "zh": "伊朗官員稱目前的局勢為“沒有戰爭，就沒有和平”，並誓言要結束它。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "德黑蘭表示，它對透過談判達成協議持開放態度，但也表示，面對日益收緊的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Tehran has said that it's open to a negotiated deal, but also signaled a readiness to escalate the conflict in the face of tightening sanctions and the blockade that are throttling Iran's economy.", "zh": "德黑蘭表示，它對透過談判達成協議持開放態度，但也表示，面對日益收緊的製裁和封鎖限制了伊朗經濟，它準備升級衝突。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "伊朗頗具影響力的議會主席顧問馬赫迪·穆罕默迪週一在社群媒體上發文稱，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "Mahdi Mohammadi, an adviser to Iran's influential parliamentary chief, posted on social media on Monday that leaders view U.S. economic pressure as an effort to create a domestic \"security crisis.\"", "zh": "伊朗頗具影響力的議會主席顧問馬赫迪·穆罕默迪週一在社群媒體上發文稱，領導人認為美國的經濟壓力是為了製造國內「安全危機」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "伊朗繼續襲擊試圖透過霍爾木茲海峽的船隻，霍爾木茲海峽從波斯灣通往公海…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "Iran has continued to attack ships seeking to transit the Strait of Hormuz, which leads from the Persian Gulf toward the open seas.", "zh": "伊朗繼續襲擊試圖透過霍爾木茲海峽的船隻，霍爾木茲海峽從波斯灣通往公海。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In Yemen, Iran-backed Houthi rebels now have solidified their control of the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, another critical shipping route.", "zh": "在也門，伊朗支持的胡塞叛軍現已鞏固了對另一條重要航運路線曼德海峽的控制。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "伊朗週二對巴林發動攻擊，此前伊朗週五襲擊了美國在該國的預警雷達設施，週日又向美國直升機基地的雷達系統開火。儘管聲稱成功，但似乎沒有造成任何損害。　這些攻擊是在美國襲擊伊朗通訊塔和正在進行的無人機監視行動之後發生的，伊朗表示正在進行報復。　伊朗革命衛隊在聲明中表示，“持續侵犯該國領空，以及利用地區軍事基地和設施對伊朗進行敵對行動，將不會得不到回應。”　埃及、卡達、沙烏地阿拉伯和阿聯酋均譴責伊朗對巴林的攻擊，稱其侵犯了巴林的主權並對其安全與穩定構成威脅。　儘管卡達加強了調解努力，但結束戰爭的談判仍陷入停滯。　卡達在一份聲明中表示，伊朗對巴林的“持續襲擊”“破壞了外交努力”，外交部發言人馬吉德·安薩裡在多哈舉行的新聞發布會上警告說，任何戰鬥升級都會對達成協議的前景構成“極其嚴重的危險”。　國際戰略研究所駐巴林國防分析師薩沙·布魯赫曼表示，這些攻擊顯示德黑蘭隨著經濟困境的加劇而變得越來越不耐煩。　布魯赫曼告訴美聯社：“向船隻開槍會引起恐懼，但不足以改變戰略平衡。” “德黑蘭知道它需要做點什麼，但我不會高估本週對陣巴林的比賽。現在還不是這樣。”　伊朗官員稱目前的局勢為“沒有戰爭，就沒有和平”，並誓言要結束它。　德黑蘭表示，它對透過談判達成協議持開放態度，但也表示，面對日益收緊的製裁和封鎖限制了伊朗經濟，它準備升級衝突。　伊朗頗具影響力的議會主席顧問馬赫迪·穆罕默迪週一在社群媒體上發文稱，領導人認為美國的經濟壓力是為了製造國內「安全危機」。　伊朗繼續襲擊試圖透過霍爾木茲海峽的船隻，霍爾木茲海峽從波斯灣通往公海。在也門，伊朗支持的胡塞叛軍現已鞏固了對另一條重要航運路線曼德海峽的控制。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/nx-s1-6044255/us-iran-war-latest-bahrain"}, {"code": "20261118-2", "ch": "2026-11-18　週三", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Nvidia board says it does not intend to reinstate Jensen Huang as CEO　／　英偉達董事會表示不打算恢復黃仁勳擔任首席執行官", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Shannon Bond、,&nbsp;，全文共 8 段、15 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：這位前英偉達執行長表示，如果董事會允許，他將「很榮幸」回歸。但董事會表示無意恢復他的職位。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/nx-s1-6044213/jensen-huang-nvidia-congress"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "英偉達表示，不打算恢復黃仁勳的職位，因為這位前執行長的盟友敦促他重新…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Nvidia said it does not intend to reinstate Jensen Huang, amid a push by the former CEO's allies to return him to lead the chipmaker he cofounded.", "zh": "英偉達表示，不打算恢復黃仁勳的職位，因為這位前執行長的盟友敦促他重新領導他共同創立的晶片製造商。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "董事會主席 Harvey Jones 在周二下午的公司財報電話會議上…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Huang \"voluntarily resigned\" on Nov. 12 after disclosing \"personal behavior inconsistent with the company's code of conduct, standards and cultural norms,\" board chair Harvey Jones said on the company's earnings call on Tuesday afternoon.", "zh": "董事會主席 Harvey Jones 在周二下午的公司財報電話會議上表示，黃在披露「個人行為不符合公司行為準則、標準和文化規範」後，於 11 月 12 日「主動辭職」。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The Nvidia board unanimously accepted his resignation and does not intend to reinstate Jensen as CEO.\"", "zh": "“英偉達董事會一致接受他的辭職，並且不打算恢復詹森擔任首席執行官。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "週二早些時候，黃仁勳曾表示，如果英偉達董事會允許，他將重返領導他共同…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Earlier on Tuesday, Huang had said he would return to lead the company he cofounded if Nvidia's board allowed him to.", "zh": "週二早些時候，黃仁勳曾表示，如果英偉達董事會允許，他將重返領導他共同創立的公司。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Huang also agreed to appear before Congress to answer questions about the national security scandals swirling around the company.", "zh": "黃也同意出席國會，回答有關該公司的國家安全醜聞的問題。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "黃仁勳在社交媒體上發布的聲明中寫道：“我沒有達到 NVIDIA 每個…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "\"I did not live up to the standards expected of everyone at NVIDIA, and I have made serious mistakes in my personal life.", "zh": "「我沒有達到 NVIDIA 每個人的期望標準，而且我在個人生活中犯了嚴重錯誤。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I created problems for the Board that I deeply regret,\" Huang wrote in a statement posted on social media.", "zh": "我為董事會帶來了問題，對此我深感遺憾。 」黃在社群媒體上發布的聲明中寫道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"I own my mistakes completely, and I am committed to cooperating with the Board's independent investigation.\"", "zh": "“我完全承認自己的錯誤，並且我致力於配合董事會的獨立調查。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "黃仁勳和英偉達總法律顧問蒂姆·泰特將於 12 月 1 日至 2 日在…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Huang and Nvidia's general counsel Tim Teter will answer questions behind closed doors from the House Foreign Affairs and Intelligence Committees and the House Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party on Dec. 1st and 2nd.", "zh": "黃仁勳和英偉達總法律顧問蒂姆·泰特將於 12 月 1 日至 2 日在眾議院外交事務和情報委員會以及眾議院中國共產黨特別委員會閉門回答問題。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "立法者表示，他們希望了解英偉達在涉嫌晶片走私以及逃避旨在阻止中國獲得…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Lawmakers say they want answers about Nvidia's role in alleged chip smuggling and efforts to evade export controls meant to block China from accessing the most advanced U.S. AI chips.", "zh": "立法者表示，他們希望了解英偉達在涉嫌晶片走私以及逃避旨在阻止中國獲得最先進的美國人工智慧晶片的出口管制方面所扮演的角色的答案。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They will also ask Huang about his involvement with Alice Huang, who was an executive with Megaspeed, a Singapore-based company that was a major customer for Nvidia's chips.", "zh": "他們還將詢問黃與 Alice Huang 的關係，後者是新加坡公司 Megaspeed 的高階主管，該公司是 Nvidia 晶片的主要客戶。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In a statement emailed to NPR, Megaspeed said it \"conducts legitimate and lawful business,\" and that Alice Huang left the company in 2025, but that it is conducting an internal investigation.", "zh": "在透過電子郵件發送給 NPR 的聲明中，Megaspeed 表示其“開展合法且合法的業務”，Alice Huang 於 2025 年離開該公司，但正在進行內部調查。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "英偉達董事會週二表示，已成立一個委員會來監督該公司的國家安全政策、美…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Nvidia's board said on Tuesday it had formed a committee to oversee the company's national security policies, compliance with U.S. export controls, and risk management of global trade.", "zh": "英偉達董事會週二表示，已成立一個委員會來監督該公司的國家安全政策、美國出口管制的遵守情況以及全球貿易的風險管理。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "週二盤後交易中，英偉達股價上漲 5%。自黃本月稍早承認有婚外情以來，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Nvidia shares were up 5% in after-hours trading on Tuesday.", "zh": "週二盤後交易中，英偉達股價上漲 5%。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The company's stock price has dropped more than 16% since Huang admitting having an extramarital affair earlier this month.", "zh": "自黃本月稍早承認有婚外情以來，該公司股價已下跌逾16%。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "英偉達表示，不打算恢復黃仁勳的職位，因為這位前執行長的盟友敦促他重新領導他共同創立的晶片製造商。　董事會主席 Harvey Jones 在周二下午的公司財報電話會議上表示，黃在披露「個人行為不符合公司行為準則、標準和文化規範」後，於 11 月 12 日「主動辭職」。 “英偉達董事會一致接受他的辭職，並且不打算恢復詹森擔任首席執行官。”　週二早些時候，黃仁勳曾表示，如果英偉達董事會允許，他將重返領導他共同創立的公司。黃也同意出席國會，回答有關該公司的國家安全醜聞的問題。　黃仁勳在社交媒體上發布的聲明中寫道：“我沒有達到 NVIDIA 每個人的期望標準，而且我在個人生活中犯了嚴重錯誤。我給董事會帶來了問題，對此我深感遺憾。” “我完全承認自己的錯誤，並且我致力於配合董事會的獨立調查。”　黃仁勳和英偉達總法律顧問蒂姆·泰特將於 12 月 1 日至 2 日在眾議院外交事務和情報委員會以及眾議院中國共產黨特別委員會閉門回答問題。　立法者表示，他們希望了解英偉達在涉嫌晶片走私以及逃避旨在阻止中國獲得最先進的美國人工智慧晶片的出口管制方面所扮演的角色的答案。他們還將詢問黃與 Alice Huang 的關係，後者是新加坡公司 Megaspeed 的高階主管，該公司是 Nvidia 晶片的主要客戶。在透過電子郵件發送給 NPR 的聲明中，Megaspeed 表示其“開展合法且合法的業務”，Alice Huang 於 2025 年離開該公司，但正在進行內部調查。　英偉達董事會週二表示，已成立一個委員會來監督該公司的國家安全政策、美國出口管制的遵守情況以及全球貿易的風險管理。　週二盤後交易中，英偉達股價上漲 5%。自黃本月稍早承認有婚外情以來，該公司股價已下跌逾16%。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/nx-s1-6044213/jensen-huang-nvidia-congress"}, {"code": "20261118-3", "ch": "2026-11-18　週三", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Trump is in Asia ahead of Xi, Putin summit. And, tech leaders want Huang back at Nvidia　／　川普在習近平和普丁峰會之前訪問亞洲。而且，技術領導者希望黃回到英偉達", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Brittney Melton，全文共 6 段、28 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：川普表示，他計劃在亞洲之行期間討論烏克蘭問題，這與白宮先前宣布的內容相矛盾。而且，矽谷領導人正在推動黃仁勳重返英偉達。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/g-s1-153950/up-first-newsletter-faa-ground-stop-trump-asia-trip-nvidia-lindsay-clancy"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "昨天晚上，美國聯邦航空管理局下令在全國範圍內停飛後，航空旅行正在恢復…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "A technology issue with United Airlines delayed departing flights yesterday evening, just as air travel was returning to normal after the Federal Aviation Administration ordered a nationwide ground stop on Friday.", "zh": "昨天晚上，美國聯邦航空管理局下令在全國範圍內停飛後，航空旅行正在恢復正常，聯合航空公司的技術問題導致出發航班延誤。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "President Trump said yesterday that he hopes this incident will prompt Congress to allocate more funds to upgrade the outdated air traffic control system.", "zh": "川普總統昨天表示，他希望這起事件能促使國會撥款更多資金來升級過時的空中交通管制系統。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "川普總統今天在馬尼拉與東協峰會上的盟友會面。明天，他將前往中國深圳，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "President Trump is in Manila today to meet with allies at the ASEAN summit.", "zh": "川普總統今天在馬尼拉與東協峰會上的盟友會面。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Tomorrow, he travels to Shenzhen, China, for a joint summit with Chinese leader Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin.", "zh": "明天，他將前往中國深圳，與中國領導人習近平和俄羅斯總統普丁舉行聯合峰會。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's the first time those three have had a joint summit.", "zh": "這是三人首次舉行聯合峰會。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The meeting will happen on the sidelines of the APEC summit that Xi is hosting in Shenzhen.", "zh": "這次會議將在習近平在深圳主持的亞太經合組織高峰會期間舉行。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "英偉達執行長黃仁勳的辭職震動了矽谷，促使一些科技領袖呼籲董事會恢復他…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang's resignation has shaken Silicon Valley, prompting calls from some tech leaders for the board to reinstate him.", "zh": "英偉達執行長黃仁勳的辭職震動了矽谷，促使一些科技領袖呼籲董事會恢復他的職位。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Trump said he agreed with them.", "zh": "川普表示他同意他們的觀點。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Meanwhile, the U.S. government introduced a rule to block remote access to advanced AI chips and servers, closing a loophole that could allow adversarial governments to access American AI technology through overseas data centers.", "zh": "同時，美國政府推出了一項規則，阻止遠端存取先進的人工智慧晶片和伺服器，堵住了敵對政府透過海外資料中心存取美國人工智慧技術的漏洞。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Nvidia is the world's dominant producer of AI chips.", "zh": "英偉達是全球領先的人工智慧晶片生產商。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "檢察官正著手對林賽·克蘭西三個孩子的死亡案進行重審。新的審判定於 2…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Prosecutors are moving to retry Lindsay Clancy for the deaths of her three children.", "zh": "檢察官正著手對林賽·克蘭西三個孩子的死亡案進行重審。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The new trial is set for March 29, 2027.", "zh": "新審判定於 2027 年 3 月 29 日進行。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Although there was speculation about potentially reducing the charges to manslaughter or second-degree murder after her previous trial ended in a mistrial, no changes were made during Monday's court hearing.", "zh": "儘管在她之前的審判以誤審結束後，有人猜測可能會將指控減少為過失殺人或二級謀殺，但周一的法庭聽證會並沒有做出任何改變。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Judge William Sullivan, who presided over the first trial, will oversee the new proceedings.", "zh": "主持第一次審判的威廉·沙利文法官將監督新的訴訟程序。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He denied Clancy's defense team's request to dismiss the charges based on double jeopardy.", "zh": "他拒絕了克蘭西辯護團隊基於雙重危險駁回指控的請求。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Clancy's defense argues that she shouldn't be held criminally responsible for killing her children because she was suffering from severe postpartum psychosis.", "zh": "克蘭西的辯護律師認為，她不應該因殺害孩子而被追究刑事責任，因為她患有嚴重的產後精神病。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "一年前，新墨西哥州成為第一個向所有家庭提供免費托兒服務的州，無論其收…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "One year ago, New Mexico became the first state to offer free childcare to all families regardless of income, as long as adults are working, seeking work, in school, or unable to work.", "zh": "一年前，新墨西哥州成為第一個向所有家庭提供免費托兒服務的州，無論其收入如何，只要成年人正在工作、尋找工作、在學校或無法工作。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Many parents have found this initiative life-changing, but capacity was limited.", "zh": "許多家長發現這項舉措改變了他們的生活，但能力有限。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Only 50% of the some 67,000 children ages 5 and under are enrolled in the universal childcare program.", "zh": "約 67,000 名 5 歲及以下兒童中，只有 50% 參加了全民托兒計畫。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Some of the remaining families participate in other programs, such as PreK and Head Start.", "zh": "剩下的一些家庭參加其他計劃，例如學前班和啟蒙計劃。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "New Mexico officials say the program must expand to meet demand.", "zh": "新墨西哥州官員表示，該計劃必須擴大以滿足需求。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The issues observed in New Mexico are mirrored across the nation, prompting policymakers and childcare advocates to closely monitor the state's initiative.", "zh": "新墨西哥州觀察到的問題也反映在全國各地，促使政策制定者和兒童保育倡議者密切關注該州的舉措。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Millions of shorebirds embark on epic migrations to Alaska each year to breed.", "zh": "每年，數以百萬計的濱鳥開始史詩般的遷徙，前往阿拉斯加繁殖。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They often travel thousands of miles from places like New Zealand, Asia and South America.", "zh": "他們經常從紐西蘭、亞洲和南美洲等地出發數千英里。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But researchers have found a concerning trend: Nearly half of the 41 shorebird species that breed in Alaska are in decline.", "zh": "但研究人員發現了一個令人擔憂的趨勢：在阿拉斯加繁殖的 41 種濱鳥中，近一半的數量正在減少。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "These birds time their journeys to coincide with peak insect availability, and climate change is throwing off their schedules.", "zh": "這些鳥類將它們的旅程安排在昆蟲數量高峰期，而氣候變遷正在打亂它們的日程。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Warmer springs lead to earlier insect emergence, creating a mismatch that could leave shorebirds without enough food supply.", "zh": "溫暖的春天導致昆蟲提前出現，造成不匹配，可能導致濱鳥沒有足夠的食物供應。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Scientists are now racing to understand if these migratory birds can adapt to the changing Arctic landscape.", "zh": "科學家現在正在競相了解這些候鳥是否能夠適應不斷變化的北極景觀。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "昨天晚上，美國聯邦航空管理局下令在全國範圍內停飛後，航空旅行正在恢復正常，聯合航空公司的技術問題導致出發航班延誤。川普總統昨天表示，他希望這起事件能促使國會撥款更多資金來升級過時的空中交通管制系統。　川普總統今天在馬尼拉與東協峰會上的盟友會面。明天，他將前往中國深圳，與中國領導人習近平和俄羅斯總統普丁舉行聯合峰會。這是三人首次舉行聯合峰會。這次會議將在習近平在深圳主持的亞太經合組織高峰會期間舉行。　英偉達執行長黃仁勳的辭職震動了矽谷，促使一些科技領袖呼籲董事會恢復他的職位。川普表示他同意他們的觀點。同時，美國政府推出了一項規則，阻止遠端存取先進的人工智慧晶片和伺服器，堵住了敵對政府透過海外資料中心存取美國人工智慧技術的漏洞。英偉達是全球領先的人工智慧晶片生產商。　檢察官正著手對林賽·克蘭西三個孩子的死亡案進行重審。新的審判定於 2027 年 3 月 29 日進行。雖然在她的上一次審判以誤審結束後，有人猜測可能會將指控減輕為過失殺人或二級謀殺，但周一的法庭聽證會沒有做出任何改變。主持第一次審判的威廉·沙利文法官將監督新的訴訟程序。他拒絕了克蘭西辯護團隊基於雙重危險駁回指控的請求。克蘭西的辯護律師認為，她不應該因殺害孩子而被追究刑事責任，因為她患有嚴重的產後精神病。　一年前，新墨西哥州成為第一個向所有家庭提供免費托兒服務的州，無論其收入如何，只要成年人正在工作、尋找工作、在學校或無法工作。许多家长发现这一举措改变了他们的生活，但能力有限。约 67,000 名 5 岁及以下儿童中，只有 50% 参加了全民托儿计划。剩下的一些家庭参加其他计划，例如学前班和启蒙计划。新墨西哥州官员表示，该计划必须扩大以满足需求。新墨西哥州观察到的问题也反映在全国各地，促使政策制定者和儿童保育倡导者密切关注该州的举措。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/g-s1-153950/up-first-newsletter-faa-ground-stop-trump-asia-trip-nvidia-lindsay-clancy"}, {"code": "20261117-1", "ch": "2026-11-17　週二", "sec": "Understanding AI", "title": "California sues OpenAI over hacking risks　／　加州因駭客風險起訴 OpenAI", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Huo Jingnan，全文共 4 段、9 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：該州總檢察長在 Hugging Face 攻擊後開始調查 OpenAI，現在表示，由於 OpenAI 的安全措施不佳，這次攻擊「完全可以預見」。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042920/california-sues-openai-hugging-face-hacking-incident"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "加州週一起訴 OpenAI，指控這家前沿人工智慧公司未能保護公眾免受…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "California sued OpenAI Monday, alleging that the frontier AI company failed to protect the public from its systems' advanced cyber capabilities.", "zh": "加州週一起訴 OpenAI，指控這家前沿人工智慧公司未能保護公眾免受其係統先進網路功能的影響。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The lawsuit stems from OpenAI's agents' attack on open-source software platform Hugging Face over the summer but also touches on a wide range of other related incidents tied to the company's agents acting without authorization.", "zh": "該訴訟源於 OpenAI 代理在今年夏天對開源軟體平台 Hugging Face 的攻擊，但也涉及與該公司代理未經授權行事有關的一系列其他相關事件。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "加州總檢察長羅布·邦塔 (Rob Bonta) 在新聞發布會上表示：…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "\"Just because the technology is new or rapidly evolving doesn't mean the people behind it are above the law,\" said California Attorney General Rob Bonta during a press conference.", "zh": "加州總檢察長羅布·邦塔 (Rob Bonta) 在新聞發布會上表示：“僅僅因為這項技術是新技術或快速發展，並不意味著其背後的人就可以凌駕於法律之上。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Whether it's a car or a toy, the law is simple: don't build or test things that can hurt people without proper safeguards.\" The lawsuit cited potential concerns about cyberattacks \"on power grids, emergency infrastructure, hospital systems, and financial institutions.\"", "zh": "「無論是汽車還是玩具，法律都很簡單：不要在沒有適當保障措施的情況下製造或測試可能傷害他人的東西。」該訴訟提到了對「電網、緊急基礎設施、醫院系統和金融機構」網路攻擊的潛在擔憂。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "其他人工智慧公司也不得不努力解決其係統以意想不到的和不良的方式運作的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Other AI companies have also had to wrestle with their systems behaving in unexpected and undesirable ways.", "zh": "其他人工智慧公司也不得不努力解決其係統以意想不到的和不良的方式運作的問題。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Anthropic and Meta have both said they found that their AI systems have hacked into places they shouldn't have.", "zh": "Anthropic 和 Meta 都表示，他們發現他們的人工智慧系統侵入了他們不應該侵入的地方。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Major AI companies have since signed onto an agreement organized by the White House to develop AI responsibly, but the agreement is nonbinding.", "zh": "此後，主要的人工智慧公司簽署了一份由白宮組織的協議，以負責任的方式開發人工智慧，但該協議不具約束力。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "根據 OpenAI 自己披露的報告，加州指控這家頂級人工智慧公司從事…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Drawing from reports including from OpenAI's own disclosures, California alleges that the top AI company has engaged in unfair competition and created a public nuisance.", "zh": "根據 OpenAI 自己披露的報告，加州指控這家頂級人工智慧公司從事不公平競爭並造成公共滋擾。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It asked the court to stop the company from further engaging in such activities and order it to pay monetary damages.", "zh": "請求法院停止該公司進一步從事此類活動，並命令其支付經濟損失。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "加州週一起訴 OpenAI，指控這家前沿人工智慧公司未能保護公眾免受其係統先進網路功能的影響。該訴訟源於 OpenAI 代理在今年夏天對開源軟體平台 Hugging Face 的攻擊，但也涉及與該公司代理未經授權行事有關的一系列其他相關事件。　加州總檢察長羅布·邦塔 (Rob Bonta) 在新聞發布會上表示：“僅僅因為這項技術是新技術或快速發展，並不意味著其背後的人就可以凌駕於法律之上。” “無論是汽車還是玩具，法律都很簡單：不要在沒有適當保障措施的情況下製造或測試可能傷害他人的東西。”該訴訟提到了對“電網和金融機構的基礎設施。　其他人工智慧公司也不得不努力解決其係統以意想不到的和不良的方式運作的問題。 Anthropic 和 Meta 都表示，他們發現他們的人工智慧系統侵入了他們不應該侵入的地方。此後，主要的人工智慧公司簽署了一份由白宮組織的協議，以負責任的方式開發人工智慧，但該協議不具約束力。　根據 OpenAI 自己披露的報告，加州指控這家頂級人工智慧公司從事不公平競爭並造成公共滋擾。請求法院停止該公司進一步從事此類活動，並命令其支付經濟損失。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042920/california-sues-openai-hugging-face-hacking-incident"}, {"code": "20261117-2", "ch": "2026-11-17　週二", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "U.S. tightens controls on remote access to AI technology amid Nvidia fallout　／　由於英偉達的影響，美國加強了對遠端存取人工智慧技術的控制", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Katie McQue，全文共 8 段、12 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：新規則彌補了一個存在的漏洞，儘管美國限制向中國出售先進的人工智慧晶片，但中國公司仍然可以遠端存取先進的人工智慧晶片。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042883/nvidia-jensen-huang-commerce-department"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "美國政府宣布了一項規則，禁止遠端存取先進的人工智慧晶片和伺服器，堵住…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The U.S. government has announced a rule to prevent remote access to advanced artificial intelligence chips and servers, closing a loophole that could let adversarial governments access American AI technology through overseas data centers.", "zh": "美國政府宣布了一項規則，禁止遠端存取先進的人工智慧晶片和伺服器，堵住敵對政府透過海外資料中心存取美國人工智慧技術的漏洞。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "Megaspeed 總部位於新加坡，在馬來西亞設有工廠。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Megaspeed is based in Singapore and operates facilities in Malaysia.", "zh": "Megaspeed 總部位於新加坡，在馬來西亞設有工廠。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "「Megaspeed 開展合法、合法的業務。該公司已聘請外部法律顧問…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"Megaspeed conducts legitimate and lawful business.", "zh": "「Megaspeed 開展正當合法的業務。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The company has retained external legal counsel to conduct a thorough internal investigation,\" the company said in a statement emailed to NPR and other news organizations on Sunday.", "zh": "該公司已聘請外部法律顧問來進行徹底的內部調查，」該公司在周日透過電子郵件發送給 NPR 和其他新聞機構的聲明中表示。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "在英偉達醜聞發生之前，川普政府一直拒絕實施額外的法規來阻止外國企業取…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Prior to the Nvidia scandal, the Trump administration had resisted imposing additional regulations to prevent foreign access to American AI technology.", "zh": "在英偉達醜聞發生之前，川普政府一直拒絕實施額外的法規來阻止外國企業取得美國人工智慧技術。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "拜登政府於 2025 年 1 月 15 日（即川普就職前五天）編寫了…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The Biden administration had written a framework designed to control worldwide distribution of advanced AI chips on January 15, 2025 – five days before Trump's inauguration.", "zh": "拜登政府於 2025 年 1 月 15 日（即川普就職前五天）編寫了一個旨在控制先進人工智慧晶片在全球範圍內分發的框架。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In May 2025, Trump's Commerce Department announced it would not enforce the rule and intended to rescind it, calling it \"ill-conceived and counterproductive.\"", "zh": "2025 年 5 月，川普的商務部宣布不會執行該規則，並打算廢除該規則，稱其「考慮不周且適得其反」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "拜登的框架還將限制被視為安全風險的國家獲得人工智慧晶片，某些晶片出口…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Biden's framework would have also limited access to AI chips by countries considered security risks, required licenses for certain chip exports, and created restrictions on the power of advanced models and computing infrastructure.", "zh": "拜登的框架還將限制被視為安全風險的國家獲得人工智慧晶片，某些晶片出口需要許可證，並對先進模型和運算基礎設施的能力設置限制。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "根據《紐約時報》報導，情報官員於 2025 年 10 月首次向川普通…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "The New York Times reported that Trump was first briefed by intelligence officials about Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy in October 2025.", "zh": "《紐約時報》報導稱，川普於 2025 年 10 月首次聽取情報官員通報黃仁勳與一名中國間諜嫌疑人的戀情。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Both Jensen Huang and Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick are expected to testify before Congress this month and next month and there will likely be further investigations into what Trump knew about the affair when the Democrats take control of Congress in January 2027, Rep.", "zh": "眾議員黃仁勳和商務部長霍華德·盧特尼克預計將於本月和下個月在國會作證，當民主黨於 2027 年 1 月控制國會時，可能會進一步調查川普對此事的了解。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Yvette Clarke, D-NY, told NPR.", "zh": "紐約州民主黨人伊維特克拉克 (Yvette Clarke) 告訴 NPR。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "克拉克說：“我們需要調查事實，讓個人在宣誓後向我們提供盡可能多的資訊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "\"We need to get the facts investigated, bring in individuals to give us as much information as possible under oath, so that we can get to the bottom of why this happened, how it occurred, and how we could prevent this type of compromise from happening again,\" said Clarke.", "zh": "克拉克說：“我們需要調查事實，讓個人在宣誓後向我們提供盡可能多的資訊，以便我們能夠查清此事發生的原因、如何發生以及我們如何防止此類妥協再次發生。”"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "美國政府宣布了一項規則，禁止遠端存取先進的人工智慧晶片和伺服器，堵住敵對政府透過海外資料中心存取美國人工智慧技術的漏洞。　Megaspeed 總部位於新加坡，在馬來西亞設有工廠。　「Megaspeed 開展合法、合法的業務。該公司已聘請外部法律顧問來進行徹底的內部調查，」該公司在周日透過電子郵件發送給 NPR 和其他新聞機構的聲明中表示。　在英偉達醜聞發生之前，川普政府一直拒絕實施額外的法規來阻止外國企業取得美國人工智慧技術。　拜登政府於 2025 年 1 月 15 日（即川普就職前五天）編寫了一個旨在控制先進人工智慧晶片在全球範圍內分發的框架。 2025 年 5 月，川普的商務部宣布不會執行該規則，並打算廢除該規則，稱其「考慮不周且適得其反」。　拜登的框架還將限制被視為安全風險的國家獲得人工智慧晶片，某些晶片出口需要許可證，並對先進模型和運算基礎設施的能力設置限制。　根據《紐約時報》報導，情報官員於 2025 年 10 月首次向川普通報了黃仁勳與一名疑似中國間諜的戀情。紐約州民主黨眾議員伊薇特克拉克 (Yvette Clarke) 告訴 NPR，黃仁勳和商務部長霍華德·盧特尼克預計將於本月和下個月在國會作證，當民主黨於 2027 年 1 月控制國會時，可能會進一步調查川普對該事件的了解情況。　克拉克說：“我們需要調查事實，讓個人在宣誓後向我們提供盡可能多的資訊，以便我們能夠查清此事發生的原因、如何發生以及我們如何防止此類妥協再次發生。”"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042883/nvidia-jensen-huang-commerce-department"}, {"code": "20261117-3", "ch": "2026-11-17　週二", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "U.N. talks seek to rein in 'killer robots' as fears over AI weapons grow　／　隨著對人工智慧武器的擔憂加劇，聯合國會談尋求遏制“殺手機器人”", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Imogen Foulkes，全文共 10 段、20 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：各國正在日內瓦舉行會議，就無需人為干預即可選擇和殺死目標的武器規則進行談判。但隨著美國、俄羅斯和以色列抵制具有法律約束力的控制措施，活動人士擔心採取行動的窗口正在關閉。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042548/un-killer-robots-ai-weapons-drones"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "日內瓦——位於日內瓦的聯合國正在就使用致命自主武器（也稱為「殺手機器…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "GENEVA — Negotiations on possible rules for the use of lethal autonomous weapons, also known as 'killer robots' are underway at the United Nations in Geneva.", "zh": "日內瓦——位於日內瓦的聯合國正在就使用致命自主武器（也稱為「殺手機器人」）的可能規則進行談判。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "自主武器管制的支持者表示，本週召開的聯合國特定常規武器會議每五年舉行…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Supporters of controls on autonomous weapons say this week's U.N. conference on Certain Conventional Weapons (or CCW), which meets just once every five years, is the last best chance to agree rules before it is too late.", "zh": "自主武器管制的支持者表示，本週召開的聯合國特定常規武器會議每五年舉行一次，是在為時已晚之前達成規則的最後最佳機會。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "戰爭技術在過去幾年中迅速發展，一些專家警告說，世界距離擁有能夠選擇目…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Warfare technology has advanced rapidly in the last few years, with some experts warning that the world is just months away from having weapons that can choose targets and make the decision to kill autonomously.", "zh": "戰爭技術在過去幾年中迅速發展，一些專家警告說，世界距離擁有能夠選擇目標並自主做出殺傷決定的武器只有幾個月的時間。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "同時，人權組織警告說，人工智慧輔助武器背後的技術正變得越來越便宜且易…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Meanwhile, human rights groups warn that the technology behind AI-assisted weapons is becoming increasingly cheap and easy to use.", "zh": "同時，人權組織警告說，人工智慧輔助武器背後的技術正變得越來越便宜且易於使用。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The more it is adopted by the military, the greater the danger of proliferation and its use by terrorist groups or law enforcement agencies in repressive regimes.", "zh": "軍隊採用的越多，擴散以及被恐怖組織或專制政權的執法機構使用的危險就越大。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In theory, a swarm of autonomous drones could be programmed to kill everyone wearing a red sweater, everyone carrying a poster or even everyone speaking a certain language.", "zh": "理論上，一群自主無人機可以被程式設計殺死每個穿紅色毛衣的人、每個拿著海報的人，甚至每個人說某種語言的人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "目前在日內瓦召開會議的許多國家都非常重視此類關切。包括愛爾蘭、義大利…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Many of the countries now meeting in Geneva take such concerns very seriously.", "zh": "目前在日內瓦召開會議的許多國家都非常重視此類關切。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "At least 50, including Ireland, Italy, Brazil, Mexico, France and Germany, are calling for a strict timetable to agree on binding rules governing autonomous weapons.", "zh": "包括愛爾蘭、義大利、巴西、墨西哥、法國和德國在內的至少 50 個國家呼籲制定嚴格的時間表，以就管理自主武器的約束性規則達成協議。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "但在已經開發和使用半自主武器的國家中，卻出現了阻力。美國、俄羅斯和以…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "But among states that are already developing and using semi-autonomous weapons, there is pushback.", "zh": "但在已經開發和使用半自主武器的國家中，卻出現了阻力。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The United States, Russia and Israel have indicated they are set to oppose legally binding rules, with Washington proposing a five-year timetable to draft non-binding guidelines instead.", "zh": "美國、俄羅斯和以色列已表示他們將反對具有法律約束力的規則，而華盛頓則提出了一個五年時間表來起草不具約束力的指導方針。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Ukraine invasion — explained How AI drones are influencing the course of the Ukraine war The U.S. is traditionally a late adopter of international treaties.", "zh": "烏克蘭入侵—解釋人工智慧無人機如何影響烏克蘭戰爭的進程美國傳統上是國際條約的較晚採用者。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It did not ratify the Ottawa Convention on landmines, for example, although it did, over time, stop deploying them and reduce its stockpiles.", "zh": "例如，它沒有批准關於地雷的《渥太華公約》，儘管隨著時間的推移，它確實停止部署地雷並減少庫存。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "在川普總統的領導下，人們對國際法的懷疑增加。華盛頓對國際刑事法院實施…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Under President Trump, doubts about international law have grown.", "zh": "在川普總統的領導下，人們對國際法的懷疑增加。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Washington has imposed sweeping sanctions on the International Criminal Court, and just this weekend, Secretary of State Marco Rubio, in a keynote speech to the Federalist Society, warned against \"quoting laws to men with swords.\"", "zh": "華盛頓對國際刑事法院實施了全面製裁，就在本週末，國務卿馬可·盧比奧在聯邦黨人協會的主題演講中警告不要「向持劍之人引用法律」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "各國在日內瓦舉行會議的問題是，聯合國關於限制特定武器的談判應該以協商…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "The problem for states meeting in Geneva is that U.N. negotiations on limiting specific weapons are supposed to be conducted by consensus.", "zh": "各國在日內瓦舉行會議的問題是，聯合國關於限制特定武器的談判應該以協商一致方式進行。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This was achieved in 1995, when countries agreed to a ban on blinding lasers, but other agreements have proved elusive.", "zh": "這一目標於 1995 年實現，當時各國同意禁止致盲激光，但事實證明其他協議難以達成。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "With landmines, countries frustrated by the delay finally took negotiations outside the U.N. process to create the Ottawa Convention.", "zh": "由於地雷問題，因拖延而感到沮喪的國家最終在聯合國制定《渥太華公約》的進程之外進行了談判。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "本週，可能會達成妥協：更長甚至不限成員名額的談判期，以製定各國可以採…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "This week, there may be a compromise: a longer or even open-ended negotiating period to come up with rules that individual states can adopt as binding or non-binding.", "zh": "本週，可能會達成妥協：更長甚至不限成員名額的談判期，以製定各國可以採用的有約束力或無約束力的規則。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "For diplomats supporting such a solution, it is a way to ensure at least some progress.", "zh": "對於支持這種解決方案的外交官來說，這是確保至少取得一些進展的一種方法。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "For campaigners, it is less than ideal, with one likening it to kicking a very dangerous can down the road.", "zh": "對於活動人士來說，這並不理想，有人將其比作將一個非常危險的罐子踢到路上。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "日內瓦——位於日內瓦的聯合國正在就使用致命自主武器（也稱為「殺手機器人」）的可能規則進行談判。　自主武器管制的支持者表示，本週召開的聯合國特定常規武器會議每五年舉行一次，是在為時已晚之前達成規則的最後最佳機會。　戰爭技術在過去幾年中迅速發展，一些專家警告說，世界距離擁有能夠選擇目標並自主做出殺傷決定的武器只有幾個月的時間。　同時，人權組織警告說，人工智慧輔助武器背後的技術正變得越來越便宜且易於使用。軍隊採用的越多，擴散以及被恐怖組織或專制政權的執法機構使用的危險就越大。理論上，一群自主無人機可以被程式設計殺死每個穿紅色毛衣的人、每個拿著海報的人，甚至每個人說某種語言的人。　目前在日內瓦召開會議的許多國家都非常重視此類關切。包括愛爾蘭、義大利、巴西、墨西哥、法國和德國在內的至少 50 個國家呼籲制定嚴格的時間表，以就管理自主武器的約束性規則達成協議。　但在已經開發和使用半自主武器的國家中，卻出現了阻力。美國、俄羅斯和以色列已表示他們將反對具有法律約束力的規則，而華盛頓則提出了一個五年時間表來起草不具約束力的指導方針。　在川普總統的領導下，人們對國際法的懷疑增加。華盛頓對國際刑事法院實施了全面製裁，就在本週末，國務卿馬可·盧比奧在聯邦黨人協會的主題演講中警告不要「向持劍之人引用法律」。　各國在日內瓦舉行會議的問題是，聯合國關於限制特定武器的談判應該以協商一致方式進行。這一目標於 1995 年實現，當時各國同意禁止致盲激光，但事實證明其他協議難以達成。由於地雷問題，因拖延而感到沮喪的國家最終在聯合國制定《渥太華公約》的進程之外進行了談判。　本週，可能會達成妥協：更長甚至不限成員名額的談判期，以製定各國可以採用的有約束力或無約束力的規則。對於支持這種解決方案的外交官來說，這是確保至少取得一些進展的一種方法。對於活動人士來說，這並不理想，有人將其比作將一個非常危險的罐子踢到路上。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042548/un-killer-robots-ai-weapons-drones"}, {"code": "20261116-1", "ch": "2026-11-16　週一", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Far from home. Voyager 1 is now farther than anything man has sent into space　／　離家很遠。旅行者一號現在比人類送入太空的任何東西都更遠", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Ava Pukatch，全文共 10 段、17 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：美國太空總署航海家一號是距離地球最遠的人造物體，本週將達到一個新的里程碑。週三，探測器將距離地球約 160 億英里。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6041716/a-long-long-ways-from-home-voyager-1-is-now-farther-than-anything-man-has-sent-into-space"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "NASA's Voyager 1 has traveled farther than anything else that humans have launched into space.", "zh": "美國太空總署航海家一號的飛行距離比人類發射到太空的任何東西都遠。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "On Wednesday, it's set to reach a new milestone: reaching a distance that is one-light day away from Earth.", "zh": "週三，它將達到一個新的里程碑：到達距離地球一光日的距離。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "美國國家航空暨太空總署 (NASA) 將舉辦「航海家之光日閃耀」活動…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "NASA is celebrating the occasion with the \"Shine Bright for Voyager's Light-Day.\" Calling it a symbolic celebration, NASA is asking the public on Tuesday night to send Voyager's call sign V-G-R into the sky in morse code.", "zh": "美國國家航空暨太空總署 (NASA) 將舉辦「航海家之光日閃耀」活動來慶祝這一時刻。美國宇航局稱其為象徵性的慶祝活動，並要求公眾在周二晚上將航行者號的呼號 V-G-R 用莫爾斯電碼發送到天空。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Use a flashlight, phone light or anything that can blink a sequence.", "zh": "使用手電筒、手機燈或任何可以按順序閃爍的東西。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "V - 3 次快閃，1 次長閃 G - 2 次長閃，1 次快閃 R …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "V - Three quick flashes, one long flash G - Two long flashes, one quick flash R - One quick flash, one long flash, one quick flash", "zh": "V - 3 次快閃，1 次長閃 G - 2 次長閃，1 次快閃 R - 1 次快閃，1 次長閃，1 次快閃"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "A light-day is the distance light travels in 24 hours, or more than 16 billion miles.", "zh": "一光日是光在 24 小時內傳播的距離，超過 160 億英里。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "This NASA spacecraft has traveled for nearly 50 years, launching Sept. 5, 1977.", "zh": "這艘 NASA 太空船自 1977 年 9 月 5 日發射以來，已經飛行了近 50 年。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Over the course of its mission, Voyager 1 has conducted flybys of Jupiter and Saturn.", "zh": "在其任務過程中，航海家一號飛越了木星和土星。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In 1979, it discovered a faint ring system on Jupiter.", "zh": "1979年，它在木星上發現了一個微弱的光環系統。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In 1980, the spacecraft took detailed photos of Saturn's rings and moons.", "zh": "1980年，太空船拍攝了土星環和衛星的詳細照片。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "While on its journey, on Feb. 17, 1998, Voyager 1 overtook the U.S. space probe, Pioneer 10, becoming the most distant human-made object in existence.", "zh": "1998 年 2 月 17 日，航行者 1 號在旅途中超越了美國太空探測器先鋒 10 號，成為現存距離最遠的人造物體。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It and its twin, Voyager 2, are the only spacecraft to have operated outside of the heliosphere, which acts like a protective shield of the solar system.", "zh": "它和它的雙胞胎航海家二號是唯一在日光層之外運作的太空船，日光層就像太陽系的保護罩。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "In addition, the Voyager spacecraft is carrying the Golden Record – an interstellar \"time capsule\" to communicate Earth's story to extraterrestrials.", "zh": "此外，航行者號飛船還攜帶著金唱片——一個星際“時間膠囊”，用於向外星人傳達地球的故事。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "這張鍍金唱片包含 115 個圖像、海浪、風和動物等自然聲音，以及 3…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "The gold-plated record contains 115 images, natural sounds such as surf, wind and animals, and spoken greetings in 35 different languages.", "zh": "這張鍍金唱片包含 115 個圖像、海浪、風和動物等自然聲音，以及 35 種不同語言的口頭問候語。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Included are instructions, in symbols, on how to play the record and the origin of the probe.", "zh": "其中包括有關如何播放唱片和探頭起源的符號說明。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "經過 49 年零兩個月零 11 天的旅行後，航行者 1 號預計將於美…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "Voyager 1 is estimated to reach \"light-day status\" at 5:16 a.m.", "zh": "Voyager 1 號預計將於凌晨 5 點 16 分達到「光日狀態」。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "ET on Wednesday, after 49 years, two months and 11 days of travel.", "zh": "美國東部時間週三，經過 49 年 2 個月 11 天的旅行。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "美國國家航空暨太空總署 (NASA) 將舉辦「航海家之光日閃耀」活動來慶祝這一時刻。美國宇航局稱其為象徵性的慶祝活動，並要求公眾在周二晚上將航行者號的呼號 V-G-R 用莫爾斯電碼發送到天空。使用手電筒、手機燈或任何可以按順序閃爍的東西。　V - 3 次快閃，1 次長閃 G - 2 次長閃，1 次快閃 R - 1 次快閃，1 次長閃，1 次快閃　這張鍍金唱片包含 115 個圖像、海浪、風和動物等自然聲音，以及 35 種不同語言的口頭問候語。其中包括有關如何播放唱片和探頭起源的符號說明。　經過 49 年零兩個月零 11 天的旅行後，航行者 1 號預計將於美國東部時間週三上午 5 點 16 分達到“光日狀態”。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6041716/a-long-long-ways-from-home-voyager-1-is-now-farther-than-anything-man-has-sent-into-space"}, {"code": "20261116-2", "ch": "2026-11-16　週一", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Who makes Sydney Sweeney's American Eagle jeans — and under what conditions?　／　Sydney Sweeney 的 American Eagle 牛仔褲是誰生產的？在什麼條件下生產的？", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Diaa Hadid，全文共 18 段、47 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：American Eagle Outfitters 告訴我們，Sydney Sweeney 的牛仔褲很棒。但是誰製造了它們呢？巴基斯坦和孟加拉的服裝廠的工作條件如何？"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6013327/sydney-sweeney-jeans-american-eagle-garment-industry"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "本篇較長，站上只收前 18 段；想讀完整篇請點上方的 NPR 原文連結。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "巴基斯坦卡拉奇——在智慧型手機上播放的 American Eagle…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "KARACHI, Pakistan — In a slum dotted with shimmering pools of sewage, a garment worker nods in recognition as Sydney Sweeney slowly zips up her jeans in an American Eagle Outfitters advertisement playing on a smartphone.", "zh": "巴基斯坦卡拉奇——在智慧型手機上播放的 American Eagle Outfitters 廣告中，西德尼·斯威尼 (Sydney Sweeney) 慢慢拉上牛仔褲的拉鍊時，在佈滿閃閃發光的污水池的貧民窟裡，一名製衣工人點頭表示認可。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "但她認得的不是史威尼，而是牛仔褲和夾克。這位女士是一位單身母親，曾在…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "But it's not Sweeney she recognizes — it's the jeans and jacket.", "zh": "但她認得的不是史威尼，而是牛仔褲和夾克。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This woman, a single mother, has worked on American Eagle production lines and seen those denim styles and similar models.", "zh": "這位女士是一位單身母親，曾在 American Eagle 生產線上工作，並見過那些牛仔款式和類似款式。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"I know how all of them are made, because I have worked on them,\" she says.", "zh": "「我知道它們是如何製作的，因為我曾經研究過它們，」她說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "去年 7 月，當斯威尼為美國之鷹拍攝的廣告以“雪梨·斯威尼擁有很棒的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "When Sweeney's advertisement for American Eagle landed in July last year, with the tagline \"Sydney Sweeney has great jeans,\" it triggered debate over whether it was a winking reference to eugenics because of Sweeney's va-va-voom beauty: thin, blonde, blue eyes, large breasts.", "zh": "去年 7 月，當斯威尼為美國之鷹拍攝的廣告以“雪梨·斯威尼擁有很棒的牛仔褲”為口號時，引發了一場爭論，即這是否是對優生學的眨眼提及，因為斯威尼的“哇哇哇”的美貌：瘦削、金發、藍眼睛、大乳房。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Following the controversy, American Eagle said in a September 2025 statement that \"'Sydney Sweeney Has Great Jeans' is and always was about the jeans.\" (Sweeney did not respond to NPR's request for comment.)", "zh": "爭議發生後，American Eagle 在 2025 年 9 月的聲明中表示，“‘Sydney Sweeney Has Great Jeans’始終是關於牛仔褲的。” （斯威尼沒有回應 NPR 的置評請求。）", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "關於這則廣告是關於牛仔褲還是關於基因的爭論中，並沒有對斯威尼所穿的美…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Missing from the debate over whether the advertisement was about jeans or genes was any significant reflection on who actually made the American Eagle jeans that Sweeney was wearing — as in, the workers.", "zh": "關於這則廣告是關於牛仔褲還是關於基因的爭論中，並沒有對斯威尼所穿的美國之鷹牛仔褲的實際製造者（例如工人）進行任何重要的反思。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The majority of garment factories operate out of Asia, so most Americans will never meet the workers making their clothes or see the conditions they're made under.", "zh": "大多數服裝工廠都在亞洲運營，因此大多數美國人永遠不會見到製作衣服的工人，也不會看到製作衣服的條件。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "工人們喜歡那個單親媽媽。她要求我們用 S.（她名字的首字母）稱呼她，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Workers like that single mother.", "zh": "工人們喜歡那個單親媽媽。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She asks that we refer to her as S., the initial of her first name, because she fears her bosses at the garment factory where she works will fire her if she's identified.", "zh": "她要求我們用 S.（她名字的首字母）稱呼她，因為她擔心如果她的身份被曝光，她工作的服裝廠的老闆會解僱她。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"If you raise your voice, they'll push you out,\" she says. \"We are helpless.\"", "zh": "「如果你提高聲音，他們就會把你趕出去，」她說。 “我們很無助。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "S. 是一名年輕女性，在一家名為 Artistic Garment …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "S., a young woman, works at a factory run by a company called Artistic Garment Industries, where she says she's paid about $144 a month, a sum that supports her son and her mother.", "zh": "S. 是一名年輕女性，在一家名為 Artistic Garment Industries 的公司經營的工廠工作，她說她每月的工資約為 144 美元，這筆錢可以養活她的兒子和母親。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "她說工廠「悶熱難受」。我們見到她時，外面的溫度是華氏 106 度，她…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "She says the factory is \"oppressively hot.\" It was 106 F outside when we met her, and she says the factory inside is even hotter.", "zh": "她說工廠「悶熱難受」。我們見到她時，外面的溫度是華氏 106 度，她說工廠裡面更熱。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She says it's hard to leave her workstation to drink water because she has to meet her production targets.", "zh": "她說，離開工作台喝水很困難，因為她必須完成生產目標。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She says she has to check the quality of 1,000 to 1,600 pieces of clothing a day — and she's fainted three times this year.", "zh": "她說她每天必須檢查 1,000 到 1,600 件衣服的品質 - 今年她已經暈倒了 3 次。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"I feel faint, and I can barely stand.", "zh": "「我感到頭暈，幾乎無法站立。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "I have no energy in my hands and feet,\" S. says.", "zh": "我的手腳沒有力氣，」S. 說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"They don't even let us sit down.\" But S. says she has no other options.", "zh": "「他們甚至不讓我們坐下。」但 S. 說她沒有其他選擇。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "Artistic Garment Industries 證實它為 A…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Artistic Garment Industries confirmed it makes clothes for American Eagle but tells NPR that it does not push out workers who complain about their working conditions.", "zh": "Artistic Garment Industries 證實它為 American Eagle 生產衣服，但告訴 NPR，它不會驅逐那些抱怨工作條件的工人。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The company says it has a robust complaints system that workers can use and says it frequently checks on temperatures inside different parts of its factories.", "zh": "該公司表示，它有一個強大的投訴系統可供工人使用，並表示它經常檢查工廠不同區域的溫度。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "在回答 NPR 向 American Eagle 提出的問題時，該公…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "In response to questions NPR sent to American Eagle, the company says it's \"committed to working directly with our suppliers to protect the health, safety, and rights of workers.", "zh": "在回答 NPR 向 American Eagle 提出的問題時，該公司表示「致力於與我們的供應商直接合作，以保護工人的健康、安全和權利。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We take the concerns raised by workers — and those whom NPR interviewed — very seriously.\"", "zh": "我們非常重視工人以及 NPR 訪談者提出的擔憂。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "S. 是我們在春季和夏季在孟加拉和巴基斯坦採訪的約 20 名工人之一…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "S. is one of around 20 workers we interviewed over the spring and summer in Bangladesh and Pakistan, two of the world's biggest global garment production hubs outside of China.", "zh": "S. 是我們在春季和夏季在孟加拉和巴基斯坦採訪的約 20 名工人之一，這兩個國家是中國以外最大的全球服裝生產中心。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Those men and women worked in five different factories.", "zh": "這些男人和女人在五個不同的工廠工作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "All of those workers asked NPR not to use their full names and to use only the initial of their first name, worried they'd lose their jobs or be blacklisted from future jobs if they were identified.", "zh": "所有這些工人都要求 NPR 不要使用他們的全名，而只使用他們名字的首字母，擔心如果他們的身份被發現，他們會失去工作或被列入未來工作的黑名單。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "儘管我們關注的是 Sweeney 在 2025 年廣告活動中穿著的 …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Although we focused on the American Eagle jeans worn by Sweeney for the 2025 campaign, the reporting led to a bigger issue: how fast fashion is made, because garment factories make clothes for multiple brands at once.", "zh": "儘管我們關注的是 Sweeney 在 2025 年廣告活動中穿著的 American Eagle 牛仔褲，但該報導引發了一個更大的問題：時尚的製作速度有多快，因為服裝工廠同時為多個品牌生產衣服。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Workers we met told us they made clothes for Levi's, Massimo Dutti, The Gap, H&M and American Eagle.", "zh": "我們遇到的工人告訴我們，他們為 Levi's、Massimo Dutti、The Gap、H&M 和 American Eagle 製作服裝。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They said it's common knowledge at the factories which brands they are making clothes for, in part because some workers are stitching on the labels.", "zh": "他們表示，工廠裡都知道他們為哪些品牌生產衣服，部分原因是一些工人負責縫製標籤。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "我們採訪的服裝工人提供了驚人相似的說法。他們在勞工和氣候權利組織的多…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "The garment workers we spoke to offered strikingly similar accounts.", "zh": "我們採訪的服裝工人提供了驚人相似的說法。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And they echoed worker testimonies in multiple reports by labor and climate rights groups.", "zh": "他們在勞工和氣候權利組織的多份報告中呼應了工人的證詞。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The workers told us they're paid low wages, even as they're expected to reach what they say are unreasonably high production targets, often laboring in sweltering factories.", "zh": "工人們告訴我們，他們的工資很低，儘管他們預計要達到他們所說的不合理的高生產目標，而且經常在悶熱的工廠裡勞動。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "這些生產目標包括每小時縫製 200 個袖子或每天檢查 1000 件衣…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "These are production targets like stitching 200 sleeves an hour or checking the quality of a thousand pieces of clothing a day.", "zh": "這些生產目標包括每小時縫製 200 個袖子或每天檢查 1000 件衣服的品質。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The workers we interviewed say they are unable to hydrate or cool down properly, even as extreme heat caused by climate change makes their workplaces and homes even hotter.", "zh": "我們採訪的工人表示，他們無法適當補充水分或降溫，儘管氣候變遷引起的極端高溫使他們的工作場所和家變得更加炎熱。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "康乃爾大學全球勞工研究所執行長賈森賈德（Jason Judd）表示，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "It can be four to six degrees hotter inside a factory, says Jason Judd, executive director of the Global Labor Institute at Cornell University, which researched heat inside garment factories and worker homes.", "zh": "康乃爾大學全球勞工研究所執行長賈森賈德（Jason Judd）表示，工廠內的溫度可能會高出四到六度，該研究所研究了服裝廠和工人住宅內的熱量。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"You've got all those bodies, all that material, all that machinery putting off heat.", "zh": "「你擁有所有這些身體、所有材料、所有散發熱量的機器。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "You've got ventilation problems.\"", "zh": "你有通風問題。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "「我們開始看到昏厥、中暑、慢性病惡化，甚至死亡，」氣候權利國際研究員…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "\"We're starting to see fainting, heat illness, exacerbation of chronic disease, even death,\" says Cara Schulte, a researcher at Climate Rights International.", "zh": "「我們開始看到昏厥、中暑、慢性病惡化，甚至死亡，」氣候權利國際研究員卡拉舒爾特說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She authored two reports on the impacts of heat on garment workers.", "zh": "她撰寫了兩份關於高溫對製衣工人影響的報告。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "舒爾特表示，工人們為了達到生產目標而承受巨大的壓力。一個主要原因是品…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Schulte says workers are put under that extreme pressure to reach production targets.", "zh": "舒爾特表示，工人們為了達到生產目標而承受巨大的壓力。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "A major reason is that brands demand their suppliers make enormous volumes of clothes on tight deadlines and on thin profit margins.", "zh": "一個主要原因是品牌要求其供應商在緊迫的期限內生產大量服裝，並且利潤微薄。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And she says garment workers are vulnerable to the heat because they're clustered in countries like Bangladesh and Pakistan.", "zh": "她說，服裝工人很容易受到高溫的影響，因為他們聚集在孟加拉和巴基斯坦等國家。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She cites U.N. publications stating that those factories are \"in areas that are warming faster than the global average, that are [already] incredibly hot and humid.\"", "zh": "她引用聯合國出版物稱，這些工廠“位於升溫速度快於全球平均水平的地區，[已經]非常炎熱和潮濕。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "H&M 是工人確認製造的品牌之一，該公司表示，它“付出了巨大努力”，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "H&M, one of the brands that workers identified making, said it \"put great effort\" in ensuring fair payment to its suppliers and that labor costs are \"excluded from the price negotiations of our product orders\" to ensure that worker wages were not driven down.", "zh": "H&M 是工人確認製造的品牌之一，該公司表示，它“付出了巨大努力”，以確保向供應商公平付款，並且勞動力成本“被排除在我們產品訂單的價格談判之外”，以確保工人工資不會被壓低。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "氣候權利國際組織的舒爾特引述她自己的研究表示，製衣工人被迫冒著健康風…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "Citing her own research, Schulte of Climate Rights International says garment workers are compelled to risk their health to survive.", "zh": "氣候權利國際組織的舒爾特引述她自己的研究表示，製衣工人被迫冒著健康風險才能生存。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's not a choice, she says.", "zh": "她說，這不是一個選擇。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Workers are not choosing to take these risks,\" she says.", "zh": "「工人們不會選擇承擔這些風險，」她說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"They're being forced into them by poverty.\"", "zh": "“他們是因為貧窮才被迫這麼做的。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "巴基斯坦卡拉奇——在智慧型手機上播放的 American Eagle Outfitters 廣告中，西德尼·斯威尼 (Sydney Sweeney) 慢慢拉上牛仔褲的拉鍊時，在佈滿閃閃發光的污水池的貧民窟裡，一名製衣工人點頭表示認可。　但她認得的不是史威尼，而是牛仔褲和夾克。這位女士是一位單身母親，曾在 American Eagle 生產線上工作，並見過那些牛仔款式和類似款式。 「我知道它們是如何製作的，因為我曾經研究過它們，」她說。　去年 7 月，當斯威尼為美國之鷹拍攝的廣告以“雪梨·斯威尼擁有很棒的牛仔褲”為口號時，引發了一場爭論，即這是否是對優生學的眨眼提及，因為斯威尼的“哇哇哇”的美貌：瘦削、金發、藍眼睛、大乳房。爭議發生後，American Eagle 在 2025 年 9 月的聲明中表示，“‘Sydney Sweeney Has Great Jeans’始終是關於牛仔褲的。” （斯威尼沒有回應 NPR 的置評請求。）　關於這則廣告是關於牛仔褲還是關於基因的爭論中，並沒有對斯威尼所穿的美國之鷹牛仔褲的實際製造者（例如工人）進行任何重要的反思。大多數服裝工廠都在亞洲運營，因此大多數美國人永遠不會見到製作衣服的工人，也不會看到製作衣服的條件。　工人們喜歡那個單親媽媽。她要求我們用 S.（她名字的首字母）稱呼她，因為她擔心如果她的身份被曝光，她工作的服裝廠的老闆會解僱她。 「如果你提高聲音，他們就會把你趕出去，」她說。 “我們很無助。”　S. 是一名年輕女性，在一家名為 Artistic Garment Industries 的公司經營的工廠工作，她說她每月的工資約為 144 美元，這筆錢可以養活她的兒子和母親。　她說工廠「悶熱難受」。我們見到她時，外面的溫度是華氏 106 度，她說工廠裡面更熱。她說，離開工作台喝水很困難，因為她必須完成生產目標。她說她每天必須檢查 1,000 到 1,600 件衣服的品質 - 今年她已經暈倒了 3 次。 「我感到頭暈，幾乎無法站立。我的手腳沒有力氣，」S. 說。 「他們甚至不讓我們坐下。」但 S. 說她沒有其他選擇。　Artistic Garment Industries 證實它為 American Eagle 生產衣服，但告訴 NPR，它不會驅逐那些抱怨工作條件的工人。該公司表示，它有一個強大的投訴系統可供工人使用，並表示它經常檢查工廠不同區域的溫度。　在回答 NPR 向 American Eagle 提出的問題時，該公司表示“致力於與我們的供應商直接合作，以保護工人的健康、安全和權利。我們非常重視工人以及接受 NPR 採訪的人提出的擔憂。”　S. 是我們在春季和夏季在孟加拉和巴基斯坦採訪的約 20 名工人之一，這兩個國家是中國以外最大的全球服裝生產中心。這些男人和女人在五個不同的工廠工作。所有這些工人都要求 NPR 不要使用他們的全名，而只使用他們名字的首字母，擔心如果他們的身份被發現，他們會失去工作或被列入未來工作的黑名單。　儘管我們關注的是 Sweeney 在 2025 年廣告活動中穿著的 American Eagle 牛仔褲，但該報導引發了一個更大的問題：時尚的製作速度有多快，因為服裝工廠同時為多個品牌生產衣服。我們遇到的工人告訴我們，他們為 Levi's、Massimo Dutti、The Gap、H&M 和 American Eagle 製作服裝。他們表示，工廠裡都知道他們為哪些品牌生產衣服，部分原因是一些工人負責縫製標籤。　我們採訪的服裝工人提供了驚人相似的說法。他們在勞工和氣候權利組織的多份報告中呼應了工人的證詞。工人們告訴我們，他們的工資很低，儘管他們預計要達到他們所說的不合理的高生產目標，而且經常在悶熱的工廠裡勞動。　這些生產目標包括每小時縫製 200 個袖子或每天檢查 1000 件衣服的品質。我們採訪的工人表示，他們無法適當補充水分或降溫，儘管氣候變遷引起的極端高溫使他們的工作場所和家變得更加炎熱。　康乃爾大學全球勞工研究所執行長賈森賈德（Jason Judd）表示，工廠內的溫度可能會高出四到六度，該研究所研究了服裝廠和工人住宅內的熱量。 “你有這麼多的身體，所有的材料，所有的機器都會散發熱量。你有通風問題。”　「我們開始看到昏厥、中暑、慢性病惡化，甚至死亡，」氣候權利國際研究員卡拉舒爾特說。她撰寫了兩份關於高溫對製衣工人影響的報告。　舒爾特表示，工人們為了達到生產目標而承受巨大的壓力。一個主要原因是品牌要求其供應商在緊迫的期限內生產大量服裝，並且利潤微薄。她說，服裝工人很容易受到高溫的影響，因為他們聚集在孟加拉和巴基斯坦等國家。她引用聯合國出版物稱，這些工廠“位於升溫速度快於全球平均水平的地區，[已經]非常炎熱和潮濕。”　H&M 是工人確認製造的品牌之一，該公司表示，它“付出了巨大努力”，以確保向供應商公平付款，並且勞動力成本“被排除在我們產品訂單的價格談判之外”，以確保工人工資不會被壓低。　氣候權利國際組織的舒爾特引述她自己的研究表示，製衣工人被迫冒著健康風險才能生存。她說，這不是一個選擇。 「工人們不會選擇承擔這些風險，」她說。 “他們是因為貧窮才被迫這麼做的。”"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6013327/sydney-sweeney-jeans-american-eagle-garment-industry"}, {"code": "20261116-3", "ch": "2026-11-16　週一", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "New Orleans port sues owners of tanker involved in Mississippi crash　／　新奧爾良港起訴參與密西西比事故的油輪船東", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Ava Pukatch，全文共 12 段、21 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：官員們正在向上週撞上遊輪的油輪船東尋求至少 100 萬美元的損失。由於沒有造成人員傷亡，這一事件被稱為「密西西比河奇蹟」。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6041677/new-orleans-port-sues-miracle-mississippi-cruise-ship"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "新奧爾良港口官員對週五在密西西比河撞上一艘停靠的遊輪的油輪的所有者和…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "New Orleans port officials filed a lawsuit against the owner and operator of the tanker that crashed into a docked cruise ship in the Mississippi River on Friday.", "zh": "新奧爾良港口官員對週五在密西西比河撞上一艘停靠的遊輪的油輪的所有者和經營者提起訴訟。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "新奧爾良港委員會正在向這艘名為「大西洋瀝青」的油輪相關人員尋求至少 …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The Board of Commissioners of the Port of New Orleans is seeking at least $1 million in damages from people connected to the tanker, which is called Atlantic Asphalt.", "zh": "新奧爾良港委員會正在向這艘名為「大西洋瀝青」的油輪相關人員尋求至少 100 萬美元的損失賠償。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The lawsuit also names the tanker's owner, Nave Shipping SA and its management company Thome Ship Management as defendants.", "zh": "該訴訟還將油輪船東 Nave Shipping SA 及其管理公司 Thome Ship Management 列為被告。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "訴訟稱，中午 12:30週五，大西洋瀝青油輪撞上了美國傳統河遊輪明輪…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "The lawsuit states that at 12:30 p.m.", "zh": "訴訟稱，中午 12:30"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Friday, the Atlantic Asphalt tanker crashed into the American Heritage river cruise paddleboat which was docked at the Thalia Street terminal for disembarkment of passengers.", "zh": "週五，大西洋瀝青油輪撞上了美國傳統河遊輪明輪船，該船停靠在塔利亞街碼頭供乘客下船。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "截至週六，仍有八人留在醫院，其中兩人傷勢嚴重。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "As of Saturday, eight people remained in the hospital, two in serious condition.", "zh": "截至週六，仍有八人留在醫院，其中兩人傷勢嚴重。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "莫雷諾市長週六表示，大西洋瀝青已被拖離現場，但他指出，完全清除美國遺…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Mayor Moreno said Saturday that the Atlantic Asphalt had been towed away from the site, but noted it could take weeks to fully remove the American Heritage.", "zh": "莫雷諾市長週六表示，大西洋瀝青已被拖離現場，但他指出，完全清除美國遺產可能需要數週。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "海岸防衛隊上尉梅蘭妮·伯納姆 (Melanie Burnham) 表…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Coast Guard Capt.", "zh": "海岸警衛隊隊長"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Melanie Burnham said that operations were now focused on fully reopening the river and safe removal of hazardous material on board the American Heritage.", "zh": "梅蘭妮·伯納姆 (Melanie Burnham) 表示，目前行動的重點是完全重新開放河流以及安全清除「美國遺產」號上的有害物質。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Burnham said it is estimated there are 160,000 gallons of fuel on board the ship.", "zh": "伯納姆表示，估計船上有 16 萬加侖的燃料。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "伯納姆說：“我們將讓潛水員進入水中，這樣他們就可以對清除它的正確路徑…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "\"We're going to have divers in the water so they can do a full assessment on what's the right path to be able to remove it,\" Burnham said.", "zh": "伯納姆說：“我們將讓潛水員進入水中，這樣他們就可以對清除它的正確路徑進行全面評估。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"We also have teams that have been deployed throughout the entire area, the river system to monitor the area for any pollution.\"", "zh": "“我們還在整個地區和河流系統部署了團隊，以監測該地區是否有任何污染。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "伯納姆說，密西西比河沿岸的船隻交通受到限制。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Burnham said there are restrictions in place for boat traffic along the Mississippi River.", "zh": "伯納姆說，密西西比河沿岸的船隻交通受到限制。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "墜機的確切原因尚不清楚，但伯納姆表示，油輪似乎有轉向問題。美國國家運…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "The exact cause of the crash is unknown, though Burnham said the tanker appeared to have an issue with steering.", "zh": "墜機的確切原因尚不清楚，但伯納姆表示，油輪似乎有轉向問題。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The National Transportation Safety Board is investigating the crash.", "zh": "美國國家運輸安全委員會正在調查這起事故。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "美國國家運輸安全委員會 (NTSB) 董事會成員約翰·德利烏 (Jo…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "John DeLeeuw, board member with the NTSB, said during a Saturday briefing that the tanker's voyage data recorder was recovered.", "zh": "美國國家運輸安全委員會 (NTSB) 董事會成員約翰·德利烏 (John DeLeeuw) 在周六的新聞發布會上表示，油輪的航行數據記錄器已被找到。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "「航程數據記錄器本質上是提供數據，」DeLeeuw 說。 “它就像飛…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "\"The voyage data recorder essentially is going to provide the data,\" DeLeeuw said.", "zh": "「航程數據記錄器本質上是提供數據，」DeLeeuw 說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"It's like a flight data recorder on an aircraft.", "zh": "「這就像飛機上的飛行數據記錄器。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We can look at speeds and all kinds of information.", "zh": "我們可以查看速度和各種資訊。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's essentially covering speed all kinds of maneuverings that was done on the ship.\"", "zh": "它本質上涵蓋了在船上進行的各種機動的速度。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "NTSB 預計將在 30 天內發布初步報告，有關可能原因和安全建議的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "A preliminary report by the NTSB is expected within 30 days, with the final report on probable causes and safety recommendations coming in 18 to 24 months.", "zh": "NTSB 預計將在 30 天內發布初步報告，有關可能原因和安全建議的最終報告將在 18 至 24 個月內發布。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "新奧爾良港口官員對週五在密西西比河撞上一艘停靠的遊輪的油輪的所有者和經營者提起訴訟。　新奧爾良港委員會正在向這艘名為「大西洋瀝青」的油輪相關人員尋求至少 100 萬美元的損失賠償。該訴訟還將油輪船東 Nave Shipping SA 及其管理公司 Thome Ship Management 列為被告。　訴訟稱，中午 12:30週五，大西洋瀝青油輪撞上了美國傳統河遊輪明輪船，該船停靠在塔利亞街碼頭供乘客下船。　截至週六，仍有八人留在醫院，其中兩人傷勢嚴重。　莫雷諾市長週六表示，大西洋瀝青已被拖離現場，但他指出，完全清除美國遺產可能需要數週。　海岸防衛隊上尉梅蘭妮·伯納姆 (Melanie Burnham) 表示，目前行動的重點是完全重新開放河流以及安全清除「美國遺產」號上的危險物質。伯納姆表示，估計船上有 16 萬加侖的燃料。　伯納姆說：“我們將讓潛水員進入水中，這樣他們就可以對清除它的正確路徑進行全面評估。” “我們還在整個地區和河流系統部署了團隊，以監測該地區是否有任何污染。”　伯納姆說，密西西比河沿岸的船隻交通受到限制。　墜機的確切原因尚不清楚，但伯納姆表示，油輪似乎有轉向問題。美國國家運輸安全委員會正在調查這起事故。　美國國家運輸安全委員會 (NTSB) 董事會成員約翰·德利烏 (John DeLeeuw) 在周六的新聞發布會上表示，油輪的航行數據記錄器已被找到。　「航程數據記錄器本質上是提供數據，」DeLeeuw 說。 “它就像飛機上的飛行數據記錄器。我們可以查看速度和各種資訊。它本質上涵蓋了船上進行的各種操縱的速度。”　NTSB 預計將在 30 天內發布初步報告，有關可能原因和安全建議的最終報告將在 18 至 24 個月內發布。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6041677/new-orleans-port-sues-miracle-mississippi-cruise-ship"}, {"code": "20261115-1", "ch": "2026-11-15　週日", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "FAA ground stop disrupts college football", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Chandelis Duster，全文共 6 段、15 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：Some college football games were delayed a few hours on Saturday or postponed to Sunday. And in Oklahoma at least, there will be perks for fans to make up for the inconvenience, including cheap beers."}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/14/nx-s1-6041115/faa-ground-stop-college-football-delays"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "美國聯邦航空管理局週五的地面停飛不僅導致了旅行的麻煩，還導致了大學體…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The Federal Aviation Administration's ground stop on Friday has led not only to travel **headaches**, but also schedule changes and delays in college sports.", "zh": "美國聯邦航空管理局週五的地面停飛不僅導致了旅行的麻煩，還導致了大學體育賽程的改變和延誤。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "週五，許多大學橄欖球隊在機場前往即將舉行的比賽，當時全國各地的地面停…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Many college football teams were in airports Friday on their way to upcoming games when the **nationwide** ground stop was issued and thousands of flights were canceled.", "zh": "週五，許多大學橄欖球隊在機場前往即將舉行的比賽，當時**全國**各地的地面停止發布，數千個航班被取消。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The FAA on Saturday said airports were returning to normal operations, but that delays and **cancellations** would continue through the day.", "zh": "美國聯邦航空局週六表示，機場正在恢復正常運營，但延誤和取消將持續一整天。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "大學橄欖球季後賽排名第二的猶他州隊將於晚上 8:30 在圖森對陣亞利…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Utah, ranked No. 2 in the College Football Playoff Rankings, will kick off against Arizona in Tucson at 8:30 p.m. local time — a three-hour delay. The Auburn vs.", "zh": "大學橄欖球季後賽排名第二的猶他州隊將於晚上 8:30 在圖森對陣亞利桑那州隊。當地時間－晚點三小時。奧本 vs."}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mississippi State game was pushed back more than four hours to start at 3:15 p.m. local time in Mississippi because of the ground stop.", "zh": "密西西比州的比賽推遲了四個多小時，於下午 3 點 15 分開始。由於地面停止，密西西比州當地時間。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The Florida Atlantic Owls were also unable to fly to Oklahoma on Friday ahead of their game against the Tulsa Golden Hurricane.", "zh": "週五，佛羅裡達大西洋貓頭鷹隊在對陣塔爾薩黃金颶風隊的比賽之前也無法飛往俄克拉荷馬州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Saturday's game, which was supposed to begin at 2:30 p.m. local time, was moved to 6:15 p.m. local time.", "zh": "週六的比賽原定於下午 2:30 開始。當地時間，移至下午 6 點 15 分。當地時間。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "雖然其他大學球隊能夠在周六抵達目的地並繼續比賽，但密西西比大學卻沒有…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "While other college teams were able to arrive at their destinations and proceed with games on Saturday, the University of Mississippi did not.", "zh": "雖然其他大學球隊能夠在周六抵達目的地並繼續比賽，但密西西比大學卻沒有。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "排名第19的密西西比大學未能按計劃於週五飛往俄克拉荷馬州與俄克拉荷馬…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Ole Miss, ranked No. 19, was not able to fly to Oklahoma as planned on Friday for its **matchup** with the University of Oklahoma Sooners.", "zh": "排名第19的密西西比大學未能按計劃於週五飛往俄克拉荷馬州與俄克拉荷馬大學捷者隊進行比賽。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The game between the two teams, which was scheduled to occur Saturday, will now take place on Sunday at 1 p.m.", "zh": "兩支球隊之間的比賽原定於週六舉行，現在將於週日下午 1 點舉行。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "ET, according to the Southeastern Conference.", "zh": "ET，根據東南會議。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The game will compete with several NFL games that will be **televised** at the same time.", "zh": "這場比賽將與幾場同時**電視轉播的** NFL 比賽競爭。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "NFL teams were largely **unaffected** by the ground stop.", "zh": "NFL 球隊基本上沒有受到地面停車的影響。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "為了幫助緩解球迷的沮喪情緒，Sooners 週六宣佈為重新安排的比賽…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "In order to help **alleviate** fans' **frustration**, the Sooners on Saturday announced \"fan appreciation\" promotions for the **rescheduled** game.", "zh": "為了幫助緩解球迷的沮喪情緒，Sooners 週六宣佈為**重新安排**的比賽進行「球迷答謝」促銷活動。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Oklahoma students can go to the game for free with their student ID and there will be reduced prices on **concession** items such as $2 for **popcorn** or a 16-**ounce** beer.", "zh": "俄克拉荷馬州的學生可以憑學生證免費觀看比賽，並且可以享受優惠商品的折扣，例如 2 美元的**爆米花**或 16 **盎司**的啤酒。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "美國聯邦航空管理局週五的地面停飛不僅導致了旅行的麻煩，還導致了大學體育賽程的改變和延誤。　週五，許多大學橄欖球隊在機場前往即將舉行的比賽，當時全國各地的地面停止發布，數千個航班被取消。美國聯邦航空局週六表示，機場正在恢復正常運營，但延誤和取消將持續一整天。　大學橄欖球季後賽排名第二的猶他州隊將於晚上 8:30 在圖森對陣亞利桑那州隊。當地時間－晚點三小時。奧本大學對陣密西西比州立大學的比賽推遲了四個多小時，於下午 3 點 15 分開始。由於地面停止，密西西比州當地時間。週五，佛羅裡達大西洋貓頭鷹隊在對陣塔爾薩黃金颶風隊的比賽之前也無法飛往俄克拉荷馬州。週六的比賽原定於下午 2:30 開始。當地時間，移至下午 6 點 15 分。當地時間。　雖然其他大學球隊能夠在周六抵達目的地並繼續比賽，但密西西比大學卻沒有。　排名第19的密西西比大學未能按計劃於週五飛往俄克拉荷馬州與俄克拉荷馬大學捷者隊進行比賽。兩支球隊之間的比賽原定於週六舉行，現在將於週日下午 1 點舉行。 ET，根據東南會議。這場比賽將與幾場同時電視轉播的 NFL 比賽競爭。 NFL 球隊基本上沒有受到地面停車的影響。　為了幫助緩解球迷的沮喪情緒，Sooners 週六宣佈為重新安排的比賽進行「球迷答謝」促銷活動。俄克拉荷馬州的學生可以憑學生證免費觀看比賽，並且可以享受優惠商品的折扣，例如 2 美元的爆米花或 16 盎司的啤酒。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "rescheduled", "sf": "rescheduled", "pos": "v.", "zh": "重新安排", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　To schedule again or at a different time.　|　本文例句　In order to help alleviate fans' frustration, the Sooners on Saturday announced \"fan appreciation\" promotions for the rescheduled game.　|　例句中譯　為了幫助緩解球迷的沮喪情緒，Sooners 週六宣佈為重新安排的比賽進行「球迷答謝」促銷活動。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "unaffected", "sf": "unaffected", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "不受影響", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　恝、爛漫、真率　|　英英定義　(very rare) To not affect.　|　本文例句　NFL teams were largely unaffected by the ground stop.　|　例句中譯　NFL 球隊基本上沒有受到地面停車的影響。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "matchup", "sf": "matchup", "pos": "n.", "zh": "對決", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A pairing of two things, people or teams, especially for a competition　|　本文例句　19, was not able to fly to Oklahoma as planned on Friday for its matchup with the University of Oklahoma Sooners.　|　例句中譯　19日，他未能按計劃飛往俄克拉荷馬州參加週五與俄克拉荷馬大學快人隊的比賽。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "alleviate", "sf": "alleviate", "pos": "v.", "zh": "減輕", "syn": "address, allay, ameliorate", "tip": "其他意思　和緩、緩和　|　英英定義　To make less severe, as a pain or difficulty.　|　本文例句　In order to help alleviate fans' frustration, the Sooners on Saturday announced \"fan appreciation\" promotions for the rescheduled game.　|　例句中譯　為了幫助緩解球迷的沮喪情緒，Sooners 週六宣佈為重新安排的比賽進行「球迷答謝」促銷活動。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "televised", "sf": "televised", "pos": "v.", "zh": "電視轉播的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　廣播　|　英英定義　To broadcast, or be broadcast, by television　|　本文例句　The game will compete with several NFL games that will be televised at the same time.　|　例句中譯　這場比賽將與幾場同時電視轉播的 NFL 比賽競爭。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "concession", "sf": "concession", "pos": "n.", "zh": "讓步", "syn": "franchise, tithe", "tip": "英英定義　The act of conceding.　|　本文例句　Oklahoma students can go to the game for free with their student ID and there will be reduced prices on concession items such as $2 for popcorn or a 16-ounce beer.　|　例句中譯　俄克拉荷馬州的學生可以憑學生證免費觀看比賽，並且可以享受優惠商品的折扣，例如 2 美元的爆米花或 16 盎司的啤酒。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "popcorn", "sf": "popcorn", "pos": "n.", "zh": "爆米花", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　爆豆　|　英英定義　A snack food made from corn/maize kernels popped by dry heating.　|　本文例句　Oklahoma students can go to the game for free with their student ID and there will be reduced prices on concession items such as $2 for popcorn or a 16-ounce beer.　|　例句中譯　俄克拉荷馬州的學生可以憑學生證免費觀看比賽，並且可以享受優惠商品的折扣，例如 2 美元的爆米花或 16 盎司的啤酒。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "cancellation", "sf": "cancellations", "pos": "n.", "zh": "消除", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　消去、注銷戳　|　英英定義　The act, process, or result of cancelling; as, the cancellation of certain words in a contract, or of the contract itself.　|　本文例句　The FAA on Saturday said airports were returning to normal operations, but that delays and cancellations would continue through the day.　|　例句中譯　美國聯邦航空局週六表示，機場正在恢復正常運營，但延誤和取消將持續一整天。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "ounce", "sf": "ounce", "pos": "n.", "zh": "盎司", "syn": "℥", "tip": "其他意思　兩、啢　|　英英定義　An avoirdupois ounce, weighing 1/16 of an avoirdupois pound, or 28.3495 grams.　|　本文例句　Oklahoma students can go to the game for free with their student ID and there will be reduced prices on concession items such as $2 for popcorn or a 16-ounce beer.　|　例句中譯　俄克拉荷馬州的學生可以憑學生證免費觀看比賽，並且可以享受優惠商品的折扣，例如 2 美元的爆米花或 16 盎司的啤酒。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "frustration", "sf": "frustration", "pos": "n.", "zh": "挫折", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　挫敗　|　英英定義　The feeling of annoyance when one's actions are criticized or hindered　|　本文例句　In order to help alleviate fans' frustration, the Sooners on Saturday announced \"fan appreciation\" promotions for the rescheduled game.　|　例句中譯　為了幫助緩解球迷的沮喪情緒，Sooners 週六宣佈為重新安排的比賽進行「球迷答謝」促銷活動。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "headache", "sf": "headaches", "pos": "n.", "zh": "頭痛", "syn": "bother, pain in the neck, cephalalgia", "tip": "其他意思　頭疼　|　英英定義　A pain or ache in the head.　|　本文例句　The Federal Aviation Administration's ground stop on Friday has led not only to travel headaches, but also schedule changes and delays in college sports.　|　例句中譯　美國聯邦航空管理局週五的地面停飛不僅導致了旅行的麻煩，還導致了大學體育賽程的改變和延誤。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "nationwide", "sf": "nationwide", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "全國", "syn": "countrywide, national", "tip": "其他意思　全國性的　|　英英定義　Extending throughout an entire nation.　|　本文例句　Many college football teams were in airports Friday on their way to upcoming games when the nationwide ground stop was issued and thousands of flights were canceled.　|　例句中譯　週五，許多大學橄欖球隊在機場前往即將舉行的比賽，當時全國各地的地面停止發布，數千個航班被取消。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/14/nx-s1-6041115/faa-ground-stop-college-football-delays"}, {"code": "20261115-2", "ch": "2026-11-15　週日", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Florida city cancels St. Patrick's Day parade, citing new anti-DEI law　／　佛羅裡達市援引新的反 DEI 法取消聖派翠克節遊行", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Marissa J. Lang，全文共 10 段、24 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：佛羅裡達州的一項新法律禁止納稅人的錢用於多元化計劃，這促使德雷比奇取消了舉辦近 60 年的聖派翠克節遊行。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/14/nx-s1-6041093/st-patricks-day-parade-canceled-florida-dei"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "佛羅裡達州一項新法律禁止納稅人的資金用於多元化計劃，該法律的首批受害…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "One of the first casualties of a new Florida law that **prohibits** taxpayer dollars from going toward diversity initiatives is a St.", "zh": "佛羅裡達州一項新法律**禁止**納稅人的錢用於多元化計劃，該法律的首批受害者之一是聖路易斯。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Patrick's Day parade in a beach town that has been celebrating its Irish American community for nearly 60 years.", "zh": "聖派翠克節遊行在海濱小鎮舉行，該小鎮近 60 年來一直在慶祝愛爾蘭裔美國人社區。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "德爾雷海灘 (Delray Beach) 是佛羅裡達州東南部的一個社…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The city lawyer for Delray Beach, a community in southeast Florida with **picturesque** beaches and a historic downtown, told the mayor that any government-sponsored celebrations of culture, ethnicity or heritage that are not a national holiday (for example: Independence Day) could run **afoul** of the new **anti-DEI** law.", "zh": "德爾雷海灘 (Delray Beach) 是佛羅裡達州東南部的一個社區，擁有風景**如畫**的海灘和歷史悠久的市中心，該市的律師告訴市長，政府主辦的任何非國定假日（例如獨立日）的文化、種族或遺產慶祝活動都可能違反新的反 DEI 法。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So, Mayor Tom Carney said, he made the difficult decision to cancel one of the city's biggest events of the year.", "zh": "因此，市長湯姆·卡尼表示，他做出了取消該市今年最大活動之一的艱難決定。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "「我們應該慶祝這些類型的活動，因為在這個國家，人們可以舉辦這些活動。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"These types of events we should be celebrating because in this country, people can have these events.", "zh": "「我們應該慶祝這些類型的活動，因為在這個國家，人們可以舉辦這些活動。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In other countries, you can't do this.", "zh": "在其他國家，你不能這樣做。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We have great freedoms here,\" he said.", "zh": "我們在這裡有很大的自由，」他說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"And if the community wants something and it's not against public policy then I would support them to do it if they're using private dollars.", "zh": "「如果社區想要某些東西並且不違反公共政策，那麼如果他們使用私人資金，我會支持他們這樣做。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "If we can do it, we should do it.\"", "zh": "如果我们能做到，我们就应该这么做。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "僅在 NPR 上報導川普的平等就業機會委員會如何攻擊 DEI 並強調…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Only on NPR How Trump's EEOC is attacking DEI and **emphasizing** white people Carney, who is of Irish descent, said the parade was privately run until about eight years ago — so returning to a **private-sponsorship** model would be a **callback** to the parade's origins.", "zh": "僅在 NPR 上報導川普的平等就業機會委員會如何攻擊 DEI 並**強調**白人 有愛爾蘭血統的卡尼表示，遊行直到大約八年前都是私人舉辦的，因此回到**私人贊助**模式將是對遊行起源的回調。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "His own family, he said, was involved in keeping the parade going during the 1980s and 1990s.", "zh": "他說，他自己的家人參與了 20 世紀 80 年代和 90 年代遊行的維持。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "德爾雷海灘官員表示，他們收到了大量選民的電子郵件、電話和社交媒體訊息…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Delray Beach officials said they have been **inundated** with emails, calls and social media messages from constituents who are angry that the community's decades-long celebration had been axed.", "zh": "德爾雷海灘官員表示，他們收到了大量選民的電子郵件、電話和社交媒體訊息，他們對社區長達數十年的慶祝活動被取消感到憤怒。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "「這對我來說是一種行動號召，」卡尼說。 “社區真的想要擁有它，所以我…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "\"It was kind of a call to action to me,\" Carney said.", "zh": "「這對我來說是一種行動號召，」卡尼說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The community really wants to have it, so we should go ahead and have it, we just need to get it privately funded.\"", "zh": "“社區真的想要擁有它，所以我們應該繼續擁有它，我們只需要得到私人資助。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "The governor, meanwhile, has accused Delray Beach of weaponizing the new **anti-DEI** measure to make a political point.", "zh": "同時，州長指責德雷比奇將新的反 DEI 措施武器化，以表達政治觀點。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "DeSantis said the city was \"engaging in \"**malicious** compliance\" in a message he posted on X following the city's cancellation announcement.", "zh": "德桑蒂斯在該市宣布取消後，在 X 上發布的一條消息中表示，該市「參與了『惡意合規』」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "“他们所做的事情不是佛罗里达州法律规定的，”州长写道。 “這只是試圖…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "\"What they are doing is not mandated by Florida law,\" the governor wrote.", "zh": "「他們所做的事情不是佛羅裡達州法律規定的，」州長寫道。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"It's just an attempt to make a political point — a point that legacy media will no doubt try to **amplify**.", "zh": "「這只是試圖表達一個政治觀點——傳統媒體無疑會試圖**放大**這一觀點。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We've seen these stunts throughout the years. Rinse and repeat.\"", "zh": "多年來我們已經看到了這些特技。沖洗並重複。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "The mayor said the city is merely trying to stay out of trouble with the law.", "zh": "市長表示，該市只是想避免觸犯法律。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The measure, SB1134, **asserts** that any official that violates the provision could face civil or legal consequences.", "zh": "這項名為 SB1134 的措施聲稱，任何違反該規定的官員都可能面臨民事或法律後果。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "「這項立法產生了意想不到的後果。州長可能真的相信他所相信的，我相信他…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "\"The legislation has **unintended** consequences.", "zh": "「該立法產生了意想不到的後果。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The governor may genuinely believe what he believes and I take him at his word; our city attorney came up with a different conclusion,\" Carney said.", "zh": "州長可能真的相信他所相信的，我相信他的話；我們的市檢察官得出了不同的結論，」卡尼說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"I'm going to leave it at that.\"", "zh": "“我就這樣吧。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "佛羅裡達州一項新法律禁止納稅人的資金用於多元化計劃，該法律的首批受害者之一是在一個海濱小鎮舉行的聖帕特里克節遊行，該小鎮近 60 年來一直在慶祝愛爾蘭裔美國人社區。　德爾雷海灘 (Delray Beach) 是佛羅裡達州東南部的一個社區，擁有風景如畫的海灘和歷史悠久的市中心，該市的律師告訴市長，政府主辦的任何非國定假日（例如獨立日）的文化、種族或遺產慶祝活動都可能違反新的反 DEI 法。因此，市長湯姆·卡尼表示，他做出了取消該市今年最大活動之一的艱難決定。　「我們應該慶祝這些類型的活動，因為在這個國家，人們可以舉辦這些活動。在其他國家，你不能這樣做。我們在這裡有很大的自由，」他說。 “如果社區想要某些東西，並且不違反公共政策，那麼如果他們使用私人資金，我會支持他們這樣做。如果我們能做到，我們就應該這樣做。”　僅在 NPR 上報導川普的平等就業機會委員會如何攻擊 DEI 並強調白人 有愛爾蘭血統的卡尼表示，遊行直到大約八年前都是私人舉辦的，因此回到私人贊助模式將是對遊行起源的回調。他說，他自己的家人參與了 20 世紀 80 年代和 90 年代遊行的維持。　德爾雷海灘官員表示，他們收到了大量選民的電子郵件、電話和社交媒體訊息，他們對社區長達數十年的慶祝活動被取消感到憤怒。　「這對我來說是一種行動號召，」卡尼說。 “社區真的想要擁有它，所以我們應該繼續擁有它，我們只需要得到私人資助。”　“他们所做的事情不是佛罗里达州法律规定的，”州长写道。 “這只是試圖表達一個政治觀點——傳統媒體無疑會試圖放大這一觀點。這些年來我們已經看到了這些噱頭。沖洗並重複。”　「這項立法產生了意想不到的後果。州長可能真的相信他所相信的，我相信他的話；我們的城市檢察官得出了不同的結論，」卡尼說。 “我就這樣吧。”"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "afoul", "sf": "afoul", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "犯規", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　(principally nautical) In a state of collision or entanglement.　|　本文例句　The city lawyer for Delray Beach, a community in southeast Florida with picturesque beaches and a historic downtown, told the mayor that any government-sponsored celebrations of culture, ethnicity or heritage that are not a national holiday (for example: Independence Day) could run afoul of the new anti-DEI law.　|　例句中譯　德爾雷海灘 (Delray Beach) 是佛羅裡達州東南部的一個社區，擁有風景如畫的海灘和歷史悠久的市中心，該市的律師告訴市長，政府主辦的任何非國定假日（例如獨立日）的文化、種族或遺產慶祝活動都可能違反新的反 DEI 法。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "callback", "sf": "callback", "pos": "n.", "zh": "打回來", "syn": "running gag", "tip": "英英定義　The return of a situation to a previous position or state.　|　本文例句　Only on NPR How Trump's EEOC is attacking DEI and emphasizing white people Carney, who is of Irish descent, said the parade was privately run until about eight years ago — so returning to a private-sponsorship model would be a callback to the parade's origins.　|　例句中譯　僅在 NPR 上報導川普的平等就業機會委員會如何攻擊 DEI 並強調白人 有愛爾蘭血統的卡尼表示，遊行直到大約八年前都是私人舉辦的，因此回到私人贊助模式將是對遊行起源的回調。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "inundated", "sf": "inundated", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "被淹沒", "syn": "beflood, deluge, flood", "tip": "其他意思　湮　|　英英定義　To cover with large amounts of water; to flood.　|　本文例句　Delray Beach officials said they have been inundated with emails, calls and social media messages from constituents who are angry that the community's decades-long celebration had been axed.　|　例句中譯　德爾雷海灘官員表示，他們收到了大量選民的電子郵件、電話和社交媒體訊息，他們對社區長達數十年的慶祝活動被取消感到憤怒。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "amplify", "sf": "amplify", "pos": "v.", "zh": "放大", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　擴大、衍　|　英英定義　To render larger, more extended, or more intense.　|　本文例句　\"It's just an attempt to make a political point — a point that legacy media will no doubt try to amplify.　|　例句中譯　「這只是試圖表達一個政治觀點——傳統媒體無疑會試圖放大這一觀點。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "anti-dei", "sf": "anti-DEI", "pos": "", "zh": "反德伊", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　The governor, meanwhile, has accused Delray Beach of weaponizing the new anti-DEI measure to make a political point.　|　例句中譯　同時，州長指責德雷比奇將新的反 DEI 措施武器化，以表達政治觀點。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "unintended", "sf": "unintended", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "無意的", "syn": "incidental, unintentional", "tip": "英英定義　Not intended; unplanned　|　本文例句　\"The legislation has unintended consequences.　|　例句中譯　「該立法產生了意想不到的後果。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "picturesque", "sf": "picturesque", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "如畫", "syn": "quaint, scenic", "tip": "其他意思　獨特的　|　英英定義　Resembling or worthy of a picture or painting; having the qualities of a picture or painting; pleasingly beautiful.　|　本文例句　The city lawyer for Delray Beach, a community in southeast Florida with picturesque beaches and a historic downtown, told the mayor that any government-sponsored celebrations of culture, ethnicity or heritage that are not a national holiday (for example: Independence Day) could run afoul of the new anti-DEI law.　|　例句中譯　德爾雷海灘 (Delray Beach) 是佛羅裡達州東南部的一個社區，擁有風景如畫的海灘和歷史悠久的市中心，該市的律師告訴市長，政府主辦的任何非國定假日（例如獨立日）的文化、種族或遺產慶祝活動都可能違反新的反 DEI 法。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "prohibit", "sf": "prohibits", "pos": "v.", "zh": "禁止", "syn": "ban, disallow, forbid", "tip": "其他意思　不准、查禁、誡、禁　|　英英定義　To forbid, disallow, or proscribe officially; to make illegal or illicit.　|　本文例句　One of the first casualties of a new Florida law that prohibits taxpayer dollars from going toward diversity initiatives is a St.　|　例句中譯　佛羅裡達州一項新法律禁止納稅人的錢用於多元化計劃，該法律的首批受害者之一是聖路易斯。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "assert", "sf": "asserts", "pos": "v.", "zh": "斷言", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　辯護、居、聲稱　|　英英定義　An assertion; a section of source code which tests whether an expected condition is true.　|　本文例句　The measure, SB1134, asserts that any official that violates the provision could face civil or legal consequences.　|　例句中譯　這項名為 SB1134 的措施聲稱，任何違反該規定的官員都可能面臨民事或法律後果。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "malicious", "sf": "malicious", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "惡意的", "syn": "evil, malevolent", "tip": "其他意思　毒、惡毒、懷惡意的、姦險　|　英英定義　Of, pertaining to, or as a result of malice or spite　|　本文例句　DeSantis said the city was \"engaging in \"malicious compliance\" in a message he posted on X following the city's cancellation announcement.　|　例句中譯　德桑蒂斯在該市宣布取消後，在 X 上發布的一條消息中表示，該市「參與了『惡意合規』」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "emphasize", "sf": "emphasizing", "pos": "v.", "zh": "強調", "syn": "betone, stress, underscore", "tip": "其他意思　硬說、注重　|　英英定義　To stress, give emphasis or extra weight to (something).　|　本文例句　Only on NPR How Trump's EEOC is attacking DEI and emphasizing white people Carney, who is of Irish descent, said the parade was privately run until about eight years ago — so returning to a private-sponsorship model would be a callback to the parade's origins.　|　例句中譯　僅在 NPR 上報導川普的平等就業機會委員會如何攻擊 DEI 並強調白人 有愛爾蘭血統的卡尼表示，遊行直到大約八年前都是私人舉辦的，因此回到私人贊助模式將是對遊行起源的回調。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "private-sponsorship", "sf": "private-sponsorship", "pos": "", "zh": "私人贊助", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　Only on NPR How Trump's EEOC is attacking DEI and emphasizing white people Carney, who is of Irish descent, said the parade was privately run until about eight years ago — so returning to a private-sponsorship model would be a callback to the parade's origins.　|　例句中譯　僅在 NPR 上報導川普的平等就業機會委員會如何攻擊 DEI 並強調白人 有愛爾蘭血統的卡尼表示，遊行直到大約八年前都是私人舉辦的，因此回到私人贊助模式將是對遊行起源的回調。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/14/nx-s1-6041093/st-patricks-day-parade-canceled-florida-dei"}, {"code": "20261115-3", "ch": "2026-11-15　週日", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "US has lost measles elimination status, global health authorities say　／　全球衛生當局稱美國已失去消除麻疹的地位", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Amy Maxmen，全文共 18 段、22 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：直接了解泛美衛生組織審議情況的研究人員表示，美國已經失去了消滅麻疹國家的地位。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/14/nx-s1-6041119/us-measles-elimination-status-vaccines-cdc-paho"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "本篇較長，站上只收前 18 段；想讀完整篇請點上方的 NPR 原文連結。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "美國已經失去了消滅麻疹國家的地位，這是二十五年前的公共衛生勝利。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The U.S. has lost its status as a country where measles is eliminated, a public health triumph secured a quarter century ago.", "zh": "美國已經失去了消滅麻疹國家的地位，這是二十五年前的公共衛生勝利。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "直接了解該國狀況審議情況的研究人員告訴 KFF 健康新聞，泛美衛生組…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Researchers with direct knowledge of the **deliberations** on the country's status told KFF Health News that the Pan American Health Organization reached the conclusion this week: Measles has **reestablished** regular transmission in the country.", "zh": "直接了解該國狀況**審議**情況的研究人員告訴 KFF 健康新聞，泛美衛生組織本週得出結論：麻疹已在該國重新建立正常傳播。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "泛美衛生組織原計劃於 11 月 17 日發佈公告。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "PAHO had planned a public announcement on Nov. 17.", "zh": "泛美衛生組織原計劃於 11 月 17 日發佈公告。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "用公共衛生術語來說，麻疹的消除取決於一個國家的零星疫情在一年內結束。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "In public health **parlance**, measles elimination depends on a country's **sporadic** outbreaks ending within a year.", "zh": "用公共衛生術語來說，麻疹的消除取決於一個國家的零星疫情在一年內結束。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That's no longer happening in the United States.", "zh": "這種情況在美國已不再發生。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "「這是一個非常悲傷的時刻，」流行病學家、美國疾病管制與預防中心前副主…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "\"It's a very sad moment,\" said Anne Schuchat, an epidemiologist and a former deputy director at the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention who was not involved in PAHO's decision.", "zh": "「這是一個非常悲傷的時刻，」流行病學家、美國疾病管制與預防中心前副主任安妮舒查特（Anne Schuchat）說，她沒有參與泛美衛生組織的決定。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "舒查特說：“麻疹會造成很多不必要的痛苦，從高燒、缺勤、缺課到進行性退…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "\"Measles causes so much unnecessary suffering, everything from a high fever and missed work and school to long-term complications like progressive **degenerative** nerve disease and death,\" Schuchat said.", "zh": "舒查特說：“麻疹會造成很多不必要的痛苦，從高燒、缺勤、缺課到進行性退化性神經疾病和死亡等長期併發症。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "麻疹爆發是完全可以預防的：兩劑麻疹-腮腺炎-德國麻疹疫苗可預防約 9…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Measles outbreaks are entirely **preventable**: Two doses of the measles-mumps-rubella vaccine prevent about 97% of infections, so when almost everyone in a community is fully **vaccinated**, the virus can't spread.", "zh": "麻疹爆發是完全可以預防的：兩劑麻疹-腮腺炎-德國麻疹疫苗可預防約 97% 的感染，因此，當社區中幾乎每個人都完全接種疫苗時，病毒就無法傳播。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "過去兩年，美國有超過 830 人因麻疹住院。約翰霍普金斯大學的研究人…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "In the past two years, over 830 people have been hospitalized with measles in the U.S. More than 8,000 people have been **sickened** in outbreaks that have cost roughly $125 million in medical care, public health response, and productivity losses, Johns Hopkins University researchers estimate.", "zh": "過去兩年，美國有超過 830 人因麻疹住院。約翰霍普金斯大學的研究人員估計，麻疹疫情已導致 8,000 多人患病，造成醫療保健、公共衛生應對和生產力損失約 1.25 億美元。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "近幾個月來，各州報告了 13 例與麻疹相關的死亡，其中包括紐約州的一…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "States have reported 13 measles-associated deaths, including a 7-month-old in New York and infants in Pennsylvania and Wisconsin in recent months.", "zh": "近幾個月來，各州報告了 13 例與麻疹相關的死亡，其中包括紐約州的一名 7 個月大的嬰兒以及賓州和威斯康辛州的嬰兒。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Babies typically aren't **vaccinated** before they're a year old.", "zh": "嬰兒通常在一歲前不會接種疫苗。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "泛美衛生組織是一個負責監督美洲健康並與世界衛生組織合作的國際組織，其…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "PAHO, an international group that oversees health in the Americas and works with the World Health Organization, based its assessment on two analyses: one by the CDC and another by an independent group of measles experts.", "zh": "泛美衛生組織是一個負責監督美洲健康並與世界衛生組織合作的國際組織，其評估基於兩項分析：一項由疾病預防控制中心進行，另一項由麻疹專家獨立小組進行。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "六月猶他州疫情爆發超過一年大關後，研究人員預期了這個結論。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Researchers anticipated this conclusion after an outbreak in Utah surpassed the one-year mark in June.", "zh": "六月猶他州疫情爆發超過一年大關後，研究人員預期了這個結論。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "美國衛生與公眾服務部發言人艾米麗·希利亞德 (Emily Hilli…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "A spokesperson for the Department of Health and Human Services, Emily Hilliard, attributed the **resurgence** of measles to **vaccination** gaps that opened years before this administration.", "zh": "美國衛生與公眾服務部發言人艾米麗·希利亞德 (Emily Hilliard) 將麻疹的死灰復燃歸因於本屆政府之前幾年就出現的疫苗接種缺口。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Indeed, rates of childhood **vaccination** have steadily declined since the COVID pandemic started.", "zh": "事實上，自從新冠病毒大流行開始以來，兒童疫苗接種率一直在穩定下降。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "但許多科學家也指責川普政府傳播疫苗錯誤訊息並扼殺對疫情的迅速、強大的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "But many scientists also blame the Trump administration for spreading vaccine **misinformation** and **stifling** a swift, strong response to outbreaks.", "zh": "但許多科學家也指責川普政府傳播疫苗錯誤訊息並扼殺對疫情的迅速、強大的反應。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "例如，政府從州衛生部門運營的兒童免疫計畫中削減了數百萬美元，並終止了…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "For example, the administration cut millions of dollars from children's **immunization** programs run by state health departments and terminated funds for research on vaccine hesitancy.", "zh": "例如，政府從州衛生部門運營的兒童免疫計畫中削減了數百萬美元，並終止了疫苗猶豫研究的資金。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "2025 年 8 月，衛生部長小羅伯特·F·肯尼迪 (Robert …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "After Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. sacked CDC director Susan Monarez in August 2025, she told Congress she was fired because she would not preapprove changes to vaccine recommendations \"without reviewing the evidence.\"", "zh": "2025 年 8 月，衛生部長小羅伯特·F·肯尼迪 (Robert F. Kennedy Jr.) 解雇了疾病預防控制中心 (CDC) 主任蘇珊·莫納雷斯 (Susan Monarez)，她告訴國會，她被解僱是因為她不會「在不審查證據的情況下」預先批准對疫苗建議的修改。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "莫納雷斯補充說，“我們已經看到了三十多年來最大規模的麻疹疫情”，並且…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Monarez added that \"we already have seen the largest measles outbreak in more than 30 years\" and that, \"if vaccine protections are weakened, **preventable** diseases will return.\"", "zh": "莫納雷斯補充說，“我們已經看到了三十多年來最大規模的麻疹疫情”，並且“如果疫苗保護作用減弱，**可預防的**疾病將會捲土重來。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "衛生與公眾服務部和白宮的發言人為政府和甘迺迪辯護，甘迺迪在掌管衛生與…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "Spokespeople for HHS and the White House defended the administration, and Kennedy, who led a prominent anti-vaccine organization before he took the helm at HHS.", "zh": "衛生與公眾服務部和白宮的發言人為政府和甘迺迪辯護，甘迺迪在掌管衛生與公眾服務部之前領導了一個著名的反疫苗組織。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The President and the Secretary have repeatedly encouraged measles **vaccination**, coordinated with states, and facilitated the deployment of vaccine doses across the country,\" White House spokesperson Allison Schuster wrote in an email.", "zh": "白宮發言人艾莉森·舒斯特在一封電子郵件中寫道：“總統和國務卿一再鼓勵麻疹疫苗接種，與各州協調，並促進在全國範圍內部署疫苗劑量。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "三十多年來，聯邦政府一直將麻疹視為一場可以預防的悲劇，大規模的疫情爆…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "For more than three decades, the federal government treated measles as a **preventable** tragedy, with sizable outbreaks triggering national efforts to boost **vaccination** and stop the virus from spreading.", "zh": "三十多年來，聯邦政府一直將麻疹視為一場可以預防的悲劇，大規模的疫情爆發引發了全國加強疫苗接種並阻止病毒傳播的努力。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "美國已經失去了消滅麻疹國家的地位，這是二十五年前的公共衛生勝利。　直接了解該國狀況審議情況的研究人員告訴 KFF 健康新聞，泛美衛生組織本週得出結論：麻疹已在該國重新建立正常傳播。　泛美衛生組織原計劃於 11 月 17 日發佈公告。　用公共衛生術語來說，麻疹的消除取決於一個國家的零星疫情在一年內結束。這種情況在美國已不再發生。　「這是一個非常悲傷的時刻，」流行病學家、美國疾病管制與預防中心前副主任安妮舒查特（Anne Schuchat）說，她沒有參與泛美衛生組織的決定。　舒查特說：“麻疹會造成很多不必要的痛苦，從高燒、缺勤、缺課到進行性退化性神經疾病和死亡等長期併發症。”　麻疹爆發是完全可以預防的：兩劑麻疹-腮腺炎-德國麻疹疫苗可預防約 97% 的感染，因此，當社區中幾乎每個人都完全接種疫苗時，病毒就無法傳播。　過去兩年，美國有超過 830 人因麻疹住院。約翰霍普金斯大學的研究人員估計，麻疹疫情已導致 8,000 多人患病，造成醫療保健、公共衛生應對和生產力損失約 1.25 億美元。　近幾個月來，各州報告了 13 例與麻疹相關的死亡，其中包括紐約州的一名 7 個月大的嬰兒以及賓州和威斯康辛州的嬰兒。嬰兒通常在一歲前不會接種疫苗。　泛美衛生組織是一個負責監督美洲健康並與世界衛生組織合作的國際組織，其評估基於兩項分析：一項由疾病預防控制中心進行，另一項由麻疹專家獨立小組進行。　六月猶他州疫情爆發超過一年大關後，研究人員預期了這個結論。　美國衛生與公眾服務部發言人艾米麗·希利亞德 (Emily Hilliard) 將麻疹的死灰復燃歸因於本屆政府之前幾年就出現的疫苗接種缺口。事實上，自從新冠病毒大流行開始以來，兒童疫苗接種率一直在穩定下降。　但許多科學家也指責川普政府傳播疫苗錯誤訊息並扼殺對疫情的迅速、強大的反應。　例如，政府從州衛生部門運營的兒童免疫計畫中削減了數百萬美元，並終止了疫苗猶豫研究的資金。　2025 年 8 月，衛生部長小羅伯特·F·肯尼迪 (Robert F. Kennedy Jr.) 解雇了疾病預防控制中心 (CDC) 主任蘇珊·莫納雷斯 (Susan Monarez)，她告訴國會，她被解僱是因為她不會「在不審查證據的情況下」預先批准對疫苗建議的修改。　莫納雷斯補充說，“我們已經看到了三十多年來最大規模的麻疹疫情”，並且“如果疫苗保護作用減弱，可預防的疾病將會捲土重來。”　衛生與公眾服務部和白宮的發言人為政府和甘迺迪辯護，甘迺迪在掌管衛生與公眾服務部之前領導了一個著名的反疫苗組織。白宮發言人艾莉森·舒斯特在一封電子郵件中寫道：“總統和國務卿一再鼓勵麻疹疫苗接種，與各州協調，並促進在全國範圍內部署疫苗劑量。”　三十多年來，聯邦政府一直將麻疹視為一場可以預防的悲劇，大規模的疫情爆發引發了全國加強疫苗接種並阻止病毒傳播的努力。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "reestablish", "sf": "reestablished", "pos": "v.", "zh": "重建", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　復興　|　英英定義　To establish again.　|　本文例句　Researchers with direct knowledge of the deliberations on the country's status told KFF Health News that the Pan American Health Organization reached the conclusion this week: Measles has reestablished regular transmission in the country.　|　例句中譯　直接了解該國狀況審議情況的研究人員告訴 KFF 健康新聞，泛美衛生組織本週得出結論：麻疹已在該國重新建立正常傳播。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "sickened", "sf": "sickened", "pos": "v.", "zh": "噁心的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　使作嘔、厭恨　|　英英定義　To make ill.　|　本文例句　More than 8,000 people have been sickened in outbreaks that have cost roughly $125 million in medical care, public health response, and productivity losses, Johns Hopkins University researchers estimate.", "trap": ""}, {"w": "parlance", "sf": "parlance", "pos": "n.", "zh": "說法", "syn": "jargon", "tip": "其他意思　發言　|　英英定義　A certain way of speaking, of using words, especially when it comes to those with a particular job or interest.　|　本文例句　In public health parlance, measles elimination depends on a country's sporadic outbreaks ending within a year.　|　例句中譯　用公共衛生術語來說，麻疹的消除取決於一個國家的零星疫情在一年內結束。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "stifle", "sf": "stifling", "pos": "v.", "zh": "窒息", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　憋、壓制　|　英英定義　A hind knee of various mammals, especially horses.　|　本文例句　But many scientists also blame the Trump administration for spreading vaccine misinformation and stifling a swift, strong response to outbreaks.　|　例句中譯　但許多科學家也指責川普政府傳播疫苗錯誤訊息並扼殺對疫情的迅速、強大的反應。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "degenerative", "sf": "degenerative", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "退化的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Characterized by or causing degeneration.　|　本文例句　\"Measles causes so much unnecessary suffering, everything from a high fever and missed work and school to long-term complications like progressive degenerative nerve disease and death,\" Schuchat said.　|　例句中譯　舒查特說：“麻疹會造成很多不必要的痛苦，從高燒、缺勤、缺課到進行性退化性神經疾病和死亡等長期併發症。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "immunization", "sf": "immunization", "pos": "n.", "zh": "免疫接種", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　The process by which an individual is safely exposed in a controlled manner to a material that is designed to prime their immune system against that material.　|　本文例句　For example, the administration cut millions of dollars from children's immunization programs run by state health departments and terminated funds for research on vaccine hesitancy.　|　例句中譯　例如，政府從州衛生部門運營的兒童免疫計畫中削減了數百萬美元，並終止了疫苗猶豫研究的資金。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "preventable", "sf": "preventable", "pos": "n.", "zh": "可預防的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Something that can be prevented.　|　本文例句　Measles outbreaks are entirely preventable: Two doses of the measles-mumps-rubella vaccine prevent about 97% of infections, so when almost everyone in a community is fully vaccinated, the virus can't spread.　|　例句中譯　麻疹爆發是完全可以預防的：兩劑麻疹-腮腺炎-德國麻疹疫苗可預防約 97% 的感染，因此，當社區中幾乎每個人都完全接種疫苗時，病毒就無法傳播。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "deliberations", "sf": "deliberations", "pos": "n.", "zh": "審議", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　熟思　|　英英定義　The act of deliberating, or of weighing and examining the reasons for and against a choice or measure; careful consideration; mature reflection.　|　本文例句　Researchers with direct knowledge of the deliberations on the country's status told KFF Health News that the Pan American Health Organization reached the conclusion this week: Measles has reestablished regular transmission in the country.　|　例句中譯　直接了解該國狀況審議情況的研究人員告訴 KFF 健康新聞，泛美衛生組織本週得出結論：麻疹已在該國重新建立正常傳播。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "misinformation", "sf": "misinformation", "pos": "n.", "zh": "誤傳", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Information that is incorrect.　|　本文例句　But many scientists also blame the Trump administration for spreading vaccine misinformation and stifling a swift, strong response to outbreaks.　|　例句中譯　但許多科學家也指責川普政府傳播疫苗錯誤訊息並扼殺對疫情的迅速、強大的反應。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "sporadic", "sf": "sporadic", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "零星的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　零落　|　英英定義　(of diseases) occurring in isolated instances; not epidemic.　|　本文例句　In public health parlance, measles elimination depends on a country's sporadic outbreaks ending within a year.　|　例句中譯　用公共衛生術語來說，麻疹的消除取決於一個國家的零星疫情在一年內結束。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "resurgence", "sf": "resurgence", "pos": "n.", "zh": "再起", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　復活　|　英英定義　An instance of something resurging; a renewal of vigor or vitality.　|　本文例句　A spokesperson for the Department of Health and Human Services, Emily Hilliard, attributed the resurgence of measles to vaccination gaps that opened years before this administration.　|　例句中譯　美國衛生與公眾服務部發言人艾米麗·希利亞德 (Emily Hilliard) 將麻疹的死灰復燃歸因於本屆政府之前幾年就出現的疫苗接種缺口。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "vaccinated", "sf": "vaccinated", "pos": "v.", "zh": "已接種疫苗", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Treat with a vaccine to produce immunity against a disease.　|　本文例句　Measles outbreaks are entirely preventable: Two doses of the measles-mumps-rubella vaccine prevent about 97% of infections, so when almost everyone in a community is fully vaccinated, the virus can't spread.　|　例句中譯　麻疹爆發是完全可以預防的：兩劑麻疹-腮腺炎-德國麻疹疫苗可預防約 97% 的感染，因此，當社區中幾乎每個人都完全接種疫苗時，病毒就無法傳播。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/14/nx-s1-6041119/us-measles-elimination-status-vaccines-cdc-paho"}, {"code": "20261114-1", "ch": "2026-11-14　週六", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "GOP state officials push to revive Trump's mail voting restrictions for 2028 election　／　共和黨州官員推動恢復川普對 2028 年大選的郵件投票限制", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Hansi Lo Wang，全文共 7 段、10 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：一些共和黨州官員正在對法院阻止郵政局執行修訂後的投票規則的命令提出上訴，以恢復 2028 年選舉郵寄投票的限制。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/13/nx-s1-6040409/trump-mail-in-voting"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "今年中期選舉的投票剛結束，但一些州的共和黨官員已經在考慮制定 202…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Voting for this year's **midterm** elections just concluded, but Republican officials in a number of states are already looking to shape how votes are cast in 2028.", "zh": "今年中期選舉的投票剛結束，但一些州的共和黨官員已經在考慮制定 2028 年的投票方式。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Twelve GOP state attorneys general are pushing to **revive** the president's bid for mail-in voting restrictions in time for the 2028 election.", "zh": "十二名共和黨州總檢察長正在推動總統在 2028 年大選前及時恢復郵寄投票限制的提案。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "On Thursday, they started the process of appealing a September order by U.S. District Judge Carl Nichols, one of the two judges who blocked the U.S. Postal Service from carrying out a plan released in response to an executive order by President Trump.", "zh": "週四，他們開始對美國地區法官卡爾·尼科爾斯 (Carl Nichols) 9 月的命令提出上訴，卡爾·尼科爾斯是阻止美國郵政局執行針對川普總統行政命令而發布的計劃的兩名法官之一。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "共和党州检察长代表阿拉巴马州、佛罗里达州、印第安纳州、堪萨斯州、路易…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "The Republican state attorneys general represent Alabama, Florida, Indiana, Kansas, Louisiana, Missouri, Montana, Nebraska, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota and Texas.", "zh": "共和黨州檢察長代表阿拉巴馬州、佛羅裡達州、印第安納州、堪薩斯州、路易斯安那州、密蘇裡州、蒙大拿州、內布拉斯加州、俄克拉荷馬州、南卡羅來納州、南達科他州和德克薩斯州。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's not clear, however, how long some of these states will continue this case, given that Democrats won up and down the **ballot** in the **midterms**.", "zh": "然而，鑑於民主黨在中期選舉中獲勝，目前尚不清楚其中一些州將繼續這種情況多久。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In Texas and Kansas, Democratic candidates are set to take control of their states' attorney general's offices in January.", "zh": "在德州和堪薩斯州，民主黨候選人將於一月份控制該州的總檢察長辦公室。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "A **whistleblower** report claimed the online system officials would need to use to follow USPS' **revised** **ballot** requirements had not been properly tested and could have resulted in many eligible voters not getting their mail-in ballots in time or at all.", "zh": "舉報人報告稱，官員為遵循美國郵政總局修訂後的**選票**要求而需要使用的線上系統尚未經過適當測試，可能導致許多符合資格的選民無法及時或根本無法收到郵寄選票。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "While the Supreme Court ultimately stopped implementation of the USPS rule for the **midterms**, Justices Samuel Alito and Clarence Thomas **dissented** from that ruling.", "zh": "雖然最高法院最終停止執行美國郵政局關於中期選舉的規則，但法官塞繆爾·阿利托和克拉倫斯·托馬斯對該裁決持有**異議**。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "同为保守派的法官布雷特·卡瓦诺在一份一致意见中表示，他认为州和地方选…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Fellow conservative Justice Brett Kavanaugh said in a concurring opinion that he believed state and local election officials did not have enough time to \"**reasonably** **implement** the rule\" this time.", "zh": "同為保守派的法官布雷特·卡瓦諾在一份一致意見中表示，他認為州和地方選舉官員這次沒有足夠的時間「**合理地**執行該規則」。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But Kavanaugh noted that \"there is at least a fair **prospect** that the final rule falls within the Postal Service's **statutory** authority.\"", "zh": "但卡瓦諾指出，“最終規則至少有可能屬於郵政服務的法定權力範圍。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "今年中期選舉的投票剛結束，但一些州的共和黨官員已經在考慮制定 2028 年的投票方式。　共和党州检察长代表阿拉巴马州、佛罗里达州、印第安纳州、堪萨斯州、路易斯安那州、密苏里州、蒙大拿州、内布拉斯加州、俄克拉荷马州、南卡罗来纳州、南达科他州和德克萨斯州。然而，鑑於民主黨在中期選舉中獲勝，目前尚不清楚其中一些州將繼續這種情況多久。在德州和堪薩斯州，民主黨候選人將於一月份控制該州的總檢察長辦公室。　同为保守派的法官布雷特·卡瓦诺在一份一致意见中表示，他认为州和地方选举官员这次没有足够的时间“合理地执行该规则”。但卡瓦諾指出，“最終規則至少有可能屬於郵政服務的法定權力範圍。”"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "concur", "sf": "concurring", "pos": "v.", "zh": "同意", "syn": "cooperate, unite, assemble", "tip": "其他意思　合作、同時發生、贊成　|　英英定義　To unite or agree (in action or opinion); to have a common opinion; to coincide; to correspond.　|　本文例句　Voting for this year's midterm elections just concluded, but Republican officials in a number of states are already looking to shape how votes are cast in 2028.　|　例句中譯　今年中期選舉的投票剛結束，但一些州的共和黨官員已經在考慮制定 2028 年的投票方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "whistleblower", "sf": "whistleblower", "pos": "n.", "zh": "檢舉人", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　One who reports a problem or violation to the authorities; especially, an employee or former employee who reports a violation by an employer.　|　本文例句　A whistleblower report claimed the online system officials would need to use to follow USPS' revised ballot requirements had not been properly tested and could have resulted in many eligible voters not getting their mail-in ballots in time or at all.　|　例句中譯　舉報人報告稱，官員為遵循美國郵政總局修訂後的選票要求而需要使用的線上系統尚未經過適當測試，可能導致許多符合資格的選民無法及時或根本無法收到郵寄選票。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "midterm", "sf": "midterm", "pos": "n.", "zh": "期中考", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A midterm school exam (i.e., halfway through the term).　|　本文例句　Voting for this year's midterm elections just concluded, but Republican officials in a number of states are already looking to shape how votes are cast in 2028.　|　例句中譯　今年中期選舉的投票剛結束，但一些州的共和黨官員已經在考慮制定 2028 年的投票方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "dissent", "sf": "dissented", "pos": "v.", "zh": "異議", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　持異議、意見不合　|　英英定義　Disagreement with the ideas, doctrines, decrees, etc. of a political party, government or religion.　|　本文例句　While the Supreme Court ultimately stopped implementation of the USPS rule for the midterms, Justices Samuel Alito and Clarence Thomas dissented from that ruling.　|　例句中譯　雖然最高法院最終停止執行美國郵政局關於中期選舉的規則，但法官塞繆爾·阿利托和克拉倫斯·托馬斯對該裁決持有異議。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "revive", "sf": "revive", "pos": "v.", "zh": "復活", "syn": "rediscover, renew, resurrect", "tip": "其他意思　复生、復甦、復興　|　英英定義　To return to life; to become reanimated or reinvigorated.　|　本文例句　Twelve GOP state attorneys general are pushing to revive the president's bid for mail-in voting restrictions in time for the 2028 election.　|　例句中譯　十二名共和黨州總檢察長正在推動總統在 2028 年大選前及時恢復郵寄投票限制的提案。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "statutory", "sf": "statutory", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "法定的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　成文、法令的　|　英英定義　Of, relating to, enacted or regulated by a statute.　|　本文例句　But Kavanaugh noted that \"there is at least a fair prospect that the final rule falls within the Postal Service's statutory authority.　|　例句中譯　但卡瓦諾指出，「最終規則至少有可能屬於郵政服務的法定權力範圍。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "reasonably", "sf": "reasonably", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "合理地", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　In accordance with reason.　|　本文例句　Fellow conservative Justice Brett Kavanaugh said in a concurring opinion that he believed state and local election officials did not have enough time to \"reasonably implement the rule\" this time.　|　例句中譯　同為保守派的法官布雷特·卡瓦諾在一份一致意見中表示，他認為州和地方選舉官員這次沒有足夠的時間「合理地執行該規則」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "ballot", "sf": "ballot", "pos": "n.", "zh": "選票", "syn": "ballot paper, voting slip", "tip": "其他意思　表決、票、抽簽　|　英英定義　Originally, a small ball placed in a container to cast a vote; now, by extension, a piece of paper or card used for this purpose, or some other means used to signify a vote.　|　本文例句　It's not clear, however, how long some of these states will continue this case, given that Democrats won up and down the ballot in the midterms.　|　例句中譯　然而，鑑於民主黨在中期選舉中獲勝，目前尚不清楚其中一些州將繼續這種情況多久。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "prospect", "sf": "prospect", "pos": "n.", "zh": "前景", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　奔頭兒、前程、前途、查勘　|　英英定義　The region which the eye overlooks at one time; view; scene; outlook.　|　本文例句　But Kavanaugh noted that \"there is at least a fair prospect that the final rule falls within the Postal Service's statutory authority.　|　例句中譯　但卡瓦諾指出，「最終規則至少有可能屬於郵政服務的法定權力範圍。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "revised", "sf": "revised", "pos": "v.", "zh": "修改", "syn": "review", "tip": "其他意思　訂、復習、改、改編　|　英英定義　To look at again, to reflect on.　|　本文例句　A whistleblower report claimed the online system officials would need to use to follow USPS' revised ballot requirements had not been properly tested and could have resulted in many eligible voters not getting their mail-in ballots in time or at all.　|　例句中譯　舉報人報告稱，官員為遵循美國郵政總局修訂後的選票要求而需要使用的線上系統尚未經過適當測試，可能導致許多符合資格的選民無法及時或根本無法收到郵寄選票。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "implement", "sf": "implement", "pos": "n.", "zh": "實施", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　鋐、傢器、器、器具　|　英英定義　A tool or instrument for working with.　|　本文例句　While the Supreme Court ultimately stopped implementation of the USPS rule for the midterms, Justices Samuel Alito and Clarence Thomas dissented from that ruling.　|　例句中譯　雖然最高法院最終停止執行美國郵政局關於中期選舉的規則，但法官塞繆爾·阿利托和克拉倫斯·托馬斯對該裁決持有異議。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "eligible", "sf": "eligible", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "有資格的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　合格、可以選　|　英英定義　One who is eligible.　|　本文例句　A whistleblower report claimed the online system officials would need to use to follow USPS' revised ballot requirements had not been properly tested and could have resulted in many eligible voters not getting their mail-in ballots in time or at all.　|　例句中譯　舉報人報告稱，官員為遵循美國郵政總局修訂後的選票要求而需要使用的線上系統尚未經過適當測試，可能導致許多符合資格的選民無法及時或根本無法收到郵寄選票。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/13/nx-s1-6040409/trump-mail-in-voting"}, {"code": "20261114-2", "ch": "2026-11-14　週六", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "FAA lifts the nationwide ground stop for all U.S. airports　／　美國聯邦航空局 (FAA) 取消美國所有機場的全國地面停留", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Joel Rose、,&nbsp;，全文共 10 段、13 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：據美國聯邦航空管理局稱，週五導緻美國航空系統癱瘓的全國性地面停靠已經結束。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/13/nx-s1-6040403/faa-nationwide-groundstop-airports"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "據美國聯邦航空管理局稱，週五導緻美國航空系統癱瘓的全國性地面停靠已經…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The **nationwide** ground stop that **paralyzed** the U.S. aviation system on Friday has ended, according to the Federal Aviation Administration.", "zh": "據美國聯邦航空管理局稱，週五導緻美國航空系統**癱瘓的****全國**性地面停靠已經結束。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "交通部長肖恩·達菲（Sean Duffy）週五早些時候表示，由於“通…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The rare stop, which lasted about four hours on Friday, ground all U.S. airports following a \"communication issue,\" Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said earlier Friday.", "zh": "交通部長肖恩·達菲（Sean Duffy）週五早些時候表示，由於“通訊問題”，這次罕見的停飛在周五持續了約四個小時，導緻美國所有機場停飛。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "這是自 2001 年 9 月 11 日以來的第二次全國性地面停止。美…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "This is only the second national ground stop since September 11, 2001.", "zh": "這是自 2001 年 9 月 11 日以來的第二次**全國**地面停留。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The U.S. last issued a ground stop of this scale in 2023, when all U.S. airports were shut down due to an **outage** in the NOTAM (Notice to Air Missions) system, which alerts pilots and airports of real-time **hazards**.", "zh": "美國上次發佈如此規模的地面停止是在 2023 年，當時美國所有機場都因向飛行員和機場發出即時危險警報的 NOTAM（空中任務通知）系統中斷而關閉。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "全國各地的地面停飛導致機場混亂，也讓旅客頭痛不已——他們中的許多人已…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "The **nationwide** ground stop has caused chaos in airports and **headaches** for **travelers** — many of whom are already too familiar with flight delays and cancelations during the holiday season.", "zh": "**全國**各地的地面停飛導致機場**混亂**，也讓旅客**頭痛**不已——他們中的許多人已經對假期期間的航班延誤和取消再熟悉不過了。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "雷吉娜·哈林(Regina Harling)在達拉斯沃斯堡國際機場等…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "At Dallas Fort Worth International Airport, Regina Harling said she waited hours — long past when her flight was supposed to **depart** — before she learned of the **nationwide** grounding by checking the news on her phone.", "zh": "雷吉娜·哈林(Regina Harling)在達拉斯沃斯堡國際機場等了幾個小時，在她透過手機查看新聞得知**全國**範圍內停飛的消息之前，她的航班已經過了原定起飛時間。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "「我面前還有一個牌子，上面寫著我們將在 16 分鐘內登機，」她說。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "\"There's still a sign right in front of me that says we're boarding in 16 minutes,\" she said.", "zh": "「我面前還有一個牌子，上面寫著我們將在 16 分鐘內登機，」她說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "哈林因家庭緊急情況需要在最後一刻前往聖地牙哥。被困在機場的她正在考慮…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Harling needed to travel last minute to San Diego for a family emergency.", "zh": "哈林因家庭緊急情況需要在最後一刻前往聖地牙哥。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Stuck at the airport, she's thinking about how soon she can make it to her family, but she's not **optimistic**.", "zh": "被困在機場的她正在考慮多久才能回到家人身邊，但她並不樂觀。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "「我只是在想，總感覺旅行比以前更困難了，」她說。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "\"I was just thinking to myself that it always feels like it's getting harder to travel than it used to be,\" she said.", "zh": "「我只是在想，總感覺旅行比以前更困難了，」她說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "在芝加哥奧黑爾國際機場，吉莉安·卡倫 (Giliann Karon)…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "At Chicago O'Hare International Airport, Giliann Karon was on board a plane when the **nationwide** ground stop was ordered.", "zh": "在芝加哥奧黑爾國際機場，吉莉安·卡倫 (Giliann Karon) 正在飛機上，當時接到了**全國**停飛的命令。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Karon said she had already experienced a flight delay the day before due to bad weather in New York City, where she is heading.", "zh": "卡倫說，由於她要去的紐約市天氣惡劣，前一天她已經經歷了航班延誤。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "「這有點像，『哦，這當然正在發生，』」她說。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "\"It's just kind of like, 'Oh, of course this is happening,'\" she said.", "zh": "「這有點像，『哦，這當然正在發生，』」她說。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "據美國聯邦航空管理局稱，週五導緻美國航空系統癱瘓的全國性地面停靠已經結束。　交通部長肖恩·達菲（Sean Duffy）週五早些時候表示，由於“通訊問題”，這次罕見的停飛在周五持續了約四個小時，導緻美國所有機場停飛。　這是自 2001 年 9 月 11 日以來的第二次全國性地面停止。美國上次發佈如此規模的地面停止是在 2023 年，當時美國所有機場都因向飛行員和機場發出即時危險警報的 NOTAM（空中任務通知）系統中斷而關閉。　全國各地的地面停飛導致機場混亂，也讓旅客頭痛不已——他們中的許多人已經對假期期間的航班延誤和取消再熟悉不過了。　雷吉娜·哈林(Regina Harling)在達拉斯沃斯堡國際機場等了幾個小時，在她透過手機查看新聞得知全國範圍內停飛的消息之前，她的航班已經過了原定起飛時間。　「我面前還有一個牌子，上面寫著我們將在 16 分鐘內登機，」她說。　哈林因家庭緊急情況需要在最後一刻前往聖地牙哥。被困在機場的她正在考慮多久才能回到家人身邊，但她並不樂觀。　「我只是在想，總感覺旅行比以前更困難了，」她說。　在芝加哥奧黑爾國際機場，吉莉安·卡倫 (Giliann Karon) 正在飛機上，當時接到了全國停飛的命令。卡倫說，由於她要去的紐約市天氣惡劣，前一天她已經經歷了航班延誤。　「這有點像，『哦，這當然正在發生，』」她說。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "outage", "sf": "outage", "pos": "n.", "zh": "停電", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A temporary suspension of operation, especially of electrical power supply.　|　本文例句　airports were shut down due to an outage in the NOTAM (Notice to Air Missions) system, which alerts pilots and airports of real-time hazards.　|　例句中譯　由於NOTAM（空中任務通知）系統中斷，機場關閉，該系統向飛行員和機場發出即時危險警報。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "paralyzed", "sf": "paralyzed", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "癱瘓的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　發獃的、癱　|　英英定義　To afflict with paralysis.　|　本文例句　The nationwide ground stop that paralyzed the U.　|　例句中譯　導緻美國癱瘓的全國性地面站。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "depart", "sf": "depart", "pos": "n.", "zh": "離開", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　終、背離、發動、放棄　|　英英定義　Division; separation, as of compound substances.　|　本文例句　At Dallas Fort Worth International Airport, Regina Harling said she waited hours — long past when her flight was supposed to depart — before she learned of the nationwide grounding by checking the news on her phone.　|　例句中譯　雷吉娜·哈林(Regina Harling)在達拉斯沃斯堡國際機場等了幾個小時，在她透過手機查看新聞得知全國範圍內停飛的消息之前，她的航班已經過了原定起飛時間。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "travelers", "sf": "travelers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "旅行者", "syn": "Gypsy, Minkier, Pavee", "tip": "其他意思　羇、羇客、客、旅客　|　英英定義　A member of a particular nomadic ethnic minority in Ireland, the Pavee.　|　本文例句　The nationwide ground stop has caused chaos in airports and headaches for travelers — many of whom are already too familiar with flight delays and cancelations during the holiday season.　|　例句中譯　全國各地的地面停飛導致機場混亂，也讓旅客頭痛不已——他們中的許多人已經對假期期間的航班延誤和取消再熟悉不過了。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "optimistic", "sf": "optimistic", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "樂觀的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　開朗的、樂天的　|　英英定義　Expecting the best in all possible ways.　|　本文例句　Stuck at the airport, she's thinking about how soon she can make it to her family, but she's not optimistic.　|　例句中譯　被困在機場的她正在考慮多久才能回到家人身邊，但她並不樂觀。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "headache", "sf": "headaches", "pos": "n.", "zh": "頭痛", "syn": "bother, pain in the neck, cephalalgia", "tip": "其他意思　頭疼　|　英英定義　A pain or ache in the head.　|　本文例句　The nationwide ground stop has caused chaos in airports and headaches for travelers — many of whom are already too familiar with flight delays and cancelations during the holiday season.　|　例句中譯　全國各地的地面停飛導致機場混亂，也讓旅客頭痛不已——他們中的許多人已經對假期期間的航班延誤和取消再熟悉不過了。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "hazard", "sf": "hazards", "pos": "v.", "zh": "冒險", "syn": "bet, pledge, skin in the game", "tip": "其他意思　賭運气、風險、拼命、遇合　|　英英定義　The chance of suffering harm; danger, peril, risk of loss.　|　本文例句　airports were shut down due to an outage in the NOTAM (Notice to Air Missions) system, which alerts pilots and airports of real-time hazards.　|　例句中譯　由於NOTAM（空中任務通知）系統中斷，機場關閉，該系統向飛行員和機場發出即時危險警報。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "nationwide", "sf": "nationwide", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "全國", "syn": "countrywide, national", "tip": "其他意思　全國性的　|　英英定義　Extending throughout an entire nation.　|　本文例句　The nationwide ground stop that paralyzed the U.　|　例句中譯　導緻美國癱瘓的全國性地面站。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "chaos", "sf": "chaos", "pos": "n.", "zh": "混亂", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　混沌、凌亂　|　英英定義　The unordered state of matter in classical accounts of cosmogony.　|　本文例句　The nationwide ground stop has caused chaos in airports and headaches for travelers — many of whom are already too familiar with flight delays and cancelations during the holiday season.　|　例句中譯　全國各地的地面停飛導致機場混亂，也讓旅客頭痛不已——他們中的許多人已經對假期期間的航班延誤和取消再熟悉不過了。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/13/nx-s1-6040403/faa-nationwide-groundstop-airports"}, {"code": "20261114-3", "ch": "2026-11-14　週六", "sec": "State of the World from NPR", "title": "What's Trump's strategy now with Iran? To keep things as they are　／　川普現在對伊朗的戰略是什麼？保持事物原樣", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Aya Batrawy，全文共 16 段、27 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：川普總統表示，隨著伊朗戰爭陷入僵局，美國中期選舉迫使從攻擊威脅轉向經濟壓力，海灣阿拉伯盟友希望維持「現狀」。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/13/g-s1-153578/whats-trumps-strategy-now-with-iran-to-keep-things-as-they-are"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "阿拉伯聯合大公國杜拜—與伊朗開戰九個月後，川普總統面臨新的現實，這讓…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "DUBAI, United Arab Emirates — President Trump is confronting new realities nine months into the war with Iran that leave him with **dwindling** options to ending the conflict.", "zh": "阿拉伯聯合大公國杜拜—與伊朗開戰九個月後，川普總統面臨新的現實，這讓他結束衝突的選擇越來越少。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "On Thursday, he waved away the need for a deal with Iran, saying the U.S. has billions of Iran's dollars frozen in overseas accounts.", "zh": "週四，他否認了與伊朗達成協議的必要性，並表示美國在海外帳戶中凍結了數十億美元的伊朗資金。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "「我們不需要與伊朗達成協議。那些日子早已過去了。我們得到了他們的錢，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"We don't need a deal with Iran.", "zh": "「我們不需要與伊朗達成協議。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Those days have long since passed.", "zh": "那些日子早已過去了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We've got their money,\" he wrote in a Truth Social post.", "zh": "我們拿到了他們的錢，」他在《真相社會》的一篇貼文中寫道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "与伊朗的谈判陷入困境，调解人卡塔尔正在努力弥合分歧。川普本週在白宮會…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Negotiations with Iran are stuck with **mediator** Qatar working to bridge the divide.", "zh": "與伊朗的談判陷入困境，**調解人**卡達正努力彌合分歧。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Trump met Qatar's prime minister at the White House this week, and said afterward that Gulf Arab allies prefer \"the status quo\" of continued economic pressure on Iran.", "zh": "川普本週在白宮會見了卡達總理，隨後表示，海灣阿拉伯盟友更願意維持對伊朗持續經濟施壓的「現狀」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He wrote that while the U.S. remains \"locked and loaded,\" an attack at this point \"seems to be quite unlikely.\"", "zh": "他寫道，雖然美國仍然“已上膛”，但此時發動襲擊“似乎不太可能”。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "与此同时，美国正在协助油轮使用靠近阿曼海岸线的路线通过霍尔木兹海峡。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The U.S., meanwhile, is assisting oil **tankers** through the Strait of Hormuz using a route that's close to Oman's coastline.", "zh": "同時，美國正在協助油輪使用靠近阿曼海岸線的路線透過霍爾木茲海峽。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "While this has helped Arab states export their oil, it does not solve the bigger problem of how to bring back the pre-war production levels of other vital products like liquified natural gas, **fertilizer** and aluminum.", "zh": "雖然這幫助了阿拉伯國家出口石油，但它並沒有解決更大的問題，即如何將液化天然氣、化肥和鋁等其他重要產品的生產**恢復**到戰前水準。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Nor does a status quo allow countries like Kuwait, Qatar and Bahrain to import goods to their ports.", "zh": "現狀也不允許科威特、卡達和巴林等國家將貨物進口到其港口。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "国际货币基金组织表示，尽管油价上涨，海湾阿拉伯国家仍因战争而陷入经济…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "The International Monetary Fund says Gulf Arab states are in economic recession as a result of the war, despite higher oil prices.", "zh": "國際貨幣基金組織表示，儘管油價上漲，海灣阿拉伯國家仍因戰爭而陷入經濟衰退。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It says Kuwait, Qatar and Iraq's economies are contracting approximately 16% this year. Bahrain's is down 11%.", "zh": "報告稱，科威特、卡達和伊拉克的經濟今年萎縮約16%。巴林下跌 11%。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "The U.S. is sending a third aircraft carrier with thousands of troops to the region, leaving open the possibility of another planned military **escalation**.", "zh": "美國正在向該地區派遣第三艘航空母艦和數千名士兵，這可能導致另一次計劃中的軍事**升級**。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "本週，伊朗公佈了一個新的地下飛彈生產基地。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "This week, Iran unveiled what it says is a new underground missile production site.", "zh": "本週，伊朗公佈了一個新的地下飛彈生產基地。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "美國和伊朗也時不時地進行針鋒相對的打擊。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "The U.S. and Iran are also still occasionally carrying out **tit-for-tat** for strikes.", "zh": "美國和伊朗也時不時地進行**針鋒相對**的打擊。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "週五，伊朗媒體稱，美國襲擊了伊朗位於霍爾木茲海峽的島嶼。這是伊朗擁有…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "On Friday, Iranian media said the U.S. struck one of its islands in the Strait of Hormuz.", "zh": "週五，伊朗媒體稱，美國襲擊了伊朗位於霍爾木茲海峽的島嶼。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's an area where Iran has radars and drone launch sites.", "zh": "這是伊朗擁有雷達和無人機發射場的地區。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Iran's Revolutionary Guard said it hit back, targeting an early warning U.S. radar in Bahrain.", "zh": "伊朗革命衛隊表示進行了反擊，目標是位於巴林的美國預警雷達。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "美國國務卿馬可·盧比奧本週對記者表示，現階段沒有必要對伊朗採取軍事行…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Secretary of State Marco Rubio told reporters this week there's no need for military action against Iran at this stage because economic sanctions are doing the job.", "zh": "美國國務卿馬可·盧比奧本週對記者表示，現階段沒有必要對伊朗採取軍事行動，因為經濟制裁正在發揮作用。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "「他們感受到的痛苦是，最終你必須吃飯。最終你必須能夠支付自己的戰士和…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "\"The pain that they're feeling is, eventually you have to eat.", "zh": "「他們感受到的痛苦是，最終你必須吃飯。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Eventually you have to be able to pay your own fighters and your own security forces,\" Rubio said.", "zh": "最終你必須能夠支付自己的戰士和安全部隊的費用，」盧比奧說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "同時，美國軍方中央司令部宣布與其他美國政府機構聯合開展一項名為「鐵門…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "Meanwhile, the U.S. military's Central Command announced a new operation, dubbed \"Iron Gate,\" with other U.S. government agencies, aimed at preventing Iran from using land routes to transport advanced weapons across its borders and the Caspian Sea.", "zh": "同時，美國軍方中央司令部宣布與其他美國政府機構聯合開展一項名為「鐵門」的新行動，旨在阻止伊朗利用陸路運輸先進武器穿越其邊境和里海。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "與伊朗衝突的另一個後果是沙烏地阿拉伯和也門胡塞武裝之間恢復全面戰爭。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "Another consequence of the conflict with Iran is the **resumption** of all-out war between Saudi Arabia and the Houthis in Yemen.", "zh": "與伊朗衝突的另一個後果是沙烏地阿拉伯和也門胡塞武裝之間**恢復**全面戰爭。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "胡塞武裝雖然不是伊朗的直接代理人，但得到伊朗的支持，他們表示，過去幾…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "The Houthis, who are not a direct **proxy** of Iran but are supported by it, say Saudi airstrikes across Yemen have killed scores of people in past months, including nearly 60 this past weekend, many of them women and children in a village near the capital Sana'a.", "zh": "胡塞武裝雖然不是伊朗的直接**代理人**，但得到伊朗的支持，他們表示，過去幾個月，沙烏地阿拉伯對也門的空襲已造成數十人死亡，其中上週末有近 60 人死亡，其中許多是首都薩那附近村莊的婦女和兒童。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "同時，沙烏地阿拉伯每天都面臨胡塞武裝的飛彈和無人機襲擊，其中包括本週…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Saudi Arabia, meanwhile, faces daily missile and drone attacks by Houthis, including some this week that hit its key East-West pipeline carrying crude oil to bypass the Strait of Hormuz.", "zh": "同時，沙烏地阿拉伯每天都面臨胡塞武裝的飛彈和無人機襲擊，其中包括本週襲擊其繞過霍爾木茲海峽輸送原油的重要東西向管道的襲擊。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Another Houthi attack hit Saudi oil company Aramco's **skyscraper** headquarters in Riyadh's financial district.", "zh": "另一次胡塞武裝攻擊襲擊了沙烏地阿拉伯石油公司阿美公司位於利雅德金融區的**摩天大樓**總部。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "阿拉伯聯合大公國杜拜—與伊朗開戰九個月後，川普總統面臨新的現實，這讓他結束衝突的選擇越來越少。　「我們不需要與伊朗達成協議。那些日子早已過去了。我們得到了他們的錢，」他在《真相社會》的一篇貼文中寫道。　与伊朗的谈判陷入困境，调解人卡塔尔正在努力弥合分歧。川普本週在白宮會見了卡達總理，隨後表示，海灣阿拉伯盟友更願意維持對伊朗持續經濟施壓的「現狀」。他写道，虽然美国仍然“已上膛”，但此时发动袭击“似乎不太可能”。　与此同时，美国正在协助油轮使用靠近阿曼海岸线的路线通过霍尔木兹海峡。雖然這幫助了阿拉伯國家出口石油，但它並沒有解決更大的問題，即如何將液化天然氣、化肥和鋁等其他重要產品的生產恢復到戰前水準。现状也不允许科威特、卡塔尔和巴林等国家将货物进口到其港口。　国际货币基金组织表示，尽管油价上涨，海湾阿拉伯国家仍因战争而陷入经济衰退。报告称，科威特、卡塔尔和伊拉克的经济今年萎缩约16%。巴林下跌 11%。　本週，伊朗公佈了一個新的地下飛彈生產基地。　美國和伊朗也時不時地進行針鋒相對的打擊。　週五，伊朗媒體稱，美國襲擊了伊朗位於霍爾木茲海峽的島嶼。這是伊朗擁有雷達和無人機發射場的地區。伊朗革命衛隊表示進行了反擊，目標是位於巴林的美國預警雷達。　美國國務卿馬可·盧比奧本週對記者表示，現階段沒有必要對伊朗採取軍事行動，因為經濟制裁正在發揮作用。　「他們感受到的痛苦是，最終你必須吃飯。最終你必須能夠支付自己的戰士和安全部隊的費用，」盧比奧說。　同時，美國軍方中央司令部宣布與其他美國政府機構聯合開展一項名為「鐵門」的新行動，旨在阻止伊朗利用陸路運輸先進武器穿越其邊境和里海。　與伊朗衝突的另一個後果是沙烏地阿拉伯和也門胡塞武裝之間恢復全面戰爭。　胡塞武裝雖然不是伊朗的直接代理人，但得到伊朗的支持，他們表示，過去幾個月，沙烏地阿拉伯對也門的空襲已造成數十人死亡，其中上週末有近 60 人死亡，其中許多是首都薩那附近村莊的婦女和兒童。　同時，沙烏地阿拉伯每天都面臨胡塞武裝的飛彈和無人機襲擊，其中包括本週襲擊其繞過霍爾木茲海峽輸送原油的重要東西向管道的襲擊。另一次胡塞武裝攻擊襲擊了沙烏地阿拉伯石油公司阿美公司位於利雅德金融區的摩天大樓總部。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "dwindling", "sf": "dwindling", "pos": "v.", "zh": "減少", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　To decrease, shrink, diminish, reduce in size or intensity.　|　本文例句　DUBAI, United Arab Emirates — President Trump is confronting new realities nine months into the war with Iran that leave him with dwindling options to ending the conflict.　|　例句中譯　阿拉伯聯合大公國杜拜—與伊朗開戰九個月後，川普總統面臨新的現實，這讓他結束衝突的選擇越來越少。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "resumption", "sf": "resumption", "pos": "n.", "zh": "恢復", "syn": "restart", "tip": "英英定義　The act of resuming or starting something again.　|　本文例句　Another consequence of the conflict with Iran is the resumption of all-out war between Saudi Arabia and the Houthis in Yemen.　|　例句中譯　與伊朗衝突的另一個後果是沙烏地阿拉伯和也門胡塞武裝之間恢復全面戰爭。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "tit-for-tat", "sf": "tit-for-tat", "pos": "", "zh": "針鋒相對", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　and Iran are also still occasionally carrying out tit-for-tat for strikes.　|　例句中譯　與伊朗之間也時不時進行針鋒相對的打擊。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "skyscraper", "sf": "skyscraper", "pos": "n.", "zh": "摩天大樓", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　摩天摟　|　英英定義　A very tall building with a large number of floors.　|　本文例句　Another Houthi attack hit Saudi oil company Aramco's skyscraper headquarters in Riyadh's financial district.　|　例句中譯　另一次胡塞武裝攻擊襲擊了沙烏地阿拉伯石油公司阿美公司位於利雅德金融區的摩天大樓總部。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "mediator", "sf": "mediator", "pos": "n.", "zh": "調解人", "syn": "negotiator", "tip": "其他意思　和事佬、中間人　|　英英定義　One who negotiates between parties seeking mutual agreement.　|　本文例句　Negotiations with Iran are stuck with mediator Qatar working to bridge the divide.　|　例句中譯　與伊朗的談判陷入困境，調解人卡達正努力彌合分歧。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "escalation", "sf": "escalation", "pos": "n.", "zh": "升級", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　An increase or rise, especially one to counteract a perceived discrepancy　|　本文例句　is sending a third aircraft carrier with thousands of troops to the region, leaving open the possibility of another planned military escalation.　|　例句中譯　美國正在向該地區派遣第三艘航空母艦和數千名士兵，這為另一次計劃中的軍事升級留下了可能性。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "fertilizer", "sf": "fertilizer", "pos": "n.", "zh": "肥料", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　化肥　|　英英定義　A natural substance that is used to make the ground more suitable for growing plants.　|　本文例句　While this has helped Arab states export their oil, it does not solve the bigger problem of how to bring back the pre-war production levels of other vital products like liquified natural gas, fertilizer and aluminum.　|　例句中譯　雖然這幫助了阿拉伯國家出口石油，但它並沒有解決更大的問題，即如何將液化天然氣、化肥和鋁等其他重要產品的生產恢復到戰前水準。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "tanker", "sf": "tankers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "油船", "syn": "armored soldier, armoured soldier, crewman", "tip": "其他意思　油車　|　英英定義　A tank ship, a vessel used to transport large quantities of liquid.　|　本文例句　, meanwhile, is assisting oil tankers through the Strait of Hormuz using a route that's close to Oman's coastline.　|　例句中譯　同時，正在協助油輪使用靠近阿曼海岸線的路線透過霍爾木茲海峽。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "proxy", "sf": "proxy", "pos": "n.", "zh": "代理人", "syn": "deputy, representative, substitute", "tip": "其他意思　代理、代理的　|　英英定義　An agent or substitute authorized to act for another person.　|　本文例句　The Houthis, who are not a direct proxy of Iran but are supported by it, say Saudi airstrikes across Yemen have killed scores of people in past months, including nearly 60 this past weekend, many of them women and children in a village near the capital Sana'a.　|　例句中譯　胡塞武裝雖然不是伊朗的直接代理人，但得到伊朗的支持，他們表示，過去幾個月，沙烏地阿拉伯對也門的空襲已造成數十人死亡，其中上週末有近 60 人死亡，其中許多是首都薩那附近村莊的婦女和兒童。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/13/g-s1-153578/whats-trumps-strategy-now-with-iran-to-keep-things-as-they-are"}, {"code": "20261113-1", "ch": "2026-11-13　週五", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Is Outlook down? Widespread outage hits Microsoft email and other apps　／　展望低落了嗎？微軟電子郵件和其他應用程式出現大規模中斷", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、The Associated Press，全文共 5 段、7 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：包括 Outlook 在內的 Microsoft 平台發生了大規模的故障，許多使用者在使用電子郵件帳戶時遇到了問題。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/nx-s1-6039343/is-outlook-down-widespread-outage-hits-microsoft-email-and-other-apps"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "A **widespread** **outage** hit Microsoft platforms including Outlook on Thursday, with many users encountering trouble using their email accounts and other errors across the tech giant's **suite** of apps.", "zh": "週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用戶在使用電子郵件帳戶時**遇到**了麻煩，並且在這家科技巨頭的應用程式套件中遇到了其他錯誤。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "下午 1 點剛過，中斷追蹤器 DownDetector 上的近 13…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Nearly 130,000 users on **outage** **tracker** Downdetector reported problems accessing Outlook just after 1 p.m. ET.", "zh": "下午 1 點剛過，中斷**追蹤器** DownDetector 上的近 130,000 位用戶報告了存取 Outlook 時出現的問題。等。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "New reports have since fallen from that peak, but many said they couldn't send and receive emails or had trouble loading their **inboxes** **altogether**.", "zh": "此後，新的報告已從高峰迴落，但許多人表示他們無法發送和接收電子郵件，或無法完全載入**收件匣**。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "目前尚不清楚到底是什麼原因導致了這次失敗。但微軟後來表示，它正在測試…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "It was not immediately clear what exactly caused that failure.", "zh": "目前尚不清楚到底是什麼原因導致了這次失敗。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But Microsoft later said it was testing a fix and rolling out an alternative method for these checks to bring impacted servers back online.", "zh": "但微軟後來表示，它正在測試修復程序，並推出一種替代方法來進行這些檢查，以使受影響的伺服器重新上線。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "Microsoft 365 Status 帳戶在 X 上寫道：“我們…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "\"We're **aggressively** **pursuing** all **pathways** to reduce impact,\" the Microsoft 365 Status account wrote on X.", "zh": "Microsoft 365 Status 帳戶在 X 上寫道：“我們正在積極尋求一切途徑來減少影響。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "當天早些時候，該公司表示已「成功修復」北美地區與 Microsoft…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Earlier in the day, the company said it had \"successfully **restored**\" problems related to Microsoft Teams in North America, although some users continued to report **connectivity** issues.", "zh": "當天早些時候，該公司表示已「成功修復」北美地區與 Microsoft Teams 相關的問題，儘管一些用戶繼續報告連線問題。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用戶在使用電子郵件帳戶時遇到了麻煩，並且在這家科技巨頭的應用程式套件中遇到了其他錯誤。　下午 1 點剛過，中斷追蹤器 DownDetector 上的近 130,000 位用戶報告了存取 Outlook 時出現的問題。等。此後，新的報告已從高峰迴落，但許多人表示他們無法發送和接收電子郵件，或無法完全載入收件匣。　目前尚不清楚到底是什麼原因導致了這次失敗。但微軟後來表示，它正在測試修復程序，並推出一種替代方法來進行這些檢查，以使受影響的伺服器重新上線。　Microsoft 365 Status 帳戶在 X 上寫道：“我們正在積極尋求一切途徑來減少影響。”　當天早些時候，該公司表示已「成功修復」北美地區與 Microsoft Teams 相關的問題，儘管一些用戶繼續報告連線問題。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "outage", "sf": "outage", "pos": "n.", "zh": "停電", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A temporary suspension of operation, especially of electrical power supply.　|　本文例句　A widespread outage hit Microsoft platforms including Outlook on Thursday, with many users encountering trouble using their email accounts and other errors across the tech giant's suite of apps.　|　例句中譯　週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用戶在使用電子郵件帳戶時遇到了麻煩，並且在這家科技巨頭的應用程式套件中遇到了其他錯誤。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "inbox", "sf": "inboxes", "pos": "n.", "zh": "收件匣", "syn": "in-basket, in-tray", "tip": "英英定義　A container in which papers to be dealt with are put.　|　本文例句　New reports have since fallen from that peak, but many said they couldn't send and receive emails or had trouble loading their inboxes altogether.　|　例句中譯　此後，新的報告已從高峰迴落，但許多人表示他們無法發送和接收電子郵件，或無法完全載入收件匣。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "connectivity", "sf": "connectivity", "pos": "n.", "zh": "連接性", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　The state of being connected　|　本文例句　Earlier in the day, the company said it had \"successfully restored\" problems related to Microsoft Teams in North America, although some users continued to report connectivity issues.　|　例句中譯　當天早些時候，該公司表示已「成功修復」北美地區與 Microsoft Teams 相關的問題，儘管一些用戶繼續報告連線問題。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "aggressively", "sf": "aggressively", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "積極地", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　侵略地　|　英英定義　In an aggressive manner.　|　本文例句　\"We're aggressively pursuing all pathways to reduce impact,\" the Microsoft 365 Status account wrote on X.　|　例句中譯　Microsoft 365 Status 帳戶在 X 上寫道：“我們正在積極尋求一切途徑來減少影響。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "tracker", "sf": "tracker", "pos": "n.", "zh": "追蹤器", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　跡人　|　英英定義　Agent noun of track; one who, or that which, tracks or pursues, as a man or dog that follows game.　|　本文例句　Nearly 130,000 users on outage tracker Downdetector reported problems accessing Outlook just after 1 p.　|　例句中譯　下午 1 點後，停電追蹤器 DownDetector 上的近 130,000 位用戶報告了存取 Outlook 時出現的問題。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "pathway", "sf": "pathways", "pos": "n.", "zh": "路徑", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　路、蹊　|　英英定義　A footpath or other path or track.　|　本文例句　\"We're aggressively pursuing all pathways to reduce impact,\" the Microsoft 365 Status account wrote on X.　|　例句中譯　Microsoft 365 Status 帳戶在 X 上寫道：“我們正在積極尋求一切途徑來減少影響。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "altogether", "sf": "altogether", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "共", "syn": "all in all, completely, wholly", "tip": "其他意思　畢、乾脆、攏共、集合體　|　英英定義　Without exception; wholly; completely.　|　本文例句　New reports have since fallen from that peak, but many said they couldn't send and receive emails or had trouble loading their inboxes altogether.　|　例句中譯　此後，新的報告已從高峰迴落，但許多人表示他們無法發送和接收電子郵件，或無法完全載入收件匣。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "restore", "sf": "restored", "pos": "v.", "zh": "恢復", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　放回、復興、歸還　|　英英定義　The act of recovering data or a system from a backup.　|　本文例句　Earlier in the day, the company said it had \"successfully restored\" problems related to Microsoft Teams in North America, although some users continued to report connectivity issues.　|　例句中譯　當天早些時候，該公司表示已「成功修復」北美地區與 Microsoft Teams 相關的問題，儘管一些用戶繼續報告連線問題。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "suite", "sf": "suite", "pos": "n.", "zh": "套房", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　房間、機組、隨從、隨員　|　英英定義　A retinue or company of attendants, as of a distinguished personage　|　本文例句　A widespread outage hit Microsoft platforms including Outlook on Thursday, with many users encountering trouble using their email accounts and other errors across the tech giant's suite of apps.　|　例句中譯　週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用戶在使用電子郵件帳戶時遇到了麻煩，並且在這家科技巨頭的應用程式套件中遇到了其他錯誤。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "widespread", "sf": "widespread", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "廣泛", "syn": "extensive, pervasive, prevalent", "tip": "其他意思　廣博的、廣布的、廣大的　|　英英定義　Affecting a large area (e.g. the entire land or body); broad in extent; widely diffused.　|　本文例句　A widespread outage hit Microsoft platforms including Outlook on Thursday, with many users encountering trouble using their email accounts and other errors across the tech giant's suite of apps.　|　例句中譯　週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用戶在使用電子郵件帳戶時遇到了麻煩，並且在這家科技巨頭的應用程式套件中遇到了其他錯誤。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "encounter", "sf": "encountering", "pos": "n.", "zh": "遇到", "syn": "brush, clash, confrontation", "tip": "其他意思　領教、遇、遇見、遻　|　英英定義　A meeting, especially one that is unplanned or unexpected.　|　本文例句　A widespread outage hit Microsoft platforms including Outlook on Thursday, with many users encountering trouble using their email accounts and other errors across the tech giant's suite of apps.　|　例句中譯　週四，包括 Outlook 在內的微軟平台發生了大範圍的故障，許多用戶在使用電子郵件帳戶時遇到了麻煩，並且在這家科技巨頭的應用程式套件中遇到了其他錯誤。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "pursue", "sf": "pursuing", "pos": "v.", "zh": "追求", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　奉行、跡、適、探求　|　英英定義　To follow urgently, originally with intent to capture or harm; to chase.　|　本文例句　\"We're aggressively pursuing all pathways to reduce impact,\" the Microsoft 365 Status account wrote on X.　|　例句中譯　Microsoft 365 Status 帳戶在 X 上寫道：“我們正在積極尋求一切途徑來減少影響。”", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/nx-s1-6039343/is-outlook-down-widespread-outage-hits-microsoft-email-and-other-apps"}, {"code": "20261113-2", "ch": "2026-11-13　週五", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Cindy Holscher wins in Kansas, holding governor's office for Democrats　／　辛蒂霍爾舍 (Cindy Holscher) 在堪薩斯州獲勝，代表民主黨擔任州長", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Larry Kaplow，全文共 7 段、16 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：霍爾舍爾是一名州參議員，他擊敗了一位更知名的共和黨人，後者在該州得到了川普的支持，而在大多數其他全州競選中，共和黨人都支持了這位共和黨人。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/g-s1-151239/kansas-governor-midterms-holscher-masterson"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "據美聯社報導，民主黨州參議員辛迪·霍爾舍爾(Cindy Holsch…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Democratic state Sen.", "zh": "民主黨州參議員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Cindy Holscher will hold onto the Kansas governor's office for her party after defeating Republican Ty Masterson, according to a race call by the Associated Press.", "zh": "據美聯社的競選電話稱，在擊敗共和黨人泰·馬斯特森後，辛迪·霍爾舍爾將為其政黨保住堪薩斯州州長職位。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。在全國 36 次州長選舉中…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Masterson, the president of the state Senate, was **endorsed** by President Trump.", "zh": "州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Of the 36 elections for governor across the country, Kansas was seen as the most likely to flip from Democratic to Republican control.", "zh": "在全國 36 次州長選舉中，堪薩斯州被認為最有可能從民主黨控制權轉向共和黨控制權。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "現任民主黨州長勞拉·凱利(Laura Kelly)在一個共和黨佔多數…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Current Democratic Gov.", "zh": "現任民主黨州長"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Laura Kelly is term-limited after serving for eight years in a state with a heavily Republican **legislature** and that usually votes for Republicans for other offices and in presidential elections.", "zh": "勞拉凱利 (Laura Kelly) 在一個共和黨佔多數立法機構的州任職八年後，任期受到限制，該州通常在其他職位和總統選舉中投票給共和黨人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of **populism**, promising to fight \"**sweetheart** deals\" for **billionaires**.", "zh": "57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有**民粹主義**色彩的競選活動，承諾為**億萬富翁**爭取「甜心交易」。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She tied Masterson to his work in the state Senate when it passed a tax cut under former Republican Gov.", "zh": "她將馬斯特森與他在州參議院的工作聯繫起來，當時州參議院透過了前共和黨州長川普領導下的減稅政策。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Sam Brownback that led to a series of budget **crises** and was later **repealed**.", "zh": "薩姆·布朗巴克法案導致了一系列預算**危機**，後來被**廢除**。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Holscher opposed school **vouchers**, calling for more support for public schools, in contrast with Masterson, who backed school vouchers.", "zh": "霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She also called for a **moratorium** on new data centers and for **legalizing** **cannabis** as a way to generate state revenue.", "zh": "她也呼籲**暫停**新資料中心的建設，並使**大麻****合法化**，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "57 歲的馬斯特森呼籲降低財產稅，並表示信仰影響了他的所有決定，包括…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Masterson, 57, called for lower property taxes and said faith influenced all his decisions, including in politics.", "zh": "57 歲的馬斯特森呼籲降低財產稅，並表示信仰影響了他的所有決定，包括政治方面的決定。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He promised to be the \"most **pro-ag**, pro-business, pro-oil and gas governor,\" the state has seen.", "zh": "他承諾成為該州「最支持農業、支持商業、支持石油和天然氣的州長」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He called Holscher, \"the most radical, liberal, socialist Democrat ever\" on a ticket in Kansas.", "zh": "他在堪薩斯州的一張選票上稱霍爾舍爾為「有史以來最激進、最自由、最社會主義的民主黨人」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "「他喜歡貼上很多標籤，」霍爾舍爾回答。 “你知道為什麼嗎？因為這就是…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "\"He likes to throw around a whole lot of labels,\" Holscher responded. \"You know why?", "zh": "「他喜歡貼上很多標籤，」霍爾舍爾回答。 「你知道為什麼嗎？"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Because that's all he's got.\"", "zh": "因為這就是他所擁有的一切。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "據美聯社報導，民主黨州參議員辛迪·霍爾舍爾(Cindy Holscher)在擊敗共和黨人泰·馬斯特森(Ty Masterson)後，將保住她所在政黨的堪薩斯州州長職位。　州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。在全國 36 次州長選舉中，堪薩斯州被認為最有可能從民主黨控制權轉向共和黨控制權。　現任民主黨州長勞拉·凱利(Laura Kelly)在一個共和黨佔多數立法機構的州任職八年後，任期受到限制，該州通常在其他職位和總統選舉中投票支持共和黨。　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。她將馬斯特森與他在州參議院的工作聯繫在一起，當時州參議院透過了前共和黨州長薩姆·布朗巴克(Sam Brownback)領導下的減稅政策，該減稅政策導致了一系列預算危機，後來被廢除。　霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。　57 歲的馬斯特森呼籲降低財產稅，並表示信仰影響了他的所有決定，包括政治方面的決定。他承諾成為該州「最支持農業、支持商業、支持石油和天然氣的州長」。他在堪薩斯州的一張選票上稱霍爾舍爾為「有史以來最激進、最自由、最社會主義的民主黨人」。　「他喜歡貼上很多標籤，」霍爾舍爾回答。 “你知道為什麼嗎？因為這就是他所擁有的一切。”"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "populism", "sf": "populism", "pos": "n.", "zh": "民粹主義", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A political doctrine or philosophy that proposes that the rights and powers of ordinary people are exploited by a privileged elite, and supports their struggle to overcome this.　|　本文例句　Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of populism, promising to fight \"sweetheart deals\" for billionaires.　|　例句中譯　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "moratorium", "sf": "moratorium", "pos": "n.", "zh": "暫停", "syn": "hiatus, interruption, recess", "tip": "英英定義　An authorization to a debtor, permitting temporary suspension of payments.　|　本文例句　She also called for a moratorium on new data centers and for legalizing cannabis as a way to generate state revenue.　|　例句中譯　她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "legalize", "sf": "legalizing", "pos": "v.", "zh": "合法化", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　認證、使合法化　|　英英定義　To make legal or permit under law. Either by decriminalising something that has been illegal or by specifically permitting it.　|　本文例句　She also called for a moratorium on new data centers and for legalizing cannabis as a way to generate state revenue.　|　例句中譯　她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "vouchers", "sf": "vouchers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "優惠券", "syn": "coupon", "tip": "其他意思　保證人、傳票、憑單、憑證　|　英英定義　A piece of paper that entitles the holder to a discount, or that can be exchanged for goods and services.　|　本文例句　Holscher opposed school vouchers, calling for more support for public schools, in contrast with Masterson, who backed school vouchers.　|　例句中譯　霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "crises", "sf": "crises", "pos": "n.", "zh": "危機", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　風波　|　英英定義　A crucial or decisive point or situation; a turning point.　|　本文例句　Sam Brownback that led to a series of budget crises and was later repealed.　|　例句中譯　薩姆·布朗巴克法案導致了一系列預算危機，後來被廢除。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "sweetheart", "sf": "sweetheart", "pos": "v.", "zh": "親愛的", "syn": "sweetie, darling, dear", "tip": "其他意思　討 ... 歡心、愛侶、愛人、戀人　|　英英定義　A person who is always very kind.　|　本文例句　Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of populism, promising to fight \"sweetheart deals\" for billionaires.　|　例句中譯　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "billionaire", "sf": "billionaires", "pos": "n.", "zh": "億萬富翁", "syn": "milliardaire", "tip": "英英定義　Somebody whose wealth is greater than one billion (109) dollars, or other currency.　|　本文例句　Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of populism, promising to fight \"sweetheart deals\" for billionaires.　|　例句中譯　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "endorsed", "sf": "endorsed", "pos": "v.", "zh": "贊同的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　合法化、擁護　|　英英定義　To support, to back, to give one's approval to, especially officially or by signature.　|　本文例句　Masterson, the president of the state Senate, was endorsed by President Trump.　|　例句中譯　州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "repeal", "sf": "repealed", "pos": "v.", "zh": "廢除", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　撤消、廢止　|　英英定義　An act or instance of repealing.　|　本文例句　Sam Brownback that led to a series of budget crises and was later repealed.　|　例句中譯　薩姆·布朗巴克法案導致了一系列預算危機，後來被廢除。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "pro-ag", "sf": "pro-ag", "pos": "", "zh": "前抗原", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　He promised to be the \"most pro-ag, pro-business, pro-oil and gas governor,\" the state has seen.　|　例句中譯　他承諾成為該州「最支持農業、支持商業、支持石油和天然氣的州長」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "cannabis", "sf": "cannabis", "pos": "n.", "zh": "大麻", "syn": "THC, bhang, dope", "tip": "其他意思　痲　|　英英定義　A tall annual dioecious plant (Cannabis, especially Cannabis sativa), native to central Asia and having alternate, palmately divided leaves and tough bast fibers.　|　本文例句　She also called for a moratorium on new data centers and for legalizing cannabis as a way to generate state revenue.　|　例句中譯　她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "legislature", "sf": "legislature", "pos": "n.", "zh": "立法機關", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　立法團体　|　英英定義　A governmental body with the power to make, amend and repeal laws.　|　本文例句　Laura Kelly is term-limited after serving for eight years in a state with a heavily Republican legislature and that usually votes for Republicans for other offices and in presidential elections.　|　例句中譯　勞拉凱利 (Laura Kelly) 在一個共和黨佔多數立法機構的州任職八年後，任期受到限制，該州通常在其他職位和總統選舉中投票給共和黨人。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/g-s1-151239/kansas-governor-midterms-holscher-masterson"}, {"code": "20261113-3", "ch": "2026-11-13　週五", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Cindy Holscher wins in Kansas, holding governor's office for Democrats　／　辛蒂霍爾舍 (Cindy Holscher) 在堪薩斯州獲勝，代表民主黨擔任州長", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Larry Kaplow，全文共 8 段、17 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：霍爾舍爾是一名州參議員，他擊敗了一位更知名的共和黨人，後者在該州得到了川普的支持，而在大多數其他全州競選中，共和黨人都支持了這位共和黨人。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/g-s1-151187/holscher-kansas-masterson-governor-midterms"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "據美聯社報導，民主黨州參議員辛迪·霍爾舍爾(Cindy Holsch…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Democratic state Sen.", "zh": "民主黨州參議員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Cindy Holscher will hold onto the Kansas governor's office for her party after defeating Republican Ty Masterson, according to a race call by the Associated Press.", "zh": "據美聯社的競選電話稱，在擊敗共和黨人泰·馬斯特森後，辛迪·霍爾舍爾將為其政黨保住堪薩斯州州長職位。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。在全國 36 次州長選舉中…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Masterson, the president of the state Senate, was **endorsed** by President Trump.", "zh": "州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Of the 36 elections for governor across the country, Kansas was seen as the most likely to flip from Democratic to Republican control.", "zh": "在全國 36 次州長選舉中，堪薩斯州被認為最有可能從民主黨控制權轉向共和黨控制權。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "經過幾天的臨時選票計票以及地方官員在這場競爭激烈的選舉中重新計票後，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "The race call came after days of counting the **provisional** ballots and with local officials doing **recounts** in the closely contested election.", "zh": "經過幾天的**臨時**選票計票以及地方官員在這場競爭激烈的選舉中重新計票後，選舉結果發出了。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "現任民主黨州長勞拉·凱利(Laura Kelly)在一個共和黨佔多數…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Current Democratic Gov.", "zh": "現任民主黨州長"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Laura Kelly is term-limited after serving for eight years in a state with a heavily Republican legislature and that usually votes for Republicans for other offices and in presidential elections.", "zh": "勞拉凱利 (Laura Kelly) 在一個共和黨佔多數立法機構的州任職八年後，任期受到限制，該州通常在其他職位和總統選舉中投票給共和黨人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of **populism**, promising to fight \"**sweetheart** deals\" for **billionaires**.", "zh": "57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有**民粹主義**色彩的競選活動，承諾為**億萬富翁**爭取「甜心交易」。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She tied Masterson to his work in the state Senate when it passed a tax cut under former Republican Gov.", "zh": "她將馬斯特森與他在州參議院的工作聯繫起來，當時州參議院透過了前共和黨州長川普領導下的減稅政策。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Sam Brownback that led to a series of budget **crises** and was later **repealed**.", "zh": "薩姆·布朗巴克法案導致了一系列預算**危機**，後來被**廢除**。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Holscher opposed school **vouchers**, calling for more support for public schools, in contrast with Masterson, who backed school vouchers.", "zh": "霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She also called for a **moratorium** on new data centers and for **legalizing** cannabis as a way to generate state revenue.", "zh": "她也呼籲**暫停**新資料中心的建設，並使大麻**合法化**，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "57 歲的馬斯特森呼籲降低財產稅，並表示信仰影響了他的所有決定，包括…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Masterson, 57, called for lower property taxes and said faith influenced all his decisions, including in politics.", "zh": "57 歲的馬斯特森呼籲降低財產稅，並表示信仰影響了他的所有決定，包括政治方面的決定。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He promised to be the \"most **pro-ag**, pro-business, pro-oil and gas governor,\" the state has seen.", "zh": "他承諾成為該州「最支持農業、支持商業、支持石油和天然氣的州長」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He called Holscher, \"the most radical, liberal, socialist Democrat ever\" on a ticket in Kansas.", "zh": "他在堪薩斯州的一張選票上稱霍爾舍爾為「有史以來最激進、最自由、最社會主義的民主黨人」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "「他喜歡貼上很多標籤，」霍爾舍爾回答。 “你知道為什麼嗎？因為這就是…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "\"He likes to throw around a whole lot of labels,\" Holscher responded. \"You know why?", "zh": "「他喜歡貼上很多標籤，」霍爾舍爾回答。 「你知道為什麼嗎？"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Because that's all he's got.\"", "zh": "因為這就是他所擁有的一切。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "據美聯社報導，民主黨州參議員辛迪·霍爾舍爾(Cindy Holscher)在擊敗共和黨人泰·馬斯特森(Ty Masterson)後，將保住她所在政黨的堪薩斯州州長職位。　州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。在全國 36 次州長選舉中，堪薩斯州被認為最有可能從民主黨控制權轉向共和黨控制權。　經過幾天的臨時選票計票以及地方官員在這場競爭激烈的選舉中重新計票後，選舉結果發出了。　現任民主黨州長勞拉·凱利(Laura Kelly)在一個共和黨佔多數立法機構的州任職八年後，任期受到限制，該州通常在其他職位和總統選舉中投票支持共和黨。　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。她將馬斯特森與他在州參議院的工作聯繫在一起，當時州參議院透過了前共和黨州長薩姆·布朗巴克(Sam Brownback)領導下的減稅政策，該減稅政策導致了一系列預算危機，後來被廢除。　霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。　57 歲的馬斯特森呼籲降低財產稅，並表示信仰影響了他的所有決定，包括政治方面的決定。他承諾成為該州「最支持農業、支持商業、支持石油和天然氣的州長」。他在堪薩斯州的一張選票上稱霍爾舍爾為「有史以來最激進、最自由、最社會主義的民主黨人」。　「他喜歡貼上很多標籤，」霍爾舍爾回答。 “你知道為什麼嗎？因為這就是他所擁有的一切。”"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "populism", "sf": "populism", "pos": "n.", "zh": "民粹主義", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A political doctrine or philosophy that proposes that the rights and powers of ordinary people are exploited by a privileged elite, and supports their struggle to overcome this.　|　本文例句　Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of populism, promising to fight \"sweetheart deals\" for billionaires.　|　例句中譯　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "moratorium", "sf": "moratorium", "pos": "n.", "zh": "暫停", "syn": "hiatus, interruption, recess", "tip": "英英定義　An authorization to a debtor, permitting temporary suspension of payments.　|　本文例句　She also called for a moratorium on new data centers and for legalizing cannabis as a way to generate state revenue.　|　例句中譯　她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "recount", "sf": "recounts", "pos": "v.", "zh": "敘事", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　述說、訴、訴說、詳述　|　英英定義　Narration, account, description, rendering　|　本文例句　The race call came after days of counting the provisional ballots and with local officials doing recounts in the closely contested election.　|　例句中譯　經過幾天的臨時選票計票以及地方官員在這場競爭激烈的選舉中重新計票後，選舉結果發出了。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "legalize", "sf": "legalizing", "pos": "v.", "zh": "合法化", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　認證、使合法化　|　英英定義　To make legal or permit under law. Either by decriminalising something that has been illegal or by specifically permitting it.　|　本文例句　She also called for a moratorium on new data centers and for legalizing cannabis as a way to generate state revenue.　|　例句中譯　她也呼籲暫停新資料中心的建設，並使大麻合法化，以此作為增加國家收入的一種方式。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "vouchers", "sf": "vouchers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "優惠券", "syn": "coupon", "tip": "其他意思　保證人、傳票、憑單、憑證　|　英英定義　A piece of paper that entitles the holder to a discount, or that can be exchanged for goods and services.　|　本文例句　Holscher opposed school vouchers, calling for more support for public schools, in contrast with Masterson, who backed school vouchers.　|　例句中譯　霍爾舍爾反對學券，呼籲為公立學校提供更多支持，而馬斯特森則支持學券。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "crises", "sf": "crises", "pos": "n.", "zh": "危機", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　風波　|　英英定義　A crucial or decisive point or situation; a turning point.　|　本文例句　Sam Brownback that led to a series of budget crises and was later repealed.　|　例句中譯　薩姆·布朗巴克法案導致了一系列預算危機，後來被廢除。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "provisional", "sf": "provisional", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "臨時", "syn": "provisory", "tip": "其他意思　浮、暫時　|　英英定義　A postage stamp issued locally before an official issue is released.　|　本文例句　The race call came after days of counting the provisional ballots and with local officials doing recounts in the closely contested election.　|　例句中譯　經過幾天的臨時選票計票以及地方官員在這場競爭激烈的選舉中重新計票後，選舉結果發出了。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "sweetheart", "sf": "sweetheart", "pos": "v.", "zh": "親愛的", "syn": "sweetie, darling, dear", "tip": "其他意思　討 ... 歡心、愛侶、愛人、戀人　|　英英定義　A person who is always very kind.　|　本文例句　Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of populism, promising to fight \"sweetheart deals\" for billionaires.　|　例句中譯　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "billionaire", "sf": "billionaires", "pos": "n.", "zh": "億萬富翁", "syn": "milliardaire", "tip": "英英定義　Somebody whose wealth is greater than one billion (109) dollars, or other currency.　|　本文例句　Holscher, 57, ran a campaign with notes of populism, promising to fight \"sweetheart deals\" for billionaires.　|　例句中譯　57 歲的霍爾舍爾發起了一場帶有民粹主義色彩的競選活動，承諾為億萬富翁爭取「甜心交易」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "endorsed", "sf": "endorsed", "pos": "v.", "zh": "贊同的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　合法化、擁護　|　英英定義　To support, to back, to give one's approval to, especially officially or by signature.　|　本文例句　Masterson, the president of the state Senate, was endorsed by President Trump.　|　例句中譯　州參議院議長馬斯特森得到了川普總統的支持。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "repeal", "sf": "repealed", "pos": "v.", "zh": "廢除", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　撤消、廢止　|　英英定義　An act or instance of repealing.　|　本文例句　Sam Brownback that led to a series of budget crises and was later repealed.　|　例句中譯　薩姆·布朗巴克法案導致了一系列預算危機，後來被廢除。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "pro-ag", "sf": "pro-ag", "pos": "", "zh": "前抗原", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　He promised to be the \"most pro-ag, pro-business, pro-oil and gas governor,\" the state has seen.　|　例句中譯　他承諾成為該州「最支持農業、支持商業、支持石油和天然氣的州長」。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/12/g-s1-151187/holscher-kansas-masterson-governor-midterms"}, {"code": "20261112-1", "ch": "2026-11-12　週四", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Democrat Scott Colom wins Mississippi Senate race　／　民主黨人史考特·科洛姆贏得密西西比州參議員競選", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Stephen Fowler、,&nbsp;，全文共 9 段、16 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：根據美聯社報導，民主黨人史考特·科洛姆擊敗共和黨參議員辛蒂·海德·史密斯，贏得密西西比州美國參議院選舉。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/g-s1-151688/mississippi-senate-race-scott-colom"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "根據美聯社報導，民主黨人斯科特·科洛姆以微弱優勢擊敗共和黨參議員辛迪…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Democrat Scott Colom has won election to the U.S. Senate from Mississippi, according to a race call by the Associated Press, **narrowly** defeating Republican Sen. Cindy Hyde-Smith.", "zh": "根據美聯社報導，民主黨人斯科特·科洛姆以微弱優勢擊敗共和黨參議員辛迪·海德·史密斯，贏得了密西西比州美國參議院選舉。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "經過一個多星期的清點未決選票、缺席選票和宣誓選票（或臨時選票）後，科…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "After more than a week of counting outstanding, **absentee** ballots and **affidavit** — or **provisional** — ballots, Colom won the closest Senate race in the country by just a few thousand votes.", "zh": "經過一個多星期的清點未決選票、缺席選票和宣誓選票（或**臨時**選票）後，科羅姆以幾千票的優勢贏得了全國最接近的參議院競選。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "His victory expands the majority Democrats will have in the new Congress to 55 seats, with the race in Alaska still **undecided**.", "zh": "他的勝利使民主黨在新國會的多數席位擴大至 55 個，而阿拉斯加的競選仍未決出勝負。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "在民主黨充滿令人震驚的中期選舉中，科羅姆的勝利突顯出，在黑人選民投票…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "In a **midterm** full of stunning upsets for Democrats, Colom's victory **underscores** a dramatic shift in the political landscape across the South driven by a surge of Black voter **turnout**.", "zh": "在民主黨充滿令人震驚的中期選舉中，科羅姆的勝利突顯出，在黑人選民投票率激增的推動下，整個南方的政治格局發生了巨大變化。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "密西西比州的黑人選民比例為全國最高，接近 40%，但川普總統在 20…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Mississippi has the highest share of Black voters in the country, at close to 40%, but President Trump won the state by 23 points in 2024.", "zh": "密西西比州的黑人選民比例為全國最高，接近 40%，但川普總統在 2024 年以 23 個百分點的優勢贏得了該州。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mississippi hasn't elected a Democrat to the U.S. Senate in more than 40 years and hasn't sent a Black senator to Washington since Reconstruction.", "zh": "密西西比州已有 40 多年沒有選出民主黨參議員進入美國參議院，自重建以來也沒有向華盛頓派出黑人參議員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "科羅姆本月稍早告訴美國國家公共廣播電台，直到最後一刻才缺乏民主黨人的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Colom told NPR earlier this month that a lack of investment from national Democrats until the last minute was a mistake.", "zh": "科羅姆本月稍早告訴美國國家公共廣播電台，直到最後一刻才缺乏民主黨人的投資是個錯誤。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "選舉 黑人投票權和川普疲勞能否打破密西西比州的紅牆？ 「現實是，密西…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Elections Can Black voting power and Trump fatigue break Mississippi's red wall?", "zh": "選舉 黑人投票權和川普疲勞能否打破密西西比州的紅牆？"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The reality is, Mississippi has never been a lost cause, we've been a **betrayed** cause,\" he said.", "zh": "「現實是，密西西比州從來都不是一個失敗的事業，我們一直是一個**被背叛**的事業，」他說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The Democratic Party has not been trying to win Mississippi.", "zh": "「民主黨並沒有試圖贏得密西西比州。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Let's stop kidding ourselves, right?", "zh": "我們別再自欺欺人了，對吧？", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They spent hundreds of millions of dollars in other states.", "zh": "他們在其他州花費了數億美元。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They spent almost nothing in Mississippi.\"", "zh": "他們在密西西比州幾乎沒有花任何錢。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "科羅姆的競選風格與海德史密斯形成鮮明對比，海德史密斯很少在華盛頓接受…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Colom's campaign was a contrast in style from Hyde-Smith, who rarely spoke to reporters in Washington and had minimal presence in the state.", "zh": "科羅姆的競選風格與海德史密斯形成鮮明對比，海德史密斯很少在華盛頓接受記者採訪，在該州的存在也很少。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "當今年早些時候被問及高牛肉價格時，養牛場主、前州農業專員海德史密斯表…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "When asked about high beef prices earlier this year, Hyde-Smith — a cattle **rancher** and **onetime** state agriculture commissioner — said that \"you have so many other proteins to choose from.\"", "zh": "當今年早些時候被問及高牛肉價格時，養牛場主、前州農業專員海德史密斯表示，“你還有很多其他蛋白質可供選擇。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "這導致了科洛姆的一則病毒式競選廣告，其中有幾個人對這位參議員「選擇另…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "That led to a viral campaign ad from Colom, which featured several people expressing **disbelief** at the senator's suggestion to \"pick another protein.\" Instead, the ad said, it was time to \"pick another senator.\"", "zh": "這導致了科洛姆的一則病毒式競選廣告，其中有幾個人對這位參議員「選擇另一種蛋白質」的建議表示不相信。相反，廣告稱，是時候「挑選另一位參議員」了。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "根據美聯社報導，民主黨人斯科特·科洛姆以微弱優勢擊敗共和黨參議員辛迪·海德·史密斯，贏得了密西西比州美國參議院選舉。　經過一個多星期的清點未決選票、缺席選票和宣誓選票（或臨時選票）後，科羅姆以幾千票的優勢贏得了全國最接近的參議院競選。他的勝利使民主黨在新國會的多數席位擴大至 55 個，而阿拉斯加的競選仍未決出勝負。　在民主黨充滿令人震驚的中期選舉中，科羅姆的勝利突顯出，在黑人選民投票率激增的推動下，整個南方的政治格局發生了巨大變化。　密西西比州的黑人選民比例為全國最高，接近 40%，但川普總統在 2024 年以 23 個百分點的優勢贏得了該州。密西西比州已有 40 多年沒有選舉民主黨進入美國參議院，自重建以來也沒有派遣黑人參議員到華盛頓。　科羅姆本月稍早告訴美國國家公共廣播電台，直到最後一刻才缺乏民主黨人的投資是個錯誤。　選舉 黑人投票權和川普疲勞能否打破密西西比州的紅牆？ 「現實是，密西西比州從來都不是一個失敗的事業，我們一直是一個被背叛的事業，」他說。 「民主黨並沒有試圖贏得密西西比州。我們別再自欺欺人了，對吧？他們在其他州花了數億美元。他們在密西西比州幾乎沒有花任何錢。”　科羅姆的競選風格與海德史密斯形成鮮明對比，海德史密斯很少在華盛頓接受記者採訪，在該州的存在也很少。　當今年早些時候被問及高牛肉價格時，養牛場主、前州農業專員海德史密斯表示，“你還有很多其他蛋白質可供選擇。”　這導致了科洛姆的一則病毒式競選廣告，其中有幾個人對這位參議員「選擇另一種蛋白質」的建議表示不相信。相反，廣告稱，是時候「挑選另一位參議員」了。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "onetime", "sf": "onetime", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "一度", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　從前的、前、前任、原　|　本文例句　When asked about high beef prices earlier this year, Hyde-Smith — a cattle rancher and onetime state agriculture commissioner — said that \"you have so many other proteins to choose from.　|　例句中譯　今年稍早被問及高牛肉價格時，養牛場主、前州農業專員海德史密斯表示，「還有很多其他蛋白質可供選擇。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "underscore", "sf": "underscores", "pos": "v.", "zh": "底線", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　劃線於 ... 下、講　|　英英定義　An underline; a line drawn or printed beneath text; the character _.　|　本文例句　In a midterm full of stunning upsets for Democrats, Colom's victory underscores a dramatic shift in the political landscape across the South driven by a surge of Black voter turnout.　|　例句中譯　在民主黨充滿令人震驚的中期選舉中，科羅姆的勝利突顯出，在黑人選民投票率激增的推動下，整個南方的政治格局發生了巨大變化。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "rancher", "sf": "rancher", "pos": "n.", "zh": "牧場主人", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　牧場工人、農場工人　|　英英定義　A person who operates a ranch.　|　本文例句　When asked about high beef prices earlier this year, Hyde-Smith — a cattle rancher and onetime state agriculture commissioner — said that \"you have so many other proteins to choose from.　|　例句中譯　今年稍早被問及高牛肉價格時，養牛場主、前州農業專員海德史密斯表示，「還有很多其他蛋白質可供選擇。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "absentee", "sf": "absentee", "pos": "n.", "zh": "缺席者", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A person who is absent from his or her employment, school, post, duty, etc.　|　本文例句　After more than a week of counting outstanding, absentee ballots and affidavit — or provisional — ballots, Colom won the closest Senate race in the country by just a few thousand votes.　|　例句中譯　經過一個多星期的清點未決選票、缺席選票和宣誓選票（或臨時選票）後，科羅姆以幾千票的優勢贏得了全國最接近的參議院競選。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "undecided", "sf": "undecided", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "未定", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　媕、踟、躕、未定的　|　英英定義　To reverse or recant (a previous decision).　|　本文例句　His victory expands the majority Democrats will have in the new Congress to 55 seats, with the race in Alaska still undecided.　|　例句中譯　他的勝利使民主黨在新國會的多數席位擴大至 55 個，而阿拉斯加的競選仍未決出勝負。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "midterm", "sf": "midterm", "pos": "n.", "zh": "期中考", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A midterm school exam (i.e., halfway through the term).　|　本文例句　In a midterm full of stunning upsets for Democrats, Colom's victory underscores a dramatic shift in the political landscape across the South driven by a surge of Black voter turnout.　|　例句中譯　在民主黨充滿令人震驚的中期選舉中，科羅姆的勝利突顯出，在黑人選民投票率激增的推動下，整個南方的政治格局發生了巨大變化。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "affidavit", "sf": "affidavit", "pos": "n.", "zh": "宣誓書", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A signed document wherein an affiant makes a sworn statement.　|　本文例句　After more than a week of counting outstanding, absentee ballots and affidavit — or provisional — ballots, Colom won the closest Senate race in the country by just a few thousand votes.　|　例句中譯　經過一個多星期的清點未決選票、缺席選票和宣誓選票（或臨時選票）後，科羅姆以幾千票的優勢贏得了全國最接近的參議院競選。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "disbelief", "sf": "disbelief", "pos": "n.", "zh": "懷疑", "syn": "incredulity", "tip": "英英定義　Unpreparedness, unwillingness, or inability to believe that something is the case.　|　本文例句　That led to a viral campaign ad from Colom, which featured several people expressing disbelief at the senator's suggestion to \"pick another protein.　|　例句中譯　這導致了科洛姆的一則病毒式競選廣告，其中有幾個人對這位參議員「選擇另一種蛋白質」的建議表示不相信。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "narrowly", "sf": "narrowly", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "狹隘地", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　精細地、險些　|　英英定義　In a narrow manner; without flexibility or latitude.　|　本文例句　Senate from Mississippi, according to a race call by the Associated Press, narrowly defeating Republican Sen.　|　例句中譯　根據美聯社的競選呼籲，來自密西西比州的參議院以微弱優勢擊敗了共和黨參議員。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "provisional", "sf": "provisional", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "臨時", "syn": "provisory", "tip": "其他意思　浮、暫時　|　英英定義　A postage stamp issued locally before an official issue is released.　|　本文例句　After more than a week of counting outstanding, absentee ballots and affidavit — or provisional — ballots, Colom won the closest Senate race in the country by just a few thousand votes.　|　例句中譯　經過一個多星期的清點未決選票、缺席選票和宣誓選票（或臨時選票）後，科羅姆以幾千票的優勢贏得了全國最接近的參議院競選。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "turnout", "sf": "turnout", "pos": "v.", "zh": "結果發現", "syn": "lay-by", "tip": "其他意思　出、發生　|　英英定義　The act of coming forth.　|　本文例句　In a midterm full of stunning upsets for Democrats, Colom's victory underscores a dramatic shift in the political landscape across the South driven by a surge of Black voter turnout.　|　例句中譯　在民主黨充滿令人震驚的中期選舉中，科羅姆的勝利突顯出，在黑人選民投票率激增的推動下，整個南方的政治格局發生了巨大變化。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "betrayed", "sf": "betrayed", "pos": "v.", "zh": "被背叛", "syn": "sell", "tip": "其他意思　背叛、出賣、負、流露　|　英英定義　To deliver into the hands of an enemy by treachery or fraud, in violation of trust; to give up treacherously or faithlessly.　|　本文例句　Elections Can Black voting power and Trump fatigue break Mississippi's red wall? \"The reality is, Mississippi has never been a lost cause, we've been a betrayed cause,\" he said.　|　例句中譯　選舉 黑人投票權和川普疲勞能否打破密西西比州的紅牆？ 「現實是，密西西比州從來都不是一個失敗的事業，我們一直是一個被背叛的事業，」他說。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/g-s1-151688/mississippi-senate-race-scott-colom"}, {"code": "20261112-2", "ch": "2026-11-12　週四", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Why is gasoline suddenly under $4 a gallon?　／　為什麼汽油價格突然低於每加侖 4 美元？", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Willa Rubin，全文共 8 段、18 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：本週一加侖汽油的平均價格幾個月來首次跌破 4 美元。這是否意味著司機將得到更多緩解？"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/nx-s1-6037588/gasoline-price-below-4-dollars-gallon"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "司機們開始看到高油價帶來的一些緩解。根據 AAA 的數據，每加侖汽油…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Drivers are starting to see some relief from high fuel prices.", "zh": "司機們開始看到高油價帶來的一些緩解。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "For the first time in months, the average price of a gallon of gasoline has **dipped** below $4, according to AAA.", "zh": "根據 AAA 的數據，每加侖汽油的平均價格幾個月來首次跌破 4 美元。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "週二，該價格跌破了 4 美元的門檻，目前已降至全國平均每加侖 3.9…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The price crossed below the $4 threshold on Tuesday, and is currently down to a national average of $3.94 for a gallon of regular.", "zh": "週二，該價格跌破了 4 美元的門檻，目前已降至全國平均每加侖 3.94 美元。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Prices have **dipped** about 40 cents over the past month, with much of that decline happening in the past two weeks.", "zh": "過去一個月價格下跌了約 40 美分，其中大部分跌幅發生在過去兩週。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "萊昂在給美國國家公共廣播電台的電子郵件中寫道，如果戰爭升級，這項進展…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "That progress could easily be reversed if the war **escalates**, León wrote in an email to NPR.", "zh": "萊昂在給美國國家公共廣播電台的電子郵件中寫道，如果戰爭**升級**，這項進展很容易被逆轉。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"President Trump may see further military action as a way to **regain** negotiating leverage before Democrats take control of Congress in January.", "zh": "「川普總統可能會將進一步的軍事行動視為在民主黨一月份控制國會之前重新獲得談判籌碼的一種方式。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "If we see renewed **escalation**, much of last week's oil price decline could quickly reverse,\" he wrote.", "zh": "如果我們看到局勢再次**升級**，上週油價的大部分跌勢可能會迅速逆轉，」他寫道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The same would be true for gas prices.", "zh": "天然氣價格也是。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "國會民主黨人表示支持結束伊朗戰爭。雖然他們這樣做的權力有限，但他們確…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Congressional Democrats have expressed their support for ending the war in Iran.", "zh": "國會民主黨人表示支持結束伊朗戰爭。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "While they have limited power to do that, they do control the power of the purse, and can **withhold** additional war funding or hold back confirmations of key officials.", "zh": "雖然他們這樣做的權力有限，但他們確實控制著財政的權力，並且可以扣留額外的戰爭資金或阻止關鍵官員的確認。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "石油公司的獲利再次飆升 目前，如果布蘭特原油價格持續下跌，加油站價格…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Business Oil company earnings **skyrocket** — again For now, if the price of Brent crude keeps falling, so could prices at the pump.", "zh": "石油公司的獲利再次飆升 目前，如果布蘭特原油價格持續下跌，加油站價格也會下跌。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"However, this does not mean a complete '**normalization**,' a return to the price levels we had before this conflict started,\" Jaime Brito, executive director of **refining** and oil markets for Dow Jones Energy, wrote in an email to NPR.", "zh": "道瓊斯能源公司煉油和石油市場執行董事傑米·布里托（Jaime Brito）在給美國國家公共廣播電台（NPR）的電子郵件中寫道：“然而，這並不意味著完全‘**正常化**’，也不意味著回到衝突開始之前的價格水平。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "為了恢復到伊朗戰爭前的天然氣價格，整個石油供應鏈必須恢復。為避開霍爾…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "To get back to pre-Iran war gas prices, the whole oil supply chain would have to recover.", "zh": "為了**恢復**到伊朗戰爭前的天然氣價格，整個石油供應鏈必須恢復。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Ships that have been running long alternative routes to avoid the Strait of Hormuz would have to return to their points of origin, then resume their normal routes, taking crude oil to **refineries**.", "zh": "為避開霍爾木茲海峽而長途跋涉的船舶必須返回出發地，然後**恢復**正常航線，將原油運往**煉油廠**。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Those **refineries** would have to pump out enough fuel to alleviate global demand — and **depleted** **stockpiles**.", "zh": "這些**煉油廠**必須生產足夠的燃料來緩解全球需求和**耗盡的**庫存。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The whole process could take months after a lasting peace deal.", "zh": "在達成持久和平協議後，整個過程可能需要幾個月的時間。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "布里托繼續說道：“要回到這些水平，就需要整個全球供應鏈恢復正常的原油…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "\"Coming back to those levels will require a return to normal crude production, shipping and **refining** of the entire global supply chain,\" Brito continued.", "zh": "布里托繼續說道：“要回到這些水平，就需要整個全球供應鏈**恢復**正常的原油生產、運輸和煉油。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "雖然目前每加侖 4 美元似乎很便宜，但 AAA 在其網站的更新中表示…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "And while $4 a gallon may seem like a bargain these days, in an update on its website, AAA said that gasoline prices are still the highest they've ever been at this time of year.", "zh": "雖然目前每加侖 4 美元似乎很便宜，但 AAA 在其網站的更新中表示，汽油價格仍然是一年中這個時候的最高水平。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "司機們開始看到高油價帶來的一些緩解。根據 AAA 的數據，每加侖汽油的平均價格幾個月來首次跌破 4 美元。　週二，該價格跌破了 4 美元的門檻，目前已降至全國平均每加侖 3.94 美元。過去一個月價格下跌了約 40 美分，其中大部分跌幅發生在過去兩週。　萊昂在給美國國家公共廣播電台的電子郵件中寫道，如果戰爭升級，這項進展很容易被逆轉。 「川普總統可能會將進一步的軍事行動視為在民主黨一月份控制國會之前重新獲得談判籌碼的一種方式。如果我們看到局勢再次升級，上週油價的大部分跌勢可能會迅速逆轉，」他寫道。天然氣價格也是。　國會民主黨人表示支持結束伊朗戰爭。雖然他們這樣做的權力有限，但他們確實控制著財政的權力，並且可以扣留額外的戰爭資金或阻止關鍵官員的確認。　石油公司的獲利再次飆升 目前，如果布蘭特原油價格持續下跌，加油站價格也會下跌。道瓊斯能源公司煉油和石油市場執行董事傑米·布里托（Jaime Brito）在給美國國家公共廣播電台（NPR）的電子郵件中寫道：“然而，這並不意味著完全‘正常化’，也不意味著回到衝突開始之前的價格水平。”　為了恢復到伊朗戰爭前的天然氣價格，整個石油供應鏈必須恢復。為避開霍爾木茲海峽而長途跋涉的船舶必須返回出發地，然後恢復正常航線，將原油運往煉油廠。這些煉油廠必須生產足夠的燃料來緩解全球需求和耗盡的庫存。在達成持久和平協議後，整個過程可能需要幾個月的時間。　布里托繼續說道：“要回到這些水平，就需要整個全球供應鏈恢復正常的原油生產、運輸和煉油。”　雖然目前每加侖 4 美元似乎很便宜，但 AAA 在其網站的更新中表示，汽油價格仍然是一年中這個時候的最高水平。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "skyrocket", "sf": "skyrocket", "pos": "v.", "zh": "飆漲", "syn": "maroon", "tip": "其他意思　飛漲、平步青雲　|　英英定義　A type of firework that uses a solid rocket engine to rise quickly into the sky where it emits a variety of effects such as stars, bangs, crackles, etc.　|　本文例句　Business Oil company earnings skyrocket — again For now, if the price of Brent crude keeps falling, so could prices at the pump.　|　例句中譯　石油公司的獲利再次飆升 目前，如果布蘭特原油價格持續下跌，加油站價格也會下跌。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "normalization", "sf": "normalization", "pos": "n.", "zh": "正常化", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　正規化　|　本文例句　\"However, this does not mean a complete 'normalization,' a return to the price levels we had before this conflict started,\" Jaime Brito, executive director of refining and oil markets for Dow Jones Energy, wrote in an email to NPR.　|　例句中譯　道瓊斯能源公司煉油和石油市場執行董事傑米·布里托（Jaime Brito）在給美國國家公共廣播電台（NPR）的電子郵件中寫道：“然而，這並不意味著完全‘正常化’，也不意味著回到衝突開始之前的價格水平。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "stockpile", "sf": "stockpiles", "pos": "n.", "zh": "儲存", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　儲藏、積存、稹　|　英英定義　A supply, especially a large one, of something kept for future use.　|　本文例句　Those refineries would have to pump out enough fuel to alleviate global demand — and depleted stockpiles.　|　例句中譯　這些煉油廠必須生產足夠的燃料來緩解全球需求和耗盡的庫存。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "withhold", "sf": "withhold", "pos": "v.", "zh": "扣壓", "syn": "retain", "tip": "其他意思　保留、拒給　|　英英定義　To keep (a physical object that one has obtained) to oneself rather than giving it back to its owner.　|　本文例句　While they have limited power to do that, they do control the power of the purse, and can withhold additional war funding or hold back confirmations of key officials.　|　例句中譯　雖然他們這樣做的權力有限，但他們確實控制著財政的權力，並且可以扣留額外的戰爭資金或阻止關鍵官員的確認。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "escalation", "sf": "escalation", "pos": "n.", "zh": "升級", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　An increase or rise, especially one to counteract a perceived discrepancy　|　本文例句　If we see renewed escalation, much of last week's oil price decline could quickly reverse,\" he wrote.　|　例句中譯　如果我們看到局勢再次升級，上週油價的大部分跌勢可能會迅速逆轉，」他寫道。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "escalate", "sf": "escalates", "pos": "v.", "zh": "升級", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　升高　|　英英定義　To increase (something) in extent or intensity; to intensify or step up.　|　本文例句　That progress could easily be reversed if the war escalates, León wrote in an email to NPR.　|　例句中譯　萊昂在給美國國家公共廣播電台的電子郵件中寫道，如果戰爭升級，這項進展很容易被逆轉。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "refining", "sf": "refining", "pos": "n.", "zh": "精製", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　提煉　|　本文例句　\"Coming back to those levels will require a return to normal crude production, shipping and refining of the entire global supply chain,\" Brito continued.　|　例句中譯　布里托繼續說道：“要回到這些水平，就需要整個全球供應鏈恢復正常的原油生產、運輸和煉油。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "depleted", "sf": "depleted", "pos": "v.", "zh": "耗盡的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　耗盡、消耗　|　英英定義　To empty or unload, as the vessels of the human system, by bloodletting or by medicine.　|　本文例句　Those refineries would have to pump out enough fuel to alleviate global demand — and depleted stockpiles.　|　例句中譯　這些煉油廠必須生產足夠的燃料來緩解全球需求和耗盡的庫存。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "refinery", "sf": "refineries", "pos": "n.", "zh": "煉油廠", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A building, or a mass of machinery, used to produce refined products such as sugar, oil, or metals.　|　本文例句　Ships that have been running long alternative routes to avoid the Strait of Hormuz would have to return to their points of origin, then resume their normal routes, taking crude oil to refineries.　|　例句中譯　為避開霍爾木茲海峽而長途跋涉的船舶必須返回出發地，然後恢復正常航線，將原油運往煉油廠。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "alleviate", "sf": "alleviate", "pos": "v.", "zh": "減輕", "syn": "address, allay, ameliorate", "tip": "其他意思　和緩、緩和　|　英英定義　To make less severe, as a pain or difficulty.　|　本文例句　Those refineries would have to pump out enough fuel to alleviate global demand — and depleted stockpiles.　|　例句中譯　這些煉油廠必須生產足夠的燃料來緩解全球需求和耗盡的庫存。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "dipped", "sf": "dipped", "pos": "v.", "zh": "浸入", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　淬、浸一下、蘸　|　英英定義　To lower into a liquid.　|　本文例句　For the first time in months, the average price of a gallon of gasoline has dipped below $4, according to AAA.　|　例句中譯　根據 AAA 的數據，每加侖汽油的平均價格幾個月來首次跌破 4 美元。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "regain", "sf": "regain", "pos": "v.", "zh": "恢復", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　复得、收回　|　本文例句　\"President Trump may see further military action as a way to regain negotiating leverage before Democrats take control of Congress in January.　|　例句中譯　「川普總統可能會將進一步的軍事行動視為在民主黨一月份控制國會之前重新獲得談判籌碼的一種方式。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/nx-s1-6037588/gasoline-price-below-4-dollars-gallon"}, {"code": "20261112-3", "ch": "2026-11-12　週四", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Greetings from Senegal, where breakdancers are competing in the Youth Olympics　／　來自塞內加爾的問候，霹靂舞者正在那裡參加青年奧運會", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Ricci Shryock，全文共 5 段、11 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：塞內加爾的霹靂舞者一直在為該國本月歷史性地主辦青奧會進行練習。這是非洲首次舉辦奧運比賽專案。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/g-s1-150228/senegal-youth-olympic-games-breakdancing"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "便攜式揚聲器播放著嘻哈音樂，六名青少年在塞內加爾首都達卡練習他們最拿…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Hip-hop music blasted over a **portable** speaker while half-a-dozen **teenagers** practiced their best breakdancing moves in Senagal's capital Dakar.", "zh": "便攜式揚聲器播放著嘻哈音樂，六名**青少年**在塞內加爾首都達卡練習他們最拿手的霹靂舞動作。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They **glided** on their shins and jumped into the air, **clutched** their heels and struck **midair** poses.", "zh": "他們用小腿**滑行**，跳到空中，抓住腳跟，擺出空中姿勢。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "塞內加爾的霹靂舞者在本月該國歷史性地舉辦青奧會之前磨練自己的技能。這…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Senegal's breakdancers were honing their **craft** ahead of the country's historic hosting of the Youth Olympic Games this month.", "zh": "塞內加爾的霹靂舞者在本月該國歷史性地舉辦青奧會之前磨練自己的技能。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's the first time an Olympic event is being held on African soil.", "zh": "這是奧運會首次在非洲土地上舉行。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "上個月我拍了這張照片，當時 15 歲的蘇珊娜·杜爾 (Suzanne…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "I took the photo above last month as 15-year-old Suzanne Toure struck a breakdancing pose.", "zh": "上個月我拍了這張照片，當時 15 歲的蘇珊娜·杜爾 (Suzanne Toure) 擺出了霹靂舞的姿勢。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She is the only girl on the Senegal National Sport Dance and Break Team.", "zh": "她是塞內加爾國家體育舞蹈和霹靂隊中唯一的女孩。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Three years ago, her little brother introduced her to breakdancing.", "zh": "三年前，她的弟弟向她介紹了霹靂舞。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "塞內加爾隊的舞者將傳統動作融入姆巴拉克斯和耶拉等民族風格的舞蹈中，以…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Dancers on the Senegalese team mix traditional moves into their routines from national styles such as mbalax and Yela, **swirling** their arms and legs in a **windmill-like** motion.", "zh": "塞內加爾隊的舞者將傳統動作融入姆巴拉克斯和耶拉等民族風格的舞蹈中，以**風車般的**動作旋轉手臂和腿。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"You can sense some American and European influence in our routines, yes, but there are also African dances.", "zh": "「是的，你可以感覺到我們的舞蹈受到了一些美國和歐洲的影響，但也有非洲舞蹈。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's about **mixing** these African dances into the breaking,\" says coach Francis Siméon Gomis.", "zh": "這是將這些非洲舞蹈融入霹靂舞中，」教練 Francis Siméon Gomis 說道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "他們認為這是向世界展示他們的國家在舞池上的能力的機會，並希望在主場贏…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "They see this as their chance to show the world what their nation can offer on the dance floor, and hope to win a medal on home turf.", "zh": "他們認為這是向世界展示他們的國家在舞池上的能力的機會，並希望在主場贏得獎牌。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "便攜式揚聲器播放著嘻哈音樂，六名青少年在塞內加爾首都達卡練習他們最拿手的霹靂舞動作。他們用小腿滑行，跳到空中，抓住腳跟，擺出空中姿勢。　塞內加爾的霹靂舞者在本月該國歷史性地舉辦青奧會之前磨練自己的技能。這是奧運會首次在非洲土地上舉行。　上個月我拍了這張照片，當時 15 歲的蘇珊娜·杜爾 (Suzanne Toure) 擺出了霹靂舞的姿勢。她是塞內加爾國家體育舞蹈和霹靂隊中唯一的女孩。三年前，她的弟弟向她介紹了霹靂舞。　塞內加爾隊的舞者將傳統動作融入姆巴拉克斯和耶拉等民族風格的舞蹈中，以風車般的動作旋轉手臂和腿。 「是的，你可以感覺到我們的舞蹈受到了一些美國和歐洲的影響，但也有非洲舞蹈。我們要把這些非洲舞蹈融入到霹靂舞中，」教練 Francis Siméon Gomis 說道。　他們認為這是向世界展示他們的國家在舞池上的能力的機會，並希望在主場贏得獎牌。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "midair", "sf": "midair", "pos": "n.", "zh": "半空中", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A collision between two or more aerospace vehicles in flight.　|　本文例句　They glided on their shins and jumped into the air, clutched their heels and struck midair poses.　|　例句中譯　他們用小腿滑行，跳到空中，抓住腳跟，擺出空中姿勢。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "windmill-like", "sf": "windmill-like", "pos": "", "zh": "風車般的", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　Dancers on the Senegalese team mix traditional moves into their routines from national styles such as mbalax and Yela, swirling their arms and legs in a windmill-like motion.　|　例句中譯　塞內加爾隊的舞者將傳統動作融入姆巴拉克斯和耶拉等民族風格的舞蹈中，以風車般的動作旋轉手臂和腿。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "swirling", "sf": "swirling", "pos": "v.", "zh": "旋轉的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　捲　|　英英定義　To twist or whirl, as an eddy.　|　本文例句　Dancers on the Senegalese team mix traditional moves into their routines from national styles such as mbalax and Yela, swirling their arms and legs in a windmill-like motion.　|　例句中譯　塞內加爾隊的舞者將傳統動作融入姆巴拉克斯和耶拉等民族風格的舞蹈中，以風車般的動作旋轉手臂和腿。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "glide", "sf": "glided", "pos": "v.", "zh": "滑行", "syn": "semiconsonant, semivowel", "tip": "其他意思　滑動、滑過、溜、滑翔　|　英英定義　The act of gliding.　|　本文例句　They glided on their shins and jumped into the air, clutched their heels and struck midair poses.　|　例句中譯　他們用小腿滑行，跳到空中，抓住腳跟，擺出空中姿勢。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "clutch", "sf": "clutched", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "離合器", "syn": "clutch bag", "tip": "其他意思　無皮帶的、無小手的、操、扼　|　英英定義　The claw of a predatory animal or bird.　|　本文例句　They glided on their shins and jumped into the air, clutched their heels and struck midair poses.　|　例句中譯　他們用小腿滑行，跳到空中，抓住腳跟，擺出空中姿勢。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "portable", "sf": "portable", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "便攜的", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　可移植、輕便、手提、攜帶　|　英英定義　A portable building used for temporary purposes, particularly:　|　本文例句　Hip-hop music blasted over a portable speaker while half-a-dozen teenagers practiced their best breakdancing moves in Senagal's capital Dakar.　|　例句中譯　便攜式揚聲器播放著嘻哈音樂，六名青少年在塞內加爾首都達卡練習他們最拿手的霹靂舞動作。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "heels", "sf": "heels", "pos": "n.", "zh": "高跟鞋", "syn": "ender, outsider", "tip": "其他意思　跟、後跟、腳跟、踵　|　英英定義　The rear part of the foot, where it joins the leg.　|　本文例句　They glided on their shins and jumped into the air, clutched their heels and struck midair poses.　|　例句中譯　他們用小腿滑行，跳到空中，抓住腳跟，擺出空中姿勢。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "teenager", "sf": "teenagers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "青少年", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　學童　|　英英定義　A person between 13 and 19 years of age; an adolescent.　|　本文例句　Hip-hop music blasted over a portable speaker while half-a-dozen teenagers practiced their best breakdancing moves in Senagal's capital Dakar.　|　例句中譯　便攜式揚聲器播放著嘻哈音樂，六名青少年在塞內加爾首都達卡練習他們最拿手的霹靂舞動作。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "mixing", "sf": "mixing", "pos": "n.", "zh": "混合", "syn": "mix together, mix up, muddle", "tip": "其他意思　混頻　|　英英定義　To stir together.　|　本文例句　It's about mixing these African dances into the breaking,\" says coach Francis Siméon Gomis.　|　例句中譯　這是將這些非洲舞蹈融入霹靂舞中，」教練 Francis Siméon Gomis 說道。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "craft", "sf": "craft", "pos": "n.", "zh": "工藝", "syn": "art, business, handicraft", "tip": "其他意思　船隻、工、詭計、航　|　英英定義　Strength; power; might; force .　|　本文例句　Senegal's breakdancers were honing their craft ahead of the country's historic hosting of the Youth Olympic Games this month.　|　例句中譯　塞內加爾的霹靂舞者在本月該國歷史性地舉辦青奧會之前磨練自己的技能。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/g-s1-150228/senegal-youth-olympic-games-breakdancing"}, {"code": "20261111-1", "ch": "2026-11-11　週三", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "House votes to effectively end the impeachment effort against Pete Hegseth　／　眾議院投票有效結束對皮特·赫格斯的彈劾努力", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Jason Breslow，全文共 12 段、18 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：眾議院共和黨人設法縮短了對肯塔基州共和黨人托馬斯·馬西針對國防部長的彈劾努力的眾議院投票。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6036813/house-votes-to-effectively-end-the-impeachment-effort-against-pete-hegseth"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "眾議院以 211 比 204 的投票結果，將針對國防部長皮特·赫格斯…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The House has voted 211 to 204 to refer the articles of impeachment filed against Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth to committee, effectively killing the impeachment effort spearheaded by Rep. Thomas Massie, R-Ky.", "zh": "眾議院以 211 比 204 的投票結果，將針對國防部長皮特·赫格斯 (Pete Hegseth) 的彈劾條款提交給委員會，這實際上扼殺了肯塔基州眾議員托馬斯·馬西 (Thomas Massie) 領導的彈劾努力。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "週二的投票縮短了對彈劾條款的任何潛在的眾議院投票，並且實際上保證了在…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Tuesday's vote short-circuits any potential floor vote on the articles of impeachment, and virtually guarantees the measure will not be taken up before the current session of Congress expires.", "zh": "週二的投票縮短了對彈劾條款的任何潛在的眾議院投票，並且實際上保證了在本屆國會會議結束之前不會採取該措施。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "這次投票為川普總統陷入困境的國防部長提供了意外的緩刑，他最早在周三就…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "The vote provided a surprise reprieve for President Trump's embattled Defense Secretary, who was facing an impeachment vote by the full House as early as Wednesday.", "zh": "這次投票為川普總統陷入困境的國防部長提供了意外的緩刑，他最早在周三就面臨眾議院全體議員的彈劾投票。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "馬西周一重新提出彈劾條款，指控赫格斯在與伊朗的戰爭、美國對伊朗的打擊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Massie reintroduced the articles of impeachment on Monday, accusing Hegseth of high crimes and misdemeanors in connection to the war with Iran and U.S. strikes against Iran and on alleged drug boats in the Caribbean Sea and Eastern Pacific Ocean.", "zh": "馬西周一重新提出彈劾條款，指控赫格斯在與伊朗的戰爭、美國對伊朗的打擊以及加勒比海和東太平洋涉嫌販毒船方面犯有重罪和輕罪。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "馬西的彈劾決議旨在罷免赫格賽斯，原因是他未經國會授權逮捕了委內瑞拉總…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Massie's impeachment resolution sought to oust Hegseth over the capture of Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro without congressional authorization, and the effort to punish Sen.", "zh": "馬西的彈劾決議旨在罷免赫格斯塞斯，因為未經國會授權逮捕了委內瑞拉總統尼古拉斯·馬杜羅，並試圖懲罰參議員馬杜羅。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Mark Kelly, D-Ariz., for a video telling service members they can refuse illegal orders.", "zh": "亞利桑那州民主黨人馬克凱利 (Mark Kelly) 拍攝一段影片，告訴軍人他們可以拒絕非法命令。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "週二，赫格斯在五角大廈舉行的一次罕見的新聞發布會上為自己反對彈劾努力…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Hegseth defended himself against the impeachment effort during a rare press conference at the Pentagon on Tuesday, criticizing Massie as a \"disgruntled and defeated congressman.\"", "zh": "週二，赫格斯在五角大廈舉行的一次罕見的新聞發布會上為自己反對彈劾努力進行了辯護，批評馬西是「心懷不滿和失敗的國會議員」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "「我支持每一項行動，」赫格斯說。 “我很自豪能夠處決他們，明天我還會…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "\"I stand behind every one of these operations,\" Hegseth said.", "zh": "「我支持每一項行動，」赫格斯說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"I was proud to execute them, and I would do it again tomorrow.\"", "zh": "“我很自豪能夠處決他們，明天我還會再這樣做。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "週一，川普在白宮舉行的一次內容廣泛的即興新聞發布會上表達了對赫格塞斯…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "On Monday, Trump expressed support for Hegseth during a wide-ranging, impromptu press briefing at the White House.", "zh": "週一，川普在白宮舉行的一次內容廣泛的即興新聞發布會上表達了對赫格塞斯的支持。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "川普說：“我會支持他。” “他贏得了兩場戰爭。他負責。我們都贏了。”", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"I'll stand by him,\" Trump said. \"He won two wars. He was in charge. We all won.\"", "zh": "川普說：“我會支持他。” “他贏得了兩場戰爭。他負責。我們都贏了。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "這次彈劾措施是馬西第二次嘗試針對赫格塞斯。他首先試圖在中期選舉之前將…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "The impeachment measure was Massie's second attempt against Hegseth.", "zh": "這次彈劾措施是馬西第二次嘗試針對赫格塞斯。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He first sought to bring the impeachment resolution to the floor before the midterm elections, prompting Speaker Mike Johnson, R-La., to call an early recess to avoid the vote.", "zh": "他首先試圖在中期選舉之前將彈劾決議提交表決，這促使路易斯安那州共和黨眾議員邁克·約翰遜(Mike Johnson)提前休會以避免投票。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That caused the resolution to expire, which is why Massie reintroduced the resolution again this week.", "zh": "這導致該決議失效，這就是馬西本週再次重新提出該決議的原因。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "雖然彈劾行動可能暫時平息，但赫格塞斯在國會山莊的麻煩還沒結束。民主黨…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "While the impeachment push may be quelled for now, Hegseth's troubles on Capitol Hill are not over.", "zh": "雖然彈劾行動可能暫時平息，但赫格塞斯在國會山莊的麻煩還沒結束。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Democrats have promised vigorous investigations into Hegseth's Pentagon once they assume the majority in January.", "zh": "民主黨人承諾，一旦他們在一月取得多數席位，就會對赫格賽斯領導的五角大廈展開積極調查。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "他們是否會發起另一次彈劾工作尚不清楚，但在上週接受美國國家公共廣播電…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "Whether they will mount another impeachment effort remains unclear, but in an interview with NPR last week, Rep.", "zh": "他們是否會發起另一次彈劾努力尚不清楚，但在上週接受 NPR 採訪時，眾議員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Hakeem Jeffries, who is expected to be the next Speaker of the House, said simply of Hegseth, \"He's got to go.\"", "zh": "預計將成為下一任眾議院議長的哈基姆·杰弗里斯在談到赫格賽斯時簡單地說：“他必須下台。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "眾議院以 211 比 204 的投票結果，將針對國防部長皮特·赫格斯 (Pete Hegseth) 的彈劾條款提交給委員會，這實際上扼殺了肯塔基州眾議員托馬斯·馬西 (Thomas Massie) 領導的彈劾努力。　週二的投票縮短了對彈劾條款的任何潛在的眾議院投票，並且實際上保證了在本屆國會會議結束之前不會採取該措施。　這次投票為川普總統陷入困境的國防部長提供了意外的緩刑，他最早在周三就面臨眾議院全體議員的彈劾投票。　馬西周一重新提出彈劾條款，指控赫格斯在與伊朗的戰爭、美國對伊朗的打擊以及加勒比海和東太平洋涉嫌販毒船方面犯有重罪和輕罪。　馬西的彈劾決議旨在罷免赫格賽斯，原因是他未經國會授權逮捕了委內瑞拉總統尼古拉斯·馬杜羅，並試圖懲罰亞利桑那州民主黨參議員馬克·凱利，因為他發布了一段影片，告訴軍人可以拒絕非法命令。　週二，赫格斯在五角大廈舉行的一次罕見的新聞發布會上為自己反對彈劾努力進行了辯護，批評馬西是「心懷不滿和失敗的國會議員」。　「我支持每一項行動，」赫格斯說。 “我很自豪能夠處決他們，明天我還會再這樣做。”　週一，川普在白宮舉行的一次內容廣泛的即興新聞發布會上表達了對赫格塞斯的支持。　川普說：“我會支持他。” “他贏得了兩場戰爭。他負責。我們都贏了。”　這次彈劾措施是馬西第二次嘗試針對赫格塞斯。他首先試圖在中期選舉之前將彈劾決議提交表決，這促使路易斯安那州共和黨眾議員邁克·約翰遜(Mike Johnson)提前休會以避免投票。這導致該決議失效，這就是馬西本週再次重新提出該決議的原因。　雖然彈劾行動可能暫時平息，但赫格塞斯在國會山莊的麻煩還沒結束。民主黨人承諾，一旦他們在一月取得多數席位，就會對赫格賽斯領導的五角大廈展開積極調查。　他們是否會發起另一次彈劾工作尚不清楚，但在上週接受美國國家公共廣播電台採訪時，預計將成為下一任眾議院議長的眾議員哈基姆·杰弗里斯在談到赫格斯時簡單地說，“他必須下台。”"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6036813/house-votes-to-effectively-end-the-impeachment-effort-against-pete-hegseth"}, {"code": "20261111-2", "ch": "2026-11-11　週三", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Supreme Court seems split over federal agencies' ability to fine for law violations　／　最高法院似乎對聯邦機構對違法行為罰款的能力有分歧", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Nina Totenberg、,&nbsp;，全文共 10 段、15 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：最高法院週二聽取了與臨時工人簽證有關的案件的辯論。涉案公司表示，執行問題應透過法院，而不僅僅是聯邦機構。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6034950/2026-11-10-nx-s1-6034950-supreme-court-seems-divided-over-federal-agencies-ability-to-fine-for-law-violations"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "週二，最高法院的法官們在這起案件中似乎存在分歧，這起案件可能會削弱許…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "At the Supreme Court, the justices seemed divided on Tuesday in a case that could undermine the ability of many federal regulatory agencies to fine businesses that violate federal laws.", "zh": "週二，最高法院的法官們在這起案件中似乎存在分歧，這起案件可能會削弱許多聯邦監管機構對違反聯邦法律的企業進行罰款的能力。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "幾十年來，農民一直依賴聯邦移民計劃，該計劃允許他們臨時僱用移民工人來…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "For decades, farmers have relied on a federal immigration program that allows them to temporarily employ migrant workers to pick crops.", "zh": "幾十年來，農民一直依賴聯邦移民計劃，該計劃允許他們臨時僱用移民工人來採摘農作物。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "除了工資之外，農場主還必須提供基本必需品，例如住房、食物和水。整個系…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "In addition to wages, farm owners must provide basic necessities, such as housing, access to meals and water.", "zh": "除了工資之外，農場主還必須提供基本必需品，例如住房、食物和水。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The whole system is essentially policed by the Department of Labor to ensure that foreign workers don't undercut domestic laborers.", "zh": "整個系統基本上由勞工部監管，以確保外籍勞工不會削弱國內工人的利益。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "律師羅伯特·約翰遜代表太陽谷果園。 “可以肯定的是，”他說，“該法規…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Lawyer Robert Johnson represented Sun Valley Orchards.", "zh": "律師羅伯特·約翰遜代表太陽谷果園。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"To be sure,\" he said, \"the statute contemplates penalties, but it says nothing about where those penalties should be adjudicated.\"", "zh": "“可以肯定的是，”他說，“該法規考慮了處罰，但它沒有說明這些處罰應該在哪裡裁決。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "隨著 ICE 投訴增多，最高法院正在考慮保護聯邦執法部門的努力。約翰…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Law Supreme Court weighs effort to shield federal law enforcement as ICE complaints rise Johnson further contended that penalties should be imposed by the federal courts, not the administrative agencies that do most of that work under current law.", "zh": "隨著 ICE 投訴增多，最高法院正在考慮保護聯邦執法部門的努力。約翰遜進一步認為，處罰應由聯邦法院實施，而不是由根據現行法律承擔大部分工作的行政機構實施。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "對此，法官科坦吉·布朗·傑克遜回答說：“看來你只是在與現實作鬥爭………", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "To that Justice Ketanji Brown Jackson replied, \"It seems like you're just sort of fighting the reality of … what Congress was trying to do … in ensuring that we don't have farm workers coming in and undercutting domestic workers.\"", "zh": "對此，法官科坦吉·布朗·傑克遜回答說：“看來你只是在與現實作鬥爭……國會試圖做的事情……以確保我們不會有農場工人進來並削弱家庭工人的利益。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "法官布雷特·卡瓦諾(Brett Kavanaugh)提出了更懷疑的觀…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "A more skeptical observation came from Justice Brett Kavanaugh: \"What you're proposing is really at war with clarity,\" he said, adding, \"I think that's not great systematically going forward.\"", "zh": "法官布雷特·卡瓦諾(Brett Kavanaugh)提出了更懷疑的觀點：“你的提議確實與清晰度相衝突，”他補充說，“我認為這在系統性上並不是很好的進展。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "塞繆爾·阿利託法官尖銳地補充道，“你所概述的是一種大雜燴的意見，也許…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Justice Samuel Alito pointedly added, \"What you're outlining is sort of a hodge-podge opinion, and maybe sometimes courts write that sort of thing,\" to which Justice Kagan quickly chimed in with a chuckling crowd in the court, \"Not ever us!\"", "zh": "塞繆爾·阿利託法官尖銳地補充道，“你所概述的是一種大雜燴的意見，也許有時法院會寫出這樣的東西，”卡根法官很快就在法庭上咯咯地笑起來，“我們從來都不是！”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "最高法院傾向於將 LGBTQ 排除在公共資助的天主教幼兒園之外 副檢…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Law Supreme Court leans toward LGBTQ exclusion for publicly funded Catholic preschools In rebuttal, Deputy Solicitor General Harris was unusually candid.", "zh": "最高法院傾向於將 LGBTQ 排除在公共資助的天主教幼兒園之外 副檢察長哈里斯反駁說，異常坦率。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"It would be a big deal for the government to lose, but an even bigger deal would be to have a mess,\" she said.", "zh": "「如果政府輸了，那將是一件大事，但更嚴重的是造成混亂，」她說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She later added, \"A lot of other statutory regimes also would be on the cutting-room floor.\"", "zh": "她後來補充道，“許多其他法定制度也將被擱置。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "她說，如果真是這樣，政府將不得不向國會提出請求。她提高了聲音，補充說…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "And if that's the case, she said, the administration will have to go to Congress.", "zh": "她說，如果真是這樣，政府將不得不向國會提出請求。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Her voice rising, she added, \"Please tell us now ... if we need to get Legislative Affairs on it right now, because this will snowball.\"", "zh": "她提高了聲音，補充說：“請現在告訴我們……我們是否需要立即處理立法事務，因為這會像滾雪球一樣越滾越大。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "週二，最高法院的法官們在這起案件中似乎存在分歧，這起案件可能會削弱許多聯邦監管機構對違反聯邦法律的企業進行罰款的能力。　幾十年來，農民一直依賴聯邦移民計劃，該計劃允許他們臨時僱用移民工人來採摘農作物。　除了工資之外，農場主還必須提供基本必需品，例如住房、食物和水。整個系統基本上由勞工部監管，以確保外籍勞工不會削弱國內工人的利益。　律師羅伯特·約翰遜代表太陽谷果園。 “可以肯定的是，”他說，“該法規考慮了處罰，但它沒有說明這些處罰應該在哪裡裁決。”　隨著 ICE 投訴增多，最高法院正在考慮保護聯邦執法部門的努力。約翰遜進一步認為，處罰應由聯邦法院實施，而不是由根據現行法律承擔大部分工作的行政機構實施。　對此，法官科坦吉·布朗·傑克遜回答說：“看來你只是在與現實作鬥爭……國會試圖做的事情……以確保我們不會有農場工人進來並削弱家庭工人的利益。”　法官布雷特·卡瓦諾(Brett Kavanaugh)提出了更懷疑的觀點：“你的提議確實與清晰度相衝突，”他補充說，“我認為這在系統性上並不是很好的進展。”　塞繆爾·阿利託法官尖銳地補充道，“你所概述的是一種大雜燴的意見，也許有時法院會寫出這樣的東西，”卡根法官很快就在法庭上咯咯地笑起來，“我們從來都不是！”　最高法院傾向於將 LGBTQ 排除在公共資助的天主教幼兒園之外 副檢察長哈里斯反駁說，異常坦率。 「如果政府輸了，那將是一件大事，但更嚴重的是造成混亂，」她說。她後來補充道，“許多其他法定制度也將被擱置。”　她說，如果真是這樣，政府將不得不向國會提出請求。她提高了聲音，補充說：“請現在告訴我們……我們是否需要立即處理立法事務，因為這會像滾雪球一樣越滾越大。”"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6034950/2026-11-10-nx-s1-6034950-supreme-court-seems-divided-over-federal-agencies-ability-to-fine-for-law-violations"}, {"code": "20261111-3", "ch": "2026-11-11　週三", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Testing the new generation of AI-enabled fire-extinguishing drones　／　測試新一代人工智慧滅火無人機", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Halle Zander，全文共 17 段、23 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：無人機製造商正在測試新型大型無人機，這些無人機可以在人工智慧的協助下運送水或阻燃劑。科羅拉多州的阿斯彭是第一個嘗試它們的地方。又酷又貴？是的。有效的？待定。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6030962/testing-the-new-generation-of-ai-enabled-fire-extinguishing-drones"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "在夏末罕見的陰天，紅白相間的消​​防車在科羅拉多州西部山區的一片草地…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "On a rare overcast day in late summer, red-and-white fire trucks pepper a grassy strip of land in the mountains of western Colorado.", "zh": "在夏末罕見的陰天，紅白相間的消​​防車在科羅拉多州西部山區的一片草地上行駛。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "阿斯彭消防區的幾名身穿制服的工作人員圍坐在 iPad 旁，看著他們的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "A persistent buzzing rises and falls as several uniformed staff from the Aspen Fire Protection District huddle around an iPad, watching one of their volunteer firefighters control a massive drone.", "zh": "阿斯彭消防區的幾名身穿制服的工作人員圍坐在 iPad 旁，看著他們的一名志願消防員控制一架巨大的無人機，持續不斷的嗡嗡聲時起時落。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "這台史無前例的機器看起來就像一個巨大的蟲子。它呈黑白相間，四個大臂上…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "This first-of-its-kind machine looks like a giant bug.", "zh": "這台史無前例的機器看起來就像一個巨大的蟲子。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Black and white with propellers attached to four large arms, it's about 10 by 12 feet wide — roughly the size of a small U-Haul trailer.", "zh": "它呈黑白相間，四個大臂上裝有螺旋槳，寬約 10 x 12 英尺，大約相當於小型 U 型拖車的大小。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "雖然消防員幾十年來一直使用無人機監測野火，但這款新產品可以使用人工智…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "While firefighters have used drones to monitor wildfires for decades, this new product could use AI to help extinguish fires.", "zh": "雖然消防員幾十年來一直使用無人機監測野火，但這款新產品可以使用人工智慧來幫助撲滅火災。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "這些無人機由加州公司 Seneca 開發，設計用於集群作業。與小型消…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Developed by the California-based company Seneca, the drones are designed to work in a swarm.", "zh": "這些無人機由加州公司 Seneca 開發，設計用於集群作業。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Similar to a small fire engine, five of them can carry 500 to 1,000 gallons of finished fire foam, and firefighters in Aspen reported they were easy to operate.", "zh": "與小型消防車類似，其中五輛可以攜帶 500 至 1,000 加侖的成品消防泡沫，阿斯彭的消防隊員報告說它們很容易操作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "「我們只是開玩笑說我 12 歲的孩子可以駕駛這些東西，」阿斯彭消防隊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "\"We were just joking that my 12-year-old could fly these things,\" said Andy Fisher, deputy chief of Aspen Fire.", "zh": "「我們只是開玩笑說我 12 歲的孩子可以駕駛這些東西，」阿斯彭消防隊副隊長安迪費雪 (Andy Fisher) 說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "當阿斯彭消防局最早於明年正式啟動其新的無人機計畫時，它將成為世界上第…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "When Aspen Fire officially launches its new drone program, as early as next year, it'll be the first fire department in the world to operate the drones independently.", "zh": "當阿斯彭消防局最早於明年正式啟動其新的無人機計畫時，它將成為世界上第一個獨立操作無人機的消防部門。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "So far, they've only been used on prescribed burns in California with support from Seneca's staff.", "zh": "到目前為止，它們僅在加州塞內卡工作人員的支持下用於治療規定的燒傷。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "費雪希望在消防員到達之前將這些無人機送到難以到達的火場，例如遠程雷擊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Fisher wants to send these drones to hard-to-reach fires, like remote lightning strikes, before firefighters arrive.", "zh": "費雪希望在消防員到達之前將這些無人機送到難以到達的火場，例如遠程雷擊。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The city of Aspen, famously home to billions of dollars in real estate, is surrounded by dense forests — like an expensive tinderbox with few evacuation routes for residents and visitors.", "zh": "阿斯彭市以擁有數十億美元的房地產而聞名，周圍環繞著茂密的森林，就像一個昂貴的火藥桶，居民和遊客的疏散路線很少。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"If we could get it quick, keep them small and attack them while they're smoldering instead of waiting for the wind to pick them up, I feel like that's the most ideal use case,\" Fisher said.", "zh": "費雪說：“如果我們能夠快速行動，讓它們變小，並在它們悶燒時攻擊它們，而不是等待風將它們吹走，我覺得這是最理想的用例。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "According to Seneca's founder Stuart Landesberg, the drones can bypass steep or otherwise treacherous terrain quickly and have a range of 5 to ten miles — double that if they're empty.", "zh": "根據 Seneca 創辦人 Stuart Landesberg 介紹，無人機可以快速繞過陡峭或其他危險的地形，航程可達 5 至 10 英里，如果空載，航程可達兩倍。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Hovering over a fire, they use an AI-supported \"sensor suite,\" that can calculate distance and wind speed, then release water or retardant at a specific angle and velocity to tamp down flames.", "zh": "他們將滑鼠懸停在火上，使用人工智慧支援的“感測器套件”，可以計算距離和風速，然後以特定角度和速度釋放水或阻燃劑來撲滅火焰。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "「你幾乎可以把它想像成一架飛行的 Waymo，」他說。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "\"You can think about it almost like a flying Waymo,\" he said.", "zh": "「你幾乎可以把它想像成一架飛行的 Waymo，」他說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "兰德斯伯格表示，无人机不会在大火中取代空中加油机，但它们可以携带工具…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "Landesberg said the drones won't replace air tankers on big fires, but they can carry tools, monitor ongoing fires and help extinguish lingering hot spots.", "zh": "蘭德斯伯格表示，無人機不會在火災中取代空中加油機，但它們可以攜帶工具、監測正在進行的火災並幫助撲滅揮之不去的熱點。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Compared to helicopters, they could also make aerial firefighting more affordable.", "zh": "與直升機相比，它們還可以使空中消防更加經濟實惠。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "「我很少見過 3,000 加侖的水滴或 5,000 加侖的阻燃劑水滴…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "\"I've seen very few times that a 3,000-gallon water drop or a 5,000-gallon retardant drop actually put anything out,\" he said.", "zh": "「我很少見過 3,000 加侖的水滴或 5,000 加侖的阻燃劑水滴實際上能撲滅任何東西，」他說。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "The FAA granted Aspen Fire a waiver in late October, and once training is complete, Fisher said the department could start flying the drones up to 200 feet in Pitkin County.", "zh": "FAA 於 10 月底向阿斯彭消防公司授予了豁免權，一旦培訓完成，費雪表示，該部門可以開始在皮特金縣將無人機飛行到 200 英尺的高度。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "他們無法讓無人機飛越人口稠密的地區，而且必須有人時時注視著它們。如果…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "They can't fly the drones over populated areas, and someone has to have eyes on them at all times.", "zh": "他們無法讓無人機飛越人口稠密的地區，而且必須有人時時注視著它們。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Firefighters can't blindly send a drone over a ridgeline without someone perched on top of a mountain or on the other side to watch them and communicate with the pilots.", "zh": "如果沒有人站在山頂或另一邊觀察無人機並與飛行員進行交流，消防隊員就不能盲目地將無人機送過山脊線。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "但如果無人機有用，阿斯彭消防公司希望擴大豁免範圍，協助撲滅全州各地的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "But if the drones are useful, Aspen Fire hopes to expand the waiver and help fight fires around the state.", "zh": "但如果無人機有用，阿斯彭消防公司希望擴大豁免範圍，協助撲滅全州各地的火災。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "在夏末罕見的陰天，紅白相間的消​​防車在科羅拉多州西部山區的一片草地上行駛。　阿斯彭消防區的幾名身穿制服的工作人員圍坐在 iPad 旁，看著他們的一名志願消防員控制一架巨大的無人機，持續不斷的嗡嗡聲時起時落。　這台史無前例的機器看起來就像一個巨大的蟲子。它呈黑白相間，四個大臂上裝有螺旋槳，寬約 10 x 12 英尺，大約相當於小型 U 型拖車的大小。　雖然消防員幾十年來一直使用無人機監測野火，但這款新產品可以使用人工智慧來幫助撲滅火災。　這些無人機由加州公司 Seneca 開發，設計用於集群作業。與小型消防車類似，其中五輛可以攜帶 500 至 1,000 加侖的成品消防泡沫，阿斯彭的消防隊員報告說它們很容易操作。　「我們只是開玩笑說我 12 歲的孩子可以駕駛這些東西，」阿斯彭消防隊副隊長安迪費雪 (Andy Fisher) 說。　當阿斯彭消防局最早於明年正式啟動其新的無人機計畫時，它將成為世界上第一個獨立操作無人機的消防部門。到目前為止，它們僅在加州塞內卡工作人員的支持下用於治療規定的燒傷。　費雪希望在消防員到達之前將這些無人機送到難以到達的火場，例如遠程雷擊。阿斯彭市以擁有數十億美元的房地產而聞名，周圍環繞著茂密的森林，就像一個昂貴的火藥桶，居民和遊客的疏散路線很少。　「你幾乎可以把它想像成一架飛行的 Waymo，」他說。　兰德斯伯格表示，无人机不会在大火中取代空中加油机，但它们可以携带工具、监测正在进行的火灾并帮助扑灭挥之不去的热点。與直升機相比，它們還可以使空中消防更加經濟實惠。　「我很少見過 3,000 加侖的水滴或 5,000 加侖的阻燃劑水滴實際上能撲滅任何東西，」他說。　他們無法讓無人機飛越人口稠密的地區，而且必須有人時時注視著它們。如果沒有人站在山頂或另一邊觀察無人機並與飛行員進行交流，消防隊員就不能盲目地將無人機送過山脊線。　但如果無人機有用，阿斯彭消防公司希望擴大豁免範圍，協助撲滅全州各地的火災。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6030962/testing-the-new-generation-of-ai-enabled-fire-extinguishing-drones"}, {"code": "20261110-1", "ch": "2026-11-10　週二", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "California voters defeat billionaire tax proposal that divided Democrats　／　加州選民否決了導致民主黨分裂的億萬富翁稅收提案", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Larry Kaplow，全文共 7 段、15 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：這項新穎的提案將對億萬富翁的大部分全部財富一次性徵收 5% 的稅，其中包括他們在公司中的所有權。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/g-s1-151625/california-billionaire-tax-referendum"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "根據美聯社報導，加州選民拒絕了一項對億萬富翁的大部分財富一次性徵收 …", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "California voters have rejected a proposal to charge **billionaires** a one-time 5% tax on most of their **wealth**, according to a race call by The Associated Press.", "zh": "根據美聯社報導，加州選民拒絕了一項對**億萬富翁**的大部分財富一次性徵收 5% 稅的提議。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "支持者表示，這項稅收可以為醫療保健籌集 1,000 億美元。由代表醫…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Proponents said the tax could raise $100 billion for healthcare.", "zh": "支持者表示，這項稅收可以為醫療保健籌集 1,000 億美元。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Led by a union that represents healthcare workers, the SEIU-UHW, **advocates** of the tax said the Republican-controlled Congress cut healthcare programs to give tax breaks to the **wealthy**, so it was time for the wealthy in California to fill the gap.", "zh": "由代表醫療工作者的 SEIU-UHW 領導的稅收倡導者表示，共和黨控制的國會削減了醫療保健計劃，為富人提供稅收減免，因此現在是加州富人填補缺口的時候了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The state has more than 200 **billionaires**, according to **estimates**, with some putting the number at a few hundred.", "zh": "據**估計**，該州有超過 200 名**億萬富翁**，有人認為這一數字為數百人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "反對者認為，這項名為「40 號提案」的提案只會將富人趕出加州，從而減…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Opponents argued that the proposal, known as Prop 40, would just drive the **wealthy** out of California, costing the state revenue and harming its economy.", "zh": "**反對**者認為，這項名為「40 號提案」的提案只會將富人趕出加州，從而減少州收入並損害其經濟。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "但這項措施在民主黨人人數遠遠多於共和黨的州內產生了分歧。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "But the measure divided Democrats in a state where they heavily **outnumber** Republicans.", "zh": "但這項措施在民主黨人人數遠遠多於共和黨的州內產生了分歧。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "該州民主黨支持第 40 號提案，加州民主黨眾議員羅·卡納 (Ro K…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The state's Democratic Party favored Prop 40, as did Rep.", "zh": "該州的民主黨和眾議員都支持 40 號提案。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Ro Khanna, D-Calif., and Sen.", "zh": "羅·卡納 (Ro Khanna)，加州民主黨人，參議員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Bernie Sanders, I-Vt., who went to the state to campaign for it. But Democratic Gov.", "zh": "佛蒙特州參議員伯尼桑德斯 (Bernie Sanders) 前往該州競選。但民主黨州長。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Gavin Newsom opposed the tax, saying it would be better to have a national tax on the **wealthy**.", "zh": "加文·紐瑟姆**反對**這項稅收，他表示最好對富人徵收全國性稅收。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The Democratic candidate for governor, Xavier Becerra, also opposed it.", "zh": "民主黨州長候選人澤維爾貝塞拉 (Xavier Becerra) 也表示**反對**。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "一個主要的教師工會也反對這項提議，因為該提議只會將所得收入的一小部分…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "A leading teachers union also opposed the proposal, which would have set aside just a small portion of the resulting revenue for schools.", "zh": "一個主要的教師工會也**反對**這項提議，因為該提議只會將所得收入的一小部分撥給學校。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And Google co-founder Sergey Brin led other **wealthy** Californians in a **surge** of campaign spending **opposing** the measure.", "zh": "谷歌聯合創始人謝爾蓋·布林(Sergey Brin)帶領其他富有的加州人發起了**反對**這項措施的競選支出激增。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "At least five times as much was spent **opposing** the measure as favoring it.", "zh": "**反對**該措施的花費至少是支持該措施的五倍。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "布林還發起了一場競選活動，將另外兩項提案列入投票，以阻止億萬富翁稅在…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Brin also drove a campaign that put two other proposals on the **ballot** to block the **billionaire** tax from taking effect, had it been approved by voters.", "zh": "布林還發起了一場競選活動，將另外兩項提案列入投票，以阻止**億萬富翁**稅在選民批准後生效。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "根據美聯社報導，加州選民拒絕了一項對億萬富翁的大部分財富一次性徵收 5% 稅的提議。　支持者表示，這項稅收可以為醫療保健籌集 1,000 億美元。由代表醫療工作者的 SEIU-UHW 領導的稅收倡導者表示，共和黨控制的國會削減了醫療保健計劃，為富人提供稅收減免，因此現在是加州富人填補缺口的時候了。據估計，該州有超過 200 名億萬富翁，有人認為這一數字為數百人。　反對者認為，這項名為「40 號提案」的提案只會將富人趕出加州，從而減少州收入並損害其經濟。　但這項措施在民主黨人人數遠遠多於共和黨的州內產生了分歧。　該州民主黨支持第 40 號提案，加州民主黨眾議員羅·卡納 (Ro Khanna) 和佛蒙特州參議員伯尼·桑德斯 (Bernie Sanders) 也前往該州為其競選。但民主黨州長加文·紐瑟姆反對這項稅收，稱最好對富人徵收全國稅。民主黨州長候選人澤維爾貝塞拉 (Xavier Becerra) 也表示反對。　一個主要的教師工會也反對這項提議，因為該提議只會將所得收入的一小部分撥給學校。谷歌聯合創始人謝爾蓋·布林(Sergey Brin)帶領其他富有的加州人發起了反對這項措施的競選支出激增。反對該措施的花費至少是支持該措施的五倍。　布林還發起了一場競選活動，將另外兩項提案列入投票，以阻止億萬富翁稅在選民批准後生效。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "outnumber", "sf": "outnumber", "pos": "v.", "zh": "數量多於", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　(stative) to be more in number than somebody or something.　|　本文例句　But the measure divided Democrats in a state where they heavily outnumber Republicans.　|　例句中譯　但這項措施在民主黨人人數遠遠多於共和黨的州內產生了分歧。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "billionaire", "sf": "billionaires", "pos": "n.", "zh": "億萬富翁", "syn": "milliardaire", "tip": "英英定義　Somebody whose wealth is greater than one billion (109) dollars, or other currency.　|　本文例句　California voters have rejected a proposal to charge billionaires a one-time 5% tax on most of their wealth, according to a race call by The Associated Press.　|　例句中譯　根據美聯社報導，加州選民拒絕了一項對億萬富翁的大部分財富一次性徵收 5% 稅的提議。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "surge", "sf": "surge", "pos": "n.", "zh": "湧", "syn": "inrush", "tip": "其他意思　波、波蕩、波瀾、波浪　|　英英定義　A sudden transient rush, flood or increase.　|　本文例句　And Google co-founder Sergey Brin led other wealthy Californians in a surge of campaign spending opposing the measure.　|　例句中譯　谷歌聯合創始人謝爾蓋·布林(Sergey Brin)帶領其他富有的加州人發起了反對這項措施的競選支出激增。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "opposing", "sf": "opposing", "pos": "v.", "zh": "反對", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　持、敵、抵抗、對　|　本文例句　And Google co-founder Sergey Brin led other wealthy Californians in a surge of campaign spending opposing the measure.　|　例句中譯　谷歌聯合創始人謝爾蓋·布林(Sergey Brin)帶領其他富有的加州人發起了反對這項措施的競選支出激增。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "ballot", "sf": "ballot", "pos": "n.", "zh": "選票", "syn": "ballot paper, voting slip", "tip": "其他意思　表決、票、抽簽　|　英英定義　Originally, a small ball placed in a container to cast a vote; now, by extension, a piece of paper or card used for this purpose, or some other means used to signify a vote.　|　本文例句　Brin also drove a campaign that put two other proposals on the ballot to block the billionaire tax from taking effect, had it been approved by voters.　|　例句中譯　布林還發起了一場競選活動，將另外兩項提案列入投票，以阻止億萬富翁稅在選民批准後生效。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "wealthy", "sf": "wealthy", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "富裕", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　豐厚、豐裕、富、富庶　|　英英定義　A rich person.　|　本文例句　California voters have rejected a proposal to charge billionaires a one-time 5% tax on most of their wealth, according to a race call by The Associated Press.　|　例句中譯　根據美聯社報導，加州選民拒絕了一項對億萬富翁的大部分財富一次性徵收 5% 稅的提議。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "advocate", "sf": "advocates", "pos": "n.", "zh": "提倡", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　鼓吹者、中保、倡、崇尚　|　英英定義　Someone whose job is to speak for someone's case in a court of law; a counsel.　|　本文例句　Led by a union that represents healthcare workers, the SEIU-UHW, advocates of the tax said the Republican-controlled Congress cut healthcare programs to give tax breaks to the wealthy, so it was time for the wealthy in California to fill the gap.　|　例句中譯　由代表醫療工作者的 SEIU-UHW 領導的稅收倡導者表示，共和黨控制的國會削減了醫療保健計劃，為富人提供稅收減免，因此現在是加州富人填補缺口的時候了。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "estimates", "sf": "estimates", "pos": "n.", "zh": "估計", "syn": "appraisal, estimation", "tip": "其他意思　揆、量、預算、測度　|　英英定義　A rough calculation or assessment of the value, size, or cost of something.　|　本文例句　The state has more than 200 billionaires, according to estimates, with some putting the number at a few hundred.　|　例句中譯　據估計，該州有超過 200 名億萬富翁，有人認為這一數字為數百人。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/g-s1-151625/california-billionaire-tax-referendum"}, {"code": "20261110-2", "ch": "2026-11-10　週二", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "France accuses Iran of cyber 'sabotage' in fridge attacks　／　法國指責伊朗在冰箱襲擊中進行網路“破壞”", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Jenna McLaughlin、,&nbsp;，全文共 18 段、27 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：法國稱，伊朗軍方駭客上個月接管了約 700 個不同零售點的冷凍控制器，導致半夜溫度升高，並破壞了價值數百萬美元的食物。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/g-s1-152724/france-iran-cyber-sabotage-fridge-attacks"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "法國指責伊朗十月對其關鍵基礎設施發動了一系列破壞性網路攻擊。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "France is accusing Iran of having launched a series of destructive cyberattacks against its critical infrastructure in October.", "zh": "法國指責伊朗十月對其關鍵基礎設施發動了一系列**破壞**性網路攻擊。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "據法國國家網路安全局 ANSSI 稱，伊朗軍事駭客接管了法國約 70…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "According to the French National **Cybersecurity** Agency, ANSSI, Iranian military hackers took over **refrigeration** controllers at around 700 different retail sites in France, from supermarkets to butcher shops, turning up the temperature in the middle of the night and spoiling millions of dollars' worth of food.", "zh": "據法國國家**網路安全**局 ANSSI 稱，伊朗軍事駭客接管了法國約 700 個不同零售場所（從超市到肉店）的冷凍控制器，在半夜提高了溫度，**破壞**了價值數百萬美元的食物。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "ANSSI 在其新聞稿中寫道，他們還針對幾個小型水力發電廠，造成了「…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "They also targeted several small **hydroelectric** power plants, resulting in \"moderate effects,\" wrote ANSSI in its press release.", "zh": "ANSSI 在其新聞稿中寫道，他們還針對幾個小型**水力發電**廠，造成了「中等影響」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "法國外交部長讓-諾埃爾·巴羅表示，這次駭客攻擊活動「無論是規模還是侵…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "The hacking campaign was \"unprecedented in both its scale and its level of aggression,\" said French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot.", "zh": "法國外交部長讓-諾埃爾·巴羅表示，這次駭客攻擊活動「無論是規模還是侵略程度都是前所未有的」。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He said it \"marks the first large-scale cyberattack aimed at **sabotage** on our national territory, and it constitutes a major attack on the nation's interests and the security of the French people.\"", "zh": "他表示，這「標誌著首次針對我國領土進行**破壞**的大規模網路攻擊，構成對國家利益和法國人民安全的重大攻擊」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "巴黎檢察官辦公室已對伊朗網路單位 Shahid Kaveh 展開調查…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The Paris Prosecutor's Office has opened its own investigation into the Iranian cyber unit, Shahid Kaveh, which the French government is linking to Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.", "zh": "巴黎檢察官辦公室已對伊朗網路單位 Shahid Kaveh 展開調查，法國政府將其與伊朗伊斯蘭革命衛隊聯繫起來。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"The Paris Public Prosecutor's Office is requesting the **issuance** of international arrest warrants,\" the office said in a statement.", "zh": "「巴黎檢察官辦公室正在請求簽發國際逮捕令，」該辦公室在一份聲明中表示。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "針對法國工業控制器的攻擊是更大趨勢的一部分。光是 2026 年，駭客…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "The attacks on French industrial controllers are part of a larger trend.", "zh": "針對法國工業控制器的攻擊是更大趨勢的一部分。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In 2026 alone, hackers have targeted **refrigeration** controllers from Europe to Israel and the United States.", "zh": "光是 2026 年，駭客就瞄準了從歐洲到以色列和美國的冷凍控制器。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "瑞典和愛爾蘭等歐洲國家的雜貨店上週也遭受了類似的攻擊。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Grocery stores in European countries including Sweden and Ireland were hit in similar attacks last week.", "zh": "瑞典和愛爾蘭等歐洲國家的雜貨店上週也遭受了類似的攻擊。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "在法國發生的另一起事件中，法國一家大型血庫的員工上週冷氣系統遭到攻擊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "In a separate incident in France, employees at a major French blood bank had to act fast to save blood samples from heating up when their **refrigeration** system was hit last week, prompting international calls for the health sector to protect its **lifesaving** products from spoiling.", "zh": "在法國發生的另一起事件中，法國一家大型血庫的員工上週冷氣系統遭到攻擊，不得不迅速採取行動，避免血液樣本升溫，促使國際社會呼籲衛生部門保護其**救生**產品免遭變質。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "今年夏天，美國軍事基地的小賣部也經歷了類似的情況，冰箱和冰櫃內的溫度…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Over the summer, **commissaries** on U.S. military bases also went through something similar, when food spoiled after the temperature shot up inside **refrigerators** and freezers overnight.", "zh": "今年夏天，美國軍事基地的小賣部也經歷了類似的情況，**冰箱**和冰櫃內的溫度一夜之間飆升，食物變質。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "法國政府是第一個正式對這波破壞性攻擊負責的國家。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "The French government is the first to formally assign blame for the wave of destructive attacks.", "zh": "法國政府是第一個正式對這波**破壞**性攻擊負責的國家。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "ANSSI 表示，他們能夠透過一系列數位線索識別駭客，包括駭客使用的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "They were able to identify the hackers through a series of digital clues, including digital infrastructure used by the hackers, connection to a propaganda outlet, and \"traces\" of the use of Farsi language in the attack, according to ANSSI.", "zh": "ANSSI 表示，他們能夠透過一系列數位線索識別駭客，包括駭客使用的數位基礎設施、與宣傳機構的連接以及攻擊中使用波斯語的「痕跡」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "儘管 NPR 和其他機構報導稱，美國官員懷疑伊朗可能是 8 月美國軍…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "While NPR and others have reported that U.S. officials suspect Iran may have been behind the attacks on U.S. military bases in August, the Pentagon has not made any official statement, even to conclude that the **disruptions** were in fact the result of a cyberattack.", "zh": "儘管 NPR 和其他機構報導稱，美國官員懷疑伊朗可能是 8 月美國軍事基地襲擊事件的幕後黑手，但五角大廈尚未發表任何官方聲明，甚至沒有得出結論稱，這些**破壞**實際上是網路攻擊造成的。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "戰爭部監察長辦公室發言人莫莉·哈爾彭 (Mollie Halpern…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "\"Consistent with our policy and to preserve the integrity of the process, the DOD [Office of Inspector General] Criminal Investigative Service does not discuss ongoing investigations,\" Mollie Halpern, a spokesperson for the Department of War Office of the Inspector General wrote in an email to NPR.", "zh": "戰爭部監察長辦公室發言人莫莉·哈爾彭 (Mollie Halpern) 在給 NPR 的電子郵件中寫道：“根據我們的政策並保持程序的完整性，國防部刑事調查局不會討論正在進行的調查。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "網路安全專家表示，如果伊朗駭客是歐洲、美國和以色列攻擊的幕後黑手，這…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "If Iranian hackers are behind the attacks across Europe, the U.S. and Israel, **cybersecurity** experts say that would fit with what they know about Iranian hackers' strategy and goals.", "zh": "**網路安全**專家表示，如果伊朗駭客是歐洲、美國和以色列攻擊的幕後黑手，這將符合他們對伊朗駭客戰略和目標的了解。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "網路安全公司 Sublime Security 的威脅情報主管 Al…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "\"Iran's cyberattacks against **refrigeration** systems likely represents the IRGC attempting to **reassert** Iranian power abroad through both physically and psychologically disruptive operations,\" Alex Orleans, the head of threat intelligence at **cybersecurity** firm Sublime Security, told NPR.", "zh": "**網路安全**公司 Sublime Security 的威脅情報主管 Alex Orleans 告訴 NPR，“伊朗針對製冷系統的網路攻擊可能代表著 IRGC 試圖透過身體和**心理上**的**破壞**性行動，在海外重新確立伊朗的實力。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Such activities continue to provide tangible and cost-effect results given how Iran's national resources remain tied down in the war.\"", "zh": "“鑑於伊朗的國家資源在戰爭中仍然受到束縛，此類活動繼續提供切實且具有成本效益的成果。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "奧爾良說：「此外，法國人特別將破壞性攻擊歸咎於伊斯蘭革命衛隊網路部隊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "\"Also, Shahid Kaveh, the IRGC cyber unit that the French specifically attributed the **disruptive** attacks to, is repeating a pattern here,\" Orleans says.", "zh": "奧爾良說：“此外，法國人特別將**破壞**性攻擊歸咎於伊斯蘭革命衛隊網路部隊沙希德·卡維（Shahid Kaveh），這裡也重複了一種模式。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He referenced a series of cyberattacks on American water treatment plants in August, which most experts believe were linked to Iran, as precedent.", "zh": "他引用了 8 月針對美國水處理廠的一系列網路攻擊作為先例，大多數專家認為這些攻擊與伊朗有關。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The U.S. government has still not officially attributed those attacks.", "zh": "美國政府尚未正式歸咎於這些攻擊。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "奧爾良說：“該部隊透過攻擊以色列目標，再次改進了其情報技術，然後將目…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "\"This unit has once again refined its tradecraft through attacks on Israeli targets before shifting their targeting to the same systems in the West,\" Orleans says.", "zh": "奧爾良說：“該部隊透過攻擊以色列目標，再次改進了其情報技術，然後將目標轉移到西方的相同系統。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "「這些人都是什麼病啊？」他問。 「他們攻擊冰箱。法國甚至沒有參與這件…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "\"What kind of **sickos** are these people?\" he asked.", "zh": "「這些人都是什麼病啊？」他問。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"They attack **refrigerators**.", "zh": "“他們攻擊**冰箱**。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "France is not even involved in this, really,\" referring to the war between the U.S. and Iran, which began in February.", "zh": "法國甚至沒有參與此事，真的，」指的是二月開始的美國和伊朗之間的戰爭。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"[These Iranians] do terrible things around the world … the news today doesn't surprise us,\" Rubio concluded.", "zh": "「[這些伊朗人]在世界各地做了可怕的事情......今天的消息並不讓我們感到驚訝，」盧比奧總結道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "法國指責伊朗十月對其關鍵基礎設施發動了一系列破壞性網路攻擊。　據法國國家網路安全局 ANSSI 稱，伊朗軍事駭客接管了法國約 700 個不同零售場所（從超市到肉店）的冷凍控制器，在半夜提高了溫度，破壞了價值數百萬美元的食物。　ANSSI 在其新聞稿中寫道，他們還針對幾個小型水力發電廠，造成了「中等影響」。　法國外交部長讓-諾埃爾·巴羅表示，這次駭客攻擊活動「無論是規模還是侵略程度都是前所未有的」。他表示，這「標誌著首次針對我國領土進行破壞的大規模網路攻擊，構成對國家利益和法國人民安全的重大攻擊」。　巴黎檢察官辦公室已對伊朗網路單位 Shahid Kaveh 展開調查，法國政府將其與伊朗伊斯蘭革命衛隊聯繫起來。 「巴黎檢察官辦公室正在請求簽發國際逮捕令，」該辦公室在一份聲明中表示。　針對法國工業控制器的攻擊是更大趨勢的一部分。光是 2026 年，駭客就瞄準了從歐洲到以色列和美國的冷凍控制器。　瑞典和愛爾蘭等歐洲國家的雜貨店上週也遭受了類似的攻擊。　在法國發生的另一起事件中，法國一家大型血庫的員工上週冷氣系統遭到攻擊，不得不迅速採取行動，避免血液樣本升溫，促使國際社會呼籲衛生部門保護其救生產品免遭變質。　今年夏天，美國軍事基地的小賣部也經歷了類似的情況，冰箱和冰櫃內的溫度一夜之間飆升，食物變質。　法國政府是第一個正式對這波破壞性攻擊負責的國家。　ANSSI 表示，他們能夠透過一系列數位線索識別駭客，包括駭客使用的數位基礎設施、與宣傳機構的連接以及攻擊中使用波斯語的「痕跡」。　儘管 NPR 和其他機構報導稱，美國官員懷疑伊朗可能是 8 月美國軍事基地襲擊事件的幕後黑手，但五角大廈尚未發表任何官方聲明，甚至沒有得出結論稱，這些破壞實際上是網路攻擊造成的。　戰爭部監察長辦公室發言人莫莉·哈爾彭 (Mollie Halpern) 在給 NPR 的電子郵件中寫道：“根據我們的政策並保持程序的完整性，國防部刑事調查局不會討論正在進行的調查。”　網路安全專家表示，如果伊朗駭客是歐洲、美國和以色列攻擊的幕後黑手，這將符合他們對伊朗駭客戰略和目標的了解。　網路安全公司 Sublime Security 的威脅情報主管 Alex Orleans 告訴 NPR，「伊朗針對製冷系統的網路攻擊可能代表著 IRGC 試圖透過身體和心理上的破壞性行動，在海外重新確立伊朗的實力。」 「鑑於伊朗的國家資源在戰爭中仍然受到束縛，此類活動繼續提供切實且具有成本效益的成果。　奧爾良說：「此外，法國人特別將破壞性攻擊歸咎於伊斯蘭革命衛隊網路部隊沙希德·卡維（Shahid Kaveh），這裡也重複了一種模式。」他引用了 8 月份針對美國水處理廠的一系列網路攻擊作為先例，大多數專家認為這些攻擊與伊朗有關。美國政府尚未正式歸咎於這些攻擊。　奧爾良說：“該部隊透過攻擊以色列目標，再次改進了其情報技術，然後將目標轉移到西方的相同系統。”　「這些人都是什麼病啊？」他問。 「他們攻擊冰箱。法國甚至沒有參與這件事，真的，」指的是二月開始的美國和伊朗之間的戰爭。 「[這些伊朗人]在世界各地做了可怕的事情......今天的消息並不讓我們感到驚訝，」盧比奧總結道。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "reassert", "sf": "reassert", "pos": "v.", "zh": "重申", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Assert again　|　本文例句　\"Iran's cyberattacks against refrigeration systems likely represents the IRGC attempting to reassert Iranian power abroad through both physically and psychologically disruptive operations,\" Alex Orleans, the head of threat intelligence at cybersecurity firm Sublime Security, told NPR.　|　例句中譯　網路安全公司 Sublime Security 的威脅情報主管 Alex Orleans 告訴 NPR，“伊朗針對製冷系統的網路攻擊可能代表著 IRGC 試圖透過身體和心理上的破壞性行動，在海外重新確立伊朗的實力。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "sicko", "sf": "sickos", "pos": "n.", "zh": "病態的", "syn": "sick day, sickie, weirdo", "tip": "英英定義　A person with unpleasant tastes, views or habits.　|　本文例句　\"What kind of sickos are these people?\" he asked.　|　例句中譯　「這些人都是什麼病啊？」他問。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "commissary", "sf": "commissaries", "pos": "", "zh": "福利社", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　Over the summer, commissaries on U.　|　例句中譯　整個夏天，美國的小賣部。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "lifesaving", "sf": "lifesaving", "pos": "n.", "zh": "救生", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Preserving life; preventing death.　|　本文例句　In a separate incident in France, employees at a major French blood bank had to act fast to save blood samples from heating up when their refrigeration system was hit last week, prompting international calls for the health sector to protect its lifesaving products from spoiling.　|　例句中譯　在法國發生的另一起事件中，法國一家大型血庫的員工上週冷氣系統遭到攻擊，不得不迅速採取行動，避免血液樣本升溫，促使國際社會呼籲衛生部門保護其救生產品免遭變質。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "hydroelectric", "sf": "hydroelectric", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "水力發電", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　That generates electricity by converting the energy of moving water, or of steam escaping under high pressure　|　本文例句　They also targeted several small hydroelectric power plants, resulting in \"moderate effects,\" wrote ANSSI in its press release.　|　例句中譯　ANSSI 在其新聞稿中寫道，他們還針對幾個小型水力發電廠，造成了「中等影響」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "refrigeration", "sf": "refrigeration", "pos": "n.", "zh": "冷藏", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　致冷　|　英英定義　The process of transferring heat from an object in order to cool it.　|　本文例句　In 2026 alone, hackers have targeted refrigeration controllers from Europe to Israel and the United States.　|　例句中譯　光是 2026 年，駭客就瞄準了從歐洲到以色列和美國的冷凍控制器。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "issuance", "sf": "issuance", "pos": "n.", "zh": "發行", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　發、發表、發佈　|　英英定義　The act of issuing, or giving out.　|　本文例句　\"The Paris Public Prosecutor's Office is requesting the issuance of international arrest warrants,\" the office said in a statement.　|　例句中譯　「巴黎檢察官辦公室正在請求簽發國際逮捕令，」該辦公室在一份聲明中表示。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "cybersecurity", "sf": "Cybersecurity", "pos": "n.", "zh": "網路安全", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Security against electronic attacks such as cyberwarfare.　|　本文例句　and Israel, cybersecurity experts say that would fit with what they know about Iranian hackers' strategy and goals.　|　例句中譯　和以色列，網路安全專家表示，這符合他們對伊朗駭客戰略和目標的了解。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "psychologically", "sf": "psychologically", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "心理上", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　In a psychological sense　|　本文例句　\"Iran's cyberattacks against refrigeration systems likely represents the IRGC attempting to reassert Iranian power abroad through both physically and psychologically disruptive operations,\" Alex Orleans, the head of threat intelligence at cybersecurity firm Sublime Security, told NPR.　|　例句中譯　網路安全公司 Sublime Security 的威脅情報主管 Alex Orleans 告訴 NPR，“伊朗針對製冷系統的網路攻擊可能代表著 IRGC 試圖透過身體和心理上的破壞性行動，在海外重新確立伊朗的實力。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "disruptive", "sf": "disruptive", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "破壞性的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Causing disruption or unrest.　|　本文例句　military bases in August, the Pentagon has not made any official statement, even to conclude that the disruptions were in fact the result of a cyberattack.　|　例句中譯　八月份軍事基地遭到破壞後，五角大廈尚未發表任何正式聲明，甚至沒有結論稱這些中斷實際上是網路攻擊的結果。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "refrigerator", "sf": "refrigerators", "pos": "n.", "zh": "冰箱", "syn": "chiller, coolchest, fridge", "tip": "其他意思　電冰箱　|　英英定義　A household appliance used for keeping food fresh by refrigeration (short form fridge).　|　本文例句　In 2026 alone, hackers have targeted refrigeration controllers from Europe to Israel and the United States.　|　例句中譯　光是 2026 年，駭客就瞄準了從歐洲到以色列和美國的冷凍控制器。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "sabotage", "sf": "sabotage", "pos": "v.", "zh": "破壞", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　踹、怠工　|　英英定義　A deliberate action aimed at weakening an enemy through subversion, obstruction, disruption, and/or destruction.　|　本文例句　He said it \"marks the first large-scale cyberattack aimed at sabotage on our national territory, and it constitutes a major attack on the nation's interests and the security of the French people.　|　例句中譯　他表示，這“標誌著我們國家領土上首次發生旨在破壞的大規模網路攻擊，是對國家利益和法國人民安全的重大攻擊。”", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/g-s1-152724/france-iran-cyber-sabotage-fridge-attacks"}, {"code": "20261110-3", "ch": "2026-11-10　週二", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Supreme Court says border wall construction can continue in west Texas　／　最高法院稱德州西部邊境牆建設可以繼續", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Carlos Morales，全文共 13 段、18 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：川普政府於 10 月初向高等法院提出緊急救濟請求，要求繼續施工，同時繼續推動有關該計劃的訴訟。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/nx-s1-6019424/border-wall-big-bend-texas-trump"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "美國最高法院週一允許川普政府繼續執行其在德州西部建造數百英里邊境屏障…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The U.S. Supreme Court on Monday allowed the Trump administration to continue with its plans to construct hundreds of miles of border barrier and security infrastructure in west Texas, while a court hearing over the effort moves forward.", "zh": "美國最高法院週一允許川普政府繼續執行其在德州西部建造數百英里邊境屏障和安全基礎設施的計劃，同時有關該努力的法庭聽證會也將繼續進行。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "聯邦政府的計劃因將大彎國家公園納入其中而激起了兩黨的強烈反對，大彎國…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The federal government's plans have stirred bipartisan backlash for its inclusion of Big Bend National Park, a beloved stretch of public land known for its sweeping canyons and **unspoiled** desert landscape.", "zh": "聯邦政府的計劃因將大彎國家公園納入其中而激起了兩黨的強烈反對，大彎國家公園是一片深受人們喜愛的公共土地，以其廣闊的峽谷和**未受破壞的**沙漠景觀而聞名。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "在周一發布的一份長達五頁的裁決中，高等法院寫道，對該命令做出裁決的聯…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "In a five-page decision issued Monday, the high court wrote that the federal judge who ruled on the order didn't have the authority to weigh in.", "zh": "在周一發布的一份長達五頁的裁決中，高等法院寫道，對該命令做出裁決的聯邦法官無權參與其中。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "未簽署的決定寫道：「因此，該禁令阻礙政府推進其在邊境安全和完整方面的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "\"The injunction thus **impedes** the Government from advancing its 'compelling interests' in border security and integrity,\" reads the **unsigned** decision.", "zh": "未簽署的決定寫道：“因此，該禁令**阻礙**政府推進其在邊境安全和完整方面的‘引人注目的利益’。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Justice Ketanji Brown Jackson was the lone dissenter in the decision.", "zh": "法官科坦吉·布朗·傑克森是該決定中唯一的反對者。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "法院寫道，聯邦法律允許國土安全部長馬克韋恩·穆林(Markwayne…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The court wrote that federal law allows the Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin to **waive** environmental protections and conservation laws, which they called a \"clear preference for expeditious border construction over the very harms respondents assert.\"", "zh": "法院寫道，聯邦法律允許國土安全部長馬克韋恩·穆林(Markwayne Mullin)**放棄**環境保護和保護法，他們稱這些法律「明顯傾向於迅速邊境建設，而不是受訪者聲稱的危害」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "在十月下旬向高等法院提出的緊急申請中，聯邦政府敦促法官進行干預並允許…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "In an emergency application to the high court in late October, the federal government urged the justices to intervene and allow the work to begin again, saying that a gap in \"border defenses\" in the Big Bend region \"would act as \"a dangerous magnet for cartels and other bad actors.\"", "zh": "在十月下旬向高等法院提出的緊急申請中，聯邦政府敦促法官進行干預並允許工作重新開始，稱大本德地區「邊境防禦」的缺口「將成為「吸引卡特爾和其他不良行為者的危險磁石」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "埃爾帕索的一名聯邦法官發布了臨時禁令，停止建造 30 英尺高的鋼鐵屏…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "A federal judge in El Paso issued the temporary injunction that halted the construction of 30-foot-tall steel barriers, patrol roads, surveillance systems and other border infrastructure.", "zh": "埃爾帕索的一名聯邦法官發布了臨時禁令，停止建造 30 英尺高的鋼鐵屏障、巡邏道路、監視系統和其他邊境基礎設施。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "環境倡導組織生物多樣性中心與一家致力於保護美墨邊境附近一座歷史教堂的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "The Center for Biological Diversity, an environmental advocacy group, brought forward the lawsuit, along with an area nonprofit working to preserve a historic church near the U.S.-Mexico border and a **landowner** who stands to lose his border property.", "zh": "環境倡導組織生物多樣性中心與一家致力於保護美墨邊境附近一座歷史教堂的地區非營利組織以及一位可能失去邊境財產的土地所有者一起提起了訴訟。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "生物多樣性中心的萊肯·喬達爾說：“這一決定為承包商開了綠燈，並允許推…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"This decision **greenlights** the contractors and allows the **bulldozers** to come roaring back into the region,\" said Laiken Jordahl with the Center for Biological Diversity.", "zh": "生物多樣性中心的萊肯·喬達爾說：“這一決定為承包商開了**綠燈**，並允許**推土機**轟鳴著返回該地區。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"It allows the dynamiting of national park canyon walls, the **bulldozing** of pristine desert.\"", "zh": "“它允許炸毀國家公園峽谷的牆壁，推平原始​​沙漠。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "訴訟稱，國土安全部的計畫違憲，如果繼續施工，大本德居民將受到「不可挽…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "The lawsuit argued that the Department of Homeland Security's plans are unconstitutional and that Big Bend residents would be \"**irreparably** harmed\" if the construction continues.", "zh": "訴訟稱，國土安全部的計畫違憲，如果繼續施工，大本德居民將受到「不可挽回的傷害」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "川普政府對備受喜愛的德克薩斯州大本德地區的計劃引起了兩黨不同尋常的強…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "The Trump administration's plans for the beloved Big Bend region of Texas have provoked an unusual bipartisan backlash.", "zh": "川普政府對備受喜愛的德克薩斯州大本德地區的計劃引起了兩黨不同尋常的強烈反對。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "People across the political spectrum say a wall isn't needed in the Big Bend––a region known for its sweeping canyons, tough terrain and **unforgiving** desert heat.", "zh": "各個政治派別都表示，大彎地區不需要建造隔離牆——該地區以廣闊的峽谷、崎嶇的地形和無情的沙漠炎熱而聞名。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They worry about the threats a wall or any other kind of infrastructure poses to the region, from the impact on the environment and Indigenous sites to the effect on the region's tourism-based economy and on wild animals.", "zh": "他們擔心隔離牆或任何其他類型的基礎設施對該地區的威脅，從對環境和原住民遺址的影響到對該地區以旅遊業為基礎的經濟和野生動物的影響。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "在川普政府向最高法院提出的緊急救濟請求中，副檢察長約翰·紹爾稱該禁令…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "In the Trump administration's emergency relief request to the Supreme Court, Solicitor General John Sauer called the injunction \"**baseless**\" and \"unprecedented\" and said any pocket of the Big Bend without a barrier would \"become a funnel point for illegal alien crossings that are **thwarted** by barriers elsewhere.\"", "zh": "在川普政府向最高法院提出的緊急救濟請求中，副檢察長約翰·紹爾稱該禁令“毫無根據”且“史無前例”，並表示大彎曲地區任何沒有屏障的區域都將“成為外國人非法過境的漏斗點，而其他地方的屏障則**阻礙**了這些非法入境”。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "從歷史上看，大彎地區崎嶇的地形意味著嘗試透過這個邊境地區進入美國的人…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "Historically, the Big Bend area's rugged landscape has meant fewer people attempting to cross into the U.S. through this pocket of the border.", "zh": "從歷史上看，大彎地區崎嶇的地形意味著嘗試透過這個邊境地區進入美國的人越來越少。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And while the Big Bend Sector, a nearly 500-mile stretch covered by U.S. Customs and Border Protection, makes up over a quarter of the U.S.-Mexico border, it regularly sees the **fewest** number of encounters along the Texas border, according to CBP data.", "zh": "根據美國海關和邊境保護局的數據，雖然大彎地區是美國海關和邊境保護局管轄的近 500 英里的一段，佔美墨邊境的四分之一以上，但根據 CBP 的數據，該地區在德克薩斯州邊境發生的衝突數量通常是**最少**的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "美國最高法院週一允許川普政府繼續執行其在德州西部建造數百英里邊境屏障和安全基礎設施的計劃，同時有關該努力的法庭聽證會也將繼續進行。　聯邦政府的計劃因將大彎國家公園納入其中而激起了兩黨的強烈反對，大彎國家公園是一片深受人們喜愛的公共土地，以其廣闊的峽谷和未受破壞的沙漠景觀而聞名。　在周一發布的一份長達五頁的裁決中，高等法院寫道，對該命令做出裁決的聯邦法官無權參與其中。　未簽署的決定寫道：「因此，該禁令阻礙政府推進其在邊境安全和完整方面的『引人注目的利益』。」法官科坦吉·布朗·傑克遜是該決定中唯一的反對者。　法院寫道，聯邦法律允許國土安全部長馬克韋恩·穆林(Markwayne Mullin)放棄環境保護和保護法，他們稱這些法律「明顯傾向於迅速邊境建設，而不是受訪者聲稱的危害」。　在十月下旬向高等法院提出的緊急申請中，聯邦政府敦促法官進行干預並允許工作重新開始，稱大本德地區「邊境防禦」的缺口「將成為「吸引卡特爾和其他不良行為者的危險磁石」。　埃爾帕索的一名聯邦法官發布了臨時禁令，停止建造 30 英尺高的鋼鐵屏障、巡邏道路、監視系統和其他邊境基礎設施。　環境倡導組織生物多樣性中心與一家致力於保護美墨邊境附近一座歷史教堂的地區非營利組織以及一位可能失去邊境財產的土地所有者一起提起了訴訟。　生物多樣性中心的萊肯·喬達爾說：“這一決定為承包商開了綠燈，並允許推土機轟鳴著返回該地區。” “它允許炸毀國家公園峽谷的牆壁，推平原始​​沙漠。”　訴訟稱，國土安全部的計畫違憲，如果繼續施工，大本德居民將受到「不可挽回的傷害」。　川普政府對備受喜愛的德克薩斯州大本德地區的計劃引起了兩黨不同尋常的強烈反對。各個政治派別都表示，大彎地區不需要建造隔離牆——該地區以廣闊的峽谷、崎嶇的地形和無情的沙漠炎熱而聞名。他們擔心隔離牆或任何其他類型的基礎設施對該地區的威脅，從對環境和原住民遺址的影響到對該地區以旅遊業為基礎的經濟和野生動物的影響。　在川普政府向最高法院提出的緊急救濟請求中，副檢察長約翰·紹爾稱該禁令“毫無根據”且“史無前例”，並表示大彎曲地區任何沒有屏障的區域都將“成為外國人非法過境的漏斗點，而其他地方的屏障則阻礙了這些非法入境”。　從歷史上看，大彎地區崎嶇的地形意味著嘗試透過這個邊境地區進入美國的人越來越少。根據美國海關和邊境保護局的數據，雖然大彎地區是美國海關和邊境保護局管轄的近 500 英里的一段，佔美墨邊境的四分之一以上，但根據 CBP 的數據，該地區在德克薩斯州邊境發生的衝突數量通常是最少的。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📝 本篇核心字彙", "ic": "📝"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "依 wordfreq 詞頻自動挑出本篇最值得學的生字（越罕用越前面）。點單字左邊的 ☆ 可標記，標完用標題列的「⭐ 只念星號」反覆聽。"}, {"k": "voc", "v": [{"w": "irreparably", "sf": "irreparably", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "無可挽回地", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Such that it cannot be repaired.　|　本文例句　The lawsuit argued that the Department of Homeland Security's plans are unconstitutional and that Big Bend residents would be \"irreparably harmed\" if the construction continues.　|　例句中譯　訴訟稱，國土安全部的計畫違憲，如果繼續施工，大本德居民將受到「不可挽回的傷害」。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "unspoiled", "sf": "unspoiled", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "未受破壞的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Not spoiled or touched; pure.　|　本文例句　The federal government's plans have stirred bipartisan backlash for its inclusion of Big Bend National Park, a beloved stretch of public land known for its sweeping canyons and unspoiled desert landscape.　|　例句中譯　聯邦政府的計劃因將大彎國家公園納入其中而激起了兩黨的強烈反對，大彎國家公園是一片深受人們喜愛的公共土地，以其廣闊的峽谷和未受破壞的沙漠景觀而聞名。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "greenlight", "sf": "greenlights", "pos": "n.", "zh": "綠燈", "syn": "allow, approve, give", "tip": "其他意思　放行　|　英英定義　To approve; to permit to proceed.　|　本文例句　\"This decision greenlights the contractors and allows the bulldozers to come roaring back into the region,\" said Laiken Jordahl with the Center for Biological Diversity.　|　例句中譯　生物多樣性中心的萊肯·喬達爾說：“這一決定為承包商開了綠燈，並允許推土機轟鳴著返回該地區。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "bulldozer", "sf": "bulldozers", "pos": "n.", "zh": "推土機", "syn": "regulator, blade", "tip": "其他意思　恐嚇者　|　英英定義　A tractor with an attached blade for pushing earth and building debris for coarse preliminary surface grading, demolishing building structures, etc.　|　本文例句　\"This decision greenlights the contractors and allows the bulldozers to come roaring back into the region,\" said Laiken Jordahl with the Center for Biological Diversity.　|　例句中譯　生物多樣性中心的萊肯·喬達爾說：“這一決定為承包商開了綠燈，並允許推土機轟鳴著返回該地區。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "unforgiving", "sf": "unforgiving", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "不寬容的", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　Unwilling or unable to forgive or show mercy.　|　本文例句　People across the political spectrum say a wall isn't needed in the Big Bend––a region known for its sweeping canyons, tough terrain and unforgiving desert heat.　|　例句中譯　各個政治派別都表示，大彎地區不需要建造隔離牆——該地區以廣闊的峽谷、崎嶇的地形和無情的沙漠炎熱而聞名。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "fewest", "sf": "fewest", "pos": "", "zh": "最少", "syn": "", "tip": "本文例句　Historically, the Big Bend area's rugged landscape has meant fewer people attempting to cross into the U.　|　例句中譯　從歷史上看，大彎地區崎嶇的地形意味著嘗試越境進入美國的人較少。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "baseless", "sf": "baseless", "pos": "adj.", "zh": "毫無根據的", "syn": "groundless, unfounded", "tip": "其他意思　莫須有　|　英英定義　Of reasoning: based on something that is not true, or not based on solid reasons or facts.　|　本文例句　In the Trump administration's emergency relief request to the Supreme Court, Solicitor General John Sauer called the injunction \"baseless\" and \"unprecedented\" and said any pocket of the Big Bend without a barrier would \"become a funnel point for illegal alien crossings that are thwarted by barriers elsewhere.　|　例句中譯　在川普政府向最高法院提出的緊急救濟請求中，副檢察長約翰·索爾稱該禁令“毫無根據”且“史無前例”，並表示大彎灣任何沒有障礙物的區域都將“成為外國人非法過境的漏斗點，而其他地方的障礙物會阻礙這些非法移民的通行。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "landowner", "sf": "landowner", "pos": "n.", "zh": "地主", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A person who owns land.　|　本文例句　-Mexico border and a landowner who stands to lose his border property.　|　例句中譯　-墨西哥邊境和一名即將失去邊境財產的土地所有者。", "trap": ""}, {"w": "impede", "sf": "impedes", "pos": "v.", "zh": "阻礙", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　礙、絆、妨礙、壅　|　英英定義　To get in the way of; to hinder.　|　本文例句　\"The injunction thus impedes the Government from advancing its 'compelling interests' in border security and integrity,\" reads the unsigned decision.　|　例句中譯　未簽署的決定寫道：“因此，該禁令阻礙政府推進其在邊境安全和完整方面的‘引人注目的利益’。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "thwarted", "sf": "thwarted", "pos": "v.", "zh": "受阻", "syn": "balk, foil, spoil", "tip": "其他意思　橫過、壅、阻礙、阻撓　|　英英定義　To cause to fail; to frustrate, to prevent.　|　本文例句　In the Trump administration's emergency relief request to the Supreme Court, Solicitor General John Sauer called the injunction \"baseless\" and \"unprecedented\" and said any pocket of the Big Bend without a barrier would \"become a funnel point for illegal alien crossings that are thwarted by barriers elsewhere.　|　例句中譯　在川普政府向最高法院提出的緊急救濟請求中，副檢察長約翰·索爾稱該禁令“毫無根據”且“史無前例”，並表示大彎灣任何沒有障礙物的區域都將“成為外國人非法過境的漏斗點，而其他地方的障礙物會阻礙這些非法移民的通行。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "unsigned", "sf": "unsigned", "pos": "n.", "zh": "未簽名", "syn": "", "tip": "英英定義　A numeric value or variable that has no sign and can only be positive.　|　本文例句　\"The injunction thus impedes the Government from advancing its 'compelling interests' in border security and integrity,\" reads the unsigned decision.　|　例句中譯　未簽署的決定寫道：“因此，該禁令阻礙政府推進其在邊境安全和完整方面的‘引人注目的利益’。”", "trap": ""}, {"w": "waive", "sf": "waive", "pos": "v.", "zh": "放棄", "syn": "", "tip": "其他意思　緩服兵役、拋棄　|　英英定義　To relinquish (a right etc.); to give up claim to; to forego.　|　本文例句　The court wrote that federal law allows the Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin to waive environmental protections and conservation laws, which they called a \"clear preference for expeditious border construction over the very harms respondents assert.　|　例句中譯　法院寫道，聯邦法律允許國土安全部長馬克韋恩·穆林 (Markwayne Mullin) 放棄環境保護和保護法，他們稱這些法律「明顯傾向於迅速邊境建設，而不是受訪者聲稱的危害」。", "trap": ""}]}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/09/nx-s1-6019424/border-wall-big-bend-texas-trump"}, {"code": "20261109-1", "ch": "2026-11-09　週一", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Nvidia launches investigation into CEO's alleged relationship with Chinese spy", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Rebecca Hersher，全文共 9 段、15 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：The chipmaking giant says it is looking into reports by The New York Times that its CEO, Jensen Huang, was the target of a Chinese intelligence operation."}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6034036/nvidia-launches-investigation-into-ceos-alleged-relationship-with-chinese-spy"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "大型人工智慧晶片製造商英偉達表示，在有報告指出該公司執行長與一名中國…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "The massive artificial intelligence chip maker Nvidia says it is launching an internal investigation, after reports that the company's CEO was in a close relationship with a Chinese spy.", "zh": "大型人工智慧晶片製造商英偉達表示，在有報告指出該公司執行長與一名中國間諜關係密切後，該公司正在啟動內部調查。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "在宣布調查的聲明中，英偉達引用了《紐約時報》最近的報導，稱英偉達首席…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "In the statement announcing the investigation, Nvidia cited recent reporting by The New York Times, which alleges Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang was the target of a Chinese intelligence operation that sought to send advanced Nvidia AI chips to China.", "zh": "在宣布調查的聲明中，英偉達引用了《紐約時報》最近的報導，稱英偉達首席執行官黃仁勳是中國情報機構的目標，該機構試圖將先進的英偉達人工智慧晶片運送到中國。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "「雖然董事會沒有理由相信國家安全或 NVIDIA 機密受到損害，但董…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"While the Board has no reason to believe that either national security or NVIDIA secrets were compromised, the Board's inquiry will examine all available information,\" the statement from the company's board of directors reads in part.", "zh": "「雖然董事會沒有理由相信國家安全或 NVIDIA 機密受到損害，但董事會的調查將檢查所有可用資訊，」該公司董事會的聲明部分內容如下。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "《泰晤士報》在過去兩週發布了一系列報導，詳細介紹了黃與一位名叫愛麗絲…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "The Times released a series of reports over the last two weeks detailing Huang's alleged relationship with a woman named Alice Huang, who is accused of being a spy for China. The two are not related.", "zh": "《泰晤士報》在過去兩週發布了一系列報導，詳細介紹了黃與一位名叫愛麗絲·黃(Alice Huang)的女子的關係，後者被指控為中國間諜。兩者沒有關係。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "NPR has reached out to the Chinese Embassy in Washington, D.C. but has not received a response.", "zh": "NPR已聯繫中國駐華盛頓大使館，但尚未收到回覆。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "「愛麗絲·黃是中國公民。她是一位神秘而迅速崛起的中國女商人，」《紐約…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "\"Alice Huang is a Chinese national.", "zh": "“黃愛麗絲是中國公民。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She's a Chinese businesswoman who had something of a mysterious and meteoric rise,\" Times reporter Ana Swanson explained on NPR's technology podcast Machine Gods.", "zh": "她是一位神秘而迅速崛起的中國女商人，」《紐約時報》記者安娜·斯旺森 (Ana Swanson) 在 NPR 的科技播客《機器之神》中解釋道。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "斯旺森表示，愛麗絲·黃 (Alice Huang) 經營著一家新加坡…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Alice Huang ran a Singapore-based company that purchased nearly $5 billion in Nvidia chip technology, Swanson says.", "zh": "斯旺森表示，愛麗絲·黃 (Alice Huang) 經營著一家新加坡公司，該公司購買了價值近 50 億美元的 Nvidia 晶片技術。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"At the same time, she was also seen personally with Jensen Huang on a couple of occasions after some industry events in Taiwan.", "zh": "「同時，在台灣參加一些業界活動後，她也多次被看到與黃仁勳在一起。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "They were photographed together both at a bar with other suppliers and then also out to dinner with some other executives.\"", "zh": "他們被拍到與其他供應商一起在酒吧，然後還與其他一些高管共進晚餐。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "上週，三名共和黨國會議員致函英偉達首席執行官，要求他向立法者簡要介紹…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Last week, three Republican members of Congress sent a letter to the Nvidia CEO requesting that he brief lawmakers about the relationship, and about the company's \"security protocols against foreign adversary espionage.\"", "zh": "上週，三名共和黨國會議員致函英偉達首席執行官，要求他向立法者簡要介紹雙方關係以及該公司「針對外國對手間諜活動的安全協議」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "根據 NPR 報導，英偉達在全球人工智慧晶片市場佔據主導地位，並且近…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Nvidia dominates the global market for AI chips, and has seen explosive growth in recent years, as NPR has reported.", "zh": "根據 NPR 報導，英偉達在全球人工智慧晶片市場佔據主導地位，並且近年來出現了爆炸性增長。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The company started as a manufacturer of chips for computer graphics, which later turned out to be crucial for training artificial intelligence.", "zh": "該公司最初是一家電腦圖形晶片製造商，後來證明這對於訓練人工智慧至關重要。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "近年來，英偉達執行長和川普總統多次一起出現在公開場合。黃說，英偉達正…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Nvidia's CEO and President Trump have repeatedly appeared in public together in recent years.", "zh": "近年來，英偉達執行長和川普總統多次一起出現在公開場合。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "According to Huang, Nvidia is helping to fund the construction of a new ballroom at the White House.", "zh": "黃說，英偉達正在幫助資助白宮新宴會廳的興建。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "大型人工智慧晶片製造商英偉達表示，在有報告指出該公司執行長與一名中國間諜關係密切後，該公司正在啟動內部調查。　在宣布調查的聲明中，英偉達引用了《紐約時報》最近的報導，稱英偉達首席執行官黃仁勳是中國情報機構的目標，該機構試圖將先進的英偉達人工智慧晶片運送到中國。　「雖然董事會沒有理由相信國家安全或 NVIDIA 機密受到損害，但董事會的調查將檢查所有可用資訊，」該公司董事會的聲明部分內容如下。　《泰晤士報》在過去兩週發布了一系列報導，詳細介紹了黃與一位名叫愛麗絲·黃(Alice Huang)的女子的關係，後者被指控為中國間諜。兩者沒有關係。 NPR已聯繫中國駐華盛頓大使館，但尚未收到回覆。　「愛麗絲·黃是中國公民。她是一位神秘而迅速崛起的中國女商人，」《紐約時報》記者安娜·斯旺森 (Ana Swanson) 在 NPR 的科技播客 Machine Gods 上解釋道。　斯旺森表示，愛麗絲·黃 (Alice Huang) 經營著一家新加坡公司，該公司購買了價值近 50 億美元的 Nvidia 晶片技術。 “與此同時，在台灣舉行一些行業活動後，人們還多次看到她與黃仁勳在一起。他們被拍到與其他供應商一起在酒吧，然後還與其他一些高管共進晚餐。”　上週，三名共和黨國會議員致函英偉達首席執行官，要求他向立法者簡要介紹雙方關係以及該公司「針對外國對手間諜活動的安全協議」。　根據 NPR 報導，英偉達在全球人工智慧晶片市場佔據主導地位，並且近年來出現了爆炸性增長。該公司最初是一家電腦圖形晶片製造商，後來證明這對於訓練人工智慧至關重要。　近年來，英偉達執行長和川普總統多次一起出現在公開場合。黃說，英偉達正在幫助資助白宮新宴會廳的興建。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6034036/nvidia-launches-investigation-into-ceos-alleged-relationship-with-chinese-spy"}, {"code": "20261109-2", "ch": "2026-11-09　週一", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "NASA is looking for astronauts to live and work on the Moon　／　美國太空總署正在尋找太空人在月球上生活和工作", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Chandelis Duster，全文共 7 段、9 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：美國太空總署需要更多的招募人員才能在離開半個多世紀後重返月球。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6034002/nasa-astronaut-class-applications-2026"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "If you have dreams of going to the moon, you now have a chance.", "zh": "如果你有登上月球的夢想，那麼你現在就有機會了。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "NASA is accepting applications for those interested in becoming an astronaut.", "zh": "美國太空總署正在接受那些有興趣成為太空人的申請。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The candidates selected to be astronauts would not only test spacecraft but would also live and work on the moon in a future moon base, said NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman in a statement released on Saturday.", "zh": "美國太空總署局長賈里德·艾薩克曼在周六發布的聲明中表示，被選為太空人的候選人不僅將測試太空船，還將在未來的月球基地中生活和工作。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "While any U.S. citizen can apply and there is no official age restriction, applicants will need to have a master's degree in a STEM-related field such as engineering or math.", "zh": "雖然任何美國公民都可以申請，並且沒有官方年齡限制，但申請人需要擁有工程或數學等 STEM 相關領域的碩士學位。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "如果被選中，入選的太空人將接受為期兩年的訓練。美國太空總署表示，太空…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "If chosen, the selected astronauts will undergo training that will last for two years.", "zh": "如果被選中，入選的太空人將接受為期兩年的訓練。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "NASA said astronauts will prepare for critical and difficult missions such as landing near the moon's South Pole.", "zh": "美國太空總署表示，太空人將為關鍵和困難的任務做好準備，例如在月球南極附近著陸。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "To achieve its goal of returning humans to the moon in 2028 – the first time since 1972 – NASA is relying on private companies such as Blue Origin and SpaceX to develop systems and spacecraft.", "zh": "為了實現 2028 年讓人類重返月球的目標（這是自 1972 年以來的首次），NASA 依靠 Blue Origin 和 SpaceX 等私人公司來開發系統和太空船。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "During a Nov. 7 press conference on the Artemis III moon mission's progress, Isaacman said he is \"very confident\" the mission will launch in 2027.", "zh": "在 11 月 7 日關於阿耳忒彌斯 III 登月任務進展的新聞發布會上，艾薩克曼表示，他「非常有信心」該任務將於 2027 年啟動。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "The starting salary is $164,395 and applications will be received through Dec. 3.", "zh": "起薪為 164,395 美元，申請截止日期為 12 月 3 日。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "如果被選中，入選的太空人將接受為期兩年的訓練。美國太空總署表示，太空人將為關鍵和困難的任務做好準備，例如在月球南極附近著陸。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6034002/nasa-astronaut-class-applications-2026"}, {"code": "20261109-3", "ch": "2026-11-09　週一", "sec": "White House", "title": "Europe to join U.S.-brokered Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, defying Kremlin objections　／　歐洲不顧克里姆林宮的反對，參加美國斡旋的阿布達比烏克蘭談判", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Willem Marx，全文共 12 段、19 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：法國表示，歐洲官員將參加本週在阿布達比舉行的美國斡旋的俄羅斯-烏克蘭會談，這是自二月以來的第一輪三方談判。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6034014/europe-join-us-brokered-ukraine-talks-abu-dhabi-russia"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "法國外交部長週日表示，歐洲官員將於本週出席美國調解的俄羅斯和烏克蘭在…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "European officials will turn up for the U.S.-mediated peace talks between Russia and Ukraine in the United Arab Emirates this week, France's foreign minister said Sunday, days after the Kremlin had insisted there could be no role for European powers at the meeting.", "zh": "法國外交部長週日表示，歐洲官員將於本週出席美國調解的俄羅斯和烏克蘭在阿拉伯聯合大公國舉行的和平談判，幾天前克里姆林宮堅稱歐洲大國不會在會議上發揮作用。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "讓-諾埃爾·巴羅特對法國電台表示：「法國將出席並確保歐洲的聲音被聽到…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "\"France will be there and will ensure that Europe's voice is heard,\" Jean-Noël Barrot told French radio.", "zh": "讓-諾埃爾·巴羅特對法國電台表示：“法國將出席並確保歐洲的聲音被聽到。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He did not say who would represent Paris, or whether French or other European officials would take part directly in negotiations, or simply observe.", "zh": "他沒有透露誰將代表巴黎，也沒有透露法國或其他歐洲官員是否會直接參與談判，或者只是旁觀。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "這將是川普政府斡旋的兩個交戰國家之間的第四輪會談，也是自今年二月日內…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "This will be the fourth round of talks between the two warring nations brokered by the Trump administration, and the first since those in Geneva this February.", "zh": "這將是川普政府斡旋的兩個交戰國家之間的第四輪會談，也是自今年二月日內瓦會談以來的第一輪會談。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Earlier U.S.-brokered meetings have made little progress, and the chances of a breakthrough have been reduced as the Trump administration focused on its war with Iran.", "zh": "早些時候由美國斡旋的會議幾乎沒有任何進展，而且由於川普政府專注於與伊朗的戰爭，取得突破的可能性也降低了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "莫斯科確認，只有在美國特使史蒂夫·威特科夫 (Steve Witko…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Moscow confirmed it would return to the negotiating table only following a visit by U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff to meet Russian President Vladimir Putin in St. Petersburg in October.", "zh": "莫斯科確認，只有在美國特使史蒂夫·威特科夫 (Steve Witkoff) 十月份在聖彼得堡會見俄羅斯總統弗拉基米爾·普京 (Vladimir Putin) 後，才會重返談判桌。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Those talks saw Putin announce the release of an American prisoner from a Russian jail — an apparent Kremlin gesture to President Trump's earlier lifting of sanctions on Russian diesel exports.", "zh": "在這些會談中，普丁宣布從俄羅斯監獄釋放一名美國囚犯——這顯然是克里姆林宮對川普總統早些時候取消對俄羅斯柴油出口制裁的姿態。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Ukraine was vehemently opposed to the fuel sales — arguing they helped replenish Moscow's war chest.", "zh": "烏克蘭強烈反對燃料銷售，認為有助於補充莫斯科的戰爭資金。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "威特科夫表示，這些最新會談的議程將包括戰後安全安排以及衝突和人道主義…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Witkoff has said the agenda for these latest talks will include postwar security arrangements and de-escalation of the conflict and humanitarian issues, shortly after Melania Trump helped broker a limited ceasefire that allowed humanitarian aid to enter a town inside Russian-occupied Ukraine.", "zh": "威特科夫表示，這些最新會談的議程將包括戰後安全安排以及衝突和人道主義問題的緩和，此前不久，梅拉尼婭·川普幫助促成了有限停火，允許人道主義援助進入俄羅斯佔領的烏克蘭境內的一個城鎮。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "一些分析師對此的預期並不高。美國前駐烏克蘭大使約翰‧赫布斯特在大西洋…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Some analysts expect little.", "zh": "一些分析師對此的預期並不高。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In an op-ed for the Atlantic Council think tank, the former U.S. ambassador to Ukraine John Herbst argued that Putin had rejected every U.S. proposal Kyiv accepted and preferred participating in peace talks than pursuing actual peace.", "zh": "美國前駐烏克蘭大使約翰‧赫布斯特在大西洋理事會智庫的一篇專欄文章中表示，普丁拒絕了基輔接受的每一項美國提議，並且更願意參與和平談判，而不是追求真正的和平。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Perhaps the only outcome of the talks,\" he wrote, \"will be to agree to another round.\"", "zh": "“也許談判的唯一結果，”他寫道，“就是同意進行另一輪談判。”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "在阿拉伯聯合大公國舉行的會議也是在民主黨取得中期勝利之後舉行的，澤倫…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "The meetings in the United Arab Emirates also follow Democrats' midterm victories, which Zelenskyy said could improve Ukraine's chances of more U.S. aid.", "zh": "在阿拉伯聯合大公國舉行的會議也是在民主黨取得中期勝利之後舉行的，澤倫斯基表示這可能會增加烏克蘭獲得更多美國援助的機會。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "烏克蘭入侵—解釋說，俄羅斯也可能希望在民主黨控制的國會明年一月到來之…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Ukraine invasion — explained Russia, too, may be looking to push for the Trump administration's outlines of a Ukraine deal — before a Democratic-controlled Congress arrives come January.", "zh": "烏克蘭入侵—解釋說，俄羅斯也可能希望在民主黨控制的國會明年一月到來之前推動川普政府制定烏克蘭協議的大綱。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "川普、習近平和普丁本月稍晚在中國深圳舉行的亞太經合組織峰會上舉行三邊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Also hovering over the talks — the prospect of Trump, Xi, and Putin gathering for a trilateral meeting at the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen, China later this month.", "zh": "川普、習近平和普丁本月稍晚在中國深圳舉行的亞太經合組織峰會上舉行三邊會議的前景也懸而未決。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "While details remain murky, all sides have confirmed discussions are underway.", "zh": "儘管細節仍不明朗，但各方均確認討論正在進行中。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "當官員前往阿布達比和平談判時，戰爭仍在繼續。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "And as officials travel to Abu Dhabi to talk peace, the war has raged on regardless.", "zh": "當官員前往阿布達比和平談判時，戰爭仍在繼續。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "澤連斯基表示，俄羅斯週六晚上向基輔地區發射了 36 枚彈道飛彈，其中…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "Zelenskyy said Russia fired 36 ballistic missiles at the Kyiv area overnight Saturday, with only four intercepted, accusing Moscow of treating diplomacy \"as a form of aggression.\"", "zh": "澤連斯基表示，俄羅斯週六晚上向基輔地區發射了 36 枚彈道飛彈，其中只有四枚被攔截，並指責莫斯科將外交視為「一種侵略形式」。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "在烏克蘭南部，科梅舒瓦哈 (Komyshuvakha) 的一個援助分…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "In southern Ukraine, the death toll from a guided-bomb strike Monday on an aid distribution site in Komyshuvakha rose to at least 55.", "zh": "在烏克蘭南部，科梅舒瓦哈 (Komyshuvakha) 的一個援助分發地點週一遭受導引炸彈襲擊，死亡人數上升至至少 55 人。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "法國外交部長週日表示，歐洲官員將於本週出席美國調解的俄羅斯和烏克蘭在阿拉伯聯合大公國舉行的和平談判，幾天前克里姆林宮堅稱歐洲大國不會在會議上發揮作用。　讓-諾埃爾·巴羅特對法國電台表示：「法國將出席並確保歐洲的聲音被聽到。」他沒有透露誰將代表巴黎，也沒有透露法國或其他歐洲官員是否會直接參與談判，或者只是旁觀。　這將是川普政府斡旋的兩個交戰國家之間的第四輪會談，也是自今年二月日內瓦會談以來的第一輪會談。早些時候由美國斡旋的會議幾乎沒有任何進展，而且由於川普政府專注於與伊朗的戰爭，取得突破的可能性也降低了。　莫斯科確認，只有在美國特使史蒂夫·威特科夫 (Steve Witkoff) 十月份在聖彼得堡會見俄羅斯總統弗拉基米爾·普京 (Vladimir Putin) 後，才會重返談判桌。在這些會談中，普丁宣布從俄羅斯監獄釋放一名美國囚犯——這顯然是克里姆林宮對川普總統早些時候取消對俄羅斯柴油出口制裁的姿態。烏克蘭強烈反對燃料銷售，認為有助於補充莫斯科的戰爭資金。　威特科夫表示，這些最新會談的議程將包括戰後安全安排以及衝突和人道主義問題的緩和，此前不久，梅拉尼婭·川普幫助促成了有限停火，允許人道主義援助進入俄羅斯佔領的烏克蘭境內的一個城鎮。　一些分析師對此的預期並不高。美國前駐烏克蘭大使約翰‧赫布斯特在大西洋理事會智庫的一篇專欄文章中表示，普丁拒絕了基輔接受的每一項美國提議，並且更願意參與和平談判，而不是追求真正的和平。 “也許談判的唯一結果，”他寫道，“就是同意進行另一輪談判。”　在阿拉伯聯合大公國舉行的會議也是在民主黨取得中期勝利之後舉行的，澤倫斯基表示這可能會增加烏克蘭獲得更多美國援助的機會。　烏克蘭入侵—解釋說，俄羅斯也可能希望在民主黨控制的國會明年一月到來之前推動川普政府制定烏克蘭協議的大綱。　川普、習近平和普丁本月稍晚在中國深圳舉行的亞太經合組織峰會上舉行三邊會議的前景也懸而未決。儘管細節仍不明朗，但各方均確認討論正在進行中。　當官員前往阿布達比和平談判時，戰爭仍在繼續。　澤連斯基表示，俄羅斯週六晚上向基輔地區發射了 36 枚彈道飛彈，其中只有四枚被攔截，並指責莫斯科將外交視為「一種侵略形式」。　在烏克蘭南部，科梅舒瓦哈 (Komyshuvakha) 的一個援助分發地點週一遭受導引炸彈襲擊，死亡人數上升至至少 55 人。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6034014/europe-join-us-brokered-ukraine-talks-abu-dhabi-russia"}, {"code": "20261108-1", "ch": "2026-11-08　週日", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Homelessness in the U.S. saw its largest drop in more than a decade last year　／　去年美國無家可歸者人數出現十多年來最大降幅", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Jennifer Ludden，全文共 11 段、21 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：無家可歸者人數在經歷多年創紀錄的高水準後有所下降，但仍保持在近 70 萬人。川普政府和無家可歸者倡導團體對這一下降給出了不同的原因。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/nx-s1-6033491/homelessness-in-the-u-s-saw-its-largest-drop-in-more-than-a-decade-last-year"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "美國無家可歸人數在多年來不斷增加至創紀錄的水平之後，到 2025 年…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "After years of increasing to record-high levels, the homeless population in the U.S. dropped more than 6% in 2025.", "zh": "美國無家可歸人數在多年來不斷增加至創紀錄的水平之後，到 2025 年將減少 6% 以上。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That amounts to roughly 49,000 fewer people without housing.", "zh": "這意味著無住房人口減少約 49,000 人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's the second year in a row that homelessness has declined, with a smaller drop in 2024.", "zh": "這是無家可歸者數量連續第二年下降，2024 年下降幅度較小。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "\"President Trump's actions to secure the border, get criminal illegals off our streets, and restore safety to our communities drove a historic decrease in homelessness,\" Housing and Urban Development Secretary Scott Turner said in a press release announcing the results of an annual count in communities around the country.", "zh": "住房和城市發展部長斯科特·特納在宣布全國各地社區年度統計結果的新聞稿中表示：“川普總統為確保邊境安全、將非法犯罪分子從我們的街道上趕走以及恢復我們社區的安全而採取的行動，推動了無家可歸者數量的歷史性減少。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The agency had not yet posted a detailed report.", "zh": "該機構尚未發布詳細報告。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "A second independent analysis based on the same count, but commissioned by the advocacy group National Alliance to End Homelessness, found a similar decline but credited different reasons for it.", "zh": "由倡導團體全國終結無家可歸者聯盟委託進行的第二項獨立分析基於相同的計數，發現了類似的下降，但歸因於不同的原因。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "\"It's good news that more people are getting housed, and that the programs that are funded by Congress are working,\" said CEO Ann Oliva.", "zh": "首席執行官安·奧利瓦 (Ann Oliva) 表示：“這是個好消息，越來越多的人得到了安置，國會資助的專案正在發揮作用。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Both analyses find there's still nearly 700,000 people in the U.S. living in shelters or on the streets, significantly more than before the COVID-19 pandemic.", "zh": "兩項分析都發現，美國仍有近 70 萬人生活在避難所或街頭，遠遠多於 COVID-19 大流行之前。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "The administration says longstanding federal policy of getting people into permanent housing first, then offering voluntary treatment, has failed, and is to blame for the pandemic spike in homelessness.", "zh": "政府表示，長期以來先讓人們進入永久住房，然後提供自願治療的聯邦政策已經失敗，並且是導致無家可歸人數激增的罪魁禍首。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But Oliva, with the homelessness alliance, said programs that get people off the street without preconditions were a big part of the latest declines, especially among veterans.", "zh": "但無家可歸者聯盟的奧利瓦表示，無先決條件地讓人們離開街頭的計畫是最近人口減少的一個重要原因，特別是在退伍軍人中。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "\"Investments in programs like that are much closer to the scale of need for veterans than for any other population experiencing homelessness,\" she said.", "zh": "她說：“對此類專案的投資更接近退伍軍人的需求規模，而不是任何其他無家可歸人群的需求規模。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Homelessness among U.S. veterans was down more than 7% last year, and has declined nearly 60% since 2010.", "zh": "去年，美國退伍軍人的無家可歸人數下降了 7% 以上，自 2010 年以來已下降近 60%。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "相較之下，奧利瓦表示，長期無家可歸、更有可能遭受心理健康問題和成癮問…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "By contrast, Oliva said more permanent housing is needed for people who are chronically homeless, and more likely to suffer from mental health problems and addiction.", "zh": "相較之下，奧利瓦表示，長期無家可歸、更有可能遭受心理健康問題和成癮問題的人需要更多的永久性住房。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Unlike other groups that saw a decline last year, there was a small uptick in people who've been homeless for a long time.", "zh": "與去年其他族群人數下降不同，長期無家可歸者人數略有上升。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "教育啟蒙讓她擺脫了無家可歸的情況。川普的提案威脅要為他人提供幫助 H…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Education Head Start got her out of homelessness.", "zh": "教育啟蒙讓她擺脫了無家可歸的情況。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Trump proposal threatens that help for others HUD also credited a crackdown on homeless encampments after the Supreme Court in 2024 said cities can ban people from sleeping and camping in public places.", "zh": "川普的提案威脅要為他人提供幫助 HUD 也將在 2024 年最高法院表示城市可以禁止人們在公共場所睡覺和露營後對無家可歸者營地的打擊做出貢獻。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Oliva said the analysis her group commissioned showed that cities with such bans \"actually did worse than the national average.\"", "zh": "奧利瓦說，她的團隊委託進行的分析顯示，實施此類禁令的城市「實際上比全國平均水平更差」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "Oliva noted last year's decline in homelessness was broad and likely due to a number of factors, including softening rental markets in some places.", "zh": "奧利瓦指出，去年無家可歸者人數大幅下降，可能是由於多種因素造成的，包括一些地方的租賃市場疲軟。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Even though rents are still high they're down from record peaks during the pandemic, and that could stem the flow of newly unhoused people.", "zh": "儘管租金仍然很高，但已較疫情期間的創紀錄高峰有所下降，這可能會阻止新的無家可歸者的流動。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "There were also declines in places that saw major weather disasters, like western North Carolina and Hawaii.", "zh": "北卡羅來納州西部和夏威夷等遭受重大天氣災害的地區的降雨量也有所下降。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "When HUD and other groups move in to help those displaced, unhoused people also get assistance they did not have before.", "zh": "當住房和城市發展部和其他團體介入幫助流離失所者時，無家可歸的人也能得到以前沒有的援助。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "美國無家可歸人數在多年來不斷增加至創紀錄的水平之後，到 2025 年將下降 6% 以上。這意味著無住房人數將減少約 49,000 人。這是無家可歸者數量連續第二年下降，2024 年下降幅度較小。　相較之下，奧利瓦表示，長期無家可歸、更有可能遭受心理健康問題和成癮問題的人需要更多的永久性住房。與去年其他族群人數下降不同，長期無家可歸者人數略有上升。　教育啟蒙讓她擺脫了無家可歸的情況。川普的提案威脅要為他人提供幫助 HUD 也將在 2024 年最高法院表示城市可以禁止人們在公共場所睡覺和露營後對無家可歸者營地的打擊做出貢獻。奧利瓦說，她的團隊委託進行的分析顯示，實施此類禁令的城市「實際上比全國平均水平更差」。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/nx-s1-6033491/homelessness-in-the-u-s-saw-its-largest-drop-in-more-than-a-decade-last-year"}, {"code": "20261108-2", "ch": "2026-11-08　週日", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Israel's president taps opposition candidate, not Netanyahu, to form a government　／　以色列總統選擇反對派候選人而非內塔尼亞胡組成政府", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Tara Neill，全文共 7 段、14 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：Gadi Eisenkot ran as the main rival to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, but neither won enough support to command a majority. Israel's main parties have recommended Eisenkot form a new government."}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/g-s1-152536/netanyahu-israel-government-eisenkot-herzog"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "以色列總統任命總理本傑明·內塔尼亞胡的主要政治對手加迪·艾森科特來嘗…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "Israel's president has tapped Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's main political rival, Gadi Eisenkot, to try to form the next government.", "zh": "以色列總統任命總理本傑明·內塔尼亞胡的主要政治對手加迪·艾森科特來嘗試組成下一屆政府。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It's a setback for Netanyahu, whose party won the most seats but failed to secure a parliamentary majority.", "zh": "這對內塔尼亞胡來說是一個挫折，他的政黨贏得了最多席位，但未能獲得議會多數。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "內塔尼亞胡的利庫德集團在上個月的選舉中贏得了 27 個席位，比艾森科…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Netanyahu's Likud party won 27 seats in last month's election, six more than Eisenkot's Yashar party.", "zh": "內塔尼亞胡的利庫德集團在上個月的選舉中贏得了 27 個席位，比艾森科特的亞沙爾黨多了 6 個席位。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But neither secured enough support to command a majority in Israel's 120-seat parliament.", "zh": "但兩人都沒有獲得足夠的支持，無法在以色列 120 席的議會中獲得多數席次。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "艾薩克·赫爾佐格總統將於下午 5 點正式授權艾森科特。當地時間週日。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "President Isaac Herzog will formally give Eisenkot the mandate at 5 p.m. local time on Sunday.", "zh": "艾薩克·赫爾佐格總統將於下午 5 點正式授權艾森科特。當地時間週日。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "艾森科特是以色列國防軍前參謀長，2015年至2019年擔任該國最高軍…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Eisenkot is a former chief of staff of the Israel Defense Forces, serving as the country's top military commander from 2015 to 2019.", "zh": "艾森科特是以色列國防軍前參謀長，2015年至2019年擔任該國最高軍事指揮官。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "A veteran of several military campaigns, he later joined Netanyahu's emergency war cabinet following the Oct. 7, 2023, Hamas attacks on Israel, but left the following year, accusing Netanyahu of failing to make progress toward ending the Gaza war and securing the release of hostages.", "zh": "作為多次軍事行動的老兵，他後來在 2023 年 10 月 7 日哈馬斯襲擊以色列後加入內塔尼亞胡的緊急戰爭內閣，但於次年離開，指責內塔尼亞胡未能在結束加薩戰爭和確保釋放人質方面取得進展。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Eisenkot lost his son, Gal, a reservist killed in Gaza, as well as two nephews during the war.", "zh": "艾森科特在戰爭期間失去了他的兒子加爾（一名預備役軍人在加薩陣亡）以及兩個侄子。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "艾森科特領導中間派亞沙爾黨，他以反腐敗和政府改革為綱領創立了該黨。他…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Eisenkot leads the centrist Yashar party, which he founded on an anti-corruption and government reform platform.", "zh": "艾森科特領導中間派亞沙爾黨，他以反腐敗和政府改革為綱領創立了該黨。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He will now have 28 days to put together a coalition government, with a possible 14-day extension.", "zh": "他現在有 28 天的時間組成聯合政府，並可能延長 14 天。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "這讓他有六週的時間與對手政黨進行談判，並獲得議會多數所需的 61 個…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "That gives him up to six weeks to negotiate with rival parties and secure the 61 seats needed for a parliamentary majority.", "zh": "這讓他有六週的時間與對手政黨進行談判，並獲得議會多數所需的 61 個席位。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "如果艾森科特失敗，赫爾佐格可以給另一位立法者一個組成政府的機會。如果…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "If Eisenkot fails, Herzog can give another lawmaker a chance to form a government.", "zh": "如果艾森科特失敗，赫爾佐格可以給另一位立法者一個組成政府的機會。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "If those efforts also fail, Israel could face another election.", "zh": "如果這些努力也失敗，以色列可能面臨另一次選舉。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Netanyahu would remain caretaker prime minister in the meantime.", "zh": "內塔尼亞胡在此期間仍將擔任看守總理。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "以色列總統任命總理本傑明·內塔尼亞胡的主要政治對手加迪·艾森科特來嘗試組成下一屆政府。這對內塔尼亞胡來說是一個挫折，他的政黨贏得了最多席位，但未能獲得議會多數。　內塔尼亞胡的利庫德集團在上個月的選舉中贏得了 27 個席位，比艾森科特的亞沙爾黨多了 6 個席位。但兩人都沒有獲得足夠的支持，無法在以色列 120 席的議會中獲得多數席次。　艾薩克·赫爾佐格總統將於下午 5 點正式授權艾森科特。當地時間週日。　艾森科特是以色列國防軍前參謀長，2015年至2019年擔任該國最高軍事指揮官。他是多次军事战役的老兵，后来在2023年10月7日哈马斯袭击以色列后加入内塔尼亚胡的紧急战争内阁，但于次年离开，指责内塔尼亚胡未能在结束加沙战争和确保释放人质方面取得进展。艾森科特在戰爭期間失去了他的兒子加爾（一名預備役軍人在加薩陣亡）以及兩個侄子。　艾森科特領導中間派亞沙爾黨，他以反腐敗和政府改革為綱領創立了該黨。他現在有 28 天的時間組成聯合政府，並可能延長 14 天。　這讓他有六週的時間與對手政黨進行談判，並獲得議會多數所需的 61 個席位。　如果艾森科特失敗，赫爾佐格可以給另一位立法者一個組成政府的機會。如果這些努力也失敗，以色列可能面臨另一次選舉。內塔尼亞胡在此期間仍將擔任看守總理。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/g-s1-152536/netanyahu-israel-government-eisenkot-herzog"}, {"code": "20261108-3", "ch": "2026-11-08　週日", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Gunman opens fire in Polish city of Krakow, killing 6 people and injuring 15　／　波蘭克拉科夫市發生槍擊事件 造成6人死亡15人受傷", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、The Associated Press，全文共 12 段、22 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：一名槍手開車進入克拉科夫主要旅遊景點的主廣場時隨機瞄準人群。警方在槍戰中開槍打傷了槍手。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/g-s1-152532/gunman-opens-fire-in-polish-city-of-krakow-killing-6-people-and-injuring-15"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "波蘭克拉科夫（美聯社）——當局稱，週六下午，一名槍手在波蘭克拉科夫一…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "KRAKOW, Poland (AP) — Six people were killed and 15 wounded after a gunman opened fire Saturday afternoon in a busy market square in Krakow, Poland, authorities said.", "zh": "波蘭克拉科夫（美聯社）——當局稱，週六下午，一名槍手在波蘭克拉科夫一個繁忙的集市廣場開槍，造成 6 人死亡、15 人受傷。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "克拉科夫警方稱，槍手是一名 24 歲的波蘭公民，他在駕車駛入市中心主…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "The gunman, a 24-year-old Polish citizen, aimed at random people as he drove into the Main Square, a major tourist destination in the center of the city, Krakow police said.", "zh": "克拉科夫警方稱，槍手是一名 24 歲的波蘭公民，他在駕車駛入市中心主要旅遊目的地主廣場時隨機瞄準人群。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Four women and two men were killed.", "zh": "四名婦女和兩名男子被殺。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Two police officers were wounded, one seriously, Poland's interior minister said on X.", "zh": "波蘭內政部長 X 表示，兩名警察受傷，其中一名嚴重受傷。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "警方稱，肇事者在距離最初暴力事件不遠的地方與警察發生槍戰時被槍擊受傷…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "The perpetrator was shot and wounded during a gunfight with officers a short distance away from the initial violence, police said, and was taken to the hospital for surgery.", "zh": "警方稱，肇事者在距離最初暴力事件不遠的地方與警察發生槍戰時被槍擊受傷，並被送往醫院接受手術。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The death toll earlier stood at five, but police updated it to six in a post on X.", "zh": "早些時候死亡人數為五人，但警方在 X 上的一篇貼文中將死亡人數更新為六人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "克拉科夫警方發言人卡塔齊娜·西斯沃表示，行凶者身穿軍用迷彩服和防彈背…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Katarzyna Cisło, a spokesperson for the Krakow police, said the perpetrator was wearing military-style fatigues and a bulletproof vest and used a military-type long gun in the attack.", "zh": "克拉科夫警方發言人卡塔齊娜·西斯沃表示，行凶者身穿軍用迷彩服和防彈背心，並在攻擊中使用軍用長槍。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Police found many other weapons, as well as ammunition, in his car.", "zh": "警方在他的車上發現了許多其他武器和彈藥。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He kept firing at the police even after being shot himself, she said.", "zh": "她說，即使他自己被槍殺，他仍繼續向警察開槍。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "西斯沃說，襲擊者在主廣場周圍進行了“瘋狂騎行”，這就是多處人員受傷的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "The attacker engaged in a \"wild ride\" around the Main Square, Cisło said, which is why people were wounded at several locations.", "zh": "西斯沃說，襲擊者在主廣場周圍進行了“瘋狂騎行”，這就是多處人員受傷的原因。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Videos posted on social media by witnesses show people running away from the square to take cover on small streets nearby.", "zh": "目擊者在社群媒體上發布的影片顯示，人們逃離廣場，躲到附近的小街道上。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "西斯沃補充說，槍手是單獨行動的，公眾是安全的。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Cisło added that the gunman acted alone and that the public is safe.", "zh": "西斯沃補充說，槍手是單獨行動的，公眾是安全的。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "目前尚不清楚週六襲擊中使用的槍支或在肇事者汽車中發現的槍支是否合法。…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "It was not immediately clear whether the firearm used in Saturday's attack, or the guns found in the perpetrator's car, were legal.", "zh": "目前尚不清楚週六襲擊中使用的槍支或在肇事者汽車中發現的槍支是否合法。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Around 411,000 people hold gun permits in Poland, which has a population of 37 million, and interest in gun ownership has been rising.", "zh": "在擁有 3,700 萬人口的波蘭，約有 411,000 人持有槍支許可證，人們對擁有槍支的興趣一直在上升。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "大規模槍擊事件在波蘭並不常見。然而，10月中旬，中部馬佐維亞省的學校…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Mass shootings are uncommon in Poland.", "zh": "大規模槍擊事件在波蘭並不常見。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "However, in mid-October three attacks at schools in the central province of Mazovia took place within four days, leaving one person dead and many wounded, including children.", "zh": "然而，10月中旬，中部馬佐維亞省的學校在四天內發生了三起攻擊事件，造成一人死亡、多人受傷，包括兒童。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "波蘭總理唐納德·圖斯克在 X 上的一篇帖子中讚揚了對週六悲劇做出反應…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk, in a post on X, praised the police officers who responded to Saturday's tragedy.", "zh": "波蘭總理唐納德·圖斯克在 X 上的一篇帖子中讚揚了對週六悲劇做出反應的警察。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Polish President Karol Nawrocki said his thoughts were with the victims, the wounded and their families.", "zh": "波蘭總統卡羅爾·納羅基表示，他與罹難者、傷者及其家人同在。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "現場影像顯示，警察和救護車覆蓋了該地區，一架波蘭醫療空中救援直升機也…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "Images from the scene showed police officers and ambulances covering the area, and a Polish Medical Air Rescue helicopter also landed in the square.", "zh": "現場影像顯示，警察和救護車覆蓋了該地區，一架波蘭醫療空中救援直升機也降落在廣場上。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "下午 3 點左右，一名電車司機報告。克拉科夫市交通公司表示，他的車輛…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "A tram driver reported around 3 p.m. that his vehicle was shot at from a man in a moving car while passing nearby the main square, the Krakow municipal transport company said.", "zh": "下午 3 點左右，一名電車司機報告。克拉科夫市交通公司表示，他的車輛在經過主廣場附近時被一輛行駛中的汽車中的一名男子槍擊。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The window to the tram driver's cabin was shattered.", "zh": "電車司機室的窗戶被震碎。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "每年約有 1500 萬遊客參觀波蘭第二大城市克拉科夫，其中大部分經過…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "Around 15 million tourists a year visit Krakow, Poland's second-largest city, the majority passing through the Main Square.", "zh": "每年約有 1500 萬遊客參觀波蘭第二大城市克拉科夫，其中大部分經過主廣場。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "波蘭克拉科夫（美聯社）——當局稱，週六下午，一名槍手在波蘭克拉科夫一個繁忙的集市廣場開槍，造成 6 人死亡、15 人受傷。　克拉科夫警方稱，槍手是一名 24 歲的波蘭公民，他在駕車駛入市中心主要旅遊目的地主廣場時隨機瞄準人群。四名婦女和兩名男子被殺。波蘭內政部長 X 表示，兩名警察受傷，其中一名嚴重受傷。　警方稱，肇事者在距離最初暴力事件不遠的地方與警察發生槍戰時被槍擊受傷，並被送往醫院接受手術。早些時候死亡人數為五人，但警方在 X 上的一篇貼文中將死亡人數更新為六人。　克拉科夫警方發言人卡塔齊娜·西斯沃表示，行凶者身穿軍用迷彩服和防彈背心，並在攻擊中使用軍用長槍。警方在他的車上發現了許多其他武器和彈藥。她說，即使他自己被槍殺，他仍繼續向警察開槍。　西斯沃說，襲擊者在主廣場周圍進行了“瘋狂騎行”，這就是多處人員受傷的原因。目擊者在社群媒體上發布的影片顯示，人們逃離廣場，躲到附近的小街道上。　西斯沃補充說，槍手是單獨行動的，公眾是安全的。　目前尚不清楚週六襲擊中使用的槍支或在肇事者汽車中發現的槍支是否合法。在擁有 3,700 萬人口的波蘭，約有 411,000 人持有槍支許可證，人們對擁有槍支的興趣一直在上升。　大規模槍擊事件在波蘭並不常見。然而，10月中旬，中部馬佐維亞省的學校在四天內發生了三起攻擊事件，造成一人死亡、多人受傷，包括兒童。　波蘭總理唐納德·圖斯克在 X 上的一篇帖子中讚揚了對週六悲劇做出反應的警察。波蘭總統卡羅爾·納羅基表示，他與罹難者、傷者及其家人同在。　現場影像顯示，警察和救護車覆蓋了該地區，一架波蘭醫療空中救援直升機也降落在廣場上。　下午 3 點左右，一名電車司機報告。克拉科夫市交通公司表示，他的車輛在經過主廣場附近時被一輛行駛中的汽車中的一名男子槍擊。電車司機室的窗戶被震碎。　每年約有 1500 萬遊客參觀波蘭第二大城市克拉科夫，其中大部分經過主廣場。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/g-s1-152532/gunman-opens-fire-in-polish-city-of-krakow-killing-6-people-and-injuring-15"}, {"code": "20261107-1", "ch": "2026-11-07　週六", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Israel's Arab-led parties in spotlight after inconclusive election　／　以色列阿拉伯領導的政黨在選舉無果後成為焦點", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Ruth Sherlock，全文共 10 段、24 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：以色列中右翼反對派有機會推翻內塔尼亞胡，但阿拉伯領導政黨的支持將是關鍵。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/g-s1-152138/israel-election-palestinian-arab-parties"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "以色列庫弗爾卡西——近年來，許多以色列巴勒斯坦公民迴避選舉，認為參與…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "KUFR QASI, Israel — In recent years many Palestinian citizens of Israel shunned elections, believing there was little to gain from participating in the politics of a state which, they say, regularly marginalizes their communities and oppresses their fellow Palestinians in the West Bank and Gaza.", "zh": "以色列庫弗爾卡西——近年來，許多以色列巴勒斯坦公民迴避選舉，認為參與一個國家的政治沒有什麼好處，他們說，這個國家經常邊緣化他們的社區，並壓迫約旦河西岸和加薩的巴勒斯坦同胞。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "但上個月，以色列的巴勒斯坦阿拉伯人以創紀錄的數量來到投票箱，幫助以色…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "But last month, Palestinian Arabs in Israel came to the ballot boxes in record numbers, helping strip Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's most far-right government in Israel's history of its majority, and giving Arab-led parties the votes they needed to become a powerful force in Israeli politics.", "zh": "但上個月，以色列的巴勒斯坦阿拉伯人以創紀錄的數量來到投票箱，幫助以色列總理本傑明·內塔尼亞胡（Benjamin Netanyahu）剝奪了以色列歷史上最右翼政府的多數席位，並為阿拉伯領導的政黨提供了成為以色列政治中強大力量所需的選票。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "參與這次活動的人群大多身著黑衣，其中一些人戴著阿拉伯頭巾，這是一種象…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "The crowd at this event, mostly dressed in black — some wearing the keffiyeh, the black and white stitched scarf symbolizing Palestinian resistance — mourned not only their lost relatives all those years ago, but also the suffering of Palestinians now: the sharp rise in discrimination against their communities in Israel since the deadly Hamas-led attacks on Israel on Oct. 7, 2023; Israel's war against Hamas in Gaza that has killed more than 74,000 Palestinians and left a population to survive amid the ruins of the enclave.", "zh": "參與這次活動的人群大多身著黑衣，其中一些人戴著阿拉伯頭巾，這是一種象徵巴勒斯坦抵抗的黑白縫製圍巾，他們不僅哀悼多年前失去的親人，也哀悼巴勒斯坦人現在所遭受的苦難：自 2023 年 10 月 7 日哈馬斯領導的對以色列發動致命襲擊以來，以色列境內對其社區的歧視已急劇增加；多名巴勒斯坦人死亡，只剩下一些人在飛地的廢墟中生存。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And the actions of Netanyahu's extreme right-wing government in the occupied West Bank, where rights groups and the U.N. say it has armed and supported settlers as they force Palestinians from their homes and agricultural lands with unprecedented violence.", "zh": "還有內塔尼亞胡極右翼政府在被佔領的約旦河西岸的行動，人權組織和聯合國表示，內塔尼亞胡政府武裝並支持定居者，以前所未有的暴力迫使巴勒斯坦人離開家園和農田。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "以色列的巴勒斯坦公民是 1948 年以色列建國時留下的人的後裔（當時…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Palestinian citizens of Israel, descendants of those who remained as the state of Israel was established in 1948 (when a majority of the prewar population was forcibly expelled or fled during the war) now make up about 20% of the population.", "zh": "以色列的巴勒斯坦公民是 1948 年以色列建國時留下的人的後裔（當時大多數戰前人口在戰爭期間被強行驅逐或逃離），現在約佔人口的 20%。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "据中央选举委员会称，这次选举中，阿拉伯人领导的政党获得的选票比上次选…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "This election, Arab-led parties received a 64% increase in votes compared to the last elections, according to the Central Elections Committee.", "zh": "據中央選舉委員會稱，這次選舉中，阿拉伯人領導的政黨獲得的選票比上次選舉增加了 64%。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The gains they made have stirred anger, and even fear, among many on Israel's political right, who see them as a threat to the country's Jewish character.", "zh": "他們所取得的成果激起了許多以色列政治右派人士的憤怒甚至恐懼，他們認為這些成果對該國的猶太性格構成了威脅。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "內塔尼亞胡和他的盟友以阿拉伯人的大量投票作為戰鬥口號。選舉日當天，內…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Netanyahu and his allies made the large Arab turnout a rallying cry.", "zh": "內塔尼亞胡和他的盟友以阿拉伯人的大量投票作為戰鬥口號。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "On election day, Netanyahu posted a video calling it an \"emergency.\" Itamar Ben Gvir, the far-right national security minister, filmed his own appeal at the entrance to Kufr Qasim: \"If you want this country to remain Jewish and Zionist … then get out and vote!\"", "zh": "選舉日當天，內塔尼亞胡發布了一段影片，稱其為“緊急情況”。極右翼國家安全部長伊塔馬爾·本·格維爾 (Itamar Ben Gvir) 在庫夫爾·卡西姆 (Kufr Qasim) 入口處拍攝了自己的呼籲：“如果你希望這個國家繼續是猶太人和猶太復國主義者……那就出去投票吧！”", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "因此，阿拉伯政黨對於如何使用他們在這次選舉中獲得的權力存在分歧。拉姆…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "So Arab parties are divided on how to use the power they gained in this election.", "zh": "因此，阿拉伯政黨對於如何使用他們在這次選舉中獲得的權力存在分歧。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Ra'am, a socially conservative Islamist party, campaigned on joining a governing coalition and put a Jewish former police official second on its list.", "zh": "拉姆是一個社會保守的伊斯蘭政黨，在競選中主張加入執政聯盟，並將一名猶太前警察官員列入其名單的第二位。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But for now the Joint List alliance that won 11 of the 19 Arab-led party seats in this election won't formally partner with Eisenkot.", "zh": "但目前，在這次選舉中贏得阿拉伯領導政黨 19 個席位中 11 個席位的聯合名單聯盟不會與艾森科特正式合作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Its leaders have said they could back his government from the outside, but won't join it, citing Israel's ongoing war in Gaza and its occupation of the West Bank.", "zh": "其領導人表示，他們可以從外部支持他的政府，但不會加入其中，理由是以色列在加薩正在進行的戰爭以及對約旦河西岸的佔領。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "President Isaac Herzog has been consulting with parties over who they would support to try to form a coalition.", "zh": "艾薩克·赫爾佐格總統一直在與各黨派協商他們將支持誰來組成聯合政府。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He is expected to announce which candidate he'll give a mandate to next week, to try to form a coalition.", "zh": "預計他將在下周宣布將授權給哪位候選人，以嘗試組成聯盟。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "That candidate will have 28 days and can ask for a further two-week extension.", "zh": "該候選人將有 28 天的時間，並且可以要求再延長兩週。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "If he fails, another candidate is given only 28 days (without extension) to try to form a government.", "zh": "如果他失敗了，另一位候選人只有 28 天（不得延期）的時間嘗試組成政府。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "And if no one manages to form a coalition, there will be repeat elections next year.", "zh": "如果沒有人能夠組成聯合政府，明年將再次舉行選舉。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "在庫夫爾卡西姆，當 1956 年大屠殺的朗誦和重演在舞台上展開時，曼…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "In Kufr Qasim, as the readings and re-enactments of the 1956 killings unfurled on stage, Mansour Shaaban said he would vote again in an instant.", "zh": "在庫夫爾卡西姆，當 1956 年大屠殺的朗誦和重演在舞台上展開時，曼蘇爾沙班表示他將立即再次投票。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Aged 33, this was the first election he had voted in.", "zh": "33歲的這是他參加的第一次選舉。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But now he said it's necessary to try to stop what he called the racism and oppression of Palestinians by Israel's extreme right.", "zh": "但現在他表示，有必要努力阻止他所謂的以色列極右派對巴勒斯坦人的種族主義和壓迫。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"There are Israelis we eat with and live alongside,\" Shaaban said.", "zh": "「我們和以色列人一起吃飯、一起生活，」沙班說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "But Netanyahu and Ben-Gvir and other leaders in these last years he said \"are making it impossible to co-exist,\" he said.", "zh": "但他說，內塔尼亞胡和本格維爾以及其他領導人在過去幾年「正在使共存變得不可能」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "他說：「即使我們這次未能成功創造變革，」現在以色列右翼政客知道該國的…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "\"Even if we don't succeed to create change this time,\" he said, now right-wing Israeli politicians know that Palestinian citizens of the country have found their voice.", "zh": "他說：「即使我們這次未能成功創造變革，」現在以色列右翼政客知道該國的巴勒斯坦公民已經找到了自己的聲音。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "以色列庫弗爾卡西——近年來，許多以色列巴勒斯坦公民迴避選舉，認為參與一個國家的政治沒有什麼好處，他們說，這個國家經常邊緣化他們的社區，並壓迫約旦河西岸和加薩的巴勒斯坦同胞。　但上個月，以色列的巴勒斯坦阿拉伯人以創紀錄的數量來到投票箱，幫助以色列總理本傑明·內塔尼亞胡（Benjamin Netanyahu）剝奪了以色列歷史上最右翼政府的多數席位，並為阿拉伯領導的政黨提供了成為以色列政治中強大力量所需的選票。　參與這次活動的人群大多身著黑衣，其中一些人戴著阿拉伯頭巾，這是一種象徵巴勒斯坦抵抗的黑白縫製圍巾，他們不僅哀悼多年前失去的親人，也哀悼巴勒斯坦人現在所遭受的苦難：自 2023 年 10 月 7 日哈馬斯領導的對以色列發動致命襲擊以來，以色列境內對其社區的歧視已急劇增加； 多名巴勒斯坦人死亡，只剩下一些人在飞地的废墟中生存。還有內塔尼亞胡極右翼政府在被佔領的約旦河西岸的行動，人權組織和聯合國表示，內塔尼亞胡政府武裝並支持定居者，以前所未有的暴力迫使巴勒斯坦人離開家園和農田。　以色列的巴勒斯坦公民是 1948 年以色列建國時留下的人的後裔（當時大多數戰前人口在戰爭期間被強行驅逐或逃離），現在約佔人口的 20%。　据中央选举委员会称，这次选举中，阿拉伯人领导的政党获得的选票比上次选举增加了 64%。他們所取得的成果激起了許多以色列政治右派人士的憤怒甚至恐懼，他們認為這些成果對該國的猶太性格構成了威脅。　內塔尼亞胡和他的盟友以阿拉伯人的大量投票作為戰鬥口號。選舉日當天，內塔尼亞胡發布了一段影片，稱其為“緊急情況”。極右翼國家安全部長伊塔馬爾·本·格維爾 (Itamar Ben Gvir) 在庫夫爾·卡西姆 (Kufr Qasim) 入口處拍攝了自己的呼籲：“如果你希望這個國家繼續是猶太人和猶太復國主義者……那就出去投票吧！”　因此，阿拉伯政黨對於如何使用他們在這次選舉中獲得的權力存在分歧。拉姆是一個社會保守的伊斯蘭政黨，在競選中主張加入執政聯盟，並將一名猶太前警察官員列入其名單的第二位。但目前，在這次選舉中贏得阿拉伯領導政黨 19 個席位中 11 個席位的聯合名單聯盟不會與艾森科特正式合作。其領導人表示，他們可以從外部支持他的政府，但不會加入其中，理由是以色列在加薩正在進行的戰爭以及對約旦河西岸的佔領。　在庫夫爾卡西姆，當 1956 年大屠殺的朗誦和重演在舞台上展開時，曼蘇爾沙班表示他將立即再次投票。 33歲的他參加了第一次選舉。但現在他表示，有必要努力阻止他所謂的以色列極右派對巴勒斯坦人的種族主義和壓迫。 「我們和以色列人一起吃飯、一起生活，」沙班說。但他說，內塔尼亞胡和本格維爾以及其他領導人在過去幾年「正在使共存變得不可能」。　他說：「即使我們這次未能成功創造變革，」現在以色列右翼政客知道該國的巴勒斯坦公民已經找到了自己的聲音。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/g-s1-152138/israel-election-palestinian-arab-parties"}, {"code": "20261107-2", "ch": "2026-11-07　週六", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "The incoming class of U.S. senators is full of historic firsts　／　即將上任的美國參議員充滿了歷史性的第一", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 Saige Miller，全文共 11 段、35 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：從第一位當選美國參議院的美國原住民女性，到第一位加入參議院的穆斯林，再到參議院第一位殘奧會運動員，選民在周二選出了歷史性的候選人。"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/nx-s1-6032814/senate-history-election-pappas-andrews-el-sayed"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "當最新一批美國參議員在一月份宣誓就職時，其中將包括一些美國的第一名。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "When the newest class of U.S. senators are sworn into office in January, it will include some of America's firsts.", "zh": "當最新一批美國參議員在一月份宣誓就職時，其中將包括一些美國的第一名。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "圖雷克將成為第一位在參議院任職的殘奧會運動員。這位民主黨人曾兩度獲得…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "Turek will be the first Paralympian to serve in the Senate.", "zh": "圖雷克將成為第一位在參議院任職的殘奧會運動員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The Democrat is a two-time gold medalist in wheelchair basketball.", "zh": "這位民主黨人曾兩度獲得輪椅籃球金牌。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Turek is paraplegic and uses a wheelchair due to spina bifida.", "zh": "由於脊柱裂，圖雷克截癱並需要使用輪椅。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He beat Republican Ashley Hinson in the general election.", "zh": "他在大選中擊敗了共和黨人阿什利·辛森。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "萊特洛現已兩度創造歷史。她是 2021 年路易斯安那州第一位當選美國…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "Letlow has now made history twice.", "zh": "萊特洛現已兩度創造歷史。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She was the first Republican woman elected to the U.S. House from Louisiana in 2021.", "zh": "她是 2021 年路易斯安那州第一位當選美國眾議院議員的共和黨女性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Letlow ran for the House in a special election to replace her late husband, Congressman Luke Letlow, who died of COVID-19 in 2020.", "zh": "萊特洛 (Letlow) 在一次特別選舉中競選眾議院議員，以取代她已故的丈夫、國會議員盧克·萊特洛 (Luke Letlow)，後者於 2020 年死於 COVID-19。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Now, Louisiana voters have decided to send her to the Senate, where she will be the first Republican woman from the state to serve.", "zh": "現在，路易斯安那州選民決定將她送入參議院，她將成為該州第一位任職的共和黨女性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She will succeed Republican Sen.", "zh": "她將接替共和黨參議員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Bill Cassidy, who Letlow beat in the primary election.", "zh": "比爾·卡西迪 (Bill Cassidy)，萊特洛在初選中擊敗了他。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "即將上任的民主黨參議員是埃及移民的兒子，也是第一位擔任參議員的穆斯林…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "The incoming Democratic senator is the son of Egyptian immigrants and is the first Muslim person elected to the upper chamber.", "zh": "即將上任的民主黨參議員是埃及移民的兒子，也是第一位擔任參議員的穆斯林人士。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "El-Sayed is an epidemiologist and the former health director for the city of Detroit.", "zh": "埃爾-賽義德是一位流行病學家，也是底特律市前衛生總監。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He beat Republican Mike Rogers for the hotly contested seat.", "zh": "他擊敗了共和黨人麥克羅傑斯，贏得了競爭激烈的席位。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "明尼蘇達州的民主黨副州長是第一位當選參議員的美國原住民女性。弗拉納根…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "Minnesota's Democratic Lt.", "zh": "明尼蘇達州民主黨中尉"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Governor is the first Native American woman elected to the Senate.", "zh": "州長是第一位當選參議員的美國原住民女性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Flanagan is a member of the White Earth Band of Ojibwe.", "zh": "弗拉納根是奧及布威白土樂團的成員。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She also made political history more than once.", "zh": "她還不只創造了政治歷史。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She was also the first woman of color elected to state office in Minnesota.", "zh": "她也是明尼蘇達州第一位當選州政府官員的有色人種女性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Flanagan will replace outgoing Democratic Sen. Tina Smith.", "zh": "弗拉納根將接替即將卸任的民主黨參議員蒂娜史密斯。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "帕帕斯是第一位當選參議員的公開同性戀者，也是第一位代表新罕布夏州的同…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "Pappas is the first openly gay man elected to the Senate and is also the first gay man to represent the state of New Hampshire.", "zh": "帕帕斯是第一位當選參議員的公開同性戀者，也是第一位代表新罕布夏州的同性戀者。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He served four terms in the House and beat Republican John Sununu in the election.", "zh": "他在眾議院連任四屆，並在選舉中擊敗了共和黨人約翰·蘇努努。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "在選舉之夜最大的冷門之一中，安德魯斯在深紅色的南卡羅來納州取得了失敗…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "In one of the biggest election night upsets, Andrews pulled out an underdog win in deep red South Carolina.", "zh": "在選舉之夜最大的冷門之一中，安德魯斯在深紅色的南卡羅來納州取得了失敗的勝利。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Andrews is the first woman elected to the U.S. senate from the Palmetto State.", "zh": "安德魯斯是第一位從帕爾梅托州當選為美國參議員的女性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She beat Darline Graham, who was appointed to replace her late brother Lindsey Graham.", "zh": "她擊敗了達林·格雷厄姆，後者被任命接替她已故的兄弟林賽·格雷厄姆。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "這兩個州都是可靠的共和黨州，都派牧師到華盛頓。這次中期選舉選民打破現…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "Both states are reliably Republican and both states are sending pastors to Washington.", "zh": "這兩個州都是可靠的共和黨州，都派牧師到華盛頓。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "This midterm election voters broke with the status quo and elected Democrats to represent them in the Senate.", "zh": "這次中期選舉選民打破現狀，選舉民主黨人在參議院代表他們。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "在德州，選民選擇民主黨人詹姆斯·塔拉里科為下一任參議員。這是長角州自…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "In Texas, voters selected Democrat James Talarico as their next senator.", "zh": "在德州，選民選擇民主黨人詹姆斯·塔拉里科為下一任參議員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It is the first time the Longhorn State has sent a Democrat to the chamber since 1988.", "zh": "這是長角州自 1988 年以來首次派遣民主黨人進入眾議院。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Talarico won against Republican nominee Ken Paxton.", "zh": "塔拉里科擊敗了共和黨候選人肯·帕克斯頓。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "近一百年後，堪薩斯州選出了一位民主黨參議員進入眾議院。亞當漢密爾頓將…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "After nearly 100 years, Kansas elected a democratic senator to the chamber.", "zh": "近一百年後，堪薩斯州選出了一位民主黨參議員進入眾議院。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Adam Hamilton will be the first Democrat that has served the state since 1932.", "zh": "亞當漢密爾頓將成為自 1932 年以來第一位為該州服務的民主黨人。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He fended off a tough race with incumbent Republican Roger Marshall.", "zh": "他在與現任共和黨人羅傑馬歇爾的激烈競爭中脫穎而出。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "這個故事的先前版本錯誤地稱佩吉·弗拉納根是第一位當選美國參議院的美洲…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "A previous version of this story incorrectly said Peggy Flanagan is the first Native American elected to the U.S. Senate.", "zh": "這個故事的先前版本錯誤地稱佩吉·弗拉納根是第一位當選美國參議院的美洲原住民。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "She is the first Native American woman elected to the upper chamber.", "zh": "她是第一位被選為上議院議員的美國原住民女性。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "當最新一批美國參議員在一月份宣誓就職時，其中將包括一些美國的第一名。　圖雷克將成為第一位在參議院任職的殘奧會運動員。這位民主黨人曾兩度獲得輪椅籃球金牌。由於脊柱裂，圖雷克截癱並需要使用輪椅。他在大選中擊敗了共和黨人阿什利·辛森。　萊特洛現已兩度創造歷史。她是 2021 年路易斯安那州第一位當選美國眾議院議員的共和黨女性。萊特洛在一次特別選舉中競選眾議院議員，以取代她已故的丈夫、國會議員盧克·萊特洛（後者於 2020 年因 COVID-19 去世）。現在，路易斯安那州選民決定將她送往參議院，她將成為該州第一位任職的共和黨女性。她將接替萊特洛在初選中擊敗的共和黨參議員比爾·卡西迪。　即將上任的民主黨參議員是埃及移民的兒子，也是第一位擔任參議員的穆斯林人士。埃爾-賽義德是一位流行病學家，也是底特律市前衛生總監。他擊敗了共和黨人麥克羅傑斯，贏得了競爭激烈的席位。　明尼蘇達州的民主黨副州長是第一位當選參議員的美國原住民女性。弗拉納根是奧及布威白土樂團的成員。她還不只創造了政治歷史。她也是明尼蘇達州第一位當選州政府官員的有色人種女性。弗拉納根將接替即將卸任的民主黨參議員蒂娜史密斯。　帕帕斯是第一位當選參議員的公開同性戀者，也是第一位代表新罕布夏州的同性戀者。他在眾議院連任四屆，並在選舉中擊敗了共和黨人約翰·蘇努努。　在選舉之夜最大的冷門之一中，安德魯斯在深紅色的南卡羅來納州取得了失敗的勝利。安德魯斯是第一位從帕爾梅托州當選為美國參議員的女性。她擊敗了達林·格雷厄姆，後者被任命接替她已故的兄弟林賽·格雷厄姆。　這兩個州都是可靠的共和黨州，都派牧師到華盛頓。這次中期選舉選民打破現狀，選舉民主黨人在參議院代表他們。　在德州，選民選擇民主黨人詹姆斯·塔拉里科為下一任參議員。這是長角州自 1988 年以來首次派遣民主黨人進入眾議院。塔拉里科擊敗了共和黨候選人肯·帕克斯頓。　近一百年後，堪薩斯州選出了一位民主黨參議員進入眾議院。亞當漢密爾頓將成為自 1932 年以來第一位為該州服務的民主黨人。他在與現任共和黨人羅傑馬歇爾的激烈競爭中脫穎而出。　這個故事的先前版本錯誤地稱佩吉·弗拉納根是第一位當選美國參議院的美洲原住民。她是第一位被選為上議院議員的美國原住民女性。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/nx-s1-6032814/senate-history-election-pappas-andrews-el-sayed"}, {"code": "20261107-3", "ch": "2026-11-07　週六", "sec": "NPR News", "title": "Trump's global health strategy is emerging. What will the Democratic Congress say?　／　川普的全球衛生戰略正在形成。民主黨國會會說什麼？", "items": [{"k": "lead", "t": "今日 NPR 新聞英語。本篇出自 NPR News，作者 By&nbsp;、Gabrielle Emanuel，全文共 18 段、33 句。畫面預設只顯示英文原句，點任一句展開中譯；右上角「🔍 全面解析」可一次展開全部中譯與字彙；「🌲 速讀」是文章結構圖＋單字克漏字測驗。　本篇摘要：川普政府使美國對全球衛生援助的方式發生了根本性轉變。新當選的民主黨國會將如何參與？"}, {"k": "src", "t": "📎 NPR 原文連結（點擊開新分頁）", "u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/nx-s1-6028828/global-health-usaid-trump-democrats-congress"}, {"k": "tip", "t": "本篇較長，站上只收前 18 段；想讀完整篇請點上方的 NPR 原文連結。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📰 原文逐句 Full Text", "ic": "📰"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 1 段", "d": "從表面上看，這是一場典型的政府儀式。穿西裝的官員。木桌周圍有黑色的大…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶1", "t": "By all appearances, it was a classic government ceremony. Officials in suits.", "zh": "從表面上看，這是一場典型的政府儀式。穿西裝的官員。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Big black chairs around a wooden table.", "zh": "木桌周圍有黑色的大椅子。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "A cluster of microphones.", "zh": "一組麥克風。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "It happened on October 8 in Lusaka, Zambia.", "zh": "這件事發生在10月8日的尚比亞盧薩卡。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Amid applause, U.S. and Zambian officials signed a global health agreement, called a Memorandum of Understanding or MOU.", "zh": "在掌聲中，美國和尚比亞官員簽署了一項全球衛生協議，稱為諒解備忘錄或諒解備忘錄。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 2 段", "d": "但美國駐尚比亞大使館臨時代辦米奇·科克表示，這項協議絕非經典。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶2", "t": "But Mich Coker — the Chargé d'Affaires at the U.S. Embassy in Zambia — said this agreement was anything but classic.", "zh": "但美國駐尚比亞大使館臨時代辦米奇·科克表示，這項協議絕非經典。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 3 段", "d": "「這份諒解備忘錄代表著根本性的轉變，」他在簽字儀式上說道。他解釋說，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶3", "t": "\"This MOU represents a fundamental shift,\" he said, speaking at the signing ceremony.", "zh": "「這份諒解備忘錄代表著根本性的轉變，」他在簽字儀式上說道。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "He explained that the relationship between the two countries was moving \"from a traditional donor-recipient model to a true partnership, one grounded in Zambian leadership, in Zambian ownership and in shared accountability.\"", "zh": "他解釋說，兩國之間的關係正在「從傳統的捐助者-受援者模式轉變為真正的夥伴關係，這種夥伴關係以贊比亞的領導、贊比亞的所有權和共同的責任為基礎」。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 4 段", "d": "世界各地政治派別的全球衛生專家都同意科克的觀點，即美國對全球衛生的態…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶4", "t": "Global health experts on all sides of the political spectrum and all over the world agree with Coker that there's been a fundamental shift in the U.S. approach to global health.", "zh": "世界各地政治派別的全球衛生專家都同意科克的觀點，即美國對全球衛生的態度發生了根本性轉變。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 5 段", "d": "全球發展中心全球健康計畫代理聯合主任珍寧·馬丹·凱勒 (Janeen…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶5", "t": "\"The shift that's currently unfolding is very large and it's very rapid,\" says Janeen Madan Keller, acting co-director of the Global Health Program at the Center for Global Development.", "zh": "全球發展中心全球健康計畫代理聯合主任珍寧·馬丹·凱勒 (Janeen Madan Keller) 表示：“目前正在發生的轉變規模非常大，而且速度非常快。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 6 段", "d": "馬丹凱勒和其他專家表示，這一根本性轉變的故事始於川普第二屆政府上任之…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶6", "t": "The story of this fundamental shift starts at the beginning of the second Trump Administration with months of global health turmoil — Madan Keller and other experts say — but has given way to a clearer strategy.", "zh": "馬丹凱勒和其他專家表示，這一根本性轉變的故事始於川普第二屆政府上任之初，當時全球衛生領域經歷了數月的動盪，但現在已經讓位給更清晰的戰略。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "One with big goals, a short timeline and a lot less transparency than what came before.", "zh": "與以前相比，它的目標遠大，時間表較短，透明度也低得多。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 7 段", "d": "以下是目前的情況以及民主黨控制的國會可能如何影響新格局。", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶7", "t": "Here is a look at where things stand now and how a Congress controlled by the Democratic Party might impact the new landscape.", "zh": "以下是目前的情況以及民主黨控制的國會可能如何影響新格局。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 8 段", "d": "川普總統的第二任期戲劇性地開始了。當他以涉嫌「欺詐、浪費和濫用」為由…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶8", "t": "President Trump's second term started dramatically.", "zh": "川普總統的第二任期戲劇性地開始了。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "When he dismantled USAID (the U.S. Agency for International Development), citing alleged \"fraud, waste and abuse,\" everything changed overnight.", "zh": "當他以涉嫌「欺詐、浪費和濫用」為由解散美國國際開發署（USAID）時，一切都在一夜之間發生了變化。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 9 段", "d": "「這是一個用混亂來形容的時期，」馬丹凱勒說。她說，“對於世界上一些最…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶9", "t": "\"It is a period that is best described as chaos,\" says Madan Keller.", "zh": "「這是一個用混亂來形容的時期，」馬丹凱勒說。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "The repercussions were massive and immediate, she says, \"for people and communities in some of the poorest countries of the world.\"", "zh": "她說，“對於世界上一些最貧窮國家的人民和社區來說”，影響是巨大而直接的。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 10 段", "d": "診所突然關閉。患者的愛滋病藥物用完了。在尚比亞以及其他一些國家，許多…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶10", "t": "Clinics shut down suddenly.", "zh": "診所突然關閉。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Patients ran out of HIV medications.", "zh": "患者的愛滋病藥物用完了。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In Zambia, as well as a number of other countries, many patients who relied on U.S.-supported clinics and programs faced tons of uncertainty and, often, dire health consequences.", "zh": "在尚比亞以及其他一些國家，許多依賴美國支持的診所和計畫的患者面臨大量的不確定性，而且往往面臨可怕的健康後果。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 11 段", "d": "KFF 高級副總裁兼全球和公共衛生政策總監 Jennifer Kat…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶11", "t": "\"For the first half of 2025, there was a complete upheaval,\" says Jennifer Kates, senior vice president and director of global and public health policy at KFF.", "zh": "KFF 高級副總裁兼全球和公共衛生政策總監 Jennifer Kates 表示：“2025 年上半年發生了徹底的劇變。”"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 12 段", "d": "接下來，美國對外援助的歷史進入了一個新階段。 「從 2025 年夏季…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶12", "t": "Next came a new stage in the history of U.S. foreign aid.", "zh": "接下來，美國對外援助的歷史進入了一個新階段。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "\"Starting over the summer of 2025 and going into September, there actually was a sort of step back to develop an actual strategy and a plan,\" says Kates.", "zh": "「從 2025 年夏季開始到 9 月，實際上需要退一步來製定實際的策略和計劃，」凱特說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 13 段", "d": "美國國務院提出了“美國第一全球健康戰略”，其既定目標是“讓美國更安全…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶13", "t": "What emerged from the State Department was the America First Global Health Strategy with the stated goal of making \"America safer, stronger, and more prosperous.\" The main way this strategy is being implemented is through agreements with individual countries.", "zh": "美國國務院提出了“美國第一全球健康戰略”，其既定目標是“讓美國更安全、更強大、更繁榮”。該戰略實施的主要方式是透過與各國達成協議。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "In the past, the U.S. had done more work through large international organizations or local non-governmental organizations.", "zh": "過去，美國更多是透過大型國際組織或地方非政府組織所做的工作。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 14 段", "d": "專家表示，這些協議的一個顯著特徵是它們是交易性的。例如，在尚比亞，「…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶14", "t": "Experts say one defining feature of these agreements is that they are transactional.", "zh": "專家表示，這些協議的一個顯著特徵是它們是交易性的。"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "For example, in Zambia \"there was a massive scandal because activists were able to show that the agreement was planning to condition access to [U.S. global health] funding on access to [Zambia's] copper and rare earth minerals,\" says Asia Russell, executive director of the HIV/AIDS advocacy organization Health GAP.", "zh": "例如，在尚比亞，「發生了一場大規模醜聞，因為活動人士能夠證明，該協議計劃以獲取（贊比亞的）銅和稀土礦產作為獲得（美國全球衛生）資金的條件，」愛滋病毒/愛滋病倡導組織健康差距（Health GAP）執行董事阿莎·拉塞爾（Asia Russell）說。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "Her organization helped expose this situation.", "zh": "她的組織幫助揭露了這一情況。", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 15 段", "d": "儘管在尚比亞引起公眾強烈抗議後，有關礦物的協議部分從全球衛生協議中分…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶15", "t": "While the part of the agreement about minerals was separated from the global health agreement after the public outcry in Zambia, many of the global health agreements do require the recipient country to share data such as pathogen information.", "zh": "儘管在尚比亞引起公眾強烈抗議後，有關礦物的協議部分從全球衛生協議中分離出來，但許多全球衛生協議確實要求受援國共享病原體資訊等數據。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 16 段", "d": "科克在尚比亞舉行的簽字儀式上發表講話，列舉了新戰略中的一些首要任務，…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶16", "t": "Speaking at the signing ceremony in Zambia, Coker ticked off some of the top priorities in the new strategy, including that recipient countries increase their financial contributions to health in the years ahead and that they are transitioned off aid in the near future.", "zh": "科克在尚比亞舉行的簽字儀式上發表講話，列舉了新戰略中的一些首要任務，包括受援國在未來幾年增加對衛生的財政捐助，並在不久的將來停止援助。"}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 17 段", "d": "他表示，在尚比亞諒解備忘錄中，美國將在五年內支付 15 億美元，“贊…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶17", "t": "He said in the Zambian MOU, the U.S. would pay $1.5 billion over five years \"with Zambia simultaneously committing to increase its own domestic health expenditures by $975 million.", "zh": "他表示，在尚比亞諒解備忘錄中，美國將在五年內支付 15 億美元，“贊比亞同時承諾將其國內衛生支出增加 9.75 億美元。”"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "", "t": "We are charting a path toward a stronger, more self-reliant health system.\"", "zh": "我們正在規劃一條通往更強大、更自力更生的衛生系統的道路。 」", "cn": 1}, {"k": "h2", "t": "第 18 段", "d": "另一個優先事項是建立一個國家自己的衛生基礎設施，而不是由非營利組織和…", "ic": "¶"}, {"k": "en", "sp": "¶18", "t": "Another priority has been building up a country's own health infrastructure — and not a parallel system run by non-profits and NGOs.", "zh": "另一個優先事項是建立一個國家自己的衛生基礎設施，而不是由非營利組織和非政府組織運作的平行系統。"}, {"k": "h1", "t": "📖 全文中譯", "ic": "📖"}, {"k": "zhblk", "t": "從表面上看，這是一場典型的政府儀式。穿西裝的官員。木桌周圍有黑色的大椅子。一組麥克風。這件事發生在10月8日的尚比亞盧薩卡。在掌聲中，美國和尚比亞官員簽署了一項全球衛生協議，稱為諒解備忘錄或諒解備忘錄。　但美國駐尚比亞大使館臨時代辦米奇·科克表示，這項協議絕非經典。　「這份諒解備忘錄代表著根本性的轉變，」他在簽字儀式上說道。他解釋說，兩國之間的關係正在「從傳統的捐助者-受援者模式轉變為真正的夥伴關係，這種夥伴關係以贊比亞的領導、贊比亞的所有權和共同的責任為基礎」。　世界各地政治派別的全球衛生專家都同意科克的觀點，即美國對全球衛生的態度發生了根本性轉變。　全球發展中心全球健康計畫代理聯合主任珍寧·馬丹·凱勒 (Janeen Madan Keller) 表示：“目前正在發生的轉變規模非常大，而且速度非常快。”　馬丹凱勒和其他專家表示，這一根本性轉變的故事始於川普第二屆政府上任之初，當時全球衛生領域經歷了數月的動盪，但現在已經讓位給更清晰的戰略。與以前相比，它的目標遠大，時間表較短，透明度也低得多。　以下是目前的情況以及民主黨控制的國會可能如何影響新格局。　川普總統的第二任期戲劇性地開始了。當他以涉嫌「欺詐、浪費和濫用」為由解散美國國際開發署（USAID）時，一切都在一夜之間發生了變化。　「這是一個用混亂來形容的時期，」馬丹凱勒說。她說，“對於世界上一些最貧窮國家的人民和社區來說”，影響是巨大而直接的。　診所突然關閉。患者的愛滋病藥物用完了。在尚比亞以及其他一些國家，許多依賴美國支持的診所和計畫的患者面臨大量的不確定性，而且往往面臨可怕的健康後果。　KFF 高級副總裁兼全球和公共衛生政策總監 Jennifer Kates 表示：“2025 年上半年發生了徹底的劇變。”　接下來，美國對外援助的歷史進入了一個新階段。 「從 2025 年夏季開始到 9 月，實際上需要退一步來製定實際的策略和計劃，」凱特說。　美國國務院提出了“美國第一全球健康戰略”，其既定目標是“讓美國更安全、更強大、更繁榮”。該戰略實施的主要方式是透過與各國達成協議。過去，美國更多是透過大型國際組織或地方非政府組織所做的工作。　專家表示，這些協議的一個顯著特徵是它們是交易性的。例如，在尚比亞，「發生了一場大規模醜聞，因為活動人士能夠證明，該協議計劃以獲取（贊比亞的）銅和稀土礦產作為獲得（美國全球衛生）資金的條件，」愛滋病毒/愛滋病倡導組織健康差距（Health GAP）執行董事阿莎·拉塞爾（Asia Russell）說。她的組織幫助揭露了這一情況。　儘管在尚比亞引起公眾強烈抗議後，有關礦物的協議部分從全球衛生協議中分離出來，但許多全球衛生協議確實要求受援國共享病原體資訊等數據。　科克在尚比亞舉行的簽字儀式上發表講話，列舉了新戰略中的一些首要任務，包括受援國在未來幾年增加對衛生的財政捐助，並在不久的將來停止援助。　他表示，在尚比亞諒解備忘錄中，美國將在五年內支付 15 億美元，“贊比亞同時承諾將其國內衛生支出增加 9.75 億美元。我們正在規劃一條通往更強大、更自力更生的衛生系統的道路。”　另一個優先事項是建立一個國家自己的衛生基礎設施，而不是由非營利組織和非政府組織運作的平行系統。"}], "_u": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/nx-s1-6028828/global-health-usaid-trump-democrats-congress"}];